Single source of truth for **open + partial** items. Add a new entry to the bottom of the value tier it belongs to (see **Ordering** below); status changes happen in place — when an item ships, move its row to the Resolved archive in **[DONE.md](DONE.md)**. The shipped-capability summary and every `✅ Done` / Removed / Won't-fix / Superseded row now live in **[DONE.md](DONE.md)** (gap IDs stay globally unique across both files, so `#NNNN` references still resolve).

**Phases:** `Now` = 0–30 days · `Soon` = 30–60 days · `Mid` = 60–120 days · `Later` = 6–12 months

**Types:** `billing` = revenue enforcement · `feature` = product capability · `arch` = architecture · `quality` = code quality · `legacy` = legacy parity · `bug` = defect · `perf` = performance

**Ordering:** active entries are grouped into four value tiers — **T1 Direct Revenue**, **T2 Conversion & Activation**, **T3 Retention & Growth**, **T4 Cost / Quality / Arch** — then sorted within each tier by Priority → Phase → Status → id. Resolved items (✅ Done / Removed / Won't-fix / Superseded) are collected at the bottom. Tiering is heuristic (type + title keywords); move a row between tiers by editing it if the call is wrong.

**Current totals (recounted 2026-06-20): 717 active — T1 91 · T2 68 · T3 352 · T4 206 — plus 578 ✅ Done and 15 closed/superseded now archived in [DONE.md](DONE.md). Overall completion = Done / (Done + active) = 578/1295 = **45%**. (2026-06-20 pass: extracted the entire Resolved archive + shipped-capability summary out of this README into [DONE.md](DONE.md), leaving the register open + partial only; per-track independence split refreshed in the Isolation Tracks table above.) For PARALLEL work + per-track completion use the Isolation Tracks (TK1–TK11) above, not these revenue tiers. All gap IDs are globally unique; the Done section is sorted by id ascending. (TK11 i18n pass 2026-06-14: closed #885 OAuth-button verbs (T2) + #444 AuthOverlay (T4) — both localized via new `auth.oauth.*` / `auth.overlay.*` keys across en/es/fr-CA; rows flipped Done in-place. T4 fix pass 2026-06-14: closed #878 job-edit field-drop, #1958 Companies tsc, #2091 work-setting/hybrid-days (richer per product owner); #1588 → Partial (slug index + normalize short-circuit landed, payload-diet/diagnostic residual); logged T4 #2090/#2092 + #979 type-normalise; renumbered #2068/#2069→#2090/#2091 to dodge concurrent-edit ID collisions. NOTE: the register is being edited by a concurrent process this session — several duplicate IDs (#2068–#2071) now exist; #2009 covers the cleanup.)** (Prior 2026-06-13 cleanup pass: moved 89 ✅ Done rows out of the active tiers into the Resolved section, restored the lost Tier 2 heading, normalised stray 🟡 status markers; logged register-integrity gap #2009 for the duplicate #1800 ID. Updated 2026-05-30 sixth pass: closed #1007 (real Scratch-shaped visual block editor — extended AST in shared/game-blocks.ts + plain-JS interpreter in block-interp.js + runtime + exported-bundle wiring + 8-category block vocabulary + tabbed workspace integration + 37 new tests across AST/interp); new sub-gap #1800 (Snap! Phase 2 polish — custom procedures, lists, pen, costumes, sound primitives, show-monitor HUD). Fifth pass: closed #1620 (MCP execution + 7 dispatch tests) and #930 (CAD 3D Phase 2 — R3F stage + primitives + mutators + migration 0184); status-synced #939/#940/#1004/#1349; new sub-gaps #1796/#1797/#1798/#1799. Fourth pass: flipped 8 — #168/#325/#810/#1339/#1361/#1471/#1503/#1692. Third pass: flipped 19 previously-Partial entries to Done — #99/#101/#109/#180/#187/#188/#287/#292/#743/#820/#1520/#1559/#127/#285/#927/#1209/#1262/#1560. Prior passes summarised above.)


### TK1 — platform-infra — Platform, Migrations, Perf & Arch (COORDINATOR) — 62 active

**Owned paths:** `api/drizzle/**`, `.github/**`, `api/src/middleware/**`, `api/src/utils/**`, `api/scripts/**`, root build/lint configs

| # | Rev | Status | Phase | Priority | Type | Gap | Notes |
|---|-----|--------|-------|----------|------|-----|-------|
| 737 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `bug` | **Drizzle-kit `_journal.json` is empty so there is no authoritative ledger of which migrations have been applied — drift like the `interview_*` tables sits silently until something queries them** (2026-05-17 — surfaced while closing #736) | [drizzle/meta/_journal.json](hired.video/api/drizzle/meta/_journal.json) is `{"entries":[]}`; migrations are applied manually via the `db:migrate` script (read one SQL file, split on `;`, run each statement). Nothing records what's been applied to which environment, so a fresh deploy or a partially-failed apply leaves the live DB out of sync with the schema and the failure surfaces only the next time a route happens to query the missing column/table. Fix: either (a) adopt a real `drizzle_migrations` ledger table + an apply-on-boot worker hook, or (b) add a `db:diff` CI check that fails the deploy when `schema/*.ts` declares a table missing from `information_schema.tables`. Both are larger than the 0089 patch we just shipped. Unblocks: the full set of silent schema-drift bugs that match #736's pattern. |
| 835 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `quality` | **No regression test for `POST /api/auth/magic-link` — the captcha gate added in commit `a564d95` (#426) silent-200'd every send in prod with `TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY` set, undetected until a user reported "email never arrives" 2026-05-19** (opened 2026-05-19) | The route at [api/src/routes/auth.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/auth.ts#L554) was the ONLY auth-send endpoint with zero unit/route coverage — `auth-handlers.test.ts` covers `handleLogin`/`handleRegister`/`handleForgotPassword` and asserts captcha behaviour for login, but the magic-link handler is inlined in the route file (not a shared `handle*` in `AuthService.ts`) and is never exercised. Even at full backend coverage, contract drift between FE and BE would still slip through: the frontend `handleMagicLink` in [Login.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Login.tsx#L154) doesn't post `cfTurnstileToken` and there is no widget in the magic-link form. Fix: (a) port `handleMagicLink` into `AuthService.ts` alongside the other `handle*` handlers, with a deps-injected captcha port + email sender, mirroring the `handleLogin` test pattern; (b) add a `tests/contract/auth.contract.test.ts` that snapshots the frontend POST body shape for each auth send route against the backend's `safeParse` schema so a future "added a required field on the backend" silently passing on the frontend gets caught. Unblocks: silent-200 failure modes on the rescue path (and any future enumeration-safe handler) can't escape into production again. |
| 962 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `bug` | **DB migration 0102 (`image_state` column + CHECK constraint relax for `'image'` kind) is checked into `api/drizzle/` but must be applied on every deployed environment — until then drawing-template saves fail server-side on the INSERT (column missing or check-constraint violation)** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced auditing why drawing-template creates may still toast a server error after the #957 / #961 frontend fixes; deploy-pipeline issue, not a code bug) | Migration file [0102_studio_projects_image_canvas_runtime.sql](hired.video/api/drizzle/0102_studio_projects_image_canvas_runtime.sql) ships the schema additions image-kind projects need: `studio_projects.image_state` JSONB column + relaxed CHECK constraint on `media_kind` to include `'image'` + mirror change on `studio_templates`. Without these the server INSERT throws either "column image_state does not exist" or "violates check constraint studio_projects_media_kind_check" — both surface as the kind-aware "Couldn't create image" toast (since #961) but read as opaque to a non-engineer. **Action per environment:** run `npm -w api run db:push` against the env's Neon DATABASE_URL after deploying the frontend bundle that includes the image kind. **Long-term**: (i) CI gate that fails the deploy if `studio_projects.image_state` is missing from the connected database; (ii) server-side boot probe that logs a warning when any expected `media_kind` value is rejected by the CHECK constraint; (iii) automated migration runner. Unblocks: drawing templates actually creating end-to-end on every deployed environment, not just dev. |
| 1588 | T4 | ⚠️ Partial | Now | P1 | `bug` | **`GET /api/resumes/:id` and `GET /api/resumes/embedded/:id` exceed Cloudflare Worker CPU limit on slug-keyed lookups** (opened 2026-05-26 from live error log: `exceededCpu` on `/api/resumes/embedded/seanhogg` at 2026-05-26T21:16:29Z, request id `a01fcd1f5fdf80ba`, plus four prior `/api/resumes/seanhogg` failures within 25 s — same fingerprint `108bf7347bc9bb6792581caa33c576a5`). Shared handler is [handleGetResume](hired.video/api/src/services/resume/ResumeService.ts) — both routes converge there. Three suspected contributors, stacked: **(a) Missing `slug` index on `resume_information`** — [schema](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/resumes.ts) only declares `resume_information_user_id_idx` + `resume_information_parent_id_idx`; [findByIdOrSlug](hired.video/api/src/repositories/resumeRepository.ts) `eq(resumeInformation.slug, idOrSlug)` therefore seq-scans the whole table on every embed / detail load (DB-side, doesn't directly burn worker CPU but compounds with all the others by holding the request open). **(b) `normalizeContent` deep-walks the entire JSONB content on every read** — [normalizeJsonResume → remapKeys](hired.video/api/src/services/resume/parse.ts) re-allocates every object + array in the tree regardless of whether the row is already canonical lowercase-keyed. For rows where `content.metaData` carries embedded media descriptors (data URIs, large skillEvidence arrays from #1349 / [[project_skill_evidence]], or legacy AI-parse residuals), the walk is O(content-size) and dominates worker CPU. **(c) `c.json(result.body)` runs `JSON.stringify` over the full normalized blob** — content fields like `metaData`, `skillEvidence`, and the new `meta.template` bag can balloon to several MB on heavy users; even at canonical shape, the serialize step is unavoidable per-request. **Fix plan**: (1) **DB**: add `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS resume_information_slug_idx ON resume_information (slug) WHERE slug IS NOT NULL` as a new migration — partial-index since most rows have a UUID-derived slug, but the conditional keeps the index small. (2) **Read-path normalization**: short-circuit `normalizeContent` when the stored row is already canonical — detect by checking whether any top-level key starts with an uppercase character; if not, return the input plus default-array fills without walking. The PascalCase normalization is only meaningful for legacy hired.video JSON-Resume exports that haven't been re-saved since the migration — i.e. a vanishingly small share of read traffic. (3) **Payload diet**: audit what `content.metaData` and `content.skillEvidence` look like on the affected slug (`seanhogg`) — if they're carrying base64 media or 1000+ evidence rows, ship a one-time backfill that moves media references to the existing `metaData` media-attachment endpoint and dedupes skillEvidence. (4) **Diagnostic**: instrument [handleGetResume](hired.video/api/src/services/resume/ResumeService.ts) to emit `console.warn("[resumes/get] large content", { resumeId, contentSize, slug })` when stringified content exceeds 256 KB so we can tell whether (b) or (c) is the dominant cost. **Adjacent**: gap #979 already flags the 30 s worker CPU budget as fragile for any sync-fanout flow; gap #1570 documents the per-invocation subrequest cap. This one is the read-side analog. **Unblocks**: every embedded resume on every public profile + Chrome-extension embed + social-feed card — the embed has been silently 5XXing for every user whose content blob crossed the size threshold. **Partial 2026-06-14 — the two CPU-side fixes are in:** (1) **slug index** already shipped via [0141](hired.video/api/drizzle/0141_studio_projects_slug_column.sql) (`CREATE INDEX … resume_information_slug_idx … WHERE slug IS NOT NULL`); this pass also corrected the Drizzle schema declaration to the matching partial form so `db:push` won't try to recreate it ([resumes.ts](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/resumes.ts)). (2) **`normalizeContent` short-circuit** — [content.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/resume/content.ts) now skips the O(content-size) `remapKeys` deep-walk + re-allocation for already-canonical rows (a cheap top-level-key scan; legacy PascalCase rows still take the full walk), covered by [resume-normalize-content.test.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/__tests__/resume-normalize-content.test.ts) (6 cases). **Still open (the data-ops + observability halves):** (c) one-time payload-diet backfill for heavy blobs (base64 media / 1000+ skillEvidence rows on the affected slug) and (d) the `console.warn("[resumes/get] large content", …)` diagnostic when stringified content > 256 KB. Umbrella #1592 tracks whether the tail quiets after deploy. |
