| 750 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `arch` | **Public-route allowlist in [app.ts](hired.video/api/src/app.ts) drifts from the per-handler "No auth required" intent every time a new public endpoint lands** (2026-05-17 — surfaced while closing #749: `/api/studio/videos/featured` shipped with the handler comment "No auth required" but `PUBLIC_PREFIXES` was never updated, so prod returned 401 UNAUTHORIZED on the homepage carousel call) | The auth requirement is asserted in TWO places: (a) the handler's docstring claims "No auth required" and the route does no auth read; (b) `PUBLIC_PREFIXES` in [app.ts](hired.video/api/src/app.ts) — a hand-maintained string array consulted by the JWT middleware. Adding a public endpoint only in (a) ships a 401 to production; the route file's intent is silently overridden. Fix options: (1) each route file exports its own `PUBLIC_PATHS: string[]` constant that app.ts unions, so the public list lives next to the handler. (2) Tag handlers via a `.public()` chain or `c.var.isPublic = true` set in a per-route middleware. (3) Replace the prefix allowlist with a per-handler `requireAuth` middleware applied at registration time — opt-in auth instead of opt-out. Unblocks: zero "forgot to allowlist" 401 regressions on every new public endpoint. The same pattern bit #324 / #747 in the past month. |
