| 697 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **SQL migration runner has no `_migrations` ledger — every deploy re-runs all 85+ files** (2026-05-16 — surfaced while fixing the failed 0085 deploy) | [api/scripts/run-sql-migrations.mjs](hired.video/api/scripts/run-sql-migrations.mjs) iterates every `drizzle/0*.sql` file on every deploy and only tolerates per-statement "already exists" errors. This forces every destructive op (DROP COLUMN, RENAME COLUMN, data backfills that reference dropped columns) to be hand-rolled idempotent — usually via `DO $$ ... END $$` guards on `information_schema.columns` / `pg_constraint`. 0085 shipped without those guards and broke the next deploy ("column video_id does not exist") because the runner also re-ran 0003 whose `CREATE INDEX ON ...(video_id)` now references a column 0085 dropped. Fix landed for 0003 + 0085, but the class of bug recurs on any future schema-rewrite migration unless the runner stores a `applied_at` ledger keyed by filename and short-circuits already-run files. Unblocks: schema rewrites stop being a deploy hazard; new migrations only need to be idempotent in their own right (not against earlier files re-running). |
| 1513 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `bug` | **CI install retry loop swallows persistent failures — `for i in 1 2 3; do npm install … && break; sleep 5; done` exits 0 even when all 3 attempts fail** (opened 2026-05-26 after the typecheck-against-empty-node_modules outage that motivated #1507's Tiptap install). The loop's overall exit code is the last `sleep` (always 0), so a hard install failure leaves node_modules unpopulated and silently lets the next step run with "Cannot find module 'react'" everywhere. Fix: track success in a variable and `exit 1` after the loop if none of the attempts succeeded, or chain three invocations via `||` so the overall command propagates the last non-zero exit. Applies to every install step in [.github/workflows/ci.yml](hired.video/.github/workflows/ci.yml). The 2026-05-26 fix swapping `npm ci` → `npm install` removes the lockfile-drift trigger but does not fix the latent bug. |
| 1618 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `bug` | **74 frontend vitest cases fail under network-mocking gaps + one real `nullToUndefined` regression** (opened 2026-05-26 when `cd frontend && npm test` was wired as an advisory CI step under gap #1617 — `vitest run` had never run in CI before, so the failures had been accumulating invisibly). Affected files include `EntityHubShell.test.tsx` (6/6 fail), `JobResumeMatch.test.tsx` (9/9), `PeopleCard.test.tsx` (8/8), `ResumeTailor.test.tsx` (8/8), `StoryboardEditor.test.tsx` (11/11). Dominant failure mode: `"Network request failed"` — these tests issue real `fetch` calls without mocking the global, so under vitest jsdom they consistently fail; suites that pass either don't make network calls or have local mocks. **One real regression**: `resume-service.passthrough.test.ts` reports `"Regression: nullToUndefined is back. Backend nulls rejected by canonical schema"` — that's a live data-shape issue, not an environment problem. **Fix path**: (1) Audit the 14 failing files and add MSW (or `vi.stubGlobal('fetch', ...)`) handlers per file. (2) Fix the resume-service `nullToUndefined` regression as its own slice once root-caused. (3) Once green, flip `continue-on-error: true` in [.github/workflows/ci.yml](hired.video/.github/workflows/ci.yml) so frontend test becomes required. **Unblocks**: every PR catches frontend regressions the same way the api side now does. **Update 2026-05-31**: three *non-network* failures fixed in a separate pass — `AIResumeScorer.test.tsx` (AppShell mounts `<EmailVerificationBanner>` whose `getVerificationStatus` was missing from the test's `useAuth` mock), `SearchBar.test.tsx` (asserted on pre-i18n copy `professionals` instead of the rendered `search.bar.placeholder.people` key), and `CreatorTemplatesPanel.test.tsx` (rendered `<ArtifactDetailsSheet>` → `useAuth` with no provider, and a stale `window.confirm` spy after the component moved to `confirmDialog`). These weren't part of the network-mocking root cause; the 14-file MSW audit + the `nullToUndefined` regression remain open. |
| 1873 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `perf` | **Unified-search cache invalidation relies on the 120s TTL backstop for a handful of low-churn write seams rather than instant `bumpSearchVersion()`** (opened 2026-06-02 alongside the `/api/search/public` read-through cache, [api/src/utils/search-cache.ts](hired.video/api/src/utils/search-cache.ts)). Instant version-bump invalidation IS wired for the primary write seams of all 10 searchable kinds (jobs via JobService create/update/delete + archive/unarchive; templates + events via their services; articles incl. admin bulk-approve + moderation gate; courses publish/unpublish/patch/delete; companies create/update/delete; voice clones create/patch/delete; videos publish + visibility; resume setprivacy; profile upsert). Still falling back to the ≤120s TTL (not instant): (a) `users.emailVerified` flip in the auth/email-confirm flow — a newly-verified user only enters the `people` bucket on the next TTL expiry; (b) resume **create** of an already-public resume + resume **delete** (only `/setprivacy` is wired); (c) jobs `/extract` + `/refresh` routes if they bypass `JobService.createJob/updateJob` with direct `db` writes (verify). Correctness is unaffected (backstop bounds staleness ≤120s); only freshness latency. To close: wire `bumpSearchVersion()` into those seams. Unblocks: strict "new content visible on next request" for every searchable mutation. |
