| 1203 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P2 | `test` | **Schema-vs-migration parity drift — 107 `pgTable(...)` declarations have no `CREATE TABLE` migration in `api/drizzle/`, and 9 migration-created tables have no Drizzle `pgTable` declaration** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the #1186 fix + the new [scripts/migration-schema-parity.test.mjs](hired.video/api/scripts/migration-schema-parity.test.mjs) regression suite) — root cause of the #1186 deploy failure was systemic: the core schema (`users`, `resumes`, `jobs`, `studio_projects`, etc.) was originally bootstrapped via an out-of-tree `drizzle-kit push` and only migrations from 0001 onward live in version control. 107 tables are frozen in the test's `KNOWN_MISSING_CREATE_TABLE` baseline (the ratchet prevents *new* drift; existing entries shrink as backfill migrations land). The 9 orphan tables (`promo_project_reviews`, `company_reviews`, `sourced_people`, `sourced_person_merge_log`, `person_identifiers`, `person_sources`, `enrichment_cache`, `data_subject_requests`, `data_suppression_list`) are migration leftovers from polymorphic refactors and the BurnRateOS sourcing-pipeline split (0054 — see project_contact_sourcing_burnrateos.md) where the table was created but never declared in Drizzle, or declared and later removed without a DROP migration. To close: (a) write a backfill `0Bxx_legacy_schema_baseline.sql` capturing the current canonical CREATE TABLE for every entry in `KNOWN_MISSING_CREATE_TABLE` (use `pg_dump --schema-only` against production as the source of truth), (b) ship targeted DROP migrations for the orphan tables that genuinely went away, (c) shrink the baseline list and the `ALLOWED_ORPHANS` set in the parity test as each one is reconciled. Unblocks fresh-DB bring-up of dev environments without manual SQL + makes the test fail loud the moment ANY drift returns. |
| 1821 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Now | P3 | `bug` | **Frontend ESLint config fails to load — `require-page-chrome` rule export mismatch** (identified 2026-05-31 during CHRO frontend lint). [frontend/eslint.config.js](hired.video/frontend/eslint.config.js) does `import requirePageChrome from "./eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js"` (default import) but [frontend/eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js](hired.video/frontend/eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js) ends with `module.exports = { ... }` (CommonJS, no ESM default export), so `eslint .` aborts with `does not provide an export named 'default'`. Pre-existing (file last touched 2026-05-25, not by the CHRO pass). This means the require-page-chrome backstop + ALL frontend ESLint is currently a no-op in CI/local. Fix: convert the rule to `export default { ... }` (or have the config import it via `createRequire`). Unblocks: frontend lint + the new-page-chrome enforcement. |
