| 389 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Other OAuth tables likely share the `youtube_accounts` schema drift** (2026-05-05) | Migration `0076_youtube_accounts_drift_fix.sql` was needed because `youtube_accounts` was created in prod by an early `drizzle-kit push` and the canonical `0043` migration's `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` then silently skipped applying the full canonical column set (most visibly `google_id`). `linkedin_accounts` (created in `0003_studio_features.sql`) and `calendar_connections` use the same `oauthConnectionColumns` helper that was added later — they may have the same drift waiting (e.g. missing `scopes` / `token_expires_at` / `is_active`). The next time one of those tables is read with a `select()` Drizzle will hit the same `column "X" does not exist` 500. Fix: write a one-shot `pg_attribute` audit comparing each Drizzle table to its prod schema and emit ALTER TABLE statements for any missing columns; or, defensively, ship `0077`-style fixup migrations for `linkedin_accounts` and `calendar_connections` mirroring 0076. Identified 2026-05-05 from the youtube_accounts drift incident. |
| 460 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Local `hired.video` git repo has a corrupt loose object — `git gc` auto-pack fails** (2026-05-09) | `.git/objects/16/6eaf950c726f153a6e92ffc8268256222e37d8` fails inflate ("incorrect header check"). Surfaces during the auto-gc that runs after each commit; commits + push themselves still succeed, the housekeeping just can't repack. Likely from an interrupted earlier write. Fix: clone fresh from origin, copy uncommitted work over, OR run `git fsck --lost-found` then `git prune` after recovering anything dangling. Unblocks: clean local gc, smaller working tree, future `git fsck` not noisy. Identified 2026-05-09 committing the vendor-sync UX update. |
| 472 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`/tools` page mixes filter UX patterns — audience + tier are select dropdowns via `useHeaderFilters`, category is the new chip row in-page; filters now disagree on UX shape** (2026-05-09) | Audience and tier should probably also become chip rows above the grid (or inversely, category should join `useHeaderFilters` as a select). Pick one shape so the page reads as one filter surface. Chip rows scan faster than nested dropdowns — likely worth migrating audience+tier to chips and deprecating the header-filter slot for /tools. Out of scope for this pass. Identified 2026-05-09 adding the category chip row. |
| 476 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Music-lane preview ignores `mix.music.gain` + fade envelopes — export honours them, preview doesn't** (2026-05-09) | `VideoPreview`'s music master GainNode applies only `audio.volume` (project-wide), not the per-lane mix config from `AudioMixerDialog` (gap #129 lane gain + fadeInSec/fadeOutSec). Pre-existing — same behaviour as the old single-track AmbientPlayer path — but now visible alongside multi-clip work. Fix: route the master through a `buildLane`-equivalent in `VideoPreview` (extract from `video-exporter.ts` into `clip-scheduler.ts` so both surfaces share). Unblocks: WYSIWYG between mixer dialog tweaks and preview playback. Identified 2026-05-09 implementing multi-clip music. |
| 521 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **drizzle-kit pulls deprecated `@esbuild-kit/*` chain causing 4 moderate audit vulnerabilities (esbuild dev-server CSRF GHSA-67mh-4wv8-2f99)** (2026-05-10) | drizzle-kit 0.31.10 (latest as of today) still bundles `@esbuild-kit/esm-loader@2.6.5` → `@esbuild-kit/core-utils@3.3.2` → vulnerable esbuild. The `@esbuild-kit/*` packages are fully deprecated upstream and will not get patches. Exposure is local-dev only — drizzle-kit runs at `db:generate` / `db:push` time, not in the production worker. Fix: upstream drizzle-kit needs to migrate off @esbuild-kit (tracked in their issue tracker; out of our hands). Workaround if it becomes a CI gate: add `overrides` forcing `esbuild` to a fixed version + accept whatever breakage that causes drizzle-kit. Until then: don't run `drizzle-kit studio` on networks with untrusted clients. |
| 551 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`/outreach` page calls `useCommHub()` (line 121) before its `isAuthenticated` gate (line 469) — same anti-pattern as the CommunicationHub bug fixed in this pass** (2026-05-13) | [pages/Outreach.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Outreach.tsx) mounts the comm-hub hook unconditionally for every visitor and only branches to the marketing layout after lots of other hooks have run. `useGatedResource` SHOULD prevent the actual `/api/inbox` fetch for anonymous users (`useApiReady` returns false), but the fact that this very gate was observed to leak from the always-mounted CommunicationHub in the header means anonymous /outreach visits are suspect too. Fix mirrors the CommunicationHub split: extract an `AuthenticatedOutreach` inner component so the hook never mounts for anonymous users. Bigger refactor than CommunicationHub because Outreach has 10+ intermixed hooks before the auth check. Unblocks: closing the second remaining `/api/inbox` 401 source + a cleaner Outreach component shape. |
| 714 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **In-memory rate limiter buckets are per-worker — effective cap scales with worker count** (2026-05-16 — surfaced while fixing user-keyed rate limit) | [rateLimiter.ts:9](hired.video/api/src/middleware/rateLimiter.ts#L9) `store = new Map<string, RateLimitEntry>()` lives in a single worker's heap. With N Cloudflare Worker / Node instances behind the LB, an attacker (or a chatty real user) can effectively make `N × cap` requests per minute before any one bucket trips, because each instance sees only its own fraction of the traffic. Today only the global limiter, register limiter, and auth-write limiter share this property; the AI token ledger is correctly central (Postgres). Fix: move the three IP/user-keyed buckets behind a Cloudflare Durable Object (or KV with TTL) so the count is shared. Unblocks: deterministic enforcement of the documented caps under horizontal scaling. |
