| 1527 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **ESLint rule banning `z.string().uuid()` / `z.uuid()` outside `shared/validation.ts`** (opened 2026-05-26 as the follow-up that prevents #1522 from being reintroduced). Today the rule "any DB-row ID validator must use `UuidLikeSchema`, never `.uuid()`" is encoded only in a doc comment on [shared/validation.ts](hired.video/shared/validation.ts) — the next reviewer can copy a `z.string().uuid()` from a tutorial and re-add the strict validator. Fix: add a `no-restricted-syntax` ESLint rule (or a one-off `eslint-plugin-local` rule) that errors on `MemberExpression[object.callee.name='string'][property.name='uuid']` and `CallExpression[callee.object.name='z'][callee.property.name='uuid']` everywhere except `shared/validation.ts`. Pairs with the existing `require-page-chrome` and `no-raw-any-array` rule patterns the repo already ships. Unblocks: the "what's the right validator for an ID?" decision is enforced by the linter, not by tribal knowledge. |
| 1693 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`npm run lint` is broken project-wide — ESLint config fails to load `require-page-chrome` rule** (opened 2026-05-28 while wiring AI generation into the interview-template modal). [eslint.config.js:9](hired.video/frontend/eslint.config.js#L9) does `import requirePageChrome from "./eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js"` (ESM default import) but [eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js](hired.video/frontend/eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js#L30) uses CommonJS `module.exports = {…}`, and [frontend/package.json:4](hired.video/frontend/package.json#L4) is `"type": "module"` — so Node loads the rule file as ESM and the default import resolves to `undefined` (`SyntaxError: does not provide an export named 'default'`). Result: every `eslint`/`npm run lint`/`lint:ci` invocation aborts before linting a single file, so the `require-page-chrome` backstop (added for `[[feedback_new_page_checklist]]`) and ALL lint rules are silently dormant in CI and locally. Fix: convert the rule to ESM (`export default { … }`, and rename any internal `require()` to `import`) — or rename it `require-page-chrome.cjs` and keep the CommonJS body. Verify with `npm run lint` returning a real result. Caution: re-enabling lint will likely surface a backlog of previously-unchecked violations across the codebase, so land the fix in its own pass and triage the fallout. Unblocks: lint coverage in CI; the page-chrome regression guard; any future lint-gated quality work. |
| 1833 | T3 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **Community Resources are keyed by lowercase geo slugs, not the canonical `locations.resolve` ids** (opened 2026-05-31, **city filtering fixed same day**). `community_resources` (migration 0191) keys rows on `country_code`/`state_code`/`city_slug` lowercase slugs so seeds + the `/in/:country/:state` route address them without numeric ids. **FIXED (a):** `listApproved` + the public route + service + `LocationResources` now thread `city` — a city page shows that city's resources PLUS state-wide (`city_slug IS NULL`) rows, not the whole state ([communityResourcesRepository.ts](hired.video/api/src/repositories/communityResourcesRepository.ts)). RESIDUAL (b): a state/city whose `/in` slug differs from its stored code (abbrev vs full-name slugs, non-US regions) still won't match — submission + seed + query all derive from the same URL slug so the US flow is consistent, but international parity wants resolving the submitted geo through `/api/locations/resolve` and storing canonical ids alongside the slugs. Unblocks: international region parity. |
