| 1608 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `perf` | **Rating CHECK constraints — primary half closed in 0142** (opened 2026-05-26 from gap-#1594 audit; primary-value half closed via [0142](hired.video/api/drizzle/0142_schema_audit_indexes_and_checks.sql) — `reviews_overall_rating_range CHECK (overall_rating BETWEEN 1 AND 5) NOT VALID`). The remaining items are pure cosmetic: (a) optional byte-storage switch (`reviews.overall_rating` `smallint → "char"` saves 1 byte per row but breaks Drizzle's `smallint` inference); (b) [scorecards.ts:256](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/scorecards.ts#L256) `scorecardSubmissions.overallScore` is an integer "weighted mean of ratings" — scale depends on the attribute count + per-attribute max; not a real bug, just under-documented. Both are deprioritized. **Unblocks**: the CHECK already prevents junk ratings (the primary correctness value); these residuals are storage / clarity wins only. |
| 2094 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **Fake-db test harness: `delete().where()` doesn't support a chained `.returning()`** (logged 2026-06-14 from #2067 work, TK1 test-infra) | [fake-db.ts](hired.video/api/src/handlers/__testing__/fake-db.ts) `delete(table).where(pred)` returns `Promise.resolve()` with no `.returning()`, but several repos delete-then-return rows (`UsageTrackingRepository.eraseByUser`/`eraseByVisitor` use `.delete(...).where(...).returning({ id })`). A buildFakeDb integration test that routes through those repos crashes on `.returning is not a function`, so #2067's test had to inject a spy repo instead of exercising the real `eraseByUser` against fake rows. Fix: make `delete().where()` return a thenable that also exposes `.returning(cols)` resolving to the removed rows (mirror the insert/update `returning()` already there). Unblocks: integration-level coverage of delete-and-return repo methods. |
