| 943 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Next | P3 | `quality` | **DRY follow-up — template-seed widget builders (`makeHeading` / `makeText` / `makeChips` / `makeCta` in `template-seeds.ts`) overlap structurally with the comic widget builders in `comic-page-builder.ts`** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced by audit of #938) | All eight builders share the `defaultWidget(kind) → narrow → assign position → assign data → return` pattern. They live in two files today because each one mutates a different `params.data` shape with kind-specific defaults — the abstraction is shallow enough that a forced unification (e.g. a generic `makeWidget<K>(kind, opts)` helper) loses ergonomics. Action: revisit during the next palette / inspector refactor pass when a third caller materialises (e.g. an AI-image-to-widget injector or the chart-editor builder). Until then both files document each other via cross-reference comments. Doesn't block any feature. |
| 886 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P4 | `quality` | **`profileVisibility` enum (`public`/`private`/`connections`) on `user_profiles` and `profileVisibleToPublic` boolean on `privacy_preferences` overlap — two columns express closely-related axes of "who can see me"** (opened 2026-05-20 — surfaced while wiring `profileVisibleToPublic` enforcement alongside the new [`promoteWithoutAuth`](hired.video/api/src/routes/users.ts) flag in migration 0097) | Per migration 0097, [`GET /api/users/:id`](hired.video/api/src/routes/users.ts) now actually enforces `privacy_preferences.profileVisibleToPublic=false` for authenticated non-owners (403). The remaining shape gap is that [`userProfiles.profileVisibility`](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/users.ts) (the `public`/`private`/`connections` enum) and [`privacyPreferences.profileVisibleToPublic`](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/users.ts) (the boolean) now both participate in the gate decision with subtly different semantics: `profileVisibility=private` blocks everyone but the owner, `profileVisibleToPublic=false` blocks every authenticated non-owner but lets anonymous viewers through when `promoteWithoutAuth=true`, and `profileVisibility=connections` requires a session at minimum. Fix: collapse to a single SSoT — either (a) deprecate `profileVisibility` and drive everything from booleans on `privacy_preferences` (`profileVisibleToPublic`, `promoteWithoutAuth`, plus a new `profileVisibleToConnectionsOnly`), OR (b) deprecate `profileVisibleToPublic` and fold it into the existing enum. (a) is cleaner because it keeps the two axes (signed-in-vs-anonymous × everyone-vs-connections-only) orthogonal rather than smushed into one 3-state enum. Unblocks: removes the chance of two settings drifting and gives the Privacy tab a single source of truth. |
| 1365 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `perf` | **JWT secret read on every request from rateLimiter + auth middleware** ([rateLimiter.ts:105](hired.video/api/src/middleware/rateLimiter.ts), [middleware/auth.ts](hired.video/api/src/middleware/auth.ts)) (opened 2026-05-25). `getJwtSecret()` / `getJwtSecretOptional()` reads `process.env.JWT_SECRET` every call. Negligible per-call cost (1–2 µs) but trivially eliminable. How to apply: encode the secret once at module scope (`const SECRET_KEY = new TextEncoder().encode(getJwtSecret())`) and import the precomputed key. |

### TK2 — billing — Billing, Payments & Payouts — 50 active

