| 1344 | T1 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Service domains with zero unit tests — gamification, learning/courses, recruiter, paid-media, career360, comics, graph, pipeline, profile, tremendous, location, moderation, sync, youtube** (opened 2026-05-25). These are three of the most actively developed domains (gamification + learning shipped in 0126; courses shipped in 0041/0042; recruiter is the core revenue surface for the bidding marketplace). The badge engine, fraud sweep, SCORM commit, xAPI statement, prerequisite-DAG cycle detection, learning-path completion, and certificate HMAC-sign all run silently. How to apply: spin up one test file per service folder using the `fake-db` harness, cover the public API surface, prioritise gamification first because its fraud sweep + idempotent badge issuance are the highest-risk if they regress. **Progress (TK6, 2026-06-14):** the prioritised gamification + learning slice is now covered. Gamification domain already had `points-engine`/`badge-engine`/`fraud-engine`/`streak-engine`/`redemption-engine` tests (+`fake-points-repo`); learning had `certificate-service`/`cohort-analytics`/`cohort-classroom`/`course-completion`. Added this pass: [scoring.test.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/learning/__tests__/scoring.test.ts) (SCORM/xAPI basis-point + gate math, weighted aggregate), [learning-path-service.test.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/learning/__tests__/learning-path-service.test.ts) (prerequisite-DAG cycle detection, computeUnlockState, isPathComplete, maybeCompletePathEnrollment guards), [lrs-forwarder.test.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/learning/__tests__/lrs-forwarder.test.ts) (xAPI mirror: target selection, auth modes, custom-header guard, success/HTTP-error/throw persistence). **Found + FIXED while testing:** the prerequisite-DAG cycle check in [learning-path-service.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/learning/learning-path-service.ts) `assertNoCycle` traversed the DEPENDENT relation (`prerequisiteCourseId = frontier`), so it let real cycles through (e.g. B→A then adding A→B) while wrongly rejecting harmless redundant transitive edges — a cycle permanently bricks the looping courses (neither ever unlocks). Now walks the requires-relation forward (`courseId = frontier`). 168 learning+gamification tests green. **Residual (TK6):** `assignment-service` (createAssignment routes through `CohortService.getManageable`, which reaches `getDb()` internally rather than the injected db, and `listForLearner`/`findCompletableForLearnerSubject` use `innerJoin` the fake-db doesn't model) and the `maybeCompletePathEnrollment` success-path flip (uses `.update(...).catch(...)` the fake chain doesn't model) + `services/courses/course-generator` remain untested — need an integration-DB harness or a fake-db `innerJoin`/`.catch`/`delete().returning()` extension (the latter three are TK1 test-infra). The non-TK6 domains in the title (recruiter, paid-media, career360, comics, graph, pipeline, profile, tremendous, location, moderation, sync, youtube) are still uncovered — keep open until those land. |
| 1362 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `perf` | **Creator dashboard analytics — N+1 artifact metadata + per-user `getSubscription` fan-out** (opened 2026-05-25 — `services/analytics/creatorRollup.ts:67-99` + `services/creators/visibility.ts:45-62`). Dashboard load fires `Promise.all(items.map(async i => db.select(...).where(eq(table.x, i.x))))` — one Neon round-trip per artifact. For 200 artifacts that's 200+ round-trips when a single `inArray()` join would do it. Same anti-pattern on `getSubscription(userId)` fanned out across visible users. Est. impact: 300–500 ms on creator dashboard load; OOM-class on creators with thousands of artifacts. How to apply: rewrite the per-artifact unique-viewer count as a single `GROUP BY artifactId` query; replace the per-user `getSubscription(id)` fan-out with `inArray()` + a Map lookup. |
