ookings.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/bookings.ts) — public reads (host page, slot grid), magic-link booker actions (comment/reschedule/cancel), host `/me/*` for offerings + availability + reservations; mounted in [app.ts](hired.video/api/src/app.ts) + `/api/bookings/public` and `/api/bookings/r` allowlisted unauthenticated. (g) [shared/__tests__/bookings.test.ts](hired.video/shared/__tests__/bookings.test.ts) — 19 node:test cases (empty rules, 9-17 weekday projection, busy-window collisions across slot boundaries, override add/block, FIT-entirely-in-window rule, effectiveFromDate gate, window-size cap throw, fee-math clamps + flooring, token URL-safety + entropy floor + length cap); all 19 pass. (h) Frontend: [bookings-service.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/bookings-service.ts) client + four surfaces — [BookPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/bookings/BookPage.tsx) public `/book/:handle` with day-grouped slot grid, [ReservationPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/bookings/ReservationPage.tsx) magic-link `/book/:handle/r/:token` (view/comment/reschedule/cancel), [BookingsHost](hired.video/frontend/pages/bookings/BookingsHost.tsx) host config + dashboard at `/bookings` with one-click enrollment via `/api/creators/opt-in` + `/api/creators/me/programs/bookings`, and [BookingsSection](hired.video/frontend/components/bookings/BookingsSection.tsx) **self-gating shared component** that queries `/api/bookings/public/host/:handle`, returns `null` when host isn't enrolled or has no active offerings (no prop-drilled `canBookSessions` boolean, per [feedback_extract_on_duplication](memory/feedback_extract_on_duplication.md)). App.tsx routes + PAGE_SEO entries registered. (i) `creator-service.ts` updated with `bookings` entries across LABEL / ICON / HOME / DESCRIPTION maps so existing creator-program panels surface "1:1 Sessions" alongside the other six programs. (j) api typecheck clean on the new surface; 2265 api tests pass; 19 shared tests pass; `lint-migrations.mjs` green on 0195. **Still open** (broken out below as separate gap entries): #1900 Stripe Connect onboarding + Payment Intent (v1 uses host-clicked "Mark paid" via `/me/reservations/:id/mark-paid` as a stopgap), #1901 Google/Outlook two-way calendar OAuth sync, #1902 BookingsSection mount on `/people/:id` (component imports cleanly; 818-line PeopleDetail.tsx wasn't touched in this pass to avoid collateral risk), #1903 Signup picker top-level "Creator / Coach / Entrepreneur" choice that routes to `role=job_seeker + profileMode=channel + auto-opt-in to bookings program`, #1904 UnifiedSearch facet "Available for sessions" via `content_audiences`, #1905 Magic-link email delivery (today the booker receives the token only via the immediate POST response — needs a transactional email on confirm), #1906 host-side reservation comment thread surface on `/bookings` (the route is wired but the dashboard renders reservation cards without the inline thread). Phase 2 (recurring subscription bookings + group sessions) remains deferred per the PRD. The eventual BurnRateOS rip-out + `api.burnrateos.com/v1/bookings/*` external API + Booking Widget are tracked in [docs/prd/bookings-and-reservations.md](hired.video/docs/prd/bookings-and-reservations.md). | (original — opened 2026-05-26 from product review with user — gymnastics-coach use case). Today the Creator persona ([project_creator_persona_model](memory/project_creator_persona_model.md)) covers "personal user with a public channel" but has no surface for selling **time** — coaches, consultants, fractional executives, resume coaches, mentors, and creators offering 1:1 sessions have nowhere to (a) import a coaching CV as a credibility surface, (b) configure recurring availability + length-tiered session offerings (30 / 60 / 90 / 120 min, the four lengths the launch use case enumerated), (c) take payment via Stripe Connect, (d) accept reservations via magic link with public slot-grid showing only `available` / `booked` and no PII, (e) let bookers comment / reschedule / cancel without signup. **Strategic split** mirrors the contact-sourcing precedent ([docs/prd/integrations-and-sourcing.md](hired.video/docs/prd/integrations-and-sourcing.md), [project_contact_sourcing_burnrateos](memory/project_contact_sourcing_burnrateos.md)): BurnRateOS owns the **operator surface** (`/bookings` module — availability, services, Stripe Connect payouts, reservation pipeline, two-way calendar sync with Google + Outlook, comments queue, refund/dispute handling, ledger entries that flow into BurnRateOS accounting), exposes it via `api.burnrateos.com/v1/bookings/*` + an embeddable Booking Widget; hired.video **consumes via API** and renders consumer surfaces — a "Services" section on `/people/[id]` that self-gates by querying the bookings API (no prop-drilled `canBookSessions` boolean per [feedback_extract_on_duplication](memory/feedback_extract_on_duplication.md)), a public `/book/[handle]` booking page, a magic-link reservation page at `/book/[handle]/r/[token]`, a UnifiedSearch facet for "available for sessions" wired through the existing `content_audiences` table (#1629). **Provisioning bridge**: a hired.video creator never visits BurnRateOS first — when they toggle "Offer sessions" in Settings → Services, hired.video calls `POST /v1/bookings/hosts` with an SSO-bridged JWT (same JWK-verified pattern the contact-sourcing widget uses for tenant auth), gets back a `bookingHostId` stored on the creator's hired.video profile, and embeds Stripe Connect onboarding inline so KYC completes without leaving hired.video. SSO handoff if the user later opens the full BurnRateOS operator surface (multi-coach workspace, accounting reports, dispute centre). **Owner-only reservation visibility** is enforced at the API layer (not the consumer layer) — `GET /v1/bookings/hosts/:id/availability` returns slot status only for unauthenticated callers and full booker identity + payment status + comment count for host auth, reusing the single-seam pattern from #1173 / [project_globe_details_owner_only](memory/project_globe_details_owner_only.md). **Reference implementation**: net-new (grep across `api/src/services/`, `frontend/lib/services/`, and `shared/` returns zero matches for `availability` / `reservation` / `booking_*`). Full PRD at [docs/prd/bookings-and-reservations.md](hired.video/docs/prd/bookings-and-reservations.md) — covers data model (9 tables), provisioning bridge, API surface, calendar sync, Stripe Connect take-rate, 5-phase rollout. **Unblocks**: (a) Creator persona becomes monetizable beyond ad-supported content and token-pricing tiers; (b) opens the senior-exec fractional / advisory bookings track (#1627) without needing recruiter sourcing infrastructure; (c) gives BurnRateOS a high-value B2B-ops module that pairs with the contact-sourcing module to form a real operator OS; (d) is reused by every audience that wants 1:1 monetization — career coaches, resume coaches, mentors, technical consultants, fitness coaches, fractional CxOs. |
