| 387 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Helcim customer record drifts when address is changed in Settings → Billing without re-running checkout** (2026-05-05) | `helcim.ts:getOrCreateCustomer` PUTs the latest address whenever it's called from a payment route, but the standalone `PUT /api/profile/billing-address` endpoint only updates our `user_profiles` columns — it doesn't push the change to Helcim. So a user who edits their address in Settings and waits a month before paying will see the old address in HelcimPay until the next checkout fires the customer-update path. Fix: have `profile.ts:put` call `provider.updateCustomerBillingAddress(...)` (new method on `PaymentProvider`) when a Helcim customerCode already exists, or piggy-back on `profileService.saveBillingAddress` to enqueue a sync job. Unblocks: invoices and modal pre-fill always reflect what the user just typed. Identified 2026-05-05. |
