| 1915 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `arch` | **Migrate ALL entity create/edit form pages into the Studio document canvas, then delete the standalone pages** (opened 2026-06-06 with #1912) | The full intent of #1912: every entity "editor" and form page is removed and editing happens ONLY in the studio document canvas. In scope to retire (redirect routes → `/studio` with the entity's input template, then drop the page + its now-unreferenced form components per the dead-code rule): resume — [ResumeBuilder](hired.video/frontend/components/ResumeBuilder.tsx), [ResumeCreatePage](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeCreatePage.tsx), [ResumeEditPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeEditPage.tsx), [ResumeUploadPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeUploadPage.tsx); job — [JobCreatePage](hired.video/frontend/pages/JobCreatePage.tsx), [JobEditPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/JobEditPage.tsx), [PostAJob](hired.video/frontend/pages/PostAJob.tsx); article/blog — the creator article editor surface. Each retirement is its own PR (route redirect + page delete + form-component dead-code sweep + deep-link/`EntityEditShell` audit). Phase 1 lands resume; the rest follow once the field-bound editable block (#1916) is proven. **Scope boundary (decided 2026-06-06):** in = content-document entities (resume/job/article/blog) + structured builders (screening-template builder, learning-path/cohort authoring — see #1918); OUT = true app chrome (settings, billing, payouts, auth) which stays native. Unblocks: a single editing surface; deletes thousands of lines of bespoke form code. **Resume CREATE retired 2026-06-06:** `/resumes/create` + `/resumes/create/:id` now redirect to `/studio?contentTemplate=resume-doc` (the document canvas); `ResumeCreatePage.tsx` deleted; all create entry points repointed ([Resumes.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Resumes.tsx) "Create" + empty-dropzone buttons, [ApplyJobButton](hired.video/frontend/components/ApplyJobButton.tsx), [JobApplicationPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/JobApplicationPage.tsx)). **Resume EDIT retired 2026-06-06:** `/resumes/edit/:id` now redirects (`ResumeEditRedirect`) to `/studio?editResume=:id`; `ResumeEditPage.tsx` deleted; StudioLanding's `?editResume` deep-link fetches the resume, seeds a `createResumeDocumentState` (entityId-bound + a block per populated section) and mints a `kind:"document"` project via the new `useCreateStudioDraft` document path; all edit entry points repointed (ResumeDetail ×3, [Resumes.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Resumes.tsx) onEdit + upload-success, [ResumeUploadSheet](hired.video/frontend/components/ResumeUploadSheet.tsx), [PeopleDetail](hired.video/frontend/pages/PeopleDetail.tsx)). Editing loads the real resume content + writes it back on save (content-safe: unshown sections preserved). So the full resume lifecycle (create + edit + upload) is now studio-only. **Job EDIT retired 2026-06-07:** `/jobs/edit/:id` now redirects (`JobEditRedirect`) to `/studio?editJob=:id`; `JobEditPage.tsx` + `JobEditForm.tsx` DELETED; job screening (a structured builder, not document content — #1918) re-homed to its own owner-only `/jobs/:id/screening` route ([JobScreeningPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/JobScreeningPage.tsx)), linked from JobDetail + the Studio job editor (see #1914 job binding, #1954 screening). **Remaining:** dead inline `ResumeBuilder` view in Resumes.tsx + orphaned form-component sweep (#1933); job `PostAJob` page still standalone; NOT browser-verified. Minor: the `resume-create` PAGE_META entry + its registry test now describe a redirect-only route (kept to avoid test churn). |
