| 291 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P1 | `feature` | **Channel page + profileMode + YouTube ingest (creator persona surface)** | 1-2 wks. Per `memory/project_creator_persona_model.md` (2026-05-03): "creator" is NOT a 4th role — it's a `profileMode` field on `users` so a `job_seeker` can opt into channel-mode without forking the role enum. ONE root profile route — same component branches on `profileMode`, channel layout matches the YouTube tab strip (Home / Videos / Shorts / Live / Podcasts / Playlists / Posts) where each tab self-gates (returns null if empty). Auto-flip resolver (multi-signal: public video count + view total + follower count) lives in one helper. New 4th onboarding card "Build an audience" sets `roles: ['job_seeker']` + `profileMode: 'channel'`. YouTube ingest: `youtube_imported_videos` table populated by an OAuth-connected channel, surfaced as embeds on the Videos tab. Recruiter search hits ONE index (creator-mode users still findable as candidates). Monetization (tipping / paid premieres / channel memberships) reuses the existing voice-marketplace Stripe Connect plumbing — NOT a new ledger. |
| 819 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P1 | `feature` | **Actor submission loop — self-tape submission against a `casting_call` job posting** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced shipping #818) | The Casting Call job template renders the role + submission instructions in prose, but there is no structured submission path: actors can't click "Submit self-tape" on the posting and have their video routed to the director's inbox. Today the closest thing is the generic `POST /api/applications` against `job_items` — it accepts an attached resume, not a self-tape video project. Spec: (a) new `casting_submissions` table — `{ jobId, actorUserId, projectId (FK studio_projects), submittedAt, roleId optional, status enum 'pending'|'shortlisted'|'rejected' }`; (b) `POST /api/casting/:jobId/submit { projectId }` endpoint that requires the project's kind matches `self_tape`/`monologue`/`showreel` and rejects otherwise; (c) director-side `GET /api/casting/:jobId/submissions` returning the inbox; (d) Casting Call detail page surfaces a "Submit a self-tape" CTA that opens the project picker filtered to film-category templates. Unblocks: the end-to-end casting workflow that makes the Director / Actor positioning more than a templates pile. |
| 1207 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P1 | `feature` | **No frontend UI for the AI Recruiter Agent v2 intake panel + follow-up scheduler** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the [intake endpoint](hired.video/api/src/services/recruiter/agent-intake.ts) and the [followup endpoints in recruiter.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/recruiter.ts)) — `POST /api/recruiter/agent/intake`, `POST /api/recruiter/agent/followups/schedule`, `GET /api/recruiter/agent/followups`, and `POST /api/recruiter/agent/followups/:id/cancel` are live with 100% test coverage, but the existing recruiter agent UI only exposes the legacy `/agent/source` form. To close: extend the recruiter agent panel with an "Intake" mode that posts a brief and auto-fills the source form, plus a "Follow-ups" tab that lists scheduled + sent reminders with cancel actions. Unblocks recruiters using Agent v2 without curling the API. |
| 1220 | T4 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P1 | `bug` | **CI deploy pipeline silently masks `db:push` failures, so SQL migrations apply onto a partially-bootstrapped DB and FK constraints to Drizzle-only tables fail** (opened 2026-05-25 — surfaced when [migration 0117](hired.video/api/drizzle/0117_recruiter_agent_followups.sql) deploy errored with `relation "recruiter_agent_runs" does not exist` despite the migration's defensive `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`). [.github/workflows/ci.yml](hired.video/.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs `db:push` (Drizzle schema sync) THEN `run-sql-migrations.mjs`. When `db:push` fails (e.g. [migration 0046](hired.video/api/drizzle/0046_sourcing_marketplace.sql) hit PostgreSQL's 1600-column limit on `job_items` because the out-of-tree legacy bootstrap left it bloated — see #1203), Drizzle-only tables like `recruiter_agent_runs`/`live_screening_sessions` never get created. SQL migrations then fail downstream with cryptic FK errors that look like the migration's fault. **Partial fix shipped 2026-05-25:** (i) [0117 hardened](hired.video/api/drizzle/0117_recruiter_agent_followups.sql) with a guarded DO-block FK addition so it survives this scenario; (ii) the four obsolete sourcing columns 0046 was adding to `job_items` (`accepts_sourcing_bids` / `sourcing_fee_cents` / `sourcing_deadline` / `sourcing_terms`) were dead — 0052 immediately drops them in favour of [`job_sourcing_listings`](hired.video/api/src/services/recruiter-marketplace/SourcingListingService.ts), and zero consumers remained across api/src/, shared/, or frontend/ — so they've been removed from 0046, taking the column-bloat blocker out of the deploy path. **Second fix shipped 2026-05-25** (after 0121's `archived_at` add on `job_items` hit the same 1600-column wall on the next deploy): (1) `run-sql-migrations.mjs` now tracks applied migrations in a runner-owned `_sql_migrations` table — each file runs at most once per database, eliminating the previous "replay every file every deploy" loop that made the `IF NOT EXISTS` defensive layer load-bearing; (2) [migration 0122](hired.video/api/drizzle/0122_reclaim_job_items_columns.sql) runs `VACUUM FULL "job_items"` to reclaim the dropped column slots — runs exactly once because the new runner records it as applied on success; (3) the failing `job_items.archived_at` add was extracted from 0121 into [migration 0123](hired.video/api/drizzle/0123_job_items_archived_at.sql) so it lands AFTER the slot reclamation; (4) [0121](hired.video/api/drizzle/0121_taxonomies_archive_versions.sql) had the broken `ALTER TABLE "job_items" ADD COLUMN "archived_at"` block excised with a header note pointing to 0122/0123. **Still open:** (a) make `db:push` failures fatal in CI by adding `set -e` and explicit exit-code propagation around the drizzle call (currently only the SQL-migrations step has `set -e`), (c) audit every Drizzle-only table in [KNOWN_MISSING_CREATE_TABLE](hired.video/api/scripts/migration-schema-parity.test.mjs) for downstream FK consumers and prepend defensive CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS in those consumer migrations the same way 0117 now does. Unblocks deploys against fresh / partial DBs without manual SQL intervention. |
| 207 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P1 | `feature` | **Candidate Submittal Agent (auto-generated executive submittal)** | Background job consumes `candidateSubmissions` row + résumé + scorecards, emits a branded submittal doc via the existing storyboard generator (`purpose: "submittal"`) and returns a tokenized share link. Reuses ATS package pattern (#118). |
| 405 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `feature` | **No cross-job pipeline kanban — staged candidate view only reachable per-job via `/jobs/:id?tab=candidates`** (2026-05-05) | Surfaced during persona-axis design (#400). The full kanban infra exists — `jobPipelineEntries` + `pipelineTouchpoints` + `pipelineShareLinks` schema (`db/schema/jobpipeline.ts`), 9-stage enum (`shared/recruiter-pipeline.ts:5`: Applied / Long List / Screening / Interviewing / Short List / Submitted / Offer / Hired / Rejected), and full UI components (`JobPipelineKanban`, `KanbanColumn`, `JobPipelineCard`, `KanbanToolbar`, `JobPipelineReports`, `useJobPipeline`, `pipeline-mutations`). Backend `pipelineService.listEntriesByStage(jobId)` is per-job only. To see all candidates across all my company's jobs grouped by stage, a recruiter has to click into each job individually — Loxo / Bullhorn / Greenhouse all expose a cross-job pipeline. Fix: (a) new backend route `GET /api/pipeline/all?stage=&jobId=` filtering `jobPipelineEntries WHERE jobId IN (resolveCompanyScope(viewer).jobIds)` reusing the per-job grouping logic; (b) new `CrossJobKanban.tsx` that composes existing `KanbanColumn` + `JobPipelineCard` with a "for [Job Name]" label per card; (c) new `pipeline` tab on `/jobs` descriptor (hiring-side) once the EntityHubShell migration brings /jobs through the shell. Out of scope for PR-1 of #400 (which only does the /resumes migration). Unblocks: cross-job recruiter ops without per-job click-through; full Loxo-style candidate dashboard. Identified 2026-05-05 from user reference to Loxo kanban screenshot. |
| 406 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `feature` | **No "Add to Job" affordance from the candidate pool — pool ↔ pipeline bridge is missing in the UI** (2026-05-05) | Today `CandidatesPanel` (the candidate_resumes pool list) shows row actions for view / share / etc. but no way to promote a pool candidate into a specific job's pipeline. Backend supports it: POST to the per-job pipeline endpoint with the candidate's name/email/resumeUrl creates a `jobPipelineEntries` row at `stage=longlist` (or whichever default the recruiter picks). The mental model is the standard ATS pool→pipeline split (Loxo / Bullhorn / Greenhouse all expose this) — pool is pre-pipeline, pipeline is per-job staged journey. Fix: row-menu item "Add to Job" on each `CandidatesPanel` row → opens a job picker (jobs in viewer's company scope) → optional starting-stage selector (default `longlist`) → POSTs an entry. Lands as part of the /resumes?tab=sourced migration in PR-1 of #400 since the pool surface is moving anyway. Unblocks: candidate moves from "in our pool" to "in our pipeline for Job X" without leaving the page. Identified 2026-05-05 alongside #400 + #405. |
| 212 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Outreach Campaign Templates library** | Seed 4 starter sequences (Candidate Outreach for Job, Email-only Outreach, Biz Dev Outreach, Biz Dev: New HM at Company). New `outreachCampaignTemplates` table; clone-into-sequence on selection. |
| 877 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **`z.string().url().optional()` rejects `""` across ~25 routes — every PUT/POST that sends an empty placeholder URL is one form away from #876's symptom** (opened 2026-05-20 — surfaced building #876) | The new [`optionalUrl`](hired.video/api/src/routes/jobs.ts) schema in `routes/jobs.ts` is the right idiom but lives in one file. Every other route with the same shape (heroImageUrl / coverImageUrl / linkedinUrl / atsApplyUrl / videoUrl / ctaUrl / destinationUrl / scormManifestUrl / etc — see `rg "z.string\(\).url\(\).optional\(\)" hired.video/api/src/routes`) will throw 400 the first time a form sends `""` instead of `undefined`. Fix: promote `optionalUrl` (and a paired `nullableOptionalUrl` for the `.nullable()` variants) into [shared/zod-helpers.ts](hired.video/shared/) (new), import-replace the ~25 sites, drop the inline copy in `routes/jobs.ts`. No behavior change for callers that already send `undefined`; unblocks forms that send `""`. Unblocks: cross-form parity; no second instance of #876 lurking in another route. |
| 1231 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **No candidate demographic capture, so a true Greenhouse-grade DEI / EEO-1 dashboard cannot be computed** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the [HiringInsightsPanel](hired.video/frontend/components/dashboard/HiringInsightsPanel.tsx) shipping with a "demographic capture not yet enabled" honesty banner). The aggregate funnel + source-mix view is live today, but axes that need self-identified candidate data (gender, race/ethnicity, veteran status, disability, age band) are not collected anywhere in the schema. To close: (a) add a `candidate_demographics` table with strict opt-in semantics, encrypted-at-rest fields, an audit row on every read, AND aggregate-anonymisation thresholds (no segment shown when N < 5 to prevent re-identification — the standard Greenhouse / SHRM rule); (b) surface a demographic-capture step at candidate signup behind a clear "skip / share later" CTA + a per-employer "we'd appreciate this data because…" disclosure; (c) wire the existing HiringInsightsPanel to a new `/api/recruiter/hiring-insights/dei` endpoint that returns aggregate-anonymised rates per stage. Unblocks: full DEI dashboard parity with Greenhouse, EEO-1 export, OFCCP-compliant hiring reports. |
| 1329 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **Pattern 13 violation — services importing `schema` directly and running Drizzle instead of going through a repository** (opened 2026-05-25). Spot-checked offenders: `services/auth/AuthService.ts:33` (writes `loginEvents` directly), `services/job/JobService.ts:57` (re-exports schema tables), `services/job/match-handlers.ts`, `services/billing/handlers.ts`, `services/user/autofill-handlers.ts`. Why: these services were written before the per-aggregate repos landed (or were extracted at the same time and the migration was partial). How to apply: add the missing methods on the corresponding `*Repository.ts`, inject `repos` via Deps, replace the direct `db.insert(schema.x)` with `repos.foo.insertX(...)`. Pair with #1327 — the route-level extraction surfaces these as a natural next step. |
| 1343 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Repositories: 30 of 31 untested** (opened 2026-05-25). Only `buildRepos.test.ts` (gap #1315 smoke test) exists. `pointsRepository` (736 LOC, 9 tables), `scorecardsRepository` (547 LOC, 6 tables), `resumeRepository` (499 LOC + heal/validate logic), `mediaRepository`, `eventsRepository`, etc. have no direct CRUD tests — they're exercised transitively via service tests, which means a regression in a repo method surfaces as a confusing failure two layers up instead of at the unit it broke. How to apply: per-repo `__tests__/<repoName>.test.ts` that constructs the repo with `fake-db` and exercises every public method (insert/findById/update/delete + any aggregate-specific helpers). Start with `pointsRepository` + `scorecardsRepository` + `eventsRepository` (newest, highest churn, zero tests). |
| 1662 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Job scraper has no staleness story — scraped rows stay `isActive=true` forever even after the source feed drops them** (2026-05-27, surfaced when reviewing the cron-driven scraper). The scraper ([api/src/services/job/scraper.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/job/scraper.ts)) inserts new `job_items` rows with `isActive: true` and dedupes by `sourceUrl` — but on re-encounter it just `skipped++` and moves on. Nothing tracks "last seen in feed at," nothing populates `expiresAt` from JSON-LD `validThrough` at insert, nothing pings `applyUrl` to detect 404 / "this job is closed" pages, and nothing flips `isActive=false` when a row stops appearing in its source feed. Net result: scraped jobs accumulate indefinitely and `/api/jobs` keeps surfacing closed listings. Fix (one bundled pass): (a) add `lastSeenAt` timestamp to `job_items` (or to a sidecar `job_items_external` table keyed by `(sourceId, sourceUrl)` so we don't bloat the main row), bumped via `UPDATE ... SET last_seen_at = now()` on re-encounter inside scraper.ts's "skipped" branch; (b) per-source TTL config in `jobBoardSources.config.staleAfterDays` (default 21); (c) daily sweep in scheduled.ts that flips `isActive=false WHERE lastSeenAt < now - ttl` (idempotent, cheap); (d) at insert time, populate `expiresAt` from JSON-LD `validThrough` when present (the JSON-LD extractor in `shared/scraping/jsonLd.ts` already parses it); (e) audit `/api/jobs` search filters to confirm `isActive=false` AND `expiresAt < now` are both excluded by default. Bundles cleanly with #473 (job_items.updatedAt doesn't auto-bump) — both touch the scraper's UPDATE path. Unblocks: search quality (no zombie listings), candidate trust (apply links actually work), gamification fairness (points for applying don't fire against dead jobs). |
| 1850 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Candidate-screening template builder lacks ref pickers for `competency_test` / `video_interview` / `tool_run` items** (opened 2026-05-31 with the screening feature) | The backend (`screening_template_items`, `validateScreeningItem` in [shared/screening.ts](hired.video/shared/screening.ts)) accepts all 8 item types, but [ScreeningTemplates.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/services/ScreeningTemplates.tsx) only offers résumé, contact, validated assessments, references, and application questions. Competency tests need a `skill_assessments` picker (→ refId), async video needs an `interview_question_sets` picker, tool-run needs a tools-catalog picker (→ config.toolId). Fixing unblocks assigning skill tests, async video interviews, and tool runs as part of a screening. |
| 1851 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Screening portal has no inline launcher for `competency_test` / `video_interview` / `references` / `tool_run`** (opened 2026-05-31) | [CandidateScreening.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/CandidateScreening.tsx) completes `contact_info` + `application_questions` inline and deep-links `resume` + `predictive_assessment` (complete-then-Refresh re-resolves via `claimRequest`). The other four show a generic "recruiter will share how" message: competency_test/references could deep-link + auto-detect (they ARE pre-satisfiable in [pitch-book-resolver.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/screening/pitch-book-resolver.ts)), but `video_interview` + `tool_run` are NOT pre-satisfiable and have no inline completion path, so a candidate can't actually finish them in the portal. Fixing unblocks true one-stop completion. |
| 2109 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `perf` | **Resume-tailor still re-emits the entire resume JSON + leans on a free-tier-only fallback chain — diff-only output contract + paid JSON primary** (split from #1801 fix 2026-05-30). With the schema guard (#1801) the 503 is gone, but the tailor call still asks the model to return the full `tailoredResume` document (`TailorResponseSchema.tailoredResume = ResumeContentSchema`), which (a) doubles prompt+completion tokens/latency/cost vs. returning only the edits, and (b) is why the schema was oversized in the first place. Highest-leverage follow-on: switch the contract to **diff-only** — model returns just `changes[]` (section/before/after/why), server applies edits to the stored `ResumeContent` and re-derives `tailoredResume` so the wire payload + the responseSchema both shrink dramatically; `validateTailorOutput`'s preserve-every-entry check becomes trivially satisfiable because untouched entries are never re-serialized. Touches [match-handlers.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/job/match-handlers.ts) (`buildTailorPrompt`, `TailorResponseSchema`/ingest, `handleTailor` persistence) + any frontend consumer that reads `changes`/`tailoredResume` ([ResumeTailor.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/tools/ResumeTailor.tsx)). Separately: the `match_tailor` profile chain ([providers.ts:223](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/providers.ts#L223) + `FREE_TIER_FALLBACK_POOL`) is ~all free-tier models that themselves 429/timeout — a user-blocking foreground flow should have a paid JSON-capable primary (mirror `match`'s Cerebras primary) so the common case doesn't depend on the free pool being healthy. Unblocks: materially cheaper/faster tailoring + fewer transient retries. |
| 2211 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **Screening-template authoring must move into the studio editor (retire the standalone builder)** (decided 2026-06-18 — establishes the general rule: NO standalone form/wizard builders, all content/config creation+editing goes through the studio; see [[feedback_builders_retire_into_studio]]) | [ScreeningTemplates.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/services/ScreeningTemplates.tsx) is a bespoke form builder (`/services/screening`). The studio should own screening-template create+edit. **Concrete blocker:** the studio document canvas authors entities via the FLAT `document-field-schema`/`SectionEditor` (what makes the `job` entity canvas-authorable) — it has no representation for a screening template's POLYMORPHIC per-itemType config (assessmentKind / minReferences / toolId / instructions) or the NESTED `questions[]` array, so items can't be authored on-canvas without a shared-editor change that risks the in-flight resume/job work (#1912-#1918). **Clean path (no flat-schema change):** register `screening_template` as a `DOCUMENT_ENTITY_KIND` + `DOCUMENT_AUTHORING` entry + `StudioSubjectKind`; author the items via a NEW custom document block (`screening-builder`) whose editor reuses the existing per-type builder UI extracted from ScreeningTemplates.tsx (non-lossy); wire load/save through the screening API in StudioEditorV2 `handleSave`; add a StudioLanding create tile; then redirect/delete `/services/screening`. ~10 files incl. 3 in-flight shared editor files — a deliberate, separately-verified pass. Until then the working builder stays (retiring it now would break screening creation). Unblocks: one authoring surface for screening + enforces the no-standalone-builders rule. (Possible enforcement follow-on: an ESLint rule flagging new `pages/**/*Builder.tsx` / wizard form pages.) |
| 153 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Save to Collection (richer than binary Track)** | Non-owner action to bookmark resumes/jobs into named collections. `userCollections` + `collectionItems` schema. `POST/GET /api/collections`, `POST /api/collections/:id/items`, drag-to-reorder. Recruiter workflow: "Engineering candidates Q2", "Design leads". Supersedes the current binary `ownership="tracked"` toggle on resumes but stays backwards-compatible — a "Saved" default collection is auto-created on first track. |
| 185 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Authenticated hiring-company collection view** | Companion to #184. When a hiring company creates an account and claims their reviewer identity, consolidate every pitch deck shared with them into a "People · Shared with you" collection. Persistent candidate list, status flags (reviewed/shortlisted/rejected), comments threaded by deck. Uses existing `company_profiles` + `user_company_role_associations` — no new tenancy needed. |
| 206 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Calendar Link Templates (Intro / Interview / Follow-up)** | Booking-page presets layered on top of #11 OAuth. New `calendarLinkTemplates` table + public booking URLs per template. |
| 218 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Talent Insights aggregate panel** | Top-10 industries / countries / states bar charts of the current result set, with Charts↔Tables toggle and Share button (tokenized read-only link). Backed by pre-aggregated facets returned alongside `/api/search/recruiter` results. |
