| 248 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Forms (custom application / intake forms)** | Tenant-scoped form builder distinct from in-video lead capture (#140). Schema: `workspaceForms` (fields JSONB), `workspaceFormSubmissions`. Public URL per form; submissions create / update candidate records. Replaces ad-hoc Google Form / Typeform usage. |
| 256 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Workday integration (in-house tenants — WS URL + OAuth2)** | Beyond #64 ATS connector. Per-tenant Workday Web Services URL + OAuth2 client/secret/refresh-token store. Job + candidate sync via SOAP. Targets the Workday-running enterprise that wants hired.video as the front-end. |
| 1371 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `perf` | **Single `/api/dashboard` instead of 4 role-branched endpoints** (opened 2026-05-25). [dashboard.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/dashboard.ts) currently exposes `/jobseeker`, `/recruiter`, `/employer`, `/admin` variants — client branches on role to pick one. The role is already in the JWT; the server can do the dispatch and clients stop branching. Same number of round-trips, but the API surface drops from 4 endpoints to 1 + the client no longer carries a 4-way switch + future role additions don't need a new endpoint. How to apply: add `GET /api/dashboard` that delegates to the role-specific service internally; mark the 4 variants `@deprecated`; migrate `useDashboard` to the new endpoint; remove the variants once no callers remain. |
| 1388 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Async calibration / debate threads on scorecard disagreements** (opened 2026-05-25 during Greenhouse-parity audit). When two evaluators disagree (>2-point spread on the same attribute, or strong_yes vs. strong_no on overall) Greenhouse just shows the delta in the debrief view and assumes the hiring manager will resolve it in a calibration meeting. We can leapfrog with async threaded debate inline on the disagreement — evaluators must each post a justification before the hiring decision can be recorded. Same UX pattern as code-review comments. To close: (a) `scorecard_disagreement_threads` table (applicationId, attributeId\|null, threshold_kind, openedAt, resolvedAt, resolutionNote), (b) `scorecard_disagreement_comments` table (threadId, authorUserId, body, createdAt), (c) auto-open trigger in the submission service when spread crosses threshold, (d) inline thread component on DebriefView, (e) `hiring_decisions` POST validates all open threads are resolved. Reuses the existing `studio_review_comments` threaded-comment pattern. |
| 1764 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Boost pricing model — bid auction vs flat slot fee decision** (split from #177 closure 2026-05-30) | Boost checkout is wired for flat pricing today (`budgetCents / durationDays = daily rate`). The original gap noted "Boost pricing model (fixed CPM vs. bid auction vs. flat slot fee) — decision pending." Auction-bid CPM requires (a) per-impression metering on the boost renderer, (b) live bid table per `(subject_type, placement_type)`, (c) win/loss attribution. Out of scope until the analytics surface is mature enough to justify the complexity. |
| 1765 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Recruiter BD pipeline dashboard Kanban UI** (split from #99 closure 2026-05-30) | Routes + service ship at [/api/recruiter-bd](hired.video/api/src/routes/recruiter-bd.ts); the dashboard surface that renders pipeline-stage columns + drag-to-move-stage interactions is the remaining work. Lands as `<BdPipelineKanban/>` on the recruiter dashboard's new "Pipeline" tab. |
| 1777 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **JobCreatePage Studio-video picker** (split from #743 closure 2026-05-30) | Picker UI on [JobCreatePage.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/JobCreatePage.tsx) that lists the employer's Studio Projects with `purpose: "job_ad" | "recruiter_brand" | "company_promo"` and writes the chosen project id to `job.videoProjectId`. Same pattern as the MediaPicker for heroImageUrl. |
