| 1792 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Mount `LiveScreenSessionsTab` inside recruiter dashboard** (split from #1209 closure 2026-05-30) | The component is shipped; needs to be added as a tab in the recruiter dashboard's existing tab structure (depends on the dashboard's tab layout decision per #1765). |
| 1794 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Top-introducers panel on search results** (split from #1262 closure 2026-05-30) | New panel on the search results page that takes the visible result IDs and fans out to `/api/graph/top-introducers` to surface "who knows the most of these candidates". |
| 1201 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P2 | `feature` | **Remaining ~1,830 hardcoded strings across 304 components** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1184; #1412 covers the parallel catalogue-quality gap that landed 2026-05-26 — these are independent: #1201 = JSX literals never extracted, #1412 = catalogue translations exist but need quality review) | Per [i18n-hardcoded-audit.txt](hired.video/frontend/i18n-hardcoded-audit.txt): after the legal-pages extraction (~354 of 2,184 strings done — Cookie + Privacy fully, ToS pending under #1200), ~1,830 strings remain. Top contributors: People.tsx (58), CompanyBuilder.tsx (49), ProductDashboard.tsx (47), ServicesManagement.tsx (46), widget-sections.tsx (43), HiringOnboarding.tsx (33), StudioSidebar.tsx (33), AccountSettings.tsx (32), AffiliateProgram.tsx (27), SearchBar.tsx (26), PayoutProfileForm.tsx (25), JobCreatePage.tsx (24), ResumeViewer.tsx (24), Jobs.tsx (22), and a long tail of 290+ smaller files. Quebec Law 25 mandates French parity on consumer-facing copy; LFPDPPP requires Spanish point-of-collection notices. Pattern is mechanical — same legal-pages methodology applies: extract into namespaced keys, batch-add en/es/fr-CA at parity, replace JSX literals with t() calls. Realistic plan: ship in tranches (auth + signup ~30 strings first; then Settings / AccountSettings / Privacy preferences ~100; then jobs / company ~200; then admin / studio ~300; then long-tail components ~1,200). |
| 1205 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P2 | `feature` | **Salary popularity helpers parse free-text `job_items.location` instead of structured `content_locations`** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the salary SEO expansion in [api/src/services/job/salary-popularity.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/job/salary-popularity.ts)) — `extractCity()` splits a free-text string on commas and drops noise tokens, which is lossy for non-US formats, postal-codeless cities, and metro labels. The new [content_locations table](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/contentLocations.ts) attaches `cityId` to scraped jobs via the `entityKind='job'` rows landed in #1154. To close: replace the `extractCity()` parsing with a JOIN through `content_locations` + `cities` for the canonical city slug + display label. Unblocks accurate international salary pages and a "nearby metros" pivot. |
| 2119 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P2 | `feature` | **`/api/recruiter/agent/followups` worker surfaces reminders but doesn't auto-send them** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside [api/src/workers/recruiter-agent-followup.ts](hired.video/api/src/workers/recruiter-agent-followup.ts)) — the worker flips due `recruiter_agent_followups` rows to `sent` and materialises a `candidate_interactions` row, but it does not dispatch the message via email, LinkedIn InMail, or SMS. Recruiter still has to manually send. To close: route the body through the messaging service / Comm Hub channel preference of the recruiter (e.g. `sendFollowupEmail`, `sendFollowupLinkedIn`) before flipping to `sent`, with a `delivery_channel` column added to the table for audit. Unblocks the full LinkedIn Hiring Assistant parity narrative — the agent v2 follow-up sequence currently still needs a human-in-the-loop. |
| 317 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Hand-migrate the last 11 pages to `<AppShell>`** | 82 of 93 pages now on `<AppShell>` (incl. all auth/transitional pages, all `pages/tools/*`, all `pages/blog/*`, all `pages/guides/*`, marketing, `Feed`, `Home`, `Outreach`, `Resumes`, `Tools`, `Settings`, `SourcingBrowse`, `PostAJob`, both `seo/*` SEO pages). Remaining 11 mount `<Sidebar>+<Navigation>+<Footer>` directly with non-canonical wrappers the migration script couldn't transform: `ServicesManagement` (multi-return), `InterviewPractice`, `PhoneDashboard` (non-canonical wrap), `ResumeDetail`, `ResumeEditPage`, `ServiceInquiries` (variant indentation), `services/CandidateDetail`, `services/HiringOnboarding`, `services/PitchDeckBuilder`, `services/PitchDecksList`, `tools/ValueProposition` (non-canonical). ~30 mins each via hand edit. No bug today — data hooks already gate via `useApiReady`/`useGatedResource`, so even without `<AppShell>` these pages don't flood the rate limiter for verification-blocked users — pure layout DRY follow-up. Identified 2026-05-04. `services/ServicesSettings` removed from list 2026-05-19 — the page was deleted when its content was folded into [Settings.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Settings.tsx) as the new Recruiter → Sharing & Branding tab. |
| 396 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`/jobs` page carries dead "Your Job Postings" + "Tracked Jobs" branches that never render** (2026-05-05) | `pages/Jobs.tsx` renders two top-of-page sections — `jobsData.owned.length > 0` (lines 738-758) and `jobsData.tracked.length > 0` (lines 761-783) — but `jobsData` is only ever populated by `loadUserJobsOnDemand` (lines 590-642), and the `useEffect` that would have called it is commented out (lines 646-650). The `getJobsForUser` stub at lines 581-587 is declared but unreferenced. Result: a recruiter / employer never sees a separate "Your Job Postings" section — their owned jobs only appear inline in the "All Jobs" grid (now showing the Edit affordance after the JobService `userId` mirroring fix). This pre-dates the user report. Fix is paired with #395: once `getPublicJobs` returns per-row `ownership`, the entire `jobsData` split becomes unnecessary and the dead branches + `loadUserJobsOnDemand` + `getJobsForUser` can be deleted in one pass. Unblocks: simpler Jobs page (one render path instead of three), and either restoring the dedicated "Your Job Postings" group from a real source or removing the UI promise. Identified 2026-05-05 while fixing the missing-owner-controls bug. |
| 432 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **Audience-tag rollout drops resume tools from recruiter / employer entity action menus — confirm intent or add per-tool override** (2026-05-07) | Same tagging that powers /tools also gates the action menu surfaced on candidate-resume cards in `/services/candidates`, `/people?tab=talent-pool`, and (post-#400) `/resumes?tab=sourced` via `getCatalogToolsForEntity`. A recruiter looking at an imported candidate resume no longer sees "Run AI Resume Scorer" / "Roast" etc. on that row. Right call for surfaces where the recruiter shouldn't be acting *as* the candidate, but there's a real workflow ("score this resume for fit", "tailor this candidate's resume to my JD") that's now blocked. Decide: (a) keep current behaviour (resume self-improvement tools are seeker-only, recruiters use a different "evaluate" tool family); (b) add a second tag like `recruiterUseOnEntity?: ToolEntityContext[]` so a tool can be tagged as seeker-audience-on-tools-page yet still appear in the recruiter's entity menu; (c) split into two catalog entries per tool. Audit recruiter pool surfaces and tally which tools are missed before deciding. Unblocks: clarity on whether seeker-tagged tools are also recruiter-evaluation tools. Identified 2026-05-07 alongside #431. |
| 435 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Variant-effectiveness analytics — sync_runs has `source_resume_id` per export but no surface that joins it to interview/offer outcomes** (2026-05-07) | `profile_sync_runs` captures which variant got pushed where, when, on every export. The complement — "this variant got 4 LinkedIn views and 1 interview, that one got 12 views and 0 interviews" — would let users prune dead variants and double down on winners. Need: a `/tools/vendor-sync` History tab (or a Variant Performance tool) that joins `profile_sync_runs` ⨝ `resume_views` ⨝ `messages` (recruiter outreach) ⨝ `interviews` to attribute outcomes per variant per platform. Unblocks: "which resume is most effective" — the framing the user explicitly asked for during vendor-sync planning. Identified 2026-05-07 shipping vendor-sync tool. |
| 436 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **Recruiter `/api/recruiter/extract-profile` and seeker vendor-sync extractor return different shapes — recruiter is `{name, title, company, experience[].duration, education[].degree}`, seeker is JSON Resume `{basics, work[]/.startDate/.endDate, education[].studyType/.area}`** (2026-05-07) | Two LLM extraction prompts now exist for the same source data (HTML of a profile page) producing structurally different outputs. Recruiter sourcing flow + seeker self-import flow need to converge on JSON Resume; recruiter card UI flattens DOWN from JSON Resume instead of the LLM producing a flat shape. Unblocks: (a) a recruiter sharing a candidate's profile directly into the candidate's hired.video master via the same merge engine, (b) one extraction prompt to maintain instead of two, (c) `experience[].duration` ("2y 3m") becomes `startDate`/`endDate` so dates are sortable. Identified 2026-05-07 shipping vendor-sync tool. |
| 884 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **`/v/:videoId` lost the "Roast your resume →" viral cross-link when its custom header was retired in favour of the standard `<AppShell variant="public">` chrome** (opened 2026-05-20 — surfaced while making the public-video page render the standard header per user request) | The previous bespoke `<header>` on [PublicVideoResume.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/PublicVideoResume.tsx) carried a right-aligned `Link to="/tools/resume-roast"` ("Roast your resume →") that pitched the resume-roast tool to anyone watching someone else's video resume — the strongest cross-product hook on the page (a viewer who watched a video resume is actively benchmarking against their own). Aligning the page with `SharedCandidateResume` / `SharedPitchDeck` (no custom CTAs in the public chrome) means that hook is now gone — the only remaining conversion surface is the existing bottom-card "Get Started Free → /signup". Fix options: (a) lift the secondary CTA into the body just under the video as a thin chip ("Get instant feedback on your own resume — Roast your resume →") so it survives the chrome rewrite without re-introducing a one-off header, OR (b) extend `<AppShell variant="public">` with an optional `headerCta` slot for shareable surfaces (then both PublicVideoResume and the share pages can opt-in to context-specific viral hooks). DRY-wise (b) is the right shape — the share pages would benefit from a "Become a hired.video recruiter →" link in the same slot. Unblocks: viral funnel from public video viewers to the resume-roast / signup flow doesn't drop on the floor. |
| 970 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **No question editing / re-ordering before assignment** | Generated questions land in `InterviewQuestions.tsx` read-only — the recruiter can't tweak a Q, add a custom one, or change a maxDurationSec before sending. Fix: editable inline cards with add/delete/reorder. Currently a copy-paste workaround works. |
| 1493 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Jobs.tsx archive toggle + menu wiring** (opened 2026-05-26 during #154 close). API for `/api/jobs/:id/archive` + `/unarchive` is shipped; jobs list page still needs the toolbar "Include archived" toggle + the archive menu item on each card. Identical work to the resumes side — copy the wiring from [Resumes.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Resumes.tsx). |
| 1971 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **Legacy recruiter `createEmailCampaign` persists no recipients / audience** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1969) | `POST /api/communication/email-campaigns` (PersonalizeMessageDialog 1-recipient recruiter outreach) inserts a campaign row but never persists its `recipients`, and sets no `audience`. Under the real engine the now-functional `/send` delegates to `CampaignService.schedule`, which 400s ("no audience selected") for these rows. Fix: route the recruiter flow through `CampaignService.create` with a `{kind:"list"}` audience built from the dialog's recipients so its send actually delivers. |
| 1988 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **PWA client-side Stage-1 is still job-seeker-only — recruiter mail mislabels mid-sync** (opened 2026-06-12 with #1979) | The server is profile-authoritative (re-runs Stage-1 with the active profile + Stage-2 LLM, ignoring the client tag), so persisted classification is correct for recruiter mailboxes. But [sync-client.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/email-integration/sync-client.ts) still runs the hardcoded job-seeker rule set for its optimistic in-sync preview, so a recruiter watching a live sync briefly sees candidate-era categories before the server result lands. Thread the active profile's `defaultRuleSet` (and user rules) to the client so its preview matches the server. |
| 2092 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Surface `work_setting` + hybrid day-split in the candidate-facing UI** (opened 2026-06-14 with #2091) | The data now persists end-to-end and the public-jobs API accepts a `workSetting` filter, but the read surfaces don't show it yet: [JobCard.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/JobCard.tsx) + [JobDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/JobDetail.tsx) should render the canonical label via the shared `formatWorkSetting(setting, onsiteDays, remoteDays)` helper (e.g. "Hybrid (2 on-site / 3 remote)") instead of the binary Remote/Onsite badge, and [Jobs.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Jobs.tsx) needs a work-setting filter control wired to the `?workSetting=` query param the backend already honors. Also fold the edit-page prefill (load existing `onsiteDaysPerWeek`/`remoteDaysPerWeek` when editing a hybrid job). Unblocks: candidates can see + filter for hybrid roles and their day cadence. |
| 2160 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Per-entity `canViewStats` naming drift after globe-drawer tightening** | The globe + Details drawer rule was tightened to owner-only across every entity kind ([`use-entity-details-permission.ts`](hired.video/frontend/hooks/use-entity-details-permission.ts) now ignores per-entity `canViewStats` and re-derives from `isOwner || adminLike`). The per-entity hooks (`use-resume-permissions.ts`, `use-company-permissions.ts`) still expose a wider `canViewStats` that includes `canManageJobs` — used by inline score-chip / list surfaces ([`ResumeCard.tsx:152-154`](hired.video/frontend/components/ResumeCard.tsx#L152-L154), etc.). The name now means two different things depending on the call site. Fixing it (split into `canViewStats` (owner-only) + `canViewHiringStats` (owner+recruiter/employer)) would let consumers self-describe their gate and prevent the next reviewer from re-widening the drawer by accident. |
