| 1389 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Candidate fairness surface — rubric transparency + post-decision feedback** (opened 2026-05-25 during Greenhouse-parity audit). Greenhouse deliberately keeps the rubric + interviewer feedback opaque to the candidate (the product is sold to employers, not candidates). We are uniquely positioned to flip this — the candidate-facing magic-link interview surface ([AsyncInterviewPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/AsyncInterviewPage.tsx)) is already half the work. Show the candidate: (a) the interview kit overview ("you'll be assessed on these 4 competencies") at the start of each stage, (b) post-decision, anonymized aggregate feedback ("3 of 4 evaluators rated Technical Depth at 'Strong', concerns were raised on Communication"), (c) opt-in feedback survey (NPS-style: "was this assessment fair?"), (d) request-re-review CTA when the candidate believes feedback was off-base. Anti-Greenhouse positioning. Schema: `candidate_decision_disclosures` table + extend `hiring_decisions` with `candidateNotifiedAt` + opt-in employer setting. |
| 1404 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `arch` | **Polymorphic `audit_touchpoints` table — promote the `pipelineTouchpoints` pattern to a shared backbone** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1349 design). The `pipelineTouchpoints` table ([jobpipeline.ts:74-85](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/jobpipeline.ts#L74-L85)) was designed for job-pipeline stage changes + recruiter notes. The same shape (entityId + entityKind + type + payload + performedByUserId + createdAt, append-only) is the right model for: timesheet approval state changes (#1349), sourcing-listing bid state changes ([sourcing.ts](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/sourcing.ts)), placement extensions (#1349 Phase 4), candidate submission status (#1349), and any future approval-driven aggregate. Without promotion every new aggregate copies the table + service code. How to apply: add `audit_touchpoints` polymorphic table (entityType varchar + entityId uuid + type varchar + payload jsonb + performedByUserId + createdAt + index on (entityType, entityId, createdAt)) under a new `audit.ts` schema; provide a shared `recordTouchpoint(entityType, entityId, type, payload)` service; migrate `pipelineTouchpoints` rows with a backfill; deprecate the per-aggregate copies. Should land before #1349 Phase 2 so timesheets ride the shared table on day one. |
| 2142 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **2-3 editorial blog posts on structured interviewing** (deferred from structured-interview marketing audit, 2026-05-26). [`frontend/data/blog-posts.ts`](hired.video/frontend/data/blog-posts.ts) has 72 posts on job-seeker topics (resume scoring, salary, video resumes, interview practice) and zero posts targeting recruiter/HM queries on scorecards, calibration, bias reduction, or take-home best practices. Add: (a) "How to use interview scorecards to reduce bias and hire faster" (covers scorecards + blind review + bias linter), (b) "Calibration sessions 101: aligning your interview panel" (covers calibration + interviewer reliability), (c) "Take-home assignments without the friction" (covers take-home + reviewer scorecard binding). Each ~1500 words with code-of-conduct screenshots from `/people/scorecards`. Content-heavy + needs editorial review — deferred from automated push. Unblocks: organic SEO traffic for recruiter/HM intent + funnel into the structured-hiring landing page (#1479). |
