| 1586 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `feature` | **Engagement-asset widgets render as a static preview in playback — no interactive form submit, chapter jump, thumbnail click-through, or review-thread popover** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside the #1579 authoring half landing). The new `engagement-asset` WidgetKind drops onto the canvas, persists into the storyboard, and renders the bound artifact's preview body in both edit and playback modes via [EngagementAssetBody](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/EngagementAssetBody.tsx). But the playback surface is still passive — the form's field stack renders as preview text, not as `<input>` elements wired to `submitVideoForm`; chapter-marker widgets don't fire a "jump to chapter" seek; thumbnail-stamp widgets don't link out to the parent video; review-pin widgets don't open the comment thread on click. Per-kind fix: (a) **forms**: render `<form>` with the real `VideoFormField[]` in playback mode, POST to `/api/studio/forms/:id/submit`, respect `requireToContinue` to gate playhead advance — see [VideoFormInlineBody](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/inline-bodies/VideoFormInlineBody.tsx); (b) **chapters**: emit a `seek` event the player consumes on click; (c) **thumbnails**: render a CTA pill linking to the parent video id; (d) **reviews**: open the reviewer-comments dialog with the thread root pre-selected. Unblocks: the "viewer fills out the form (entering submissions)" promise behind #1579, plus the implicit promise of every kind once it's draggable. |
| 1592 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `bug` | **Production worker has been exceeding CPU limits across multiple surfaces** (opened 2026-05-26 from a `wrangler tail --env production` capture during the save-draft 503 investigation — within ~3 min: `GET /api/resumes/embedded/:id` ×~20, `GET /api/resumes/:id` ×~10, plus the `*/5` cron tick once. Gaps #1588 / #1589 / #1590 fix three independent contributors; this one is the umbrella that tracks whether their landing actually quiets the tail. Validation plan: after deploy, re-run `wrangler tail` and watch for `Exceeded CPU Limit` over a 15-min window. If quiet → close. If still firing on routes outside the three fixed surfaces, those land here. **Adjacent**: gap #979 (Worker 30s CPU budget) is the long-running architectural item; this is the acute incident under it. |
| 1916 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `feature` | **Field-bound editable blocks + per-entity input-template seeds — the canvas IS the form** (opened 2026-06-06 with #1912) | Replaces tab/form editors with click-to-fill on the canvas. Two pieces: (a) the generalized `DeclarativeResumeRenderer` gains an INLINE-EDIT mode where each `section` block renders its item fields as in-place editable controls (text / date / bullet-list / chips) that write back to the entity content — not a read-only render; (b) each entity ships a canonical "input template" seed (a default `DocumentState` exposing every field as an editable block) that a "new X" starts from, replacing the blank-form page. Both need a declarative per-entity FIELD SCHEMA (which fields, types, validation, repeat-groups) — extract it from the existing bespoke editors ([resume-sections/*](hired.video/frontend/components/resume-sections/), the job form, the article editor) into one schema the renderer drives, so render + inline-edit + validation share a source (DRY). Unblocks: #1915 (form pages can't be retired until their fields are editable on canvas). **Landed (partial) 2026-06-06:** declarative [resume-field-schema.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/resume-field-schema.ts) (per-section field defs: text/textarea/date/list, id-keyed `newItem`) drives [SectionEditor.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/SectionEditor.tsx) — inline add/remove/edit of section items on the canvas, wired into `DocumentStage` section blocks (editable when content+callback present) + persisted via #1931. Text blocks are double-click editable. `createBlankDocumentState("resume")` pre-seeds the core sections so a new resume opens ready-to-fill. **Generalized to jobs 2026-06-07:** the field schema is now entity-keyed ([document-field-schema.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/document-field-schema.ts), renamed from `resume-field-schema.ts`) with object/array section shapes + new field input types (number / select / image), and `SectionEditor` is entity-agnostic — so JOB sections are inline-editable on the canvas the same way resume sections are (#1914). **Remaining:** field validation; chips-type fields; richer per-field controls (real date pickers, MediaPicker for `image`); job publishing-field widgets (multiselect/date — #1953); article field schema; generalize `DeclarativeResumeRenderer` for full-fidelity read render. |
| 2152 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `feature` | **Unified paged-document Studio canvas — author every content entity (resume first) on a fixed-page WYSIWYG canvas** (opened 2026-06-06) | The "reinvision how we create content" initiative: a new `document` mediaKind whose runtime is a paged WYSIWYG canvas (Letter/Legal/A4 × orientation) reusing the FULL studio shell — layers, zoom, drag-and-drop, `<FloatingLayersPanel>`, properties panel, undo/redo, AI prompt + enhance-selection. Two planes: a reflowing data-bound document body (sections as flow blocks, detachable to absolute bounding boxes with column snap) + an overlay plane of stock studio `Widget`s for interactive media layers. Renderer = a generalized `DeclarativeResumeRenderer` mounted in edit mode AND read-only (preview === render). Structure (page+theme+layout) saves to the template library; content saves to the entity row. **Foundation landed 2026-06-06:** (1) [document-state.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/document-state.ts) (the `DocumentState` model — pages, flow blocks, overlay widgets reusing `Widget`, theme reusing the resume theme registry, `mediaBinding` for interactive section media, `DOCUMENT_ENTITY_CAPABILITIES` page-mode gate). (2) `document` mediaKind REGISTERED in [media-kinds.ts](hired.video/shared/media-kinds.ts) (enum + UI hints + PDF/PNG output profiles + `mediaKindUsesCanvasStateAuthoring`/`...TimelineExport` → false); `document` added to shared `ARTIFACT_KINDS`; `MediaKindBadge`/`WaveformThumbnail`/`kind-marketing` Record<MediaKind> consumers given document entries; the 3 exhaustive switches (`runtime-state-payload`/`export-facade`/`template-dispatch`) carry explicit `case "document"` throwing-guards until the runtime wires them. (3) Migration **0197** + schema: `studio_projects.document_state` JSONB column, media_kind CHECK relaxed to include document (AND the latent missing `cad_3d`/`interactive_comic`), media_kind widened varchar(16)→(24). tsc clean both projects. **Runtime landed 2026-06-06 (create→edit→save→load loop works, tsc clean both projects):** [DocumentStage](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/DocumentStage.tsx) (paged sheet at true print size × zoom; flow + absolute blocks; overlay render; add/remove/reorder/detach/reflow; resume-only page-size + orientation control; double-click inline text editing — a first slice of #1916) + [document-edit.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/document-edit.ts) pure mutations + block palette presets; mounted via [CanvasRouter](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/CanvasRouter.tsx) `document` surface + `useKindHydration` + own undo/redo history in [StudioEditorV2](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx); persistence end-to-end (`runtimeStatePayload` document case → `studioService.saveDraft` `documentState` → API save/`toProjectDto` → `document_state` column); `template-dispatch` seeds a blank resume DocumentState; [StudioLanding](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx) creatable via the `resume_doc` catalog entry (mediaKind document). **Content authoring landed 2026-06-06:** content-binding (#1931 — fetch/seed `ResumeData`, persist to the resume row, create-on-first-save) + inline FIELD editing (#1916 partial — `SectionEditor` + `resume-field-schema`, add/remove/edit section items on the canvas) + new-resume seeded with core sections. Resume CREATE retired into the canvas (#1915 — `/resumes/create*` redirect, `ResumeCreatePage` deleted). **Edit + view + export landed 2026-06-06:** resume EDIT retired into the canvas (#1915 — `/resumes/edit/:id` redirect, `ResumeEditPage` + `ResumeBuilder` deleted, `?editResume` opens the existing resume with content + a block per populated section); basics editor block; read-only [DocumentView](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/DocumentView.tsx) renderer (inline-styled, schema-driven full-content render) + **PDF export** via [print-document.tsx](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/print-document.tsx) (browser print → Save as PDF, `@page` from the doc geometry; wired into `handleExport`, replacing the export-facade throw for document). **Cross-surface viewer landed 2026-06-06:** the canvas LAYOUT is snapshotted onto the resume content's `meta.documentLayout` on save (`ResumeMetaSchema` is `.catchall` so it round-trips), and [ResumeDetail](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeDetail.tsx) renders `<DocumentView>` for it (graceful fallback to the declarative template when absent) — so `/resumes/:id` shows the authored layout: **preview === render === view** for resumes. **Remaining (Phase 1, resume):** interactive media overlays drag-from-library (#1913); save-as-template / publish wiring (needs a template-store decision — overlaps the co-developed document design-template registry); resume master/variant *picker* UI; left-rail drag-drop palette; richer item-render fidelity in `DocumentView`. **Remaining (other entities, #1914):** job (co-developed `job_doc`), article/blog block models + per-entity content binding; structured builders (#1918). NOT runtime-verified in a browser yet. Unblocks: one creation experience across all content; easier template authoring. |
| 134 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P1 | `feature` | **AI avatar / talking-head generation (HeyGen / Synthesia replacement)** | Generate a fully synthetic presenter video from a text script for users who do not want to appear on camera. Library of 10–20 pre-built avatars (ethnicities, genders, business styles) plus optional custom avatar from a 2-minute selfie sample. Reuses existing TTS + voice cloning (#113, #121) for audio. Lip-sync via D-ID / HeyGen / Synthesia API behind a swappable `services/avatar.ts` provider stub. New `studio_avatars` + `studio_avatar_renders` tables. UI: "Use AI Avatar" tab in `VoiceoverPanel.tsx` as an alternative to `WebcamRecorder.tsx`. Critical for displaced workers, ESL candidates, and employer brand teams that lack on-camera talent. Replaces HeyGen / Synthesia ($30–$200/mo). |
