| 374 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Resume analyzer LLM emits free-form `category` strings — frontend has to keyword-match to pick a wand** (2026-05-05) | The merged `services/resume/analyze.ts` system prompt asks the LLM for `{ severity, category, title, description, impact }` per recommendation. Categories are free text ("ats" / "keywords" / "format" / "content" / "impact" / "structure"); no structured `{ actionId, args }` is emitted alongside. Consequence: `frontend/lib/tools/find-wand-for-recommendation.ts` has to keyword-match `title + description` to dispatch the right wand (`consolidate_section_highlights`, `standardize_resume_dates`, `shorten_bullet`), so action coverage is fragile and depends on the LLM phrasing the imperative consistently. Fix: extend `ResumeRecommendationSchema` (`shared/tool-schemas.ts`) with optional `actionId: z.enum([...registered tool ids])` + `actionArgs: z.record(z.unknown())`; update the analyzer prompt to emit them when the recommendation maps to a known wand; resolver becomes `rec.actionId ?? findWandForRecommendation(...)`. Unblocks: Action button works for *every* category covered by a registered wand without prompt-tuning the keyword matcher. Identified 2026-05-05 during the Scorer/Optimizer collapse. |
| 522 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Direct deprecated deps `mp4-muxer` + `webm-muxer` need migration to `mediabunny` — code change, not a version bump** (2026-05-10) | Both packages emit `npm warn deprecated` "superseded by Mediabunny." [package.json](hired.video/frontend/package.json) lists them as direct deps used by the NLE / WebCodecs render pipeline (Studio video export per gap #278). Mediabunny exposes a different API (single unified `Mux` class vs. the per-format muxers we use). Migration: import mediabunny, swap `Mp4Muxer` / `WebmMuxer` callsites for the equivalent `Mux({ format: 'mp4' \| 'webm' })`, re-test the render pipeline against the existing studio fixtures. Out of scope for the audit-fix pass; tracked here so the deprecation warning isn't ignored indefinitely. Unblocks: matching upstream's recommended muxer + getting any future bug fixes (current packages are now in maintenance mode). |
| 595 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Per-widget motion renders in the editor preview but is NOT applied during MP4 export** (2026-05-13) | [timeline-emit.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/timeline-emit.ts) now carries `Widget.motion` through to `ClipEffect.params.motion`, but the matching applier in [lib/timeline/effects/canvas-v2.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/timeline/effects/canvas-v2.ts) doesn't yet read `params.motion` to drive per-frame opacity/transform during render. Result: a user authoring a fade-in sees the fade in the preview but the exported clip pops in instantly. Fix: each `canvas-v2:*` applier should call `motionStyleAt(...)` (or an equivalent renderer-side helper) and multiply the resulting opacity / apply the transform onto its draw call. Unblocks: animations land in exports. Pairs with #283 (Pro export polish). |
| 639 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **V1 deprecation cutover — when V1 is dropped from the UI, the following code paths can be deleted: v1 editor (`StudioLayout` storyboard surface, `StudioSidebar`, `StudioEditor`, `StudioPreview`), v1 sidebar `WorkspaceSwitcher` mount, v1 compiler / renderer (after #638 lands), `canvasStateToScript` (after #637 lands), `script` field on `saveDraft`, all V2→V1 conversion utilities (#625 / #626 already wontfix)** (2026-05-14 — V1 deprecation hardening) | Track this as the deletion checklist so when the product flag for V2-only flips, removal is a mechanical task instead of a hunt. Each individual blocker (#637 = save-side dependency, #638 = render-side dependency, #611 = migration completeness) must close BEFORE this can. Unblocks: ~thousands of lines of legacy code deletion + a cleaner mental model for new contributors. |
| 696 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Studio embed endpoint still keys off `videos.id` — projects without a rendered MP4 can't share an embed snippet** (2026-05-16 — surfaced while closing #695) | `GET /api/studio/videos/:videoId/embed` ([studio.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/studio.ts)) looks up the `videos` table by id and 404s with NOT_AVAILABLE for saved-public-but-unrendered projects (the post-#665 case). The Studio share dropdown / [StudioVideoEmbedSheet.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/StudioVideoEmbedSheet.tsx) only show "Embed code" when `isPublic && embedVideoId`, so the menu item is silently hidden for those projects. Fix: serve `<iframe src="https://hired.video/embedded/projects/:projectId">` for project-keyed embeds (mirrors the resume-embedded pattern) — the unified `<StudioPlayer/>` already serves saved-public projects without a render. Once shipped, drop the `embedVideoId` gate in [StudioProjectActions.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioProjectActions.tsx). Unblocks: every saved-public project gains a shareable embed, not just the rendered subset. |
| 718 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `bug` | **Render-time `RenderAudioContextError` surfaces a "try silent fallback" toast but no underlying device/WebAudio diagnostic is captured — repeat failures look identical to first failures** (2026-05-16) | Reported by sean@ during a Republish click (before #716 removed Republish): "The AudioContext encountered an error from the audio device or the WebAudio renderer." `withAudioErrorRecovery` in [StudioEditorV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx) catches `RenderAudioContextError` and offers a silent-fallback retry, but doesn't surface device info (sample rate, channel count, active sinkId, ctx.state) to telemetry — so we can't tell whether the failures cluster around a specific Bluetooth headset, Windows audio session switch, or browser quirk. Fix: enrich the thrown `RenderAudioContextError` with `{ contextState, sampleRate, deviceId? }` snapshot, log via `apiClient.post("/api/telemetry/render-failure", ...)` on first hit, and gate the silent-fallback offer on "non-trivial audio in the project" (skip the prompt entirely for projects with no music + no voiceover — should just succeed via the silent path automatically). Unblocks: actionable telemetry + smoother UX for the no-audio-anyway majority of renders. |
| 731 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **`stockMediaAssets` has no garbage collection — assets never deleted even when `userStockMediaUsage.pickCount` falls to zero across all users** (2026-05-16 — surfaced while closing #729) | [studio-features.ts:2059](hired.video/api/src/routes/studio-features.ts#L2059) PUTs `stock/{sha256}.{ext}` keyed by hash and inserts the `stockMediaAssets` row, but nothing ever decrements / sweeps. Even if every project that referenced the asset is deleted, the row + R2 blob stay forever. Fix: nightly cron that selects `stockMediaAssets` rows with `NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_stock_media_usage WHERE asset_hash = …)` for >30 days and reclaims both row + R2 key. Unblocks: stock library doesn't grow unbounded with vibe-search churn. |
| 792 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Resume Template publish/consent dialog (DRY of `PublishAsTemplateDialog.tsx`)** | #158 specifies the resume-template equivalent of the shipped video-template publish dialog. Per DRY: extract a shared `PublishCreatorListingDialog` generic over the listing kind (resume vs video), parameterise by service-method (`studioTemplatesService.publish` vs a new `resumeTemplatesService.publish`), shared consent + 95% copy block + creator-gate. Backend needs a `POST /api/resume-templates/:id/publish` mirroring the studio templates route — snapshots fee via `resolveCreatorFeeBps(userId)` from #157 and records `legalDocumentAcceptance` for kind `resume_template_creator_terms`. Unblocks the last per-sale content type's consent flow. |
| 793 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Denormalised rating-aggregate columns on article / template / certification listing rows** (opened 2026-04-20 — surfaced wiring #787) | `courses.averageRating` / `courses.ratingCount` already exist and the `recomputeAggregateCache` `course` branch shipped today writes them. The other four review subjects (`article`, `resume_template`, `video_template`, `certification`) need the same `average_rating real`, `rating_count integer not null default 0` columns + the matching `recomputeAggregateCache` branches so listing cards render `4.7 ★ (218)` without a join through `reviews`. Single migration touches `articles` + `resume_templates` + `studio_templates` + `course_certificates` (or skip certs if reviews aren't surfaced on the verify page). Unblocks: featured-creator ranking (#180) reading rating signals across content types without per-card aggregate queries. |
| 806 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Per-clip colour grading + LUT loading on video widgets** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced shipping the Director's Cut bundle and ruling chroma in / colour grading out for the first pass) | [video-filters.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/video-filters.ts) exposes six per-SCENE filters (brightness / contrast / saturation / hue / blur / warmth) wired to the FiltersPicker in [scene-sections.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/inspector/scene-sections.tsx); there is no per-clip equivalent and no LUT loading. Directors expect per-shot color (different LUT on the interview vs the b-roll). Spec: lift `VideoFilters` into a per-widget field on `VideoWidgetParams` (mirroring the new `chromaKey` field), surface a FiltersPicker on the video inspector, and register a `lut` effect with a 1D-LUT applier in the canvas-v2 pixel pass — the registry already supports a `lut` kind ([effects/lut.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/timeline/effects/lut.ts)), confirm whether it's wired. The shared editor preview already handles CSS-equivalent filters via `widgetEffectsToCss`, so adding a `filter:` CSS string in the video body is the preview half. Render-side dependent on #805. Unblocks: colourist workflow + premium "movie studio" optics on the video widget. |
| 833 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Canvas-side linked-content drawer doesn't yet pixel-match the DOM `<LinkedContentBody>` — full template fidelity is a separate Phase 6** (opened 2026-05-18 — partial fidelity gap noted closing #829) | #829 closed by drawing kind label + title + subtitle + body bullets + badge chips + CTA pill — substantially better than the prior thumbnail card, but still not the FULL `<DeclarativeResumeRenderer/>` / `<DeclarativeJobRenderer/>` / `<Markdown/>` output the editor's DOM `LinkedContentBody` paints. A user watching the export sees structured content; the editor's inline LinkedContentBody (mounted on the static authoring canvas) renders the full template. With #830 now sharing the export's canvas-v2 effects with the player too, this delta is the LAST drift between authoring inline DOM preview and playback canvas preview. Spec: per-kind canvas drawer (`drawResumeToCanvas(ctx, resume, rect)`) that ports each entity's template renderer's structured output to canvas-2D. The Resume drawer is the highest leverage — port `DeclarativeResumeRenderer`'s section walker to a canvas pipeline that respects the same template descriptor (Modern Clean / Bold Hero / Print Serif). Job + Article + Profile + Company + Video drawers ship incrementally. With drawers in place, the DOM `LinkedContentBody` becomes purely an inline-authoring affordance — playback + export already produce the faithful image. Unblocks: full pixel parity between the editor's inline entity preview and the playback/export canvas. |
| 861 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Resume metrics adapter — wire [`<MetricsPanel/>`](hired.video/frontend/components/analytics/MetricsPanel.tsx) onto resume views with geo + traffic sources** (opened 2026-05-19 — deferred from #860 reusable-panel work) | Resume view tracking ([resumeRepository.insertView](hired.video/api/src/repositories/resumeRepository.ts) + [services/resume/view.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/resume/view.ts)) currently records `viewerId / ipHash / referrer / userAgent` but no `ipCountry`, and there is no aggregator endpoint that returns the country / referrer rollups the panel needs. Fix: (a) add `ip_country` column to the resume views table + capture `cf-ipcountry` in the insert path, (b) add `GET /api/resumes/:id/metrics` that returns `ArtifactMetrics` (totalViews, viewers, referrers, countries — no heatmap until scroll-depth tracking lands), (c) replace the bespoke chart card on `pages/Resumes.tsx` with `<MetricsPanel kind="resume">`. Unblocks: consistent "viewers + countries + traffic sources" answer on resumes, candidate-facing parity with the studio view. |
| 990 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **"Review my whole resume in XYZ" wizard — step-through every work/volunteer/project entry's bullets + summary in one flow** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside the per-entry XYZ wands) | The per-entry XYZ wands now live on every highlights list (work/volunteer/project) and every summary/position field, but a candidate with 5 jobs has to click 15+ wands to rewrite their whole resume. The "Review all" shortcut the user requested in the original spec is deferred. To close: add a `<XyzReviewAllWizard>` component mounted as a top-level "✨ Review my resume (XYZ)" button on [ResumeBuilder.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/ResumeBuilder.tsx). On click, walk every section item in order (work[i] → highlights, then summary, then position; same for volunteer, project), reusing the same `/api/resumeoptimizer/rewrite-xyz-*` endpoints. Each step shows the same [BulletReviewDialog.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/resume-sections/BulletReviewDialog.tsx) / single-string review UI with Apply / Skip / Cancel-all. Persist a `wizardProgress` cursor in component state so refresh doesn't restart. Pairs with #989 — if the skills wand exists by then, fold it into the wizard's final step. |
| 1006 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Game levels can host ONLY `GameSprite[]` — no way to overlay `canvas-v2:text` / `image` / `video` / `chart` / `cta` / `linked-content` widgets inside a level. Tutorial banners, score HUDs, level-intro titles, end-cards, and any "branded chrome" around the playable canvas require the standard video widget kinds to be droppable into a game level, but [game-state.ts](hired.video/shared/game-state.ts) `GameLevel` has only `sprites` + transitions** (opened 2026-05-23 — user "Games is missing all the standard Video widgets (text/media/etc)") | The user's gap is clear: the studio has 13+ canvas-v2 widget appliers wired for Timeline kinds (text, image, video, shape-rect/circle, divider, chips, chart, webcam, cta, linked-content, speech-bubble, caption-box, sfx-burst), but the game runtime is a hermetic sprite-only world. Authors can't drop a `<canvas-v2:text>` "Level 1" intro card, a `<canvas-v2:chart>` mini-leaderboard, a `<canvas-v2:cta>` "Try Pro" interstitial, or a `<canvas-v2:linked-content>` "watch this video resume" overlay on top of their game. To close: (a) Extend `GameLevel` with `overlays: ClipEffect[]` — same shape as the Timeline's per-clip effect chain, drawing through the existing `canvas-v2:*` appliers. The runtime paints overlays AFTER sprites each frame so they layer over gameplay. (b) Surface a Widget Palette tab in the game editor — reuse `<WidgetPalette>` with a `mediaKind="game"` prop that filters to overlay-appropriate kinds (no scene-effects, no audio-clip widgets). (c) Editor wiring: drop a widget onto the canvas → appends to `level.overlays` + selection routes to the inspector. (d) Asset cache: overlays referencing R2 URLs ride the existing `preloadCanvasV2Media()` path so the runtime's first-frame paint is correct. (e) Touch / click handling: overlays with a `cta` widget block sprite-click hit-tests below them. Pairs with #1007 (widget overlays drive most of what users will visually script with Snap blocks — show overlay / hide overlay / move overlay). |
| 1101 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Resize + rotate handles on selected layers (extract V2-Video's widget transform chrome into a reusable `<TransformHandles/>` primitive)** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #1100; deferred because extracting CanvasStage's selection chrome is a substantial refactor) | [CanvasStage.tsx WidgetView](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/CanvasStage.tsx#L355) embeds the selection ring + bottom-right resize handle + rotation ball INSIDE the per-widget DOM. The math (un-rotate-delta for axis-aligned resize on a rotated widget, atan2 angle diff for rotation) lives in widget-local closures. Extract into a shared `<TransformHandles rect onMove onRotate onResize/>` primitive that BOTH `<CanvasStage>` (Timeline widgets) and `<DrawingStage>` (image-kind layers with new `transformScale` + `transformRotation` fields on `ImageLayer`) can mount. Per DRY: ONE transform-chrome across the editor. Pairs with #1100. |
| 1328 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **Pattern 7 violation — 13 route files redeclare `ok` / `fail` / `HandlerResult` locally instead of importing from `handlers/shared.ts`** (opened 2026-05-25). Files: `studio.ts`, `studio-features.ts`, `resumes.ts`, `video-pitch.ts`, `vendor-sync.ts`, `upload.ts`, `resume-roast.ts`, `phone.ts`, `nle.ts`, `interview.ts`, `interview-question-sets.ts`, `interview-assignments.ts`, `admin-r2.ts`. Why: these were extracted before `handlers/shared.ts` consolidation landed (which was Pattern 7's whole point — see the 2026-04-20 blank-title production bug). How to apply: delete the local declarations, `import { ok, fail, requireAuth, type HandlerResult } from "../handlers/shared.js"`. Verify the envelope field names match (`error.code`, `error.message`, `status`) so the call sites don't drift. ~30 lines of dead code removed per file. |
| 1331 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **`api/src/routes/studio.ts` is 4,015 LOC — decompose by feature into `studio/` subdirectory** (opened 2026-05-25). Why: every studio iteration adds more (#940 PSD round-trip + outpaint + selection, #939 inspector content sections, #929/#930 interactive_comic + cad_3d kinds, etc.) and the file has more than doubled since the README last said 1,716. It now mixes project CRUD, brand kits, campaigns, draft-save/publish, storyboard generation, image generation, script editing, upload routing, video analytics, comic scaffolding, and palette/genre fetches. How to apply: extract `routes/studio/projects.ts` (CRUD + clone + status + visibility), `routes/studio/brand-kits.ts`, `routes/studio/campaigns.ts`, `routes/studio/storyboard.ts` (incl. dynamic LLM path + image gen), `routes/studio/comics.ts` (scaffolder, genre/palette), `routes/studio/upload.ts`. Each gets its own `*-handlers.ts` + `*-deps.ts` per Pattern 1 (#1327). Pair with #1316f to fix the `firstName`/`lastName`/`ComicPalette`/`ComicSpecPage` type drift during the extraction. |
| 1332 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **`api/src/routes/studio-features.ts` is 3,398 LOC — decompose by sub-feature** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1331). The file owns 11 unrelated sub-features: TTS, captions, LinkedIn OAuth + publish, webcam/screen recording, AI delivery coaching, ATS package generation, interview question library + sessions, skills demos, voice cloning + marketplace claim/cart, async interviews + responses, and heatmap analytics. How to apply: split into `routes/studio/{tts,captions,linkedin,recording,coaching,ats,interview,skills,voice-clones,async-interviews,analytics}.ts` — one mount per sub-feature in `app.ts`. None of them share state across requests beyond the DB, so the split is mechanical. After split, each file should be ≤ 350 LOC. |
| 1574 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **TextNarrator scrubber-seek is approximate for Web Speech mid-utterance** (opened 2026-05-26 during #1573). The narrator's range-input scrubber maps seconds → word index via the pre-estimated `estimateWordTimestamps` (160 WPM ÷ speed). For WebGPU engines (Kokoro / Piper / VibeVoice) the seek path is "stop + re-synthesize the tail from word N," which is accurate. For Web Speech mid-utterance, the seek path is the same restart-from-word-N flow — accurate to within ~1 word, but the visible playhead lags actual word-boundary events by up to one boundary tick (the estimator vs. the engine's real timing drift on rare words). Fix: drive the playhead exclusively from the engine's `onBoundary` callbacks and let the estimator only own `durationMs` / scrubber-max. Cosmetic — playback itself is correct. |
| 1575 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Narrator mute is implemented as "stop the audio" rather than a true gain-node mute** (opened 2026-05-26 during #1573). `SpeechSynthesisUtterance.volume` can't be changed after `.speak()`, and the WebGPU engines play through a Web Audio `AudioBufferSourceNode` without a routed `GainNode` ([tts-engines.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/tts-engines.ts) `playPcm`). The simplest cross-engine mute is "stop the audio while muted" — that's what shipped. Side effect: muting drops the playhead to the active word index rather than continuing silently, so unmuting resumes from the last word, not from where audio would have been by now. Fix: own a `GainNode` inside `tts-engines.ts` so both web-speech (via a Media Stream wrapper) and the PCM playback path can be silenced without losing playhead position. Larger rewrite — file under "would be nice." |
| 1576 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **JobDetail narrator flattens UIJobRequirement / UIJobBenefit objects locally rather than via a shared serializer** (opened 2026-05-26 during #1573). [textFromJobDescription](hired.video/frontend/lib/audio/narrator-text.ts) accepts `string[]` lists, but [JobDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/JobDetail.tsx) carries `UIJobRequirement = { skill, level, required }[]` and `UIJobBenefit = { type, description }[]`. The page maps both into strings inline at the call site. The DeclarativeJobRenderer + the API-to-PDF text exporter likely flatten the same way — there's almost certainly a third copy in the resume-PDF / job-PDF exporter. Extract one shared serializer (`jobRequirementToText`, `jobBenefitToText`) in `shared/jobs/` and consume from every surface that paints job text. Unblocks: consistent phrasing across narration + PDF + JSON-LD JobPosting + ATS export. |
| 1580 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Per-chapter viewer dwell isn't instrumented — Engagement tab in the Details drawer shows chapter list with no telemetry** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside #1579). `videoChapters` rows define start times but the heatmap in [ArtifactAnalyticsDashboard](hired.video/frontend/components/analytics/ArtifactAnalyticsDashboard.tsx) is whole-video, not chapter-aggregated. [EngagementResultsPanel.ChaptersSection](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/shared/EngagementResultsPanel.tsx) renders the static chapter list and explicitly footnotes the gap. Fix: extend the video-view tracker ([video-tracker.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/analytics/video-tracker.ts)) to bucket `secondsWatched` into chapter ranges (read chapter boundaries from the same endpoint the player consumes), persist a `chapter_dwell_seconds[chapterId]` field on the view row, and surface per-chapter completion + drop-off in the Engagement results panel + Metrics heatmap. Unblocks: "which chapter killed retention" — the highest-value chapter-marker payoff. |
| 1581 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Per-thumbnail-variant click-through rate isn't tracked — only `isSelected` is known** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside #1579). [thumbnailCandidates](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/studio-features-service.ts) lets the author score + pick one variant, but views/clicks land on the project as a whole — there's no way to A/B which thumbnail drove clicks. [EngagementResultsPanel.ThumbnailsSection](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/shared/EngagementResultsPanel.tsx) shows the variant grid with the LIVE badge but no CTR. Fix: stamp the served thumbnail id onto the view-event row (`thumbnail_id` column on `artifact_views`), expose `cyclingMode` on `selectThumbnail` so the player can round-robin during a holdout window, and surface per-variant impressions / clicks / CTR in the Engagement results panel. Unblocks: data-driven thumbnail picking, parity with the YouTube/TikTok variant-test surface. |
| 1583 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Studio Voiceover preview (`VoiceoverPanel`) doesn't pick up the shared narrator volume slider** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside #1582). [VoiceoverPanel](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/VoiceoverPanel.tsx) calls `speakWithEngine` directly to preview voices and doesn't pass a `volume`, so the editor's per-user volume preference doesn't apply to voice previews. Trivial fix: pass the same `volume` value the narrator persists in localStorage (or expose a `getUserNarratorVolume()` helper) and forward `volume` on every `speakWithEngine` call. Unblocks: editor users who turned their narrator volume down don't get blasted by a voice preview. |
| 1587 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Engagement-asset widgets don't theme-stamp colours at insert time** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside #1579). `insertEngagementAsset` in [StudioEditorV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx) uses the default warm-card colours from [DEFAULT_ENGAGEMENT_ASSET_COLORS](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/engagement-assets.ts); linked-content cards (the sibling pattern) pull the active theme through `resolveLinkedContentColors` so a card dropped onto a dark-cinematic template adopts that template's chrome. Fix: add `resolveEngagementAssetColors(state)` mirroring the linked-content helper and call it from the insert path + extend `applyThemeToState` to re-stamp engagement-asset widgets when the user switches themes (per gap #582's "single source of truth" requirement). |
| 1660 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **3D world studio — broader video-editor parity in the 3D-asset left rail (backgrounds, music, voiceover, stickers, AI image gen)** (opened 2026-05-27, follow-on to #1659). The 3D left rail today shows primitives + sprite library + MediaPicker custom upload. The Timeline (video) editor exposes additional libraries the 3D editor should match: (1) **Backgrounds** — the existing stock-media background library should be drag-droppable into the 3D world as a sky texture / floor texture / billboard backdrop. (2) **Music + voiceover** — environmental audio + per-entity sounds (trigger sound on hazard / collectible). The 3D scene currently has no audio source nodes. (3) **Stickers / decals** — small image overlays placeable as decals on existing entities or as billboards. (4) **AI image generation** — the existing `<MediaAiPromptPanel kindNoun="sprite">` should be reachable from inside the 3D world too, with the generated image dropping into the scene as a textured entity (instead of the sprite library). **Fix path**: extract a shared `<StudioAssetLibrary>` component (or a thin wrapper around MediaPicker tabs) that the video, image, AND game editors all mount in their left rail; the 3D world subscribes to the drag events with the same `x-world3d-asset` MIME. For audio: extend `World3DEntity` with optional `audioUrl` + add `<PositionalAudio>` from drei when present; add a `audio` entity kind for ambient/environmental sound. **Unblocks**: the customer ask — every video-editor library feature should be reachable from the 3D world; closes the "I shouldn't have to switch editors to pick a song / a background / an AI-generated texture" gap. |
| 1872 | T1 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Broader pre-existing lint debt surfaced by #1868 (115 errors + 2684 warnings repo-wide), triaged** (opened 2026-05-31; config false-positives cleared 2026-06-14, TK1) | With ESLint actually running, `npx eslint .` reports **115 errors + 2684 warnings**. Of the errors, ~105 are CONFIG FALSE-POSITIVES not code bugs: **81 `react/no-unknown-property`** are all React-Three-Fiber JSX props (`position`/`args`/`intensity`/…) in [components/studio/game/world-3d/*](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/game/world-3d) + [components/studio/cad-3d/*](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/cad-3d) — needs the R3F-aware plugin config (or rule-off for those globs); **24 `no-undef`** are browser/Node globals in plain-JS files ([lib/studio/game/runtime-core.js](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/game/runtime-core.js) ×18, scripts/build-youtube-banner.cjs ×6) — needs `env`/`globals` config per override. Only ~10 errors are genuine minor issues (3 no-unused-vars, 2 no-extra-boolean-cast, 2 no-useless-escape, 1 no-unreachable, 1 no-fallthrough, 1 react/jsx-key). Warnings (advisory): 783 no-explicit-any, 571 no-unnecessary-type-assertion, 382 no-non-null-assertion, 339 no-unused-vars, 166 hiredvideo/require-page-chrome (#1869), 80 no-duplicate-imports. Fix: add ESLint overrides (R3F + plain-JS env), fix the ~10 real errors, then chip at warnings. Unblocks: a genuinely green `npm run lint` so it can gate CI. (Separately, the pre-existing #1870 frontend-test-suite red is still owed.) **Partial (2026-06-14, TK1 — the config-false-positive slice):** [frontend/eslint.config.js](hired.video/frontend/eslint.config.js) — (1) extended the R3F `react/no-unknown-property:off` override to `components/studio/cad-3d/**` (verified cad-3d 18 errors → 0; world-3d already covered → all 81 R3F false-positives now cleared); (2) added a `lib/studio/game/**/*.{js,jsx}` override declaring the browser runtime globals (window/performance/Image/requestAnimationFrame/…) so the plain-JS game runtime no longer trips `no-undef` while genuine typos + `no-unused-vars` still fail (verified runtime-core.js 19 errors → 1); (3) broadened the `scripts/**` glob to include `.cjs` so build scripts get the Node env. **Residual (genuine code errors + warnings, owned by the file's domain track, NOT config):** the ~10 real errors — incl. the 1 remaining `no-unused-vars` in [runtime-core.js:521](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/game/runtime-core.js#L521) (`initial` → `_initial`), plus no-extra-boolean-cast / no-useless-escape / no-unreachable / no-fallthrough / jsx-key scattered across domain files — and the advisory warning backlog. |
| 1918 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **Structured (non-paged) builders share the studio editable-block foundation but NOT the document page model** (opened 2026-06-06 with the #1915 scope decision) | The scope line (#1915) brings structured builders into the studio — [ScreeningTemplates](hired.video/frontend/pages/services/ScreeningTemplates.tsx) and learning-path / cohort authoring (see [[project_learning_cohorts]] / [[project_learning_pathways]]). These are content-like (they deserve the unified field-bound editable-block experience + input-template seeds + structure/content split) but they are NOT printable documents — they are ordered lists / DAGs, not Letter sheets, and have no PDF path. So the SHARED foundation (#1916 field-bound blocks, the studio shell, the per-entity field schema) must be factored ABOVE the paged `DocumentState`: `document` (resume/job/article/blog) is one canvas runtime consuming it; a non-paged structured-builder runtime is a second. Do NOT cram screening/learning-path into `DocumentEntityKind` with a forced Letter geometry. Decide the second runtime's layout model (list vs graph) when the first structured builder migrates. Unblocks: structured builders join the unified editor without inheriting an irrelevant page/print model. |
| 1934 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Document canvas UX layout pass — left-rail palette + drag-drop + footer pagination guides (landed); follow-ups** (opened 2026-06-06, user-directed) | Per user direction the document editor chrome moved OFF the canvas. **Landed 2026-06-06:** (1) on-canvas toolbar removed; authoring controls now live in the LEFT rail [DocumentLeftPanel](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/DocumentLeftPanel.tsx) (design Templates + the section palette as draggable chips + page size/orientation), mounted via the kind-aware `<CollapsiblePanel side="left">` in [StudioEditorV2](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx); (2) sections drag onto the page ([DocumentStage](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/DocumentStage.tsx) `onDrop` reads the `DOCUMENT_BLOCK_DRAG_MIME` preset index) OR click-to-append; (3) the sheet now GROWS (removed `overflow-hidden` — fixes sections below the fold being clipped) with per-print-page break guides + "Page N" labels measured from content height; (4) RIGHT rail gains an Upload-existing-résumé panel below the AI (reuses `<ResumeUploadSheet>` then the `?editResume` round-trip). tsc clean both projects + 24 document unit tests green. **Follow-ups:** (a) drag-drop appends to flow — dropping at the cursor (absolute block at drop point / insert-between) isn't wired; (b) page guides are visual, not a true reflow into discrete fixed sheets (print pagination is correct via `@page`); (c) the document AI panel still runs the image-generator (`addMediaWidget` onto the unused CanvasState) — for documents it should drop an image block/overlay or be an AI-write/enhance-selection prompt; (d) drag-from-library interactive media overlays (#1913) still pending. **Update 2026-06-06 (user-directed, item 4 reworked):** the right-rail upload is no longer a button → slide-out (which read as "create a new resume" when the user had already opened one). It now embeds `<ResumeUpload compact minimal>` inline (new `minimal` mode hides the name/privacy/master new-resume fields; `submitLabel="Convert & import"`) and on success `handleResumeUploaded` builds the doc-state via the shared `createResumeDocumentState` + `resetDocumentHistory` and renders the parsed résumé on the CURRENT canvas in place — no navigation. `onCancel` is now optional in `ResumeUpload` (Cancel hidden when embedded). The new-row-vs-overwrite semantic is now resolved — see #1935. |
| 1950 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **No tests for the resume-feedback service** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1946) | `ResumeFeedbackService` (access resolution incl. token-claim + expiry, annotation lifecycle, `acceptAnnotation` content application, proposal accept/reject with pre-snapshot) and `content-edit.ts` (`applySuggestedEdit` path setter — basics vs array-item-by-id, bracketed paths, missing-target → CONFLICT; `validateProposedDraft`) ship with zero coverage. Add happy/boundary/exception cases with real-shape resume fixtures (seed-derived item ids, not just clean v4 UUIDs) per the schema-test convention. |
| 1960 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Comic+ (`interactive_comic`) has no dedicated editing surface — falls back to the timeline editor** (opened 2026-06-07 while adding Comic+ starter templates) | `CanvasRouter` ([CanvasRouter.tsx:104](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/CanvasRouter.tsx#L104)) returns `surfaces.interactive_comic` if provided, but [StudioEditorV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx#L3349) supplies no `interactive_comic` slot, so picking a Comic+ template seeds comic pages + a blank `interactiveComicState` (via [template-dispatch.ts:107](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/template-dispatch.ts#L107)) and opens the **timeline** canvas. The branch graph is persisted but cannot be authored visually. An [`InteractiveComicStage`](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/comic/InteractiveComicStage.tsx) component already exists but isn't mounted. **Fix**: wire `InteractiveComicStage` into the editor's `surfaces.interactive_comic` slot (branch-node graph editor + per-page choice authoring) so the seeded graph is editable. **Unblocks**: the Comic+ kind becomes authorable end-to-end, not just persistable (#929). |
| 1995 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Shared `resolveNarrationEngine()` seam + wire dubbing & AI-script narration to the clone engine** (opened 2026-06-13, PRD §4) | One shared resolver `({voiceId, preferClone}) → {engineId, synthesize()}` so no call site branches on `provider` or re-checks the license. Route the [StudioDubbingPanel](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/dubbing/StudioDubbingPanel.tsx) "cloned-voice preferred" path and an AI-script "Narrate in my voice" toggle through it. Makes the "dub in your own cloned voice" claim real once #1994 lands. |
| 1996 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Voice-clone consent attestation + provenance disclosure + publish moderation** (opened 2026-06-13, PRD §5) | `POST /voice-clones` requires an explicit "my voice / I have permission" attestation → persist `consent_attested_at` + `consent_text_version` on `studio_voice_clones` (ToS §9a). Public listings route through `moderationService` before going live (impersonation = takedown category); cloned-voice exports carry an AI-generated disclosure. Legal/abuse gate before GA. |
| 2050 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `bug` | **`PublishDestinationId` for `tiktok`/`youtube-shorts`/`instagram-reels`/`instagram-feed`/`x-post`/`facebook-page` are not in the registry, and the `studio_project_publications.destination` CHECK must be ALTERed to admit them** (found 2026-06-13 during the social-publishing PRD pass, #2043) | [shared/media-kinds.ts](hired.video/shared/media-kinds.ts) `PUBLISH_DESTINATIONS` stops at YouTube/LinkedIn/profile + per-kind niche destinations — no social-short surfaces exist, so the Studio publish menu can't even *render* a TikTok/Reels row. Fixing requires (a) extending the `PublishDestinationId` union + array, and (b) an idempotent ALTER of the `studio_project_publications` destination CHECK constraint (per #1625) so publication rows for the new ids persist. Bundled into Phase 2 (#2045) but logged separately as the concrete schema-drift item. |
| 2101 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Resume canvas EDITING surface still edits in single-column fields — declarative columns only show in preview/view/print** (opened 2026-06-07 with the render-engine unification) | The studio preview, the `/resumes/:id` view, and the PDF export now all render resumes through ONE engine — `DeclarativeResumeRenderer` (columns, themes, hero, per-section layout) — via the new `DocumentState`→descriptor bridge ([resume-document-descriptor.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/resume-document-descriptor.ts) + [ResumeDocumentView.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/ResumeDocumentView.tsx); [DocumentPagedView](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/DocumentPagedView.tsx) delegates resume docs to it, [exportDocument](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/export-document.ts) routes resume print through the in-app declarative PDF route, and [ResumeDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeDetail.tsx) renders one declarative path). This closes "preview doesn't look like the viewer." **Residuals not done this pass:** (1) the EDITING canvas ([DocumentStage](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/DocumentStage.tsx) "One Page" mode) is still the generic single-column field editor — it does NOT show the two-column declarative layout WHILE editing, so edit≠preview for columned templates (the original #1912/#1916 "full-fidelity inline section rendering" goal — see DocumentStage header comment). (2) **Free-form canvas blocks (`text`/`image`/`divider`/`spacer`) the user adds on a RESUME doc are dropped from the declarative render** — the bridge only maps section/component blocks (the descriptor model has no free blocks). Resumes are structured so this is acceptable, but it IS render-time data loss to record. (3) The "One Page | Individual Pages" toggle is now a no-op for resumes (the declarative render is a responsive flow, not a fixed sheet), so true per-page (multi-page) preview/zoom of a resume is gone — the windowing engine only slices the generic `DocumentView`. Unblocks: true WYSIWYG columned editing + multi-page resume preview + custom block support inside the declarative engine. |
| 2128 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Editor & resume-detail surfaces don't capture CTA-hotzone clicks** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced fixing the `/v/[slug]` analytics gap) | The shared [CtaHotzonesOverlay](hired.video/frontend/components/video/CtaHotzonesOverlay.tsx) now self-fires `POST /api/studio/projects/:id/cta-click` whenever an `analyticsProjectId` is supplied, and the three public-watch branches in [StudioVideoSurface.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/StudioVideoSurface.tsx) (`PublicStudioCanvas` / `RawVideoPlayback` / `BakedVideo`) all pass it through. The editor preview ([StudioPlayerCanvas](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/StudioPlayerCanvas.tsx)) deliberately omits it so author rehearsal doesn't pollute the dashboard, but [ResumeDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeDetail.tsx) (in-platform watch surface) and any other consumer that mounts `StudioPlayer` directly also skip it — clicks on those surfaces never reach the rollup. Spec: decide whether in-platform on-platform watches count as CTA clicks; if yes, plumb `analyticsProjectId` into the StudioPlayer mount points outside `/v/[slug]`. Unblocks: full-funnel CTR for owners who share the in-platform link instead of the public URL. |
| 2153 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Preserve resume interactivity (`content.metaData` media + `content.skillEvidence`) through the document-canvas authoring path** (opened 2026-06-06 with #1912) | Resumes are interactive: section items carry attached media via `content.metaData[]` (`ResumeSectionMeta` bound to an item by stable `referenceId`) and skills carry `content.skillEvidence[]`. The document canvas must keep this data in the ENTITY content (never copy it into `DocumentState`) and let a dragged-on overlay image carry a `mediaBinding` ([document-state.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/document-state.ts)) that writes back a `metaData` row for the bound item — so dropping a studio-made image onto an experience card makes it interactive and survives section reorder (binding by id, not index). Renderer keeps driving `ItemMediaStrip` + `enrichSkillsWithEvidence` unchanged. Needs: the drop→metaData-upsert handler in `<DocumentStage>`, and round-trip tests with real seed-derived fixtures (per [feedback_tests_with_real_fixtures]). Unblocks: interactive resumes authored visually instead of via the metadata modal. |
| 2201 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Dark-mode color audit — components with hardcoded Tailwind colors don't adapt** (opened 2026-06-16 with the "Soft Slate" / "Midnight" theme rollout) | Dark mode (palette D "Midnight") is now reachable app-wide via next-themes + the `.dark` token block in [global.css](hired.video/frontend/global.css) (toggle in [Navigation.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/Navigation.tsx) + the Settings appearance select, both applied through the single [use-theme-preference.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/theme/use-theme-preference.ts) seam; server preference synced via [ThemeSync.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/theme/ThemeSync.tsx) off the shared account-settings cache; no-FOUC bootstrap in [index.html](hired.video/frontend/index.html)). Components styled via **semantic tokens** (`bg-background`/`bg-card`/`text-foreground`/`text-muted-foreground`/`bg-primary`…) adapt automatically. But any component using **hardcoded** Tailwind palette classes (`bg-white`, `text-gray-700`, `bg-green-50`, `border-slate-200`, etc.) stays light under `.dark` → low-contrast / broken surfaces. [Settings.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Settings.tsx) already models the correct pattern (status cards pair `bg-green-50 dark:bg-green-950`), but most pages predate dark mode and have no `dark:` variants. Fix: sweep `frontend/{pages,components}/**` for raw color utilities and either swap to semantic tokens or add `dark:` variants; consider an ESLint guard against bare `bg-white`/`text-gray-*` in app surfaces. Unblocks: a visually-correct dark theme on every surface, not just token-based UI. The light default ("Soft Slate", palette A) needs no such audit — it only softened the canvas; cards stay white. |
| 137 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **AI eye-contact correction** | Real-time gaze redirection so users reading the teleprompter (#116) appear to look directly into camera. NVIDIA Maxine WebRTC SDK on compatible GPUs; fallback to server-side pass via `sieve.ai` or open-source LookOnce on non-GPU clients. Toggle in `WebcamRecorder.tsx` settings. Closes the "obvious teleprompter user" tell — users no longer have to choose between scripted delivery and natural eye contact. |
| 138 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Auto-reframe for vertical / square formats** | When the user switches aspect ratio (#133), MediaPipe Face Detection WASM re-detects the speaker per frame and generates per-time-range crop offsets stored on `storyboardScenes.reframeKeyframes`. `frame-renderer.ts` and `caption-renderer.ts` apply offsets at render time so faces are never cropped out of 9:16 or 1:1 outputs. Adobe Premiere Pro auto-reframe parity. Critical for repurposing landscape video resumes into TikTok / Reels / Shorts without re-shooting. |
| 208 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Self-updating CRM Agent (background person re-enrichment)** | Cron walks `talentPoolCandidates` older than N days, calls BurnRateOS reconcile API, snapshots deltas onto local refs, logs change-set on the person timeline. No external provider call from hired.video. |
