| 1562 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Dubbing track timing isn't elastic — translated cues clip when target language is longer** (opened 2026-05-26 during #1558). The dubbing splice in `StudioDubbingPanel` places each synthesized cue at its source cue's `start` time; when the target language is naturally longer (English → German is +25–30%, English → Spanish is +20%), later cues clip the trailing audio of earlier ones. Fix: either (a) auto-rescale TTS speed per cue so the synthesized duration fits the source window (`speed = sourceDuration / synthesizedDuration`, clamped 0.85–1.25), (b) shift downstream cues to absorb overflow and resync on the next scene boundary, or (c) emit a new captions track that matches the dub's actual timing. Option (a) is the cleanest first pass. Unblocks: production-ready dub quality on EN→FR / DE / ES / PT. |
| 1776 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **IP attestation at template submission time** (split from #188 closure 2026-05-30) | Add `ipAttestation` text column on the template tables + require non-empty at submission. Legal sign-off for resale of user-submitted templates. |
| 1779 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Editor UI for film credit sub-schema** (split from #820 closure 2026-05-30) | Field group on ACTOR_HEADSHOT_HERO + DIRECTOR_FILMOGRAPHY_SERIF templates that captures `roleName`/`roleType`/`production`/etc. and writes to `resumeData.projects[i].film`. |
| 1781 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **`content_audiences` mapping for film credits** (split from #820 closure 2026-05-30) | Map actor/director resumes to the `content_audiences` taxonomy so casting search composes with the existing audience pickers. |
| 1785 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Avatar painter consumes BYO portrait** (split from #1559 closure 2026-05-30) | Extend the painter in [paint.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/avatar/paint.ts) to use the uploaded portrait + face-bbox + mouth-region instead of the stylized presenter base when `portraitSourceId` is set. |
| 1788 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **`<GameStage/>` editor component dispatching on mediaKind=game** (split from #927 closure 2026-05-30) | StudioEditorV2 dispatcher mounts `<GameStage/>` instead of `<CanvasStage/>` when `mediaKind === "game"`. Lays out the scene picker + asset library + script editor. |
| 1789 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Phaser-3 game runtime + sandboxed script-execution iframe** (split from #927 closure 2026-05-30) | The actual Phaser-3 hydrate-from-GameState runtime, run inside a sandboxed iframe so script eval can't reach the studio's main JS context. |
| 2131 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `quality` | **Heatmap-derived "Total Views" still under-counts vs. the `/view` POST counter** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced wiring `recordProjectView` from PublicVideoResume) | The dashboard's "Total Views" card now prefers `eventCounts.views` (one row per page mount via `POST /api/studio/projects/:id/view`) and falls through to `analytics.totalViews` (heatmap row count) only when the events endpoint 403s ([VideoAnalyticsDashboard.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/VideoAnalyticsDashboard.tsx)). Because the heatmap tracker only flushes on the 30s tick / `beforeunload` / `ended`, drive-by visits never produce a heatmap row, so the two counts will drift forever (heatmap < view-count). The current behaviour is correct for the headline metric but the heatmap density is misleading when read as "% of viewers" — the denominator should be the heatmap row count, not Total Views. Spec: relabel the heatmap legend, or store per-mount heatmap rows (zero seconds-watched is acceptable) so the two numbers reconcile. Unblocks: trustworthy "% viewers" tooltip on the heatmap bars. |
| 2154 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Generalize the document canvas beyond resume — article/blog need a block model (Tiptap `bodyJson` ↔ document blocks), job needs template DB rows** (opened 2026-06-06 with #1912) | Phase 1 is resume-only (the declarative descriptor + `resume_templates` + `template_licenses` already exist). To extend the unified canvas: (a) ARTICLE/BLOG have no descriptor/block model — body is raw Tiptap/ProseMirror `bodyJson` ([articles.ts](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/articles.ts)); needs a `bodyJson`↔`DocumentBlock[]` adapter (or treat ProseMirror nodes as flow blocks) so they ride the same `DocumentState`; (b) JOB templates are static frontend descriptors ([job-template.ts](hired.video/frontend/types/job-template.ts)) with no DB marketplace rows — `template_licenses` already supports `templateKind:'job'` but nothing writes them; add the rows + publish path; (c) factor the common spine of `ResumeTemplateDescriptor` + `JobTemplateDescriptor` into a shared `ContentTemplateDescriptor` once a second entity is on the canvas. Unblocks: "same flow for article, job, blog". **Article/blog canvas authoring landed 2026-06-06:** `article_doc` + `blog_doc` catalog entries (mediaKind document, `documentEntityKind` article/blog) make both creatable from the studio landing; they author via the free-content block palette (`blockPresetsForEntity` → text/image/divider/spacer), open seeded with a Title+Body starter (`defaultBlocksFor`), persist via the document runtime (`document_state`), render read-only via `DocumentView`, and PDF-export — all on the existing infrastructure (no Tiptap adapter needed for canvas authoring). Job is on the canvas via the co-developed `job_doc` + design templates. **Article/blog entity-row publishing landed 2026-06-06:** on save, the entity-aware document-persistence branch in [StudioEditorV2](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx) derives a title + markdown body from the canvas blocks via [document-to-article.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/document-to-article.ts) and **upserts an `articles` row** (`articleService.create`/`update`, kind `article`, create-on-first-save binding `entityId`) — so a canvas-authored article/blog enters the articles system as a draft. **Article round-trip completed 2026-06-06:** reverse adapter [document-from-article.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/document-from-article.ts) (markdown body → blocks) + a `?editArticle=<id>` deep-link in [StudioLanding](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx) (fetch via `articleService.getMine`, convert, mint a `kind:"document"` project bound to the article) — so a PRE-EXISTING article opens on the canvas, edits, and saves back via the entity-aware persistence path. **Job entity-row binding + EDIT landed 2026-06-07:** the document content model is now generalized off `ResumeData` to a loose `DocumentEntityContent` ([document-state.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/document-state.ts)); the field schema is entity-keyed ([document-field-schema.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/document-field-schema.ts) — object/array section shapes + new field types number/select/image) with job sections (`overview`/`responsibilities`/`requirements`/`details`); [job-content.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/job-content.ts) maps the `job_items` row ↔ canvas content (full editable-field parity with the retired form, publishing fields passthrough); `createJobDocumentState` seeds the posting; the entity-aware fetch + save-back in [StudioEditorV2](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx) loads via `jobService.getJobById` and writes via `updateJob` (create-on-first-save for fresh drafts); `?editJob` deep-link in [StudioLanding](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx). So a PRE-EXISTING job opens, edits, and saves back on the canvas — same lifecycle as resume. **Remaining:** (a) wire the creator article surface's "Edit" buttons → `?editArticle` (the deep-link exists + works; the existing creator-editor entry points aren't repointed yet) + richer markdown/Tiptap fidelity in both adapters; (b) job template DB rows / `template_licenses` writes; (c) the shared `ContentTemplateDescriptor` factoring; (d) job publishing-field widgets + read-only render polish (#1953). |
| 657 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P3 | `quality` | **V2 widget radius UX: two radius controls on shape-rect + sticky-collapsed accordion state masks the field for returning users** | shape-rect shows BOTH "Corner radius" (Content section, drives `ShapeWidgetParams.cornerRadius` on the inner fill) AND "Radius" (Container style section, drives `ContainerStyle.borderRadius` on the outer wrapper) — visually identical effect, two write paths, no shared component. Pick one source of truth or label/scope the controls so the user understands the difference. Separately, [InspectorSectionList.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/inspector/InspectorSectionList.tsx) persists open/closed state in localStorage scoped by `storageKey`, so users who already collapsed Container style before its `defaultOpen: true` flip (2026-05-15) still won't see Radius until they manually expand — needs a one-shot migration or a "reset panel layout" action. Fixing unblocks V1-parity discoverability for rounded-corners and any other future shared-tail field. |
| 299 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **`StudioLayout` and `AdminLayout` should compose `<AppShell>` (or vice versa)** | Studio (`pages/studio/StudioLayout.tsx`) and Admin (`components/admin/AdminLayout.tsx`) each maintain their own outer chrome composition with sidebar collapse state, mobile menu plumbing, and Navigation/Footer mounts — parallel to but separate from `<AppShell>`. Today they don't fire the API-flood bug because access is gated upstream (admin permission, studio auth). But three parallel chrome owners is one too many — pick one of: (a) make Studio/Admin render *inside* `<AppShell>` and only own their inner panel split, (b) hoist the `useVerificationBlocked()` short-circuit to a shared `<ChromeRoot>` that all three layouts compose. Whichever direction, the predicate currently consumed by `<AppShell>`/`<GlobalChrome>`/`GlobalVerificationGate`/`RequireVerified` should be the only place it lives. Identified 2026-05-04 during AppShell extraction. |
| 329 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`authService.getCurrentUser` and `userService.getCurrentUser` are duplicate `/me` fetchers** | Both methods exist in parallel — auth-service normalizes via `normalizeAndPersist` (writes `current_user` localStorage), user-service normalizes via `normalizePublicUserToProfile` (no persistence). Two distinct `UserProfile` types, two normalizers, two callers (StudioWizard + ProfileIntake on the user-service side). Should consolidate to one fetch + one canonical type so future schema drift can't open a divergence. Both already share the same verification gate after #327, so the consolidation is now purely a typing / normalization unification. Identified 2026-05-04 during the verification-gate extraction (#327). |
| 359 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Vite worker.format = "iife" forces a static-import constraint workers must follow but main-thread code violates** | Workers in this repo bundle as IIFE (no code-split), so `await import("mp4-muxer")` inside a worker fails the build with `Invalid value "iife" for option "worker.format"`. `frontend/workers/render-encode.worker.ts` uses a static `import { Muxer, ArrayBufferTarget } from "mp4-muxer"` to comply, but `lib/renderer/video-exporter.ts:38` and `lib/timeline/proxy-generator.ts:97` still use the dynamic form on the main thread — both work today (main bundle splits fine), but if either is ever moved into a worker the build will break the same way. Fix: either flip vite to `worker.format: "es"` (one config knob, lets workers code-split) OR codify a lint rule that worker files must use static imports for chunked deps. Unblocks: future worker-shifted code paths (e.g. moving proxy generation into a worker for #355). Identified 2026-05-05 while making the build pass after #341/353 work. |
| 376 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **Resume Scorer + Optimizer have one shared engine but two backend routes — collapse to a single canonical `/api/resume-analysis` after monitoring** (2026-05-05) | `api/src/routes/resume-scorer.ts::/score` and `api/src/routes/resume-optimizer.ts::/optimize` are now both thin proxies over `services/resume/analyze.ts` (one prompt, one Zod schema, one fallback). Two routes still exist for SEO continuity (different funnel pages) and for tool-run history (`tool_id = "ai-resume-scorer"` vs `"resume-optimizer"`). Long-term, one canonical `/api/resume-analysis` route with a `?surface=score\|optimize` query param (or just one route that returns the union shape and lets the page project) would simplify deploys, telemetry, and the `ai-api-registry.ts` mapping. Fix sequence: monitor for 2-4 weeks → add `/api/resume-analysis` as alias → migrate Chrome extension + frontend callers → 410 the legacy routes. Unblocks: one route to maintain, one rate-limit policy, one access-policy entry. Identified 2026-05-05 during the Scorer/Optimizer collapse. |
| 407 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **31 pre-existing test failures stem from test-scaffolding rot — components evolved to require AuthProvider / Router contexts that the test mounts no longer provide** (2026-05-06) | Inventory: `components/__tests__/PeopleCard.test.tsx` (8 fails — `useAuth must be used within an AuthProvider` because `PeopleCard` now embeds `EntityVideos` which calls `useApiReady`); `components/__tests__/StoryboardEditor.test.tsx` (9 fails — `useNavigate() may be used only in the context of a <Router>`); `__tests__/pages/Tasks.test.tsx` (7 fails — DOM query for "Kanban", "Add Task", "Task Details" buttons that have been renamed/restructured); `__tests__/pages/JobResumeMatch.test.tsx` (1 fail — error-banner DOM query drifted); `lib/config/__tests__/ai-api-registry.test.ts` (2 fails — `getAPIsForContext('resume-edit').length === 0`, registry config drifted to no-longer-include resume-edit context); `lib/services/__tests__/ai-orchestration-service.test.ts` (1 fail — same root cause as ai-api-registry); `lib/__tests__/card-feed.test.ts` (1 fail — fanout assertion). Fix is mechanical per-file: wrap renders in `<MemoryRouter>` / `<AuthProvider>` mocks; update DOM queries to match current button labels; sync the AI registry test fixture to whatever actions live in the registry today. Each file is a 5–20 line edit but there are ~7 files, so it's a separate scoped pass — bundling with the persona-axis PR would balloon the diff. Unblocks: green CI signal so the rest of the persona-axis migration (#400 + #401 + #402) can rely on the test suite as a regression gate. Identified 2026-05-06 while picking up PR-2 of #400. Confirmed pre-existing by stash-bisect against `main` before the persona-axis branch. |
| 479 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Live-preview music doesn't resync on big seeks — playhead can be 10s into the timeline while music is still 2s in** (2026-05-09) | Initial implementation had a drift-detection effect that tore down + rebuilt the schedule when `currentTime` jumped > 0.5s, but it added churn (effect deps included `currentTime`, firing every RAF tick) and timing edge-cases caused premature rebuilds during normal playback. Removed in this pass — playback now stays in sync as long as the user only Plays/Pauses; scrubbing the playhead while playing leaves the music running on its original schedule. Fix: use `performance.now()` to compute drift independently of `audio ctx.currentTime` (which has its own offset), or expose a "rebuild from this offset" entry on `ClipScheduleHandle` so seeks can transplant rather than tear-down + re-decode. Identified 2026-05-09 simplifying the audio effect. |
| 589 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Drop-target chrome only highlights the canvas — scene thumbnails in the ScenesRail aren't kind-aware drop targets, so users can't drop a background or theme onto a specific scene from the rail** (2026-05-13) | The new shared [CanvasDropOverlay](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/CanvasDropOverlay.tsx) + `detectDragKind` / `DRAG_KIND_META` in [drag-protocol.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/drag-protocol.ts) light up the canvas with a kind-aware ring + badge during drag. The same pattern should apply to each [ScenesRail](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/ScenesRail.tsx) scene-thumbnail tile: hovering a `background` drag should highlight the tile and dropping should apply the bg to THAT scene's `backgroundColor` (not the active scene's). Same for `theme` if we want per-scene theme overrides. Fix: each tile mounts `CanvasDropOverlay` + wires a drop handler that calls `onSceneBackgroundChange(scene.id, bgValue)`. Unblocks: target a specific scene with a drag from the Design panel. |
| 591 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Studio v2 cut/copy/paste is in-tab only — no OS-clipboard sync for cross-tab / cross-app paste** (2026-05-13) | [useCanvasClipboard](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/use-canvas-clipboard.ts) holds the yanked widget/scene in a hook-local ref. Copying a widget in one Studio tab and pasting it in another (or in the desktop app vs the web app) doesn't work. Fix: also serialise the snapshot to `navigator.clipboard.writeText(JSON.stringify({ kind, payload }))` on copy/cut, and on paste try `clipboard.readText()` + JSON.parse first, falling back to the in-memory ref. Needs a clipboard-permission prompt fallback path. Unblocks: cross-tab + future cross-window paste. |
| 596 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Per-widget Filters not implemented — Filters still live on the Scene** (2026-05-13) | The inspector design intent was "each artifact defines its own meta" including a per-widget Filters chain for image/video widgets. The data model only carries `Scene.filters` (one filter chain per scene applied uniformly via CSS). Fix: add an optional `filters?: VideoFilters` to `ImageWidgetParams` / `VideoWidgetParams`, surface a Filters section in `WIDGET_INSPECTOR.image` / `.video`, fuse the widget's filter into the rendered `filter:` CSS on its container, and pipe through timeline-emit so renders match. Unblocks: per-image / per-video colour-grade without affecting siblings. |
| 597 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **No automated tests for the inspector schema registry or motion timing** (2026-05-13) | Untested invariants worth pinning before they regress: (a) `WIDGET_INSPECTOR` has an entry for every `WidgetKind` (catches a new kind whose UI silently drops to zero sections); (b) every per-kind Content section actually keys off its widget's `params.kind` (the early-return guards exist but aren't enforced); (c) `motionStyleAt` returns `null` outside `[visibleFrom, visibleTo]`, IDENTITY when motion is null, and crosses through the `presence=1` midpoint when `t=duration` for fade; (d) round-trip `canvasStateToTimeline → timelineToCanvasState` preserves `widget.motion` for every motion kind. Unblocks: confident schema extension without manually clicking through the UI. |
| 658 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Two ways to spell "particles" in V2: bg-encoded `BgPreset.value="particles:#color"` AND the registry `{kind:"particles"}` scene/widget effect now both render via the same `drawParticleField` helper** (2026-05-15) | After [particle-field.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/timeline/effects/particle-field.ts) consolidation, the visual result is identical for both encodings, but `BG_PRESETS` in [visual-themes.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/visual-themes.ts) still ships a "Particles" preset whose `value` writes to `Scene.backgroundEffect` — a parallel surface to the registry effect. Pick one path: either keep the bg-encoding (delete the registry `particles` kind from the picker) or delete the bg-encoding (migrate the BG_PRESETS Particles entry to instead write `{backgroundColor: solidColor, effects: [{kind:"particles", params:{color}}]}` and rip out the `case "particles"` branch in [paintRichBackground](hired.video/frontend/lib/timeline/effects/canvas-v2.ts) + the `particles` decode case in `decodeBackgroundValue`). Fixing collapses the duplication and unblocks the same approach for `dark-tech-grid` (next on the bg-encoded list). |
| 662 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **No SEO sitemap / OG worker consumes `metaDescription` / `keywords` / `slug` / `socialCardImage` yet** (2026-05-16 — Details drawer landing) | The Details drawer ([ProjectDetailsSheet.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/shared/ProjectDetailsSheet.tsx)) writes through `studioService.saveDraft` into `storyboard._metaDescription` / `_slug` / `_keywords` / `_socialCardImage` and `toProjectDto` surfaces them. Today no downstream worker reads them — public video pages still emit a default `<meta>` block and there's no `/sitemap.xml` for studio videos. Fix: add `frontend/workers/sitemap.ts` (or extend the existing pages worker) to enumerate `isPublic` projects + render `<meta>` + an `<urlset>` from these fields. Unblocks: Google / LinkedIn previews actually using the values the user typed. |
| 686 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **YouTube-branch `/v/:id` videos don't fire `timeupdate` so CTA hot-zones never light up** (2026-05-16 — surfaced while closing #681) | The new `CtaHotzonesOverlay` requires a `currentTimeSec` stream from the player; the URL branch wires it to `<video>.onTimeUpdate` but the YouTube `<iframe>` branch in [VideoPlayer.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/VideoPlayer.tsx) emits nothing (the basic embed has no API). Result: a project published to YouTube and viewed via the embed shows the baked CTA as pixels but the overlay never matches a time window, so it stays invisible. Fix: load YouTube IFrame Player API, expose its `onStateChange` + `getCurrentTime()` poll loop via a `youtubeRef` prop equivalent, OR fall back to using the linked CDN MP4 URL whenever both are present (most accurate; YouTube becomes the secondary publish destination, not the player). Unblocks: CTAs convert on the YouTube embed path too. |
| 689 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Slot binders missing for job_ad / company_promo / sizzle_reel / code_walkthrough / data_analysis / design_portfolio / tool_promo** (2026-05-16 — surfaced while closing #688) | `TEMPLATE_SLOTS` in [template-content-slots.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/template-content-slots.ts) only declares bindings for 4 of 12 templates. The CHRO can still open the other 8 from chat, but the hydrated canvas keeps the seed's `[bracket]` placeholders because the slot map is empty for those template ids. Fix per template: `job_ad`/`company_promo` need an owned-Job / owned-Company picker (extend `UserContentSnapshot` with `jobs[]`/`companies[]` + a picker arg on the tool); `sizzle_reel` needs a clip picker over `studio_projects` the user already owns; `code_walkthrough`/`design_portfolio`/`data_analysis`/`tool_promo` need a project-meta picker (linked GitHub / Behance / dataset / tool from the catalog). Unblocks: "make me a job ad for my Senior PM role" filling in title, hook, benefits from the actual posting. |
| 694 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **#477 + #478 closures landed in V1 surfaces (`VideoPreview`, `StoryboardEditor`, `StudioSidebar`)** (2026-05-16 — surfaced during studio architecture review) | The two audio bug fixes kept (debounced `clipsKey` in `VideoPreview`, `getActiveMusicLabel` helper consumed by StoryboardEditor + StudioSidebar) all sit on V1 surfaces that #639 will delete. The reusable pieces (the helper itself, the debounce pattern) survive the cull as standalone modules under `lib/audio/*`; the call sites disappear with V1. Tracked here so the V1 cull doesn't get caught off-guard removing what it thinks is dead code — and so a future V2 audio preview consumer (#559 / #560 / #567) wires through the same helper rather than re-implementing the label resolution. Unblocks: nothing on its own — this is a tracking entry for cull-time visibility. |
| 715 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`ResumeInputTabs` still client-ships full resume JSON when a saved resume is selected — same anti-pattern just fixed on `ResumeAnalysisToolPage`** (2026-05-16 — surfaced while fixing Resume Optimizer saved-resume payload) | [ResumeInputTabs.tsx:82-88](hired.video/frontend/components/ResumeInputTabs.tsx#L82-L88) + [ResumeInputTabs.tsx:136-142](hired.video/frontend/components/ResumeInputTabs.tsx#L136-L142) still call `resumeService.getResumeById(id)` and JSON.stringify the entire content into `resumeText` before handing it to consumers. Every page that mounts the widget (Job-Resume Match, Resume Tailor, Skill Extractor, Resume Roast, Resume Consolidator, etc.) then forwards that bloated body to its respective API. Fix: extend `ResumeInputValue` to allow `{ resumeId, source: "existing" }` without a precomputed `resumeText`, and have each consumer endpoint resolve the id server-side via the shared [resolve-resume-content.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/resume/resolve-resume-content.ts) helper (the one Resume Scorer + Optimizer now use). Unblocks: smaller request bodies, no server trust in a client-supplied resume snapshot, and one canonical "how does the analyze surface read a saved resume?" path. |
| 794 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **`/studio` owned-template cards have no edit / republish / delete affordances** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced building the owned-template surface; updated 2026-05-17 after the section was consolidated into the unified Templates carousel) | `OwnedTemplateCard` only exposes Use + Preview. Created-by-me rows have no way to rename, change visibility, or archive from `/studio` — the user has to open the side-sheet `CreatorTemplatesPanel` for any of that. Spec: when `provenance === 'created'`, surface a hover Edit (rename / visibility / price) + Delete affordance on the card. Pairs with #793 so we consolidate to one surface. Unblocks: managing a created template without leaving `/studio`. |
| 824 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Pre-existing TS error in `LinkedContentBody.tsx:273` — `<Icon>` prop type rejects `style` attr** (opened 2026-05-18 — surfaced during final typecheck after SP architecture pass) | [frontend/components/studio/v2/LinkedContentBody.tsx:273](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/LinkedContentBody.tsx#L273) passes `{ className, style: { color: ... } }` to an icon component whose props type is `IntrinsicAttributes & { className?: string }` — TS2322. Unrelated to the SP refactor (file not touched). Likely a lucide-react vs `IconType` typing drift introduced by an unrelated linter edit. Fix: either tighten the icon prop type to accept `style`, or move the colour onto `className`/CSS-var. Unblocks: clean frontend typecheck. |
| 854 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Marketplace-template thumbnail can be uploaded / picked from stock / generated by AI, but cannot be snapshotted from the current canvas frame the creator is staring at** (opened 2026-05-19 — same pass) | [PublishAsTemplateDialog](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/PublishAsTemplateDialog.tsx) + [CreatorTemplatesPanel](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/CreatorTemplatesPanel.tsx) now both wire `<MediaPicker accept="image" />` for thumbnail selection (Upload + Stock + AI tabs), which closes the "no way to set a thumbnail" gap. The natural fourth source — "Use current canvas frame" — would let a V2 creator snapshot the composition they already designed in one click instead of re-rendering and uploading. Implementation: capture the canvas-v2 `<CanvasStage>` via `html2canvas` (or a direct read off the existing 2D canvas if all widgets paint to it) → upload via `uploadImage` → preselect as the thumbnail. Gated on V2 only because V1 has no canvas to snapshot. Unblocks: lower-friction publishing for the most common case (creator just finished a design they're happy with). |
| 855 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **No user-facing toggle to hide [SafeZoneOverlay](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/SafeZoneOverlay.tsx) on the V2 authoring canvas — guides are always on when the active format declares safe zones** (opened 2026-05-19 — deferred polish from the aspect-presets + safe-zone step that landed today) | Safe-zone dashed overlays are presentation-only and pointer-event-disabled, but a user composing a tricky widget cluster near the bottom-25% TikTok caption band may still want a clean visual surface. Fix: add a `showSafeZones: boolean` field to a new localStorage-backed `useStudioGuides()` hook (mirrors the [useEditorPreference](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/preferences.ts) pattern), expose a "Show safe zones" checkbox in the inspector's `canvas-format` section, and have [SafeZoneOverlay](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/SafeZoneOverlay.tsx) self-gate on the hook (DRY rule — consumers always mount it, the hook decides visibility). Also covers a parallel "Show grid" / "Show rulers" toggle family that will land alongside the keyframe-track work. Out of scope for the current pass but cheap to add when the next guide feature lands. |
| 856 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Safe zones only declared on landscape-1080p + portrait-1080p — 720p, 4K, and square presets are unzoned** (opened 2026-05-19 — deferred from the safe-zone pass) | The three new billboard presets (4:1, 6:1, 1:2) carry the shared `BLEED_SAFE_ZONE` (5% bleed) which is correct for outdoor mounting. The remaining six "social" formats are unzoned — 720p + 4K landscape / portrait should share the same SMPTE action-safe / platform-UI zones their 1080p siblings carry (destination is identical, just rasterised at a different resolution). Fix: lift the zone descriptor onto a `(aspect → SafeZone[])` table in [video-formats.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/video-formats.ts) and apply by aspect, dropping the per-format `safeZones` field in favour of a derived lookup. That's the right DRY shape; the current per-format declarations are a placeholder while the catalog has only two zoned formats. |
| 866 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Resume templates are not surfaced on the public profile's per-program tab strip — only studio templates appear (inside the Video tab)** (opened 2026-05-19 — surfaced while shipping the per-program tab refactor on `/people/:slug`) | The new [`ProfileProgramPanel`](hired.video/frontend/components/profile/sections/programs/ProfileProgramPanel.tsx) renders one tab per active creator program (video / voice / services / articles / courses) and the Video tab also lists [`studioTemplatesService.listPublicByCreator`](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/studio-templates-service.ts). Resume templates published by the same creator (template-marketplace at `/search?category=templates` — `template_licenses.templateKind="resume"`) are NOT surfaced anywhere on the profile. Fix: (a) add an authored-by-user endpoint mirroring the studio one (the `resumes` table already carries author identity; just filter `template_kind = 'resume'` + `isPublic`), (b) surface inside the Video tab as a second section ("Resume templates") OR introduce a top-level Templates tab when `studioTemplates.length + resumeTemplates.length > 0`. Pairs with [project_template_marketplace.md](C:/Users/seanh/.claude/projects/c--code-hired/memory/project_template_marketplace.md) memory — resume templates exist today but have no per-creator surface. Unblocks: creators selling resume templates can drive purchases from their profile. |
| 883 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`HeroVideoSpotlight` empty-state placeholder still hard-codes the "Your video resumes land here" / "Be one of the first creators" copy via `messages.videoResumesLandHere` + `messages.beOneOfFirstCreators` but renders identically for visitors and signed-in users** (opened 2026-05-20 — surfaced while reviewing mobile rendering) | [HeroVideoSpotlight.tsx:189-204](hired.video/frontend/components/HeroVideoSpotlight.tsx#L189-L204) renders the same empty-state card for everyone when there are no SA-curated featured videos AND no real video on the fallback skeleton. A signed-in creator who hasn't published yet sees the same "Be one of the first creators" pitch as an anonymous visitor — for the creator it should be a one-click "Record your first video resume" CTA pointing at `/studio`, for the visitor it should keep the signup nudge. The component already navigates to `/studio` on its primary CTA below, so the empty-state center pitch should branch on auth. Cheap fix: read `useAuth()`, branch the inner two `<p>` lines + add a play-arrow that doubles as the Studio link when authed. Unblocks: stronger creator-onboarding CTA on the empty hero state for the population most likely to convert (logged-in but unpublished). |
| 902 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Sizzle Reel is audience-agnostic — generic onset scoring + 4-scene generic seed; no slow-mo / play detection for athletes, no role-chips / section-breaks for actors, no setlist / venue chips for musicians, no agent / coach / booking end-card** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced evaluating Sizzle Reel improvements per audience) | [SizzleReelIntake.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/intake/SizzleReelIntake.tsx) uses generic onset scoring ([highlight-scoring.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/sizzle/highlight-scoring.ts)) and a 4-scene generic seed (Open / Cut / Testimonial / Build, [template-seeds.ts:532-568](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/template-seeds.ts#L532-L568)). Athletes need slow-mo / play detection (motion-energy spikes ≠ best play) and jersey-# / position / season chips; actors need per-clip role / project chips + TV / Film / Theater section breaks + agent contact CTA (overlaps with `showreel` but they share the engine); musicians need beats exposed as setlist / venue chips + streaming-link end-card; directors need DP / cinematographer reel structure (chronological vs. style-grouped). Add `audience` selector to `SizzleReelIntake` (defaults from `?audience=…` query param set by #900's landing CTA) that swaps (a) scoring weights, (b) seed scene set, (c) end-card metadata fields. Activates after #899's audience taxonomy. Pairs with #903 for net-new audience-specific templates that don't fit a Sizzle structure (athlete-recruit needs stat lower-thirds Sizzle can't host). |
| 911 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **Clearing the Slug field in `ProjectDetailsSheet` silently diverges UI state from the server** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced fixing the social-card-image clear bug) | Today's pass accepted empty string in the `slug` validator at [studio.ts:1149](hired.video/api/src/routes/studio.ts#L1149) (was rejecting `""` with a misleading "slug must be kebab-case" error), so the save no longer 400s. The existing server resolver at [studio.ts:1199-1218](hired.video/api/src/routes/studio.ts#L1199-L1218) treats `slug === ""` as "carry forward `priorMeta._slug`" — correct, because a public video can't have an empty slug — but [ProjectDetailsSheet.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/shared/ProjectDetailsSheet.tsx) keeps its local form state at `""` after the autosave returns. The `onChange(res.data)` callback flows the resolved slug back to the parent, but the seed-from-project effect only re-runs on `[project?.id, open]` change — so the input remains empty in the UI while the persisted row still has the prior slug. Fix: either re-seed the form state from `res.data` after each successful save, OR explicitly reject `""` with a user-friendly "slug can't be empty" toast and let the user re-enter one. Unblocks: the Details drawer state matching what's actually persisted. |
| 920 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`public/sitemap.xml` hand-lists 14 audience routes + 20 template routes — drifts every time `AUDIENCES` or `TEMPLATE_CATALOG` changes** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced shipping #900 + #901 first cuts) | The sitemap entries for `/for/:audience` and `/templates/:slug` are static XML in [public/sitemap.xml](hired.video/frontend/public/sitemap.xml) but the source-of-truth registries — [audiences.ts](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/audiences.ts) and [TEMPLATE_CATALOG](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/catalog.tsx) — are TypeScript. Add a new template / audience and you must remember to hand-edit the sitemap, or its SEO ages out silently. Per the standing DRY rule the registries should be the single source. Fix: a Vite build-time plugin (or a one-shot `scripts/generate-sitemap.ts` invoked from `package.json` `prebuild`) that imports both registries, merges them with the existing hand-maintained legal / blog / tool entries, and writes the full XML to `public/sitemap.xml` on every build. Pairs with the hand-maintained `<lastmod>` field — the generator can stamp current date so freshness is honest. Unblocks: every new template / audience auto-indexes without a manual sitemap PR. |
| 922 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Landing-page heros are placeholders — `/templates/:slug` uses a Lucide icon in a colored box; `/for/:audience` is label + blurb only with no audience imagery** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced shipping #900 + #901 first cuts; consolidates the "audience-specific hero artwork" + "hero video render" follow-ons noted on #900 + #901) | [TemplateLandingPage.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/landing/TemplateLandingPage.tsx) renders `<Icon className="h-12 w-12" />` inside a `bg-primary/10` square; [AudienceLandingPage.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/landing/AudienceLandingPage.tsx) renders `AUDIENCES[slug].label` + `.blurb` over a gradient with no imagery. Per #901's original spec, the template hero should render the template's seed canvas (from [template-seeds.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/template-seeds.ts) via `seedCanvasFromTemplate`) as a static PNG at build time (cacheable, CDN-able, fast) or as a `<canvas>` clientside on first paint. Audience hero should carry an audience-specific hero image or a per-kind illustration mix. Bundle the fix with new `heroCopy?: string` + `heroImageUrl?: string` fields on `AudienceDef` (the field was foreshadowed in [audiences.ts:36-40](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/audiences.ts) as "added by #900 — a separate `heroCopy` field will join this registry then" — this IS that follow-on). Depends on #921 (TemplateThumb cases) only if the hero falls back to TemplateThumb for missing canvas renders. Unblocks: marketing pages that look like marketing pages, not placeholders. |
| 925 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **`ActionsPanel.LeftPanelSection` ordering is video-shaped — audio-only kinds would benefit from "Recording & Audio" being the first / only-expanded section, with Media + AI Tools + Engagement collapsed by default** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced wiring #924's kind-aware editor defaults) | [ActionsPanel.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/ActionsPanel.tsx) renders 5 sections in a fixed order (Recording & Audio → Media → AI Tools → Engagement → Advisory). The collapsible state is persisted per-section via `useCollapsibleSections("studio.v2.left.actions.sections")` — but the defaults are kind-agnostic. After #924's auto-arm wires the user into the Voiceover sheet, they still see "Media" and "AI Tools" expanded below — most of which (image upload, AI rewrite, AI headshot) doesn't apply to an audio-only project. Fix: extend `deriveKindDefaults` with a `sectionPriority: Record<SectionId, "expanded" \| "collapsed">` field that the `useCollapsibleSections` initial state reads. For audio-only kinds, expand Recording & Audio + collapse Media / AI Tools by default; user toggles still persist on top of that baseline. Pairs with #923's voice-specific intake — if the Voiceover sheet is the primary surface, the rest of the rail can stay tucked away. Unblocks: audio-only project rail reads as "this is where you record" instead of a kitchen-sink menu. |
| 941 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **WebGPU client-side image-gen engine (`webgpu-sd-turbo`) — registration slot exists in `image-gen-engine.ts` but `isAvailable()` returns false today because transformers.js v3 has no text-to-image pipeline** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced while wiring #932 Phase 1; the user's web-first / server-fallback ordering is enforced by the engine registry today but the WEB side is a stub) | The engine ordering in [image-gen-engine.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/image-gen-engine.ts) is `webgpu-sd-turbo` → `server-cf-sdxl-lightning` so the moment a real WebGPU implementation lands the entire app flips primary engine without a single call-site change (DRY). What's missing: transformers.js v3 doesn't expose a `text-to-image` pipeline (same constraint the headshot generator hit — see `headshot-engine.ts:3-24`). Two close paths: (a) wait for transformers.js to ship the pipeline + register the body; (b) port web-stable-diffusion or `wonnx`-backed SD-Turbo directly (~1.5GB model, cached after first download). Either way the work is a self-contained `engine.generate()` body — the facade, the call sites, and the cost-saving "no server roundtrip" UX win all already exist on the seam. |
| 942 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **V1 callers (`StoryboardEditor`, `SceneElementsGallery`) still call `studioService.generateImage` directly — won't benefit from the WebGPU primary when it lands** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced wiring #932; V1 is being deleted per [project_v1_deprecation](hired.video/.claude/projects/c--code-hired/memory/project_v1_deprecation.md), so the right fix is to let V1 die rather than migrate it) | Both files import + call `studioService.generateImage(prompt)` directly. The pluggable engine facade (`image-gen-engine.ts`'s `generateImage()`) is the post-#932 SoT — MediaPicker has been migrated. The V1 callers are intentionally NOT migrated because: (a) V1 is on the deletion path; (b) V1's "AI image" UX hardcodes `imageUrl` semantics the WebGPU engine can't satisfy (it returns a Blob, no durable URL). When V1 is finally deleted the parallel `studioService.generateImage` call sites die with it; until then they're frozen pointing at the server path. Action: delete on V1 deletion pass (no work needed here). |
| 944 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **`api/src/routes/studio.ts:947-949` — `row.firstName / row.lastName / row.bio` referenced on a `userProfiles` row that doesn't have those columns (schema drift; typecheck-breaking pre-existing error)** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced running `npm run typecheck` after #932 closure; the failure pre-dates the image work) | The route's `loadProfileFlat()` helper at [studio.ts:940-951](hired.video/api/src/routes/studio.ts#L940-L951) selects from `userProfiles` and reads `row.firstName / row.lastName / row.bio` — but the `userProfiles` Drizzle schema only declares `headline / summary / location / website / phone / linkedIn / github / twitter / currentRole / currentCompany / …` (no name or bio columns). Identity fields live on the `users` table. The error is silent at runtime because the result is just empty-string concatenation, but `tsc --noEmit` blocks on six `TS2339`s. Fix: either (a) JOIN `users` and read names from there + replace `bio` with `summary` (which IS on userProfiles), or (b) add `firstName / lastName / bio` columns to userProfiles via a migration if the original intent was for those to live there. Unblocks: green API typecheck. |
| 952 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Recruiter / employer pricing copy still mentions "Video resume screening" verbatim — once recruiters can screen comic / podcast resumes too, those bullets need updating** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced closing #951; recruiter-side screening is video-only today, so the copy is accurate but will drift when #937's consumer-side comic / podcast playback ships on the recruiter ATS) | Three call-sites carry video-only screening copy: [Pricing.tsx:218](hired.video/frontend/pages/Pricing.tsx#L218) (recruiter Pro feature bullet "Video resume screening & transcript search"), [Pricing.tsx:237](hired.video/frontend/pages/Pricing.tsx#L237) (employer Pro feature bullet), [Pricing.tsx:1319-1320](hired.video/frontend/pages/Pricing.tsx#L1319) (recruiter table row "Video resume transcript search"). These accurately describe what recruiters can screen TODAY (video resumes via the transcript search feature). When #937 lands and the recruiter ATS can play comic / podcast / game submissions, update the bullets to "Multi-format submission screening (video transcripts, comic captions, podcast transcripts)". Two i18n keys still carry video-only language: `labels.videoStudio` + `marketing.pricing.section.aiVideoStudio` in `en.json` / `es.json`. |
| 955 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **`TemplateThumb` switch still misses 15 cases — 3 image (drawing_blank, drawing_social_square, drawing_og_card) + 12 comic genres (comic_hero / comic_noir / comic_scifi / comic_fantasy / comic_romance / comic_slice / comic_manga / comic_horror / comic_comedy / comic_retro80s / comic_webtoon / comic_adventure)** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced shipping #900/#901 second pass; #921 covered film+podcast+voice but image+comic landed after that close) | [TemplateThumb.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/TemplateThumb.tsx) now covers 27 cases through `memory_match` but every image + comic template falls through to `undefined` → blank rounded-box thumbnail. Affects every surface that mounts the card: [StudioLanding.tsx `BuiltinTemplateCard`](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx) (chooser), [StudioTemplateLinkCard.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/StudioTemplateLinkCard.tsx) (`/for/:audience` + `/templates/:slug` marketing grids), `NewVideoSplitButton` (chooser dropdown). Fix mirrors #921's pattern: 15 mock-slide CSS+SVG cases — drawing templates get an artboard / brush stroke / OG-card framing visual; comic genres reuse the per-genre palette already declared in [comic-genres.ts](hired.video/shared/comic-genres.ts) (each genre has a `palette` field) to render a tiny 4-panel layout swatch. Each case ~10 lines of JSX. Comic case could be generated programmatically from `COMIC_GENRES.map(...)` to stay DRY with the catalog-generation pattern. Unblocks: visually consistent template grids across in-app + marketing surfaces, especially #900's audience pages where image + comic templates dominate the illustrator-audience grid. |
| 974 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Reuse Video's animation / motion / transition system for game sprites — fade-in, slide-in, scale, easings exist on `MotionPreset` for Timeline kinds but don't apply to game sprite behaviors** (opened 2026-05-23 — user reframe: "Lots of animations etc from the Video can be applied to games.") | Timeline kinds carry rich animation via the V2 editor's motion presets (minimal / moderate / cinematic) + per-widget enter / exit transitions; the Game runtime today has none of this — sprites just appear in place and start running their behavior. To close: (a) Extract a runtime-agnostic `AnimationSpec` (`{ kind: "fade-in" \| "slide-in" \| "scale-up" \| ..., durationMs, easing }`) from the Timeline-side motion code. (b) Add `onMount: AnimationSpec` to `GameSprite` so a sprite can fade in / slide in when its level mounts. (c) Add the same to `GameLevel.transitionIn` so the level itself fades in. (d) Implement the interpreter in `runtime-core.js` — a per-sprite `mountTs` plus an easing lookup feeds an alpha / offset / scale multiplier applied in `drawFrame`. Same SoT pattern as behaviors: editor inspector picks the preset, runtime interprets identically. Single source benefits: a polish pass on Video transitions ripples into games for free. Pairs with #973 (block scripts could also drive animations) + #939 (Phaser has its own tween library — when Phaser swaps in, the spec stays the same but the implementation moves to Phaser's tweener). |
| 988 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Contract tests for paid-media adapters — pin platform request payload shapes against vendor mock servers** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #975) | Each adapter in [services/paid-media/adapters/](hired.video/api/src/services/paid-media/adapters/) makes specific REST request shapes (field names, units like cents-vs-micros, status enum values). A platform API drift would break us silently because we have no contract test. To close: write a `__tests__/contract.test.ts` per adapter that captures the request payload via a mock fetch and asserts the exact JSON shape against a fixture file. When a platform changes their API surface, the fixture diff highlights it. Use a single shared `mockAdapterFetch(platform)` helper so the assertion style is identical across all 5 adapters. Doesn't need real vendor credentials; runs offline in CI. |
| 1005 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Animation publish backends — `giphy`, `tenor`, `r2-host` publish-destination buttons render in [StudioSaveMenuV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/StudioSaveMenuV2.tsx) (lines 74–76) but no `publishHandlers` body exists for any of them; clicking either button does nothing or surfaces a "not implemented" toast** (opened 2026-05-23 — full studio-gap audit) | Mirror of the #939 / #1008 problem on the game side: the dispatcher seam is wired (icons + labels in the menu) but the actual API integrations aren't. To close: (a) **Giphy upload API** — `https://upload.giphy.com/v1/gifs` accepts a GIF blob + API key + tags; backend route `/api/studio/publish/giphy` proxies the upload (keep the API key server-side). (b) **Tenor upload** — Tenor's API doesn't accept third-party uploads at the regular API tier; investigate Tenor Partner Program OR remove the destination. (c) **R2 host link** — uploads the GIF/WebP to R2 under `studio/animations/<projectId>.gif`, returns a short shareable URL — this one is fully buildable from the existing R2 client; no third-party OAuth needed. (d) Add `GIPHY_API_KEY` env binding + secret rotation; add the route + service layer. Tenor decision (build vs drop) is a product call. Pairs with #1004 — none of these matter until the encoders produce a real GIF blob. |
| 1008 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **itch.io / GitHub Pages / `game-web-embed` publish handler bodies still stubs — the dispatcher seam in [StudioSaveMenuV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/StudioSaveMenuV2.tsx) is wired (icons + entries for `itch-io` / `github-pages` / `game-web-embed`) but #939's closure note explicitly deferred them as "external-credential plumbing"** (opened 2026-05-23 — full studio-gap audit; reopens the deferred slice of #939) | #939 closed with the user directive "stop creating Open Gaps" but called out itch.io + GitHub Pages publish handlers as blocked on OAuth setup (Butler API key, GitHub OAuth app) — i.e. NOT actually implementable from a stateless code pass without per-tenant credentials. The user has now framed all-up "close the studio gaps" as a real requirement. To close: (a) **itch.io** — itch.io's Butler tool is the canonical upload path (no OAuth — uses a per-user API key the user pastes into Profile→Integrations). Backend route `/api/studio/publish/itch` accepts the bundle blob + project slug + the user's stored API key from `user_integration_credentials` (new table or extend existing oauth_credentials) and pipes it to Butler over the Butler push protocol. (b) **GitHub Pages** — register the existing GitHub OAuth app (already on the platform for other purposes? — audit), grant `repo` scope, push the bundled HTML5 ZIP to a `gh-pages` branch on a user-named repo via the GitHub REST API. (c) **`game-web-embed`** — uploads the bundle to R2 under `studio/games/<projectId>/index.html` + bundled assets; returns the embeddable `<iframe>` URL. This third one needs no third-party credentials; ship it first. Per the project memory: hired.video deliberately does NOT do BYOK for API keys — re-evaluate the itch.io key-paste UX against that posture; the platform's posture may force this destination to be platform-app-owned rather than user-keyed. |
| 1010 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Game audio surface — the `play-sound` block action exists in [game-state.ts](hired.video/shared/game-state.ts) line 150 but no editor wiring, no sound library, no music tracks, no per-asset volume / loop / spatial-audio controls. Authors can't attach a jump-sound to a sprite, a level-music loop to a level, or a victory-sting to a transition** (opened 2026-05-23 — full studio-gap audit) | Block-action layer declares the intent but the runtime + editor are missing the supporting surface. To close: (a) **Asset kind expansion** — `GameAsset.kind` already supports `"audio"` but the SpritePalette / MediaPicker flow doesn't surface audio-pickable. Add an Audio tab to the game's `<MediaPicker>` mount + the stock-audio library wired the same way the video stock-music library (Pixabay Music + Mixkit per #283) will be when M3 lands. (b) **Level-music slot** — `GameLevel.backgroundMusic?: { assetId, loop, volume }`. Runtime starts on level mount + stops on level unmount. (c) **Sprite SFX slots** — `GameSprite.sfx?: { onMount, onCollide, onDespawn }`. (d) **Volume controls** — game-wide master volume + per-asset volume override. (e) **Implement `play-sound` in the runtime** — the action shape exists but `executeActions` in runtime-core.js needs to actually `new Audio()` (or use the WebAudio API for low-latency) the asset and play it. Currently `play-sound` is in the type but unimplemented in the runtime's switch. Pairs with #1009 (Phaser's audio mixer would solve a lot of this for free if track (a) chosen there). |
| 1011 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Game HUD primitives — no built-in score counter, lives counter, timer overlay, or game-state variables panel. Today authors have to fake these with sprites + `set-message`, which paints a 2-second pill instead of a persistent HUD** (opened 2026-05-23 — full studio-gap audit) | Casual games (the genre the studio actually targets) lean on score / lives / timer HUDs. The runtime has no concept of game-state variables; the editor has no HUD layout surface. To close: (a) **Variables on `GameState`** — `variables: Record<string, number | string>` populated from initial values + mutated by block scripts (`change score by 10`, `set lives to 3`). Required for #1007's Snap variables primitive too. (b) **HUD overlay primitive** — `GameLevel.hud?: HudWidget[]` where each widget is `{ kind: "score" | "lives" | "timer" | "text" | "image", binding: variableName, position, font, color }`. (c) **Runtime paints HUD AFTER sprites + overlays** in `drawFrame` (per the layer order in #1006). (d) **Editor: HUD inspector** mounted when the level is selected + no sprite selected. (e) **Built-in `score` / `lives` / `timer` variables** seeded by default — block actions `add-score / lose-life / start-timer / stop-timer` ship as built-ins so non-coders don't need to manually declare them. Pairs with #1006 (HUD widgets ARE overlays — could share the overlay shape) and #1007 (variable primitive). |
| 1012 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Game runtime is keyboard / mouse only — [runtime-core.js](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/game/runtime-core.js) attaches `keydown` / `keyup` / `pointerdown` listeners but no `touchstart` / `touchmove` / `touchend` and no gamepad polling. Mobile users opening a published game on a phone get a non-functional control surface** (opened 2026-05-23 — full studio-gap audit) | hired.video's profile-attached games will be played in mobile browsers — possibly most of the time. To close: (a) **Touch handlers** — `touchstart` / `touchmove` / `touchend` mapped to the same hit-test path that drives `pointerdown` for sprite clicks; passive: false so the runtime can `preventDefault()` to stop scroll. (b) **Virtual D-pad / button overlay** — toggleable on small screens; a 4-direction touch D-pad + 1–2 action buttons painted as a HUD layer (reuses #1011) that re-emits as the same `BlockTrigger { kind: "on-key-press", key: "ArrowLeft" }` so authored block logic doesn't fork by input modality. (c) **Gamepad API polling** — every frame check `navigator.getGamepads()` + map axis / buttons to keyboard equivalents (Steam Big Picture / Xbox controller users). (d) **Auto-detect input** — on first touch / first gamepad-button-press, hide the alternate UI. Pairs with #1006 (HUD overlay primitive) — the virtual D-pad is just a special-case overlay. |
| 1020 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Legacy view tables (`resume_views` / `profile_views` / `company_views` / `studio_video_heatmap`) are now read-redundant once `artifact_views` is the source of truth (#1019 L1). They stayed intact for the bake window so existing readers (`computeViewerExtras` / `getResumesViewerStats` / dashboard.ts profileViews query / profileStats.ts query / studio-features.ts heatmap GET) keep working unchanged. After verifying the new `/api/analytics/artifacts/*` paths cover every read path, drop the legacy tables in one migration** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1019 closure) | To close: (a) Audit every caller of `recordResumeView` / `recordCompanyView` / `insertView` and confirm the corresponding read has moved to `artifact_views` (the dual-write stays; only the legacy READ has to be migrated). (b) Migrate `resume_views`-backed view-count queries in `ResumeRepository.countViews` / `countViewsBulk` to count from `artifact_views WHERE artifact_kind='resume'`. (c) Repoint `dashboard.ts` + `profileStats.ts` profile-view queries to `artifact_views WHERE artifact_kind='profile'`. (d) Repoint `studio-features.ts /analytics/projects/:id` reads to `artifact_views WHERE artifact_kind='video'` and delete the legacy heatmap-specific aggregation code. (e) Drop tables: `resume_views`, `profile_views`, `company_views`, `studio_video_heatmap`. (f) Drop the dual-write call paths in `recordResumeView` (legacy `repo.insertView`) + `companies.ts` (`recordCompanyView`) + `studio-features.ts /analytics/track` (legacy `studioVideoHeatmap` insert). Pairs with #1021 (profile_views legacy table had no insert site — already inert; just need the read drop). |
| 1023 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Animated WebP / APNG / VP9-alpha encoders for the animation kind — currently the `animation-webp` / `animation-apng` / `animation-mp4-alpha` output profiles fall back to MediaRecorder/WebM** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside the #1004 partial closure) | [animation-export.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/animation/animation-export.ts) `encodeViaMediaRecorder` routes the three non-GIF profiles to a WebM/VP9 recording of the frame strip. Output file mime preserves the user-picked container so the file extension stays correct, but the actual bytes are WebM — not animated WebP / APNG / VP9-alpha. To close: (a) **Animated WebP** — vendor a minimal WebP-VP8L encoder or wait for ffmpeg.wasm to land (#286) and route through `libwebp`. (b) **APNG** — write a focused encoder (PNG header + IHDR + acTL + per-frame fcTL/IDAT/fdAT + IEND + zlib-deflate payload using `CompressionStream`) — ~250 lines doable in-tree. (c) **VP9-alpha** — ffmpeg.wasm `-c:v libvpx-vp9 -pix_fmt yuva420p` once the strategy is wired (note: the `animation-mp4-alpha` profile's declared `h265` codec doesn't survive in-browser; consider switching the profile to VP9-alpha-in-WebM as the practical implementation). Until then the export pipeline produces a valid file but not the format the user picked. |
| 1102 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Marquee tool only supports RECTANGULAR selections — Photoshop-parity needs lasso + magic wand + quick-select** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #1100) | Rect covers ~70% of selection use cases. Each non-rect selection fits the existing engine pattern: `selectLassoPath` / `selectMagicWand` / `selectEdgeAware` — all returning a 1-bit mask the existing `clearRectOnLayer` / `fillRectOnLayer` ops can intersect with. Add `MarqueeSelection` (rect | path | mask) so the action chips work regardless of selection shape. Pairs with #1100. |
| 1103 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **AI inpaint-with-selection — when a marquee is active, the AI prompt should fill ONLY the selected area instead of generating a full new image** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #1100) | Partially closed in #1100 (Replace active layer toggle); next refinement is mask-aware inpaint. Cloudflare Workers AI doesn't expose inpaint today; would route through Replicate / OpenAI gpt-image-1 edit endpoint. Client clears the masked area + draws the AI result inside the mask. Pairs with #1100 + #1102. |
| 1141 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Two legacy `VideoAnalyticsDashboard` call sites still default `mediaKind` to "video" because the consumer only has `projectId` in scope** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1137) | [`VideoAnalyticsSheet.tsx`](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/VideoAnalyticsSheet.tsx) and [`V2AdvisoryDialogs.tsx`](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/V2AdvisoryDialogs.tsx) mount `<VideoAnalyticsDashboard projectId={…}/>` without a `mediaKind` prop, so the wrapper falls back to "video" (same as pre-#1137). For a non-video studio project mounted from V2 the analytics axis copy is wrong (says "Watch Time" for a banner project). To close: (a) thread `mediaKind` from the V2 editor host into `<V2AdvisoryDialogs/>` and forward it down — same shape ProjectDetailsSheet uses post-#1137 — OR (b) make `VideoAnalyticsDashboard` itself fetch the project via `studioService.getProject(projectId)` to resolve the kind, trading a network call for caller simplicity. (a) is preferable since the V2 editor already has the project in state. Pairs with #1137. |
| 1694 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **`GET /api/users/:id/stats` returns hardcoded zeros (`resumeCount`/`connectionCount`/`jobApplicationCount`)** (opened 2026-05-28 while fixing #1021). [users.ts:872-882](hired.video/api/src/routes/users.ts#L872) is a stub that never queries. [getProfileStats](hired.video/api/src/services/profile/profileStats.ts) already computes these counts, but returning its full result would leak owner-only data (`totalViews` + `recentViewers`) to any caller. **Fix**: return only the public count subset (resume/connection/application) to non-owners, or owner-gate the full stats and reuse the SSoT. **Unblocks**: real counts on public profile surfaces without a privacy regression. |
| 1811 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`traceId` is only echoed on the two AI routes that return a `usage` object (chat + course-generate); the larger set of AI-backed routes that return only content (resume tailor/roast/optimize, match insights, interview prep, studio storyboard, career360, article writer, etc.) don't surface it** (opened 2026-05-30 alongside #1810). `toClientUsage` is the single seam, but those routes discard `usage` entirely and return just the generated artifact, so there's no support-quotable trace on the most-used AI surfaces. Fix: decide a consistent envelope field (e.g. echo `traceId` from the call's `usage` into each route's success payload, or thread it through the standard response envelope's optional `meta`) and apply it across the `callJson`/`callText`/`callMessages` consumers. Unblocks: end-to-end traceability on every AI feature, not just the two that happened to already return token counts. |
| 1870 | T4 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **Pre-existing frontend test suite ships red — 59 failing cases across 10 files, none in dashboard/feed code (baseline captured 2026-05-31 during the #1845-#1849 build; API suite green at 2153/2153)** — `vitest run` in `frontend/`: **1197 pass / 59 fail**. Failing files: [EntityHubShell.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/__tests__/EntityHubShell.test.tsx) (6), [PeopleCard.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/__tests__/PeopleCard.test.tsx) (8), [StoryboardEditor.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/__tests__/StoryboardEditor.test.tsx) (11), [resume-service.passthrough.test.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/__tests__/resume-service.passthrough.test.ts) (2), [JobResumeMatch.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/pages/JobResumeMatch.test.tsx) (9), [ResumeTailor.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/pages/ResumeTailor.test.tsx) (8), [Tasks.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/pages/Tasks.test.tsx) (11), [template-dispatch.test.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/__tests__/template-dispatch.test.ts) (2), [registry.test.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/tools/__tests__/registry.test.ts) (1), [templates-by-audience.test.ts](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/__tests__/templates-by-audience.test.ts) (1). Plus [card-feed.test.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/__tests__/card-feed.test.ts) fails *collection* with `No "PublicUserSchema" export is defined on the "@/lib/services/user-service" mock` (incomplete `vi.mock`). The run also surfaces `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` in the shared apiClient NetworkError-retry path — likely genuine infinite recursion. To close: triage each file (mostly mock/fixture drift), add the missing `PublicUserSchema` to the card-feed user-service mock, fix the apiClient GET-retry recursion. Unblocks: a green frontend suite so real regressions are not masked by standing red. **UPDATE 2026-05-31: AppShell-provider cluster fixed (28 cases) — JobResumeMatch (9), ResumeTailor (8), Tasks (11) all green.** Root cause was one shared gap: page tests rendered AppShell-mounted chrome (`<MarketingPageVideo>` → useQuery; `ToolPageHeader` → useEffectiveRole → usePersonaPreview; `<EmailVerificationBanner>` → getVerificationStatus) without the app-root providers. Fix: new shared [__tests__/test-render.tsx](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/test-render.tsx) (`renderWithProviders` = QueryClient + PersonaPreviewProvider + Router; `mockAuthValue` = complete useAuth shape incl. EmailVerificationBanner methods), adopted by all 4 page tests; global `Element.prototype.scrollIntoView` no-op shim in [setup.ts](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/setup.ts) (PageHeader tab strip calls it); fixed two stale assertions (JobResumeMatch error-banner regex matched neither the i18n key nor the English value; Tasks Kanban `getByText('To Do')` was ambiguous vs the per-card status badge — scoped to column testids). **REMAINING ~31 cases, distinct root causes:** StoryboardEditor (11 — `useNavigate()` outside Router: harness needs Router; `renderWithProviders` would fix), PeopleCard (8 — `useAuth` outside AuthProvider: harness needs AuthProvider), EntityHubShell (6), resume-service.passthrough (2 — **real schema regression**: `nullToUndefined` is back, canonical `ResumeSchema` rejects backend nulls e.g. `archivedAt`), template-dispatch (2 — `interactive_comic`+`cad_3d` mediaKinds don't dispatch), registry (1 — coach tool specs 15≠16), templates-by-audience (1 — game_dev audience count drift), card-feed (collection: missing `PublicUserSchema` mock export). **UPDATE 2026-06-01 — frontend suite now FULLY GREEN (128 files / 1268 tests, 0 fail).** Closed every remaining cluster: StoryboardEditor + PeopleCard via new `renderWithAppProviders` (adds real `AuthProvider` on top of QueryClient+PersonaPreview+Router — kept separate from `renderWithProviders` because page tests auto-mock `@/lib/auth`, which would no-op the provider); EntityHubShell self-resolved (the scrollIntoView shim); resume-service.passthrough was **not** a `nullToUndefined` regression after all — the canonical schema correctly requires `archivedAt` (the backend emits it, per resumes.ts:1235 + the backend contract test), the two frontend fixtures were stale → added `archivedAt: null`; **real prod bug fixed in template-dispatch.ts** — the `cad_3d` + `interactive_comic` cases used `require("@shared/…")`, which fails under Vite ESM (no `require` in the browser) so `seedTemplate` threw for those mediaKinds in production — converted to static imports (+ the test's `hasSomePayload` OR-check was missing `cad3dState`/`interactiveComicState`); registry expectation didn't mirror `getCoachToolSpecs`'s `requiresSuperAdmin` gate (SA-only `generate_video_from_page` correctly hidden from the non-SA view) — fixed + added a SA-view assertion; templates-by-audience now derives the expected game list from the catalog (game_3d_world was the 4th); **card-feed.ts: `fetchEvents` bypassed the service layer with a raw relative `fetch("/api/events")`** (un-mockable + would fail in any non-browser context) — refactored to `eventsService.search()` (apiClient, consistent with sibling fetchers), then mocked the 3 networked services the aggregator added since the test was written (studio-templates, article, events — unmocked they hit a dead localhost and retried into the 5s timeout) and `...actual`-spread the user-service mock so `PublicUserSchema` survives. **RESIDUAL (non-fatal, does not fail CI):** WebcamRecorder.test.tsx leaks an unhandled-rejection `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` at WebcamRecorder.tsx `stopAllStreams` — only manifests when the full file's 30 tests run together (a cross-test async leak: a late-rejecting promise / RAF composite loop executing after teardown), not reproducible per-test, and NOT the apiClient recursion originally guessed. Browser `track.stop()` doesn't re-fire `ended`, so no production recursion. Needs test-isolation cleanup (flush/cancel the composite RAF + MediaRecorder.onstop on unmount in the test, or `vi.useFakeTimers`), tracked here. |
| 1945 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **Resume template switched AFTER a canvas doc is saved doesn't re-skin the editor (themed-layout drift)** (opened 2026-06-07 alongside the resume-edit→studio fixes) | The resume-edit→studio template/font bugs were fixed for two cases: (a) [StudioLanding.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx) now seeds a brand-new canvas doc from `content.meta.template` via [resumeTemplateOption](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/document-templates.ts)+`applyDocumentTemplate`, and (b) [StudioEditorV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx) re-skins an **un-themed stub** (a doc minted by a prior "Edit" click but never themed — `!documentState.templateId`) on load. **Residual:** once a resume's canvas doc HAS been themed/saved (`documentState.templateId` set + `content.meta.meta.documentLayout` persisted), switching the default template via the [ResumeDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeDetail.tsx) dropdown re-skins the read-only view ONLY (`layoutTemplateOverrideId`, view-local) and is never written back to the project's `documentState` / `content.meta.documentLayout`. So the detail-view dropdown pick and the editor canvas drift apart for already-themed resumes. The deliberate guard (`!documentState.templateId`) avoids clobbering real canvas edits, so the correct fix is to PERSIST the dropdown pick: write `applyDocumentTemplate(documentLayout, option)` back to both `content.meta.documentLayout` and the linked `document` project on selection (one source of truth), then the editor reload reflects it. Unblocks: template switching that survives a save and stays consistent between /resumes/:id and the studio canvas. |
| 1959 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Studio template Type-filter pills don't self-gate empty media kinds** (opened 2026-06-07 while adding Comic+ / 3D starter templates) | [TemplateCatalogFilters.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/TemplateCatalogFilters.tsx#L67) renders a Type pill for **every** entry in `MEDIA_KINDS`, so any kind with zero catalog templates becomes a dead-end pill that always lands on the "No <kind> templates match your search yet" empty state ([StudioLanding.tsx:1239](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx#L1239)). This pass added starter templates for `interactive_comic` (Comic+) and `cad_3d` (3D), which were the two empty kinds — but the structural issue remains: the next kind added to `MEDIA_KINDS` before its first template re-introduces a dead pill. **Fix**: derive the pill set from kinds that have ≥1 built-in (or owned) template instead of the raw enum — the catalog already knows its kinds. **Unblocks**: no dead filter pills as new runtimes land pre-content. |
| 1967 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Post impressions undercount — only the detail page beacons a view** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1965) | `recordArtifactView({kind:"post"})` fires only on `GET /api/feed/posts/:id` (the permalink). A post scrolled past in the in-feed timeline (Home) records no impression, so the author's PostStatsSheet "impressions" reflect permalink opens, not reach. Add an in-feed impression beacon (IntersectionObserver → a batched `POST /api/feed/posts/:id/view`, deduped per session) the same way the resume/article scroll-trackers beacon. Until then the Metrics drawer reads as "detail views", which may mislead. |
| 1991 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **PWA auto-reload-on-update can discard unsaved in-app work (esp. Studio NLE)** (opened 2026-06-13 with the PWA update-notification pass) | [PWAUpdatePrompt.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/PWAUpdatePrompt.tsx) now force-reloads 30s after a new SW is detected (`updateServiceWorker(true)`) unless the user clicks "Later". An auto-reload while the user is mid-edit in the Studio document canvas / NLE (or any unsaved form) would lose that work — the countdown is the only guard and a backgrounded tab won't be watched. Fix: gate the auto-reload behind a global "dirty/unsaved-work" signal (e.g. a shared `useUnsavedWork` store the editor + long forms register into) so the timer pauses (toast stays, no forced reload) while work is unsaved, and/or honor a `beforeunload` veto. Unblocks safe always-on auto-update without data-loss risk. |
| 1997 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **AI value-prop/pitch → one-click spoken pitch + LLM-generated clone calibration script** (opened 2026-06-13, PRD §4) | The value-proposition generator's output becomes a one-click spoken video-resume intro in the user's cloned voice; on clone setup the LLM generates a read-aloud calibration script + suggested name/description from the profile to lower sample-quality friction. Depends on #1994/#1995. |
| 2106 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **V2 SceneBlock missing left-trim handle + per-scene split/delete buttons on AdvancedTimeline** (opened 2026-05-30 during #1499 verify). V2 [SceneBlock](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/AdvancedTimeline.tsx#L368-L389) ships a right-edge resize only — no left-edge handle and no per-scene split/delete affordance. V1's NLETimeline has the full set (left+right trim, S/M/D/Delete shortcuts, toolbar buttons). The V2 `WidgetBlock` already carries left+right trim + body-move (lines 496-510), so the gap is scoped to the scene strip. Fix: add a left-edge `<span>` mirroring the right-edge resize, wire it to a `onResizeLeft` callback that shifts both `start` and `durationSeconds` so the scene grows/shrinks from the head; add a per-scene context menu (split-at-playhead + delete + duplicate). Unblocks: parity with V1 NLE's scene operations. |
| 2122 | T3 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Job document canvas — structured publishing fields, fresh-draft create fidelity, and read-only render polish** (opened 2026-06-07 with the job→studio migration #1914/#1915) | Job EDIT happens on the document canvas ([job-content.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/job-content.ts) maps the job row ↔ canvas content; job section schemas in [document-field-schema.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/document/document-field-schema.ts); `/jobs/edit/:id` → `?editJob` redirect; saved back via `jobService.updateJob`). **Mostly closed 2026-06-07:** (a) the publishing/role config is now FIELD-EDITABLE on the canvas — new field types `multiselect` (number[]) + `day` (`<input type="date">`) added to the schema + [SectionEditor](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/SectionEditor.tsx); job sections regrouped to `overview`/`responsibilities`/`requirements`/`compensation`/`details`/`publishing`; `employmentType` (multiselect), `workSetting`/`status`/`privacy_ShowJob` (select), `hiringTarget` (number), `goLiveDate`/`expirationDate` (day) all reuse the canonical `*_OPTIONS` from [constants/enums.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/constants/enums.ts) (DRY). (b) fresh-draft create now guards on a non-empty title (skips `createJob` until titled, so an empty draft persists as a document without a 422). (c) read-only [DocumentView](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/document/DocumentView.tsx) renders the job `title` as a prominent heading + multiselect/select as joined labels. (d) `heroImageUrl` now uses `<MediaPicker>` (image library/upload/AI) instead of a raw URL input. **Residual:** `seniority` + `industry` stay PASSTHROUGH (preserved on save, not yet editable) because their numeric taxonomy isn't a canonical `*_OPTIONS` list — needs a verified seniority/industry option source before exposing as select/multiselect; and full job PDF fidelity still trails the public [DeclarativeJobRenderer](hired.video/frontend/components/job-renderer/DeclarativeJobRenderer.tsx) (the generalized renderer, #1912). |
| 2126 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **`useCreateStudioDraft` template-create drops the `interactiveComicState` seed (saveDraft has no such arg)** (opened 2026-06-06) | The template-create path in [use-create-studio-draft.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/use-create-studio-draft.ts) now carries `timelineSpec`/`gameState`/`imageState`/`animationState`/`cadState`/`cad3dState`/`documentState` from the seed (the latter three fixed 2026-06-06 — they were silently dropped, losing a cad/document template's pre-arranged state on create). `interactiveComicState` is STILL dropped because [studioService.saveDraft](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/studio-service.ts) accepts no `interactiveComicState` arg — an interactive-comic template's branch graph isn't persisted at create (the editor re-seeds a blank one). Fix: add `interactiveComicState` to the saveDraft arg type + the API save schema/destructure/write (mirror the `documentState` wiring in migration 0197's pass), then spread it in the template branch. Unblocks: interactive-comic templates that ship a starter branch graph. |
| 2130 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`CreatorTemplatesPanel` side-sheet now overlaps with the `/studio` unified Templates section** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced adding owned-template rows to [StudioLanding.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx); updated 2026-05-17 after the two-section layout was consolidated into one Templates section with All / built-in categories / Created / Purchased filter pills) | The consolidated section ([UnifiedTemplateCarousel + OwnedTemplateCard](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx)) renders user-owned templates inline on `/studio` alongside the starter catalog, calling `studioTemplatesService.listMyLicensedTemplates()` against `GET /api/studio/templates/me/licensed`. Meanwhile [CreatorTemplatesPanel.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/CreatorTemplatesPanel.tsx) is still the only surface that exposes per-row management (republish / make private / delete) and only shows the user's *created* templates (no purchased/claimed half). Spec: either (a) extend `OwnedTemplateCard` to surface the same management affordances (with `provenance === "created"` gating the destructive actions) and retire `CreatorTemplatesPanel` entirely, or (b) keep the panel as the management surface and add a header link from the `/studio` Templates filter row → opens the panel. Today users see their templates in two places with different action sets. Unblocks: single, drift-free surface for "templates I own". |
| 2135 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Wizard "Theme & Style" step has no per-kind analog for non-video kinds** | The kind-aware wizard skips the video-frame [Theme & Style](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioWizard.tsx) step entirely for voice / comic / game / image / animation / cad because `VISUAL_THEMES` + `BG_PRESETS` are video-frame defaults. There is no parallel step for those kinds — comic should get a genre-palette swatch picker (palettes already exist per `comic_<genre>` template), image / animation should get a base-style / size picker, game should get a sprite-pack picker, voice should get a default-voice picker. Fixing this would close the "fewer wizard steps for non-video" UX asymmetry and let users dial in look/feel before they hit the editor, matching the video flow. |
| 2138 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Vendor Sync autofill — Experience + Skills sections still paste-only on LinkedIn** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the #433 partial close). [linkedinConnector](hired.video/api/src/services/sync/connectors/linkedin.ts) ships `autofillSelector` for Headline + About only; the Skills typeahead and the Experience modal are multi-step DOM interactions (typeahead requires per-skill keypress + arrow-down + enter; Experience requires opening a "Add experience" modal then filling Title / Company / Dates / Description). Need: an orchestrator that walks the modal sequence one step at a time, asking the user to confirm each step (no anti-bot trip). Alternative for Skills: send a series of single-skill paste-then-pick prompts. Unblocks: full LinkedIn write-back from the master resume in one session. |
| 2204 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **Pre-existing FE type errors in canvas-v2.ts (Canvas vs OffscreenCanvas context)** (surfaced 2026-06-16 once #2203 unblocked the FE typecheck) | [canvas-v2.ts:586,645](hired.video/frontend/lib/timeline/effects/canvas-v2.ts) pass a `CanvasRenderingContext2D | OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D` where a `CanvasRenderingContext2D` is required (TS2345). Doesn't break the app (Vite bundles via esbuild, no typecheck), but keeps `npx tsc --noEmit` red. TK4/timeline-owned. Fix: narrow the context type or widen the callee's param to the union. |
| 2205 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Pre-existing API test won't typecheck — `.ts` import extensions** (surfaced 2026-06-16) | [publishVideoUseCase.test.ts:27,31](hired.video/api/src/services/youtube/__tests__/publishVideoUseCase.test.ts) import paths end in `.ts` but `allowImportingTsExtensions` is off (TS5097), so `npx tsc --noEmit` for the API is red on this TK10/youtube test. Fix: drop the `.ts` from the two imports (use `.js`) or enable the flag for tests. |
| 260 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **RingCentral integration (click-to-call + call-log sync)** | Complements existing SignalWire phone (#97) for tenants standardised on RingCentral. Per-user OAuth; inbound call events land on the person timeline. |
| 303 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Audio mix not piped through ffmpeg.wasm exporter** | `exportFfmpegWasm` is video-only — it composites and encodes RGBA frames but doesn't pipe ambient music / voiceover / per-scene `sceneAudio` into the ffmpeg pass. The h264 path keeps using MediaRecorder for audio-bearing exports; switching to ffmpeg means feeding mixed-down WAV into ffmpeg as `-i audio.wav` with `-c:a` matching `compiledVideo.audioCodec`. The shared `AmbientPlayer` already produces a mixed PCM buffer — wire it through. Closes feature parity for ProRes / DNxHD / VP9 with sound. Identified 2026-05-04 during Slice D. |
| 305 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `arch` | **Encode-loop Worker only covers ffmpeg pass — composite still on main thread** | `workers/ffmpeg-encode.worker.ts` runs the ffmpeg encode off the main thread, but the per-frame compositor (`renderFrame()` → `drawNode()`) still executes on the main thread because it depends on DOM `Image` / `<video>` elements. For >30 second renders this is the visible UI freeze. Path: re-target `canvas-nodes.ts` and `frame-renderer.ts` at OffscreenCanvas + ImageBitmap inputs (preloaded on the main thread, transferred to the worker), then move the composite loop into a worker. Substantial refactor — every node draw helper that currently calls into the DOM has to be audited. Identified 2026-05-04 during Slice F. |
| 357 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **NLE: multicam UX — angle-switcher overlay + audio-waveform auto-sync** | `switchMulticamAngle()` ships as a programmatic op but there's no canvas overlay that renders the angles 1..N in a grid + accepts clicks to cut. Auto-sync today is `syncOffsetFrames: 0` for every angle — pro NLEs auto-align via audio-waveform cross-correlation or timecode metadata. Fix: build `MulticamSwitcher` overlay component + a one-shot waveform-cross-correlation aligner. Unblocks: actual interview / podcast / live-event editing UX. Identified 2026-05-05 closing #345. |
| 375 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Wand coverage gap on Optimizer recommendations: no tool yet for "consolidate similar work entries", "add metric to bullet", "rewrite weak verbs", or "fill missing section"** (2026-05-05) | After the 2026-05-05 collapse the registry exposes 3 new mutation tools — `consolidate_section_highlights`, `standardize_resume_dates`, `shorten_bullet` — plus the pre-existing `apply_resume_rewrite` / `update_resume_summary` / `add_resume_skill`. Common analyzer recommendations *not* yet covered: (a) "Consolidate similar roles" (would need a `merge_work_entries` tool that combines two work[] entries), (b) "Add a metric to this bullet" (needs an LLM-generated metric proposal + accept/reject), (c) "Replace weak verbs" (could be `apply_resume_rewrite` + a verb-strengthening prompt), (d) "Add a Skills section" or "Add a Summary" (would need `init_resume_section` tools). For these recommendations the Action button is hidden by design (`<RecommendationActionButton>` self-gates to null). Fix: add the four wand tools to `frontend/lib/tools/registry.ts` with backend endpoints for the LLM-driven ones. Unblocks: every analyzer recommendation having an Action button instead of just "actionable when keyword-matched". Identified 2026-05-05 during the Scorer/Optimizer collapse. |
| 403 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **No `/resumes?tab=watched` surface despite `watched_resumes` table existing — followed-resume concept is back-end only** (2026-05-05) | The `watched_resumes` table (referenced from `fake-db.test.ts` and the resume schema in `db/schema/resumes.ts:76`) supports a viewer→resume "I'm watching this candidate" relationship, but no `/api/resumes/watched` endpoint is exposed and no UI tab consumes it. The dead `ownership === "tracked"` filter on `Resumes.tsx:1352` (called out in #400) was meant to surface this but was never wired end-to-end. Deferred from the persona-axis pass (#400 PR-1) because it requires a new backend route. Fix: build `GET /api/resumes/watched` returning `ResumeWithOwnership[]` with `ownership: "watched"`, then add a `watched` tab to the Resumes descriptor for hiring-side personas. Unblocks: the `/resumes?tab=sourced` (own-company) + `/resumes?tab=watched` (cross-company candidate-following) split, mirroring the People connections-vs-talent-pool split. Identified 2026-05-05 alongside #400. |
| 513 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Streaming + profile-chain fallback is architecturally incompatible — can't retry once we've started streaming bytes to the user** (2026-05-09, surfaced during contract audit) | None of our 31 call sites stream today, but the studio storyboard generator (#481 — currently 30s spinner) is a candidate. Problem: our `dispatchTextCompletion` walks `[primary, ...fallbacks]` and retries on failure. With streaming we'd commit to the primary's bytes immediately; we can't retry under the user without re-emitting "false" content first. Fix on our side (when streaming work begins): split streaming dispatch into "TTFB race" (try primary, on first-byte timeout fall over to fallback before either has emitted) vs "progressive" (commit to whichever profile produced first byte, no fallback). Tracked here so the architecture decision is recorded — out of scope for the port today, but unblocks any future "stream studio script as it generates" UX. |
| 560 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `arch` | **Music track on Timeline references `sourceId: 'music:<id>'` that has no MediaSource entry — server-side render skips the audio** (2026-05-13) | [canvasStateToTimeline](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/timeline-emit.ts) emits a clip with sourceId prefixed `music:` to A1 when the user picks a stock track, but Timeline's render facade resolves clips through `MediaSource[]` which we don't populate — so on export the music is silent. Fix: synthesize a MediaSource for each music track (`{ id: 'music:<id>', kind: 'audio', url: '/audio/<id>.mp3', durationFrames }`) and inject into the render strategy's source map. Single seam so the preview player + the export both find the music. |
| 563 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `arch` | **Webcam / Screen recordings + Original Music composer drop blob: URLs into widgets/music — they don't survive a page reload** (2026-05-13) | [ActionsPanel](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/ActionsPanel.tsx)'s recording handlers call `URL.createObjectURL(blob)` and stamp the resulting `blob:` URL into a Video widget or onto `state.musicTrackId`. localStorage autosave keeps the state pointer but the blob is garbage-collected on reload. Fix: pipe each blob through `studioService.uploadVideo` / R2 upload + voiceover-upload (the same path v1 uses) before stamping the URL into CanvasState. Single seam in ActionsPanel since every recording path emits a Blob. Unblocks: re-openable v2 drafts that include recorded media. |
| 564 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Studio v2 voiceover clips persist in CanvasState but aren't emitted to Timeline JSON audio tracks** (2026-05-13) | `state.voiceovers` is populated by the VoiceoverPanel adapter but [canvasStateToTimeline](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/timeline-emit.ts) doesn't lay them on the A2 track. So voiceovers play in the editor preview if/when we hook them up, but won't render on export. Add: for each `VoiceoverClip`, emit a clip on A2 starting at the voiceover's anchor-scene cursor (0 when anchorSceneId is null). Unblocks: voiceovers in exported MP4s. |
| 568 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `arch` | **Studio v2 custom-music selections (Original Music Composer output) don't survive save/reload — Timeline JSON doesn't carry the blob URL** (2026-05-13) | [canvasStateToTimeline](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/timeline-emit.ts) emits `music:<selectionId>` for both stock + custom, but [timelineToCanvasState](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/timeline-emit.ts) only reconstructs stock selections (custom URLs aren't carried in the Timeline JSON). Fix: stash the custom URL + label in a `meta` field on the audio clip, OR upload-to-R2 before save and reference the R2 URL. Coupled with gap #563 (R2 upload of recorded blobs). Unblocks: composed music survives reload. |
| 570 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Studio v2 Preview overlay renders only the active scene at the playhead — multi-scene compositions don't transition smoothly the way the export will** (2026-05-13) | [PreviewOverlay](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/PreviewOverlay.tsx) mounts a single CanvasStage and swaps the scene whenever the playhead crosses a boundary. Hard cut, no cross-dissolve / fade-to-black even when the Timeline JSON has transitions. Fix: render through the same `frame-renderer` the export uses (against an offscreen canvas in a rAF loop) instead of React DOM. Reuses gap #559's "shared Web Audio scheduler" plumbing for synced A/V. Unblocks: WYSIWYG preview that matches the rendered MP4. |
| 576 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Studio v2 missing v1's version-history dialog — `studio_project_versions` snapshots aren't reachable from v2** (2026-05-13) | v1's [VersionHistoryDialog.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/VersionHistoryDialog.tsx) lists snapshots + lets the user restore by overwriting the current script. v2 has no entry point and the snapshot shape is VideoScript-only. Fix: extend the `studio_project_versions` table (or add a sibling) to carry a CanvasState blob, mount the dialog in v2's editor header overflow menu, and have restore branch on `project.kind` to pick the right deserializer. Unblocks: same undo-the-day safety net users have on v1. |
| 583 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Per-scene filters apply via CSS in the editor preview but the render pipeline doesn't yet bake them into exported frames** (2026-05-13) | `filtersToCss()` is applied to the CanvasStage div for instant preview. The matching render-side step (run the same brightness/contrast/saturation/hue/blur/warmth math against the canvas pixel buffer in frame-renderer.ts) is missing — exports of v2 projects with filters look unfiltered. Fix: add a `canvas-v2:filters` effect kind and call it once per V1 background clip with the scene's filter values; the existing color-wheels primitive can do most of the heavy lifting. Unblocks: colour-graded MP4 exports. |
| 588 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Drag-and-drop coverage gap: font / music / MediaPicker-search-result drag targets aren't wired** (2026-05-13) | The shared drag protocol ([lib/studio/editor-v2/drag-protocol.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/drag-protocol.ts)) defines `font` and `music` MIME kinds and `media-url` for media drops, but the FontPicker / MusicPicker tiles don't write payloads on dragstart, and the MediaPicker's stock-search thumbnails / AI results aren't draggable. Drop targets are also missing — font drops should target a text widget (not the whole canvas), music should target the timeline strip, and MediaPicker drags should bypass the modal so users can drop directly onto the canvas. Fix: make those pickers write payloads via `writeDragPayload`, add `onFontDropOnWidget` to the per-widget drop target in CanvasStage, and add a music drop target to TimelineDock. Unblocks: complete drag-everywhere UX parity with Canva / Figma. |
| 590 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Studio v2 has undo/redo + cut/copy/paste, but no visible "history list" panel with per-action labels** (2026-05-13) | [useCanvasHistory](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/use-canvas-history.ts) ships a flat past/future stack of CanvasState snapshots — toolbar buttons + Cmd/Ctrl+Z / Shift+Cmd+Z / Y are wired in [StudioEditorV2](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx). Missing: a Photoshop / Figma-style history sidebar where each entry has a human label ("Add Heading", "Move Text", "Delete Scene") and clicking jumps to that point. Requires plumbing a `label?` arg through every `setState` call site in the editor and stashing it alongside the snapshot in the history hook. Unblocks: scrub-back UX for power users. |
| 630 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **V2 subject deep-linking (`?subject=resume:\<id\>`) doesn't yet bind the subject to the new project — the v1 `handleLinkSubject` flow that auto-links on save isn't replicated in v2** (2026-05-14) | The shared landing page forwards `?subject=` to `/studio/new` so v2 users CAN deep-link with a subject, but [StudioEditorV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx) doesn't read it and doesn't call `studioService.linkSubject(projectId, subject)` on save. Result: clicking 'New video' from a Resume row creates a video but the subject link isn't persisted. Fix: read `searchParams.get('subject')` on mount, parse via `parseStudioSubject`, call `linkSubject` on first saveDraft. Pairs with gap #613 (project-management chrome in v2). Unblocks: EntityVideos / CreateVideoMenuItem deep-links land with the subject attached. |
| 668 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **`computeScriptHash` can't detect asset-URL content drift — if a scene references an R2 image whose contents change at the same URL the hash won't notice and a stale baked video would be served** (2026-05-16 — #665) | [baked-freshness.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/baked-freshness.ts) `computeScriptHash` hashes the asset URL string, not the asset's content. In practice scene assets are addressed by sha256-prefixed R2 keys so a content change ⇒ URL change; this gap only bites if a future writer mutates an existing R2 object in place. Fix options: (a) include asset Last-Modified / ETag in the hash via a small lookup, (b) enforce immutable R2 keys for all scene-referenced assets (current convention, just not load-bearing). Low likelihood, but the player will silently serve a wrong-looking video when it hits, so document the invariant either way. |
| 669 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **No server-side render workers — every Publish-to-* still encodes via ffmpeg.wasm in the user's tab** (2026-05-16 — #665) | The Save/Publish split made client-side encoding more visible: clicking "Publish to YouTube" on a stale project now blocks the user's tab for ~30s of WebCodecs+ffmpeg work while they wait. Fix: a Cloudflare Workers (or external) render service that accepts `(scriptJson, branding)` and returns a CDN URL — the same `ensureRendered` seam can dispatch to it. Unblocks: faster Publish UX, parallel renders, ability to render on devices without WebGPU/WebCodecs. |
| 706 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **`/studio/new` sentinel + `routeId === "new"` URL-param fallback left in [StudioEditorV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx) for stale-URL grace** (2026-05-16 — left in place after the #699 migration) | After #699 every internal entry point mints a real project server-side and navigates to `/studio/<real-id>`. The `projectId = routeId ?? "new"` line + the URL-param consumers (`templateHint`, `studioTemplateSlug`, `urlSubject`) are now dormant for new flows but still kick in if a user bookmarks the old `/studio/new?subject=…` URL. Fix: instrument the dormant branches with a Sentry / GlitchTip event, wait one release cycle, then delete the sentinel + the dependent URL-parsing branches + drop the `/studio/new` route from `App.tsx` (or replace with a `Navigate to="/studio"`). Unblocks: smaller v2 editor mount path; one less "is this still wired?" hazard. |
| 733 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **`uploads/{userId}/{images,videos,files,avatars,ai-images}/...` are not persisted in any DB table** (2026-05-16 — surfaced while closing #729) | [upload.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/upload.ts) and [studio.ts:1349](hired.video/api/src/routes/studio.ts#L1349) (AI-generated images) PUT directly to R2 without inserting a tracking row. The new orphan detector keeps them alive via the path-encoded `{userId}` check, which is correct as long as the user exists — but means there's no surface to (a) show a user their own uploaded files, (b) reclaim avatars when a new one overwrites the same key, (c) prune AI-image generations the user discarded. Fix: introduce a minimal `user_uploads(id, user_id, key, mime, size, created_at, scope)` table and a thin repo. Avatar upload should also delete the previous avatar key. Unblocks: file-manager surface for users + tighter cleanup than "wait for user-delete cascade". |
| 797 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Public watch page sets meta tags client-side only — share previews still see the SPA shell** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced overlaying Meta-tab fields into `applyOgTags`) | [PublicVideoResume.applyOgTags()](hired.video/frontend/pages/PublicVideoResume.tsx) now correctly merges the Meta-tab fields (`metaDescription` / `keywords` / `socialCardImage`) with the video defaults, but the merge happens in `useEffect` after the SPA hydrates. LinkedIn / Slack / X unfurl bots read the initial HTML response and never execute the client bundle, so they still see the static `index.html` defaults. The Cloudflare Pages prerender step (`scripts/prerender.mjs`) handles a static list of marketing routes — `/v/:slug` is dynamic so it falls through. Spec: serve `/v/:slug` (and `/v/:id`) via a Cloudflare Worker / Function that fetches the public payload, injects the resolved og: / twitter: tags into the HTML response, then streams the same SPA bundle — or move to server-rendered metadata via prerendering keyed off the `studio_projects.slug` column added in migration 0084. Unblocks: rich share previews on every social platform, not just on-platform navigation. |
| 808 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Keyframed transform animation (per-widget position/scale/rotation over time) on V2 widgets** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced shipping the Director's Cut bundle) | `WidgetPosition` carries a single static `{x, y, width, height, rotation}` per widget; the only "animation" today is the enter/exit `WidgetMotion` block. Directors expect the ability to set keyframes (5s: widget at A, 10s: widget at B, lerp in between) — character animation, camera moves, animated lower-thirds. Spec: extend `Widget` with an optional `keyframes?: Array<{atSec, position: Partial<WidgetPosition>}>`, drive interpolation through a new shared `evaluateWidgetPositionAt(widget, scenePlayheadSec)` helper consumed by both the editor preview (`CanvasStage.WidgetView`) and the canvas-v2 effect appliers' `readRect()`. Pairs with the existing `computeAnimateOutput` plumbing — those are enter/exit animations on a fixed pose; keyframes drive the pose itself. Unblocks: real motion graphics on the V2 canvas instead of static layouts. |
| 821 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **`film` template category doesn't surface its own landing-page section on /studio** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced shipping #818) | The new `film` category is registered in `TEMPLATE_CATEGORIES` so the /studio landing filter pills include "Film & Acting" alongside "Promote / Showcase / Hiring / Quick" — but the StudioLanding "Your templates" + featured-template rails don't render a dedicated film section, only the pill filter. For the premium-Director positioning to read on the landing surface, the film templates need their own labelled rail (the way Promote/Showcase already get visual hierarchy). Spec: add a `category="film"` rail to [StudioLanding.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx) above the generic catalog grid, gated to only render when `TEMPLATE_CATALOG.some(t => t.category === 'film')` (self-gating per DRY — never write `{filmTemplates.length > 0 && <FilmRail/>}` in the consumer). Unblocks: marketing affordance for the demographic — they land on /studio and immediately see their templates, not a generic grid. |
| 827 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **`template` entity kind missing from linked-content registry (#814 deferred half)** (opened 2026-05-18 — surfaced shipping the 5 other kinds in #814) | [LINKED_CONTENT_REGISTRY](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/linked-content.ts) ships six entity kinds (resume / job / article / profile / company / video) but the original #814 spec included `template` — marketplace-listed resume templates and studio video templates the user authored. The reason it's deferred: there are TWO template surfaces today ([studioTemplatesService](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/studio-templates-service.ts) for `studio_templates` and the in-progress resume-template publish dialog from #792). A single `template` kind would have to disambiguate between them — either by a sub-kind discriminator (`template:resume:<id>` / `template:studio:<id>`), by adding two separate kinds (`resume_template`, `studio_template`), or by waiting until #792 lands so both stores share a unified listing service. Spec: defer until #792 ships, then add ONE registry row whose `listForUser` UNIONs both stores (with a per-row discriminator surfaced in the subtitle), and a `TemplateInlineBody` that branches the renderer on the discriminator. Unblocks: dragging your authored marketplace templates into a sales/pitch reel — closes #814's final ask. |
| 834 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `arch` | **Template publish is the last `canvasStateToScript` consumer — needs a V2-native template format (with widget tokenization) before the V1 compile path can be deleted** (opened 2026-05-18 — deferred half of #832) | [PublishAsTemplateDialog.getVideoScript](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/PublishAsTemplateDialog.tsx) still calls `canvasStateToScript(state)` and sends the V1 script to the server. Server's [`sanitiseScriptForTemplate`](hired.video/api/src/services/studio/StudioTemplatesService.ts) walks scene.elements and replaces `el.role === "name"` text with `{{name}}` so a buyer of the template gets THEIR name inserted, not the original author's — that's the privacy + multi-user-template-instantiation contract. V2 widgets carry no equivalent role tag, so the tokenization model needs redesign: (a) add `role?: "name" | "headline" | "tagline" | …` to V2 widget text data so the inspector can tag what's substitutable; (b) extend the server's sanitization to walk `canvas-v2:text` widgets and substitute by role; (c) update `extractScriptMeta` to read duration / motion from Timeline JSON; (d) only then change the dialog to send Timeline JSON. Pairs with #639 (V1 editor cull) and #831 (last `canvasStateToScript` removal). Unblocks: deletion of `canvasStateToScript()` + `canvas-to-script.ts` and the V1 compile path's last V2-facing footprint. |
| 864 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Scroll-depth tracking → percent-watched heatmap for resume / article** (opened 2026-05-19 — deferred from #860) | The studio video case populates `metrics.heatmap` (per-second viewer-retention curve). Static artifacts could populate the same field with **percent-scrolled** buckets (0–100, `heatmapUnit: "%"` already supported by [EngagementHeatmap.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/analytics/EngagementHeatmap.tsx)) by emitting a beacon on each 10% scroll milestone. Land after #861/#862. Optional but high-signal: makes "did anyone read past the headline" visible without a video. |
| 947 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Auto-fallback to picker on detection failure — today the picker requires a user click; the original `linkedin.com/jobs/view/4416913834/` complaint would be better served by automatically offering the picker the moment `detectJobInPage` returns null on a `looksLikeJobUrl` host** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced as a UX polish on #945) | #945 ships the picker as a manual escape hatch (button on the empty-state banner). The next UX evolution: when the active-page banner is in the "no job detected" state AND the URL passes `looksLikeJobUrl()` AND we've stayed on it for >3s, surface a one-click "Detection failed — open picker?" prompt so users don't have to know about the manual button. The picker telemetry already records `picker_launched` with a `source` discriminator (`manual` vs `autoFallback`) so the SA viewer can A/B the success rates. Out of scope for #945 because it requires UX validation — the auto-prompt is at risk of being annoying on hired.video itself / non-job pages that pattern-match. |
| 1494 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Resume-editor autosave-on-keystroke hook** (opened 2026-05-26 during #155 close). Backend `POST /api/resumes/:id/versions { isAutosave: true }` is shipped + capped + retention-pruned. The resume editor still uses the existing /save endpoint as its only persistence path; a debounced autosave that opens a new version row every ~30s is the missing piece. Lift the Tiptap `onAutosave` debounce pattern from [ArticleEditor.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/articles/ArticleEditor.tsx). |
| 1529 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **YouTube-URL parsing duplicated across 6 components — new `lib/media-url.ts` helper isn't consumed by pre-existing call sites** (opened 2026-05-26 during #1514). New canonical helpers `getYouTubeVideoId` / `getYouTubeThumbnail` / `getYouTubeEmbedUrl` live at [frontend/lib/media-url.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/media-url.ts); the new `<ItemMediaStrip>` is the only consumer today. Pre-existing duplicates: [MediaCard.tsx:48-91](hired.video/frontend/components/MediaCard.tsx#L48-L91), [MetaBadge.tsx:85-101](hired.video/frontend/components/MetaBadge.tsx#L85-L101), [MediaModal.tsx:16-34](hired.video/frontend/components/MediaModal.tsx#L16-L34), [ResumeViewer.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/ResumeViewer.tsx), [ResumeDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeDetail.tsx), [ToolPromoVideo.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/ToolPromoVideo.tsx). Fix: mechanical replacement at each site. Out of scope for #1514 per the "don't refactor unrelated working code" rule. Unblocks: one place to fix when YouTube changes its URL shapes (Shorts, live, etc.). |
| 1530 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Media-led `layout: "cards"` variant for `projects` — poster-first credit cards instead of text-row + thumbnail strip** (opened 2026-05-26, depends on #1515). Today `showMedia: true` on Actor / Director templates renders the existing text layout (Project · Role · Director / Network row) with a thumbnail strip beneath. A `cards` layout would promote the first attached still / poster to the card header (full-bleed) with text overlay, more closely matching the "moodboard" feel of Spotlight / Backstage / Actors Access. Wiring: extend [DeclarativeResumeRenderer.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/resume-renderer/DeclarativeResumeRenderer.tsx) `projects` case to branch on `layout === "cards"` and render `MediaTile` at full width as the card hero. Unblocks: visually-dominant film / theatre credit walls for actor / director / future music + influencer templates. |
| 1531 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **`SAMPLE_RESUME` is software-engineer-shaped — Actor / Director / Theatre marketplace template previews look incongruous** (opened 2026-05-26 during #1514). [/marketplace/templates/actor-headshot-hero](https://hired.video/marketplace/templates/actor-headshot-hero) and `director-filmography-serif` both render against [lib/sample-resume.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/sample-resume.ts) — Sean Hogg, CTO/VPE — so the new media-tiles plumbing has no project-bound `metaData` rows to display, and the credits read "Contact Manager SaaS · Urban Science" instead of "Hamlet · Laertes · Royal Court". Fix: per-template sample resumes, or a registry that maps `descriptor.industry` → sample fixture. Each new sample needs `projects[].id` populated + `metaData[]` rows with `referenceId === project.id` for stills + reels. Unblocks: marketplace previews that actually look like what an actor / director would publish, so prospective users can evaluate the template against a relevant sample instead of an industry-mismatched one. |
| 1585 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Web Speech engine ignores live volume / mute changes mid-utterance** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside #1582). `SpeechSynthesisUtterance.volume` is captured at `.speak()` time and can't be changed without `.cancel()` + new utterance. The WebGPU engines route through a GainNode so live mute + drag works perfectly; Web Speech does not. The narrator's compromise is "live-mute zeroes the engine gain node (which is a no-op for the Web Speech path) and the next utterance picks up the new value." Real fix: route Web Speech output through a `MediaElementAudioSourceNode` by attaching a hidden `<audio>` and a `MediaStreamDestination`, then both engines share one GainNode. Larger rewrite — file under "would be nice." Closes the residual half of #1575 once landed. |
| 1874 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `arch` | **Search-cache invalidation is hand-wired at ~25 scattered write call-sites instead of a single repository-level seam** (opened 2026-06-02). `bumpSearchVersion()` is called explicitly from each content-mutation handler/service because ~101 route files still issue direct `db.insert/update/delete` (see #1327) — there is no chokepoint to intercept writes. This is fragile: a future write path to any searchable table won't know to bump, and will silently serve ≤120s-stale search results. Once the repository-layer migration (#1327) lands, replace the scattered calls with an auto-invalidating decorator on the repositories that own searchable aggregates (jobs, companies, profiles, resumes, voice clones, studio templates, videos, articles, events, courses) so invalidation is structural, not remembered. Unblocks: DRY, drift-proof search invalidation. |
| 1951 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `perf` | **Promote resume-feedback CHECK constraints to VALIDATED** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1946) | The `source` / `status` / `kind` / `proposal_status` CHECKs in migration 0200 are `NOT VALID` per the template (validate-on-write only). After 0200 is applied to prod and the tables are confirmed clean, add a follow-up migration running `VALIDATE CONSTRAINT` on each. |
| 1998 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Client-side WebGPU clone bundle behind the same engine seam (converge to hybrid)** (opened 2026-06-13, PRD §3.2) | When a production-grade zero-shot clone web ESM bundle is published, register it as a `clone` provider (set the CDN / flip the flag) so capable browsers synthesize at $0 while mobile/Safari keep the #1994 server path. No call-site changes — the facade already load/synthesize/fallbacks. Retire the hardcoded `VIBEVOICE_AVAILABLE`/`VIBEVOICE_CDN` constants once the provider registry replaces them (verify zero refs). |
| 2097 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `perf` | **NLE scrubbing proxies are uploaded but never consumed by a live preview** (opened 2026-06-14 with #304, TK4) | After #304 the proxy generate→persist→scrub pipeline is complete: `RendererState.useProxies` makes [frame-renderer.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/timeline/frame-renderer.ts) read `src.proxyUrl ?? src.url`. BUT no production code ever sets `useProxies: true` — the only `createRendererState` callers ([webcodecs-render.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/timeline/webcodecs-render.ts), [comic-export.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/comic/comic-export.ts)) are EXPORT paths that correctly use masters. The V2 live canvas ([CanvasStage.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/v2/CanvasStage.tsx) `VideoBody`) plays `source.url` directly and never resolves a `sourceId`→`proxyUrl`. Net: tall masters generate + store a 720p proxy that is dead weight — scrubbing still buffers the master. Fix: a live NLE/timeline preview that builds a renderer state with `useProxies: true` (or, for the V2 canvas, resolve sourceId video blocks to `proxyUrl` while `isPlayback === false`). Unblocks the actual scrubbing-perf payoff of #304/#341. |
| 2125 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Wishlist hearts not yet on template cards** (opened 2026-06-06 with #1922) | The wishlist is now type-generic (backend + page registry), but `resume_template` / `video_template` aren't wired: no `entityExists` case, no `enrichWishlist` arm, no heart on the template cards (the search "templates" category is a union of studio templates + public-resumes-as-templates rendered via the catalog/`TemplateThumb`, with differing id semantics). Add the two entity types + enrichers + a heart on the template card to complete unified saved-items. |
| 2164 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **`interview_analyze` + `studio_script` JSON-mode call sites haven't been audited for strict-enum drift yet** (2026-05-10) | Gap-#535 covered the four highest-traffic strict-enum sites (match-handlers tailor, match-handlers insights, resume scorer/optimizer, skills extractor). Two remaining call sites carry strict enums in their JSON-mode response shapes but weren't migrated this pass: `interview_analyze` ([interview.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/interview.ts) — sentiment / category buckets on the analyzed transcript) and `studio_script` ([studio.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/studio.ts) — `SCENE_TYPES` enum on each generated scene). Both should follow the same `defineLenientIngest({ name, ingest, coerce })` pattern using `coerceEnum` for the enum fields. Audit + migration is straight-line application of the helper now that the seam exists. Unblocks: full strict-enum drift coverage across every JSON-mode LLM call. Identified 2026-05-10 wrapping #535. |
| 126 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **Text-based editing via transcript (Descript-style)** | After Whisper transcription, render the full transcript as editable text. Deleting or editing a word automatically trims the corresponding video segment and removes the audio range. Requires aligning word-level timestamps (already generated by `services/tts.ts` and `services/transcription.ts`) to clip time ranges and applying cuts on export. `POST /studio/projects/:id/edit-by-transcript`. High-value for long-form recordings where finding specific segments is slow. |
