| 1132 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **`TemplateDef` lacks a `defaultFormatId` field — social-video ad seeds set canvas width/height in the seed function rather than declaratively on the template** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1126) | Today the seed functions in [`template-seeds.ts`](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/template-seeds.ts) call `emptyCanvasState({ width, height, fps })` with hardcoded numbers — the connection to [`video-formats.ts`](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/video-formats.ts) is implicit (string-matched by the developer who wrote both). To close: add `defaultFormatId: VideoFormat["id"]` to [`TemplateDef`](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/templates/catalog.tsx); seeds read dimensions from `findFormatById(template.defaultFormatId)` so the SSoT in `VIDEO_FORMATS` is the only place the numbers live. Pairs with #1126 + the standing DRY rule. |
