| 1237 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **Video Pitch Lab's pitch URL isn't durable** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1233) — the recorder uploads to the studio recordings pipeline, but the resulting URL isn't saved against the user (no `user_profiles.video_pitch_url`), so candidates have to copy-paste it manually into every application and lose it on refresh. To close: add `users.video_pitch_url` column + "Save as my profile pitch" button on the review step; surface the URL on the candidate's public profile (gated by [project_globe_details_owner_only](memory/project_globe_details_owner_only.md) visibility rules). Pairs with #1233. |
| 1333 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `arch` | **`frontend/pages/studio/StudioLayout.tsx` is 2,319 LOC — extract feature panels into hooks + presentational components** (opened 2026-05-25). The single component currently owns auth gate + project state + voiceover wiring + captions wiring + version-history dialog + autosave debounce + 3-panel layout + tab switching + auth overlay. How to apply: extract `useStudioProject()` (state + autosave), `useStudioAuthGate()` (visibility gate), `useStudioPanels()` (which panel is open + persisted prefs), and lift the version-history dialog + auth overlay into siblings. Target ≤ 600 LOC for the shell component. |
| 1334 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **`as any` density — 2,173 occurrences across 284 files; actionable density in `studio.ts` (~38) and `creators.ts` (~36)** (opened 2026-05-25). Per [feedback_dry_solid_default.md](C:/Users/seanh/.claude/projects/c--code-hired/memory/feedback_dry_solid_default.md) `as any` is banned for first-commit code; the existing density is the accumulated drift. How to apply: do NOT do a repo-wide sweep — most occurrences are intentional (Hono context narrowing in `app.ts`, test mocks in `fake-db.ts`, schema row inference in repos). Instead, add `as any` to the per-PR review checklist and bias new commits toward proper types; over time the hot-density files drop. The two routes worth a focused pass are `studio.ts` (during the #1331 decomposition) and `creators.ts` (during the next iteration on creator surfaces). |
| 1335 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `perf` | **Dynamic `await import()` in 11 per-request handlers** (opened 2026-05-25). Locations: `routes/analytics.ts:423`, `routes/feed.ts:313`, `routes/jobs.ts:214`, `routes/search.ts:767`, `routes/tool-runs.ts:184-185`, `routes/studio.ts:1000,1068,1089`, `routes/paid-media.ts:179,425,454`. Each hits the V8 parser + bundler tree-shake bypass on every request. Already noted under [Deferred architectural work](#deferred-architectural-work) ("Remove dynamic `await import()` from Hono routes") but tracked as a discrete entry here so it stops drifting. How to apply: hoist to top-of-file imports; if a cycle appears, factor the shared interface into a thin `*-shared.ts` module. Blast radius small. |
| 1340 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `perf` | **All 141 routes eagerly mounted in `app.ts` → monolithic Worker bundle pays parse cost on every cold-start** (opened 2026-05-25). [app.ts](hired.video/api/src/app.ts) is 716 LOC and does 141 `app.route()` calls with static imports of every route module — so a `/api/jobs/:id` request still parses studio + courses + comics + nle + paid-media + email-integration + everything else into the isolate before serving. How to apply: either (a) split the Worker by domain (a `jobs-and-candidates` Worker + a `studio` Worker + a `billing-and-admin` Worker) and route at the edge via `wrangler.toml` route patterns, or (b) keep one Worker but lazy-load route handlers via a path-prefix dispatcher (`app.all("/api/studio/*", lazyStudioHandler)`). (a) wins on cold-start latency; (b) wins on operational complexity. Decide before doing the work. |
| 1391 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **Real-time panel video room with shared scorecard drawer** (opened 2026-05-25 during Greenhouse-parity audit). Greenhouse hands off live interviews to Zoom + relies on each interviewer to fill the scorecard after. We own the recording stack ([WebcamRecorder](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/WebcamRecorder.tsx)) + the upcoming Durable-Object chat transport (#1230) — both the prerequisites for a multi-party live interview room with a shared scorecard drawer where every panellist sees the rubric + types ratings + adds private notes that only resolve to the debrief view on submission. Differentiator: zero context-switch from "talking to the candidate" → "filling the scorecard." To close: (a) `live_interview_rooms` table layering on `live_screening_sessions` (#1239), (b) WebRTC video via Cloudflare Calls + DO-backed signalling, (c) `LiveInterviewRoom.tsx` 3-pane layout (video feed / shared rubric / private notes), (d) on room-end, each panellist's notes are pre-loaded into a fresh ScorecardSubmission draft. Mid-term play once #1230 transport + #1239 live-screen UI are settled. |
| 1393 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **Outbound call status streaming + recording-URL backfill on interactions** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1359 ship). The extension's `placeBusinessCall()` writes an interaction with the SignalWire SID at dial time, but the `callLogs` row's `status` (queued→ringing→answered→completed) and the `recording_url` only land via SignalWire's call-status webhooks. The webhooks are wired ([phone.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/phone.ts) `POST /webhook/call`), but there's no SSE / Durable Object channel pushing the lifecycle events back to the side panel and no backfill onto the original `candidateInteractions` row when the recording URL becomes available. To close: (a) extend `phoneRoutes.post("/webhook/call-status", ...)` to update the matching `callLogs.status` + emit a Durable-Object broadcast keyed by `signalwireCallSid`, (b) extend `phoneRoutes.post("/webhook/recording", ...)` to find the original interaction by SID and patch its `metadata.recordingUrl`, (c) extension side panel opens a brief EventSource to `/api/phone/calls/:sid/events` and renders the lifecycle into the existing call-status banner. Unblocks: full call recordings show up alongside notes on the candidate's activity timeline. |
| 1607 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `smell` | **Slug / email / hash uniqueness — partial close** (opened 2026-05-26 from gap-#1594 audit; partial close 2026-05-26 via migration [0149](hired.video/api/drizzle/0149_studio_ats_uniqueness_and_match_indexes.sql)). **Closed**: [studiofeatures.ts](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/studiofeatures.ts) `studio_ats_packages.slug` promoted from non-unique `idx_studio_ats_slug` → `uq_studio_ats_packages_slug` (UNIQUE), with a pre-flight `row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY slug)` dedup so any duplicate slugs that slipped through during the non-unique era are collapsed to the oldest row. **Still open**: [events.ts:61-66](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/events.ts#L61-L66) `eventAttendees.lower(guestEmail)` unique index has no `COLLATE` — locale-dependent ICU behavior could allow collisions across locales; [autofill.ts:62-88](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/autofill.ts#L62-L88) `answerCache.questionHash` has no collision-detection telemetry (silent cache poisoning if hash collides). Both are observability / hardening items rather than load-bearing correctness bugs. **Unblocks**: studio_ats slug contract now enforced at DB; remaining items are residual. |
| 1655 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **3D world studio — IndexedDB cache hydration at editor mount** (opened 2026-05-26, follow-on to #1636 PWA work). [game-state-cache.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/game/game-state-cache.ts) shipped with the write side wired into [GameStage3D.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/game/GameStage3D.tsx). **Still open**: read-at-mount fallback when `studioService.getProject(id)` fails on no network. **Fix path**: extend the project-load seam — (1) start IDB read in parallel with API call; (2) if API resolves, prefer server row; (3) if API fails AND IDB has a row, hydrate + set `pendingSyncFromOffline` flag; (4) clear flag on next successful save. **Unblocks**: full offline editing — kids can work on a flight, sync when they land. |
| 1798 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **CAD 3D — true CSG evaluation via `three-bvh-csg`** (split from #930 closure 2026-05-30). The boolean-op node renders its children layered with a yellow-wireframe pending-op marker today; switching the `case "boolean":` branch in [Cad3DEntityMesh.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/cad-3d/Cad3DEntityMesh.tsx) to a real CSG evaluator (three-bvh-csg, ~30KB gzip) makes union/difference/intersection produce a single merged mesh that matches every other CAD app's behaviour. State shape is already CSG-ready (`CadBooleanOp.children: string[]`); no data migration needed. Unblocks: pocket / hole / cutout / fillet (via boolean differences) and real subtractive modelling. |
| 1908 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `arch` | **External `/api/mcp` endpoint can't drive the client-only Studio editor actions** (opened 2026-06-04 with #1907). The studio `studio_*` tools mutate in-browser CanvasState through the module-level studio-editor bridge, so only the in-app AI CHRO (same tab as the editor) can run them — the server-side MCP server ([mcp.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/mcp.ts), which dispatches HTTP tools) cannot. Exposing recording / widget-insert / scene-ops to an EXTERNAL MCP client (Claude.ai, IDE agents) would need a remote-control channel (e.g. a per-session WebSocket/Durable Object the editor subscribes to, with the MCP `tools/call` forwarded to the live tab). Unblocks: "drive my open Studio editor from an external agent". |
| 2108 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **`useCanvasHistory` sidecar captures on commit but never seeds the initial checkpoint sidecar** (opened 2026-05-30 during #592 closure). [useCanvasHistory](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/use-canvas-history.ts) starts with `checkpointSidecarRef.current = undefined` and only populates it when a commit fires. If the user makes one edit then undoes back below the first edit, the restore path sees `undefined` and skips the sidecar — selection stays wherever it last was instead of resetting to "scene 0". For typical sessions this never bites (the user can't undo past the project's loaded state), but `reset()` callers that pre-populate selection via separate setters won't see selection restored via undo from the loaded state. Fix: invoke `sidecarRef.current?.capture()` once during initial render OR in `reset()` before clearing the stacks. Already mitigated by the `if (sidecar !== undefined) restore(...)` guard, but worth seeding for correctness. |
| 2146 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **Per-scene-type renderer style maps in StoryboardEditor stay in lock-step with `SCENE_TYPES` only via TS exhaustiveness** (opened 2026-05-25 during #1430 dedupe). [StoryboardEditor.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/StoryboardEditor.tsx) holds `SCENE_IMAGE_BASE` (prompt-base per scene type) and `TYPE_COLOURS` (badge palette per scene type) as `Record<SceneType, string>` literals — TS enforces an entry for every scene type so adding one to the shared union forces an update here, which is the right pressure but means *visual* styling lives outside the shared module. Two options to harden: (a) co-locate the visual maps in `shared/scene-types.ts` so the colour + prompt-base data accompany the union (one edit per scene type, three side effects); OR (b) replace the records with a switch that has a default branch, accept the loss of TS exhaustiveness and gain forward-compat at the cost of silent fallthrough. (a) is cleaner; flag because the next person adding a scene type will probably forget the maps even with the TS error. |
| 2147 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **TextNarrator could swap Web Speech for the existing WebGPU TTS engines + R2-cached audio blobs** (opened 2026-05-26 during #1519 close). Today's narrator uses `speechSynthesis.speak()` — zero infra, works everywhere, but the voice quality is browser-OS dependent (Edge's neural voices > Chrome's > Firefox's). The richer path: call the [WebGPU TTS engines](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/tts-engines.ts) (Kokoro-82M / Piper) that already power Studio voiceovers, cache the resulting MP3 per `(lessonId, voiceId, rate)` tuple on R2, and serve cached audio on repeat plays. Cost: zero per repeat play (CDN hit), one local GPU synth on first play, gracefully degrades to Web Speech on non-WebGPU browsers. Estimated ~3 days. Self-contained inside `<TextNarrator>` — no consumer changes. |
| 2149 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **`workspaces.owner_user_id` / `owner_company_id` backfill from app context** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside #1640 closure). Migration 0164 created the parent table with placeholder rows (NULL owners). The XOR CHECK is NOT VALID so legacy NULLs pass. To promote `VALIDATE CONSTRAINT workspaces_owner_xor` a service-level backfill walks every existing `workspace_id` and resolves the owner via app context (recruiter membership tables, company-owner role joins, etc.). Tractable but needs the canActFor() seam extended to "what workspace owns this workspace_id" — touches services/studio/workspace.ts. **Unblocks**: DB-enforced ownership instead of "trust the app." |
| 2166 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **12 frontend test files fail under broader test-infra issues unrelated to SCORM/learning work** (surfaced 2026-05-25 during the SCORM ship's full-suite run). Specifically: `StoryboardEditor`, `PeopleCard`, `SearchBar`, `EntityHubShell`, `JobResumeMatch`, `ResumeTailor`, `AIResumeScorer`, `Tasks`, `CreatorTemplatesPanel` all fail with `useNavigate must be used within a Router` (missing MemoryRouter wrapper) OR `useAuth must be used within an AuthProvider` (missing AuthContext wrapper) OR network mocks. `template-dispatch.test.ts` fails on missing `@shared/interactive-comic-state` / `@shared/cad-3d-state` modules. `ai-api-registry.test.ts` + `ai-orchestration-service.test.ts` have stale fixture assertions. None of these are caused by SCORM/learning code; they predate this work. To close: extract a shared `renderWithProviders()` helper that wraps `<MemoryRouter><AuthProvider><PersonaPreviewProvider>...</...></...></...>` so any component-level test gets the canonical surround in one line — same pattern Next.js / Remix use. Then audit + fix the dozen failing tests in one pass. |
| 2168 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **3D world multiplayer — WebRTC TURN-server fallback for symmetric NAT** (opened 2026-05-26, follow-on to #1636). [useGameRoom](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/game/use-game-room.ts) configures Google STUN only. ~10% of users behind symmetric NAT can't establish direct WebRTC; today they silently fail to "alone in the world." **Fix path**: provision a TURN server (Cloudflare WARP / coturn on Fly.io / Metered.ca / Twilio TURN — pricing-tier decision required), inject creds into `ICE_SERVERS` via a short-lived signed-creds endpoint. **Unblocks**: reliable multiplayer across corporate/school networks + carrier-grade NAT mobile. |
| 881 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P4 | `quality` | **Chrome ext: row-scoped success + warning messages ("Already tailored — download instead", "Page scanned — nothing new to save", "No tailored variation found yet") all still post to the global `#quickStatus` banner** (opened 2026-05-20 — same #879 scope decision) | #879 only relocated **error** messages off the page-banner — success and warning toasts emitted by `rowTailorJob` (cache short-circuit), `handleRefreshJob` (no-update branch), `rowDownloadResume` (no-variation branch), `handleStatusChange` (success), `rowDeleteTrackedJob` (success), `rowDeleteTailoredVariation` (success) still call `showQuickStatus(..., 'success' \| 'warning')` and land in the page-banner. Same disconnect as #879's bug. Fix: extend `showRowError` into a `showRowFeedback(jobId, message, kind)` covering all four `alert` kinds, mirror the warning/success palette out of the existing `.alert-warning`/`.alert-success` tokens, and flip the row-action success/warning sites. Holding off now because the user's complaint was specifically about errors and the success-toast disconnect is less misleading (green success in the banner reads as "something worked" even without knowing which row), but the symmetry argument is the same and we should close it before adding a fifth row-action that needs feedback. |
| 1911 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P4 | `bug` | **`studio_*` tools are exposed for non-timeline-chrome project kinds (game/image) where the recorder is a visual no-op** (opened 2026-06-04 with #1907). `requiresStudioEditor` self-gates on "any editor mounted", but game/image kinds don't render the scenes/Actions left panel (`usesTimelineChrome` false), so `studio_start_recording`/`openRecorder` set state with no visible recorder, and scene tools are meaningless for those runtimes. Tighten the gate: the bridge should advertise a `supportsRecording`/`supportsScenes` capability (derive from `mediaKindUsesCanvasStateAuthoring`) and `getCoachToolSpecs` should drop the inapplicable tools — or the bridge simply shouldn't register the recorder methods for those kinds. Unblocks: no dead AI affordances on game/image projects. |
| 679 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P4 | `feature` | **Details panel "Engagement" tab opens with no scene boundaries / duration — Chapter dialog falls back to manual entry** (2026-05-16) | The [Engagement tab inside ProjectDetailsSheet.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/shared/ProjectDetailsSheet.tsx) has no canvas-state context when opened from the /studio landing card, so `<EngagementToolset>` mounts without `sceneBoundaries` (the auto-seed source for ChapterEditor) and without `durationSec` (used by ThumbnailsDialog to space candidate frames). Chapters falls back to manual authoring; Thumbnails uses the loaded `<video>`'s native duration. Fix: either derive `chapterSeedSource?: SceneBoundary[]` on the `StudioProject` DTO from `timelineSpec` in `toProjectDto`, or have the panel lazy-load the timeline via `studioService.getProject` on tab activation. Unblocks: parity with the editor's chapter-auto-seed UX from outside the editor. |
| 2162 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P4 | `quality` | **`PianoComposer` mobile multi-touch + sustained-chord recording not exercised on a touch device** (2026-05-09) | PianoComposer's `PianoKey` uses PointerEvents with `setPointerCapture`, which in theory tracks multiple simultaneous fingers each with a distinct `pointerId`. In practice — not verified on iOS/Android. Risk: a chord held with two fingers may register only the first pointer-down because `heldRef` is per-component and the second pointer may not get its own `start()` call if the second-finger event lands on the same component instance. Also untested: chord recording (does each note get its own `recorded` entry with overlapping `startSec` ranges?). To validate: open Studio Actions → Original Music → Piano on an iPad / Android phone, hold a triad, hit Record, play a sequence with overlaps, render WAV, confirm all notes present. Identified 2026-05-09 porting Piano from APEX synth. |
| 132 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Studio plugin / extension system** | Hook registry in the compiler pipeline: `registerScenePlugin(type, { compile, render, settingsUI })`. Plugins can add new SceneNode types, visual effects, or panel tabs. Plugin manifest loaded from `studioPlugins` table (URL, version, permissions). Sandboxed via iframe + postMessage for safety. Developer-facing API documented alongside OpenAPI spec. Enables community-built templates, brand kits, and integrations without core changes. |
| 351 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **NLE: no third-party plugin / effect SDK** | All effects ship via `frontend/lib/timeline/effects/registry.ts`'s in-tree `registerEffect()` calls — there's no public effect API, no manifest format, no sandboxed runtime for community-supplied VFX. The browser delivery model makes a VST/AU-style plugin ecosystem hard but a JSON-effect-spec + WebGPU-shader contribution path is feasible. Fix: define an effect manifest schema (params, shader, license) + a creator submission flow that lands effects in a marketplace listing (mirrors the voice marketplace pattern). Unblocks: creator economy expansion; deliberately Later because the in-tree registry covers v1 needs. Identified 2026-05-05 during studio NLE audit. |
| 577 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Studio missing brand-kit / watermark / logo overlay across both editors** (2026-05-13) | Audit of v1 confirmed neither editor supports a brand-kit (logo, lower-third template, watermark toggle). Fix: a new `brand_kits` row keyed off `companyId` + a `BrandKitOverlay` widget kind in v2 (with a `canvas-v2:brand` effect on the render side). Unblocks: agency users who can't ship without their logo baked in. |
| 1024 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Game physics — dynamic-vs-dynamic collisions + deep-penetration AABB resolution** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside the #1009 closure) | The hand-rolled AABB solver in [runtime-core.js](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/game/runtime-core.js) `stepPhysics` handles dynamic-vs-(static|kinematic) collisions cleanly but skips the dynamic-vs-dynamic case (`if (pb.kind === "dynamic") continue;`) — two boxes stacked on top of each other will pass through. Likewise the resolution uses the shallowest-penetration axis + body-centre comparison to pick the push direction, which breaks down when a body has passed the wall's centre in a single step (the resolver pushes the wrong way). To close: (a) Add dynamic-vs-dynamic with momentum exchange weighted by `mass`. (b) Use the body's velocity SIGN (not the centre comparison) to pick the resolution direction so deep-penetration cases push back along the entry path. (c) Optional: substep the integration when velocity per frame > body width (continuous collision detection). Reference: Box2D's discrete + bullet-body distinction. Until then the test suite documents the known shortcomings (the "deep penetration" comment in [game-physics.test.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/__tests__/game-physics.test.ts)). |
| 1107 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Quick-select uses tolerance flood-fill (same as magic wand) — Photoshop's quick-select uses edge-aware brush grow (Sobel/Canny edge detection limits the flood per dab)** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1102) | Today's `quickSelectAccumulate` accumulates magic-wand flood-fills per dab. The Photoshop UX users expect: the brush samples + grows a mask within the brushed region, stopping at strong edges. To close: add an edge-strength pass over the source canvas (Sobel kernel → magnitude → threshold), gate the flood-fill BFS at high-strength pixels, then accumulate. Reuses the same engine API surface; just a smarter `quickSelectAccumulate` body. Doesn't block the user's flow — tolerance flood-fill works for most use cases. |
| 1131 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Display-ad templates default to the right canvas dimensions but don't render IAB-specific safe-zone overlays (clickable-area inset, mobile-tap minimums, GDN compliance margins)** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1126) | [`video-formats.ts`](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/video-formats.ts) `SafeZone` infrastructure exists and is consumed by `SafeZoneOverlay` for landscape + portrait + billboards, but the IAB presets carry no `safeZones[]`. To close: add IAB-spec safe insets (e.g. 320×50 mobile: keep the tap-target ≥44px ≈ 88% vertical; 970×250 billboard: 90% bleed-safe; GDN dynamic banners: 5% creative margin) and surface them on DrawingStage so the user sees the boundary while authoring. Pairs with #1126. |
| 1133 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Campaigns tab in Outreach lacks a creative-size-grouped view — a user running a multi-asset campaign across IAB + social can't see the asset coverage at a glance ("do I have a 728×90? a Reel? an OG card?")** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1127) | [`CampaignsTab.tsx`](hired.video/frontend/components/outreach/tabs/CampaignsTab.tsx) shows raw counts. The marketer's actual question is "what creative sizes does this campaign cover?" — answered by fetching the studio projects + grouping them by `findFormatByDimensions(width, height)?.category`. Render a small matrix per campaign card: rows = `FORMAT_CATEGORY_ORDER`, cells = count. Highlights gaps (e.g. "0 display-ad assets" when running a Google Display Network campaign). Pairs with #1127 + #1130. |
| 1218 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `quality` | **`/v/<id>` route name is video-specific even though it now serves every mediaKind** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the EntityMedia / ProjectPlayer dispatch closure) — the route worked when the studio was video-only; now the URL slug a podcast / image / game owner copies still reads `/v/<id>`, which is misleading in the address bar and on share previews. Optional rename to `/m/<id>` (media) with a permanent redirect from `/v/<id>`; cost is updating the SaveMenuV2 share URL builder + the `[videoId].js` social-crawler edge function + the `frontend/functions/v` directory layout. Low priority because every `/v/<id>` URL now lands on the right surface — this is a polish-only change. |
| 1254 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **DEFERRED — Badge printing, lead-retrieval scanners, multi-track conference scheduling, on-site staff portal, age gating** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1240). All flagged as Eventbrite-class feature graveyard for a v1 networking-events platform. Won't ship unless a specific customer demands. |
| 1804 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `perf` | **NLE bin folder rename does a workspace-scoped LIKE scan — fine at 100 sources, sluggish at 10K** (opened 2026-05-30 during #358 closure). The new `POST /api/nle/sources/folders/rename` matches via `binFolder = from OR binFolder LIKE 'from/%'`. Postgres can use the existing `(user_id, bin_folder)` index for the equality branch but the `LIKE 'prefix/%'` branch needs a `text_pattern_ops` index to be fully indexed. At workspace sizes today (<1K sources/user) this is fine; at 10K+ it becomes a sequential scan within the workspace. Fix when bin volumes get there: add a `text_pattern_ops` index on `nle_media_sources.bin_folder` and verify the LIKE branch hits it. Not blocking. |
| 1909 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **AI CHRO can't auto-START a recording — only open the armed recorder** (opened 2026-06-04 with #1907). `studio_start_recording` surfaces the recorder armed to the requested mode, but `getDisplayMedia`/`getUserMedia` require a user gesture (transient activation), which a tool call resolved in the async loop doesn't have — so the user must still click Record. This is a browser constraint, not a bug; documented in the tool's summary text. A future workaround could pre-grant a persistent screen-capture permission, but that's a deliberate UX/privacy decision. |
| 2107 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Layout preset `rightPanelOpen` binding is inert until V2 right panel gains a visibility toggle** (opened 2026-05-30 during #349 closure). [useLayoutPreset](hired.video/frontend/lib/studio/editor-v2/use-layout-preset.ts) carries `rightPanelOpen?: boolean` on every preset (true on Editing / Color, false on Audio / Preview) but [StudioEditorV2](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx)'s `PreviewLayoutGroup.onApplyLayout` only wires `leftTab` + `advancedTimelineOpen` — the right inspector panel is always mounted today. Fix: when the right panel gains a `rightPanelVisible` useState, thread `bindings.rightPanelOpen` into its setter so the "Preview" layout actually collapses both side panels. Cheap follow-on after the right-panel visibility toggle lands. |
| 2111 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Wizard step 0 lacks an inline search field (parity with /studio chooser)** | The [studio landing](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLanding.tsx) chooser carries a Search input alongside the Type + Use-for filter pills (3-axis filter UX). The Wizard's step-0 chooser ([StudioWizard.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioWizard.tsx)) now reuses the same `<TemplateCatalogFilters>` pills but does NOT carry the search box, so a user who knows the template name has to scroll the filtered grid. Adding a search Input + threading the value into `filterBuiltinTemplates(..., query)` (the helper already accepts it) closes the parity gap. |
