| 1570 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `bug` | **AI dispatch chain blows itself up when Cerebras rejects a Zod-derived JSON schema, then Cloudflare subrequest cap kills the remaining failovers** (opened 2026-05-26 from a live `AI_UNAVAILABLE` 503, `correlationId=llm-2cc6ba1b-34e8-4024-ada0-b8b55e3f1798`). Two coupled failures: **(1) Builderforce-side schema-translation bug.** [llm-client.ts deriveJsonSchema](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/llm-client.ts#L518-L533) hands `toJSONSchema(zodSchema)` to the gateway as `JsonSchemaSpec { strict: true, schema }`. Zod emits `maxLength` on every `z.string().max(N)`, but Cerebras's strict-schema validator rejects `maxLength` on `type: "string"` (`400 invalid_request_error / wrong_api_format: Invalid fields for schema with types ['string']: {'maxLength'}`). The gateway's job per [llm-client.ts:7-12](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/llm-client.ts#L7-L12) — *"Vendor identity is invisible to route code"* — includes translating JSON-Schema dialects per vendor. Today it forwards the schema verbatim, so the first two Cerebras-routed profiles in the fallback chain die before the model even runs. Fix belongs in `@seanhogg/builderforce-sdk` / the gateway worker: strip Cerebras-incompatible keys (`maxLength`, `minLength`, possibly `pattern`/`format`) before forwarding to that vendor. **(2) hired.video-side subrequest exhaustion.** Once the first two attempts burn subrequests, attempts 3–6 all return `Too many subrequests by single Worker invocation` (Cloudflare's per-invocation cap — 50 on free, 1000 on paid). The dispatch loop in [llm-client.ts dispatch](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/llm-client.ts#L588-L721) does one `fetch` per profile in the chain, and any subrequests the route already spent on auth + budget check + token-ledger reads + KV reads + Sentry breadcrumbs are competing for the same budget. To close on the hired.video side: (a) instrument subrequest counts per request via a Hono middleware so we can see which routes are near the cap; (b) consider trimming the fallback chain for use cases whose first vendor frequently 400s on schema (`USE_CASE_PROFILES` in [providers.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/providers.ts)) since a 5-profile chain inside an already-subrequest-heavy route is structurally fragile; (c) short-term band-aid until Builderforce ships the schema translator — audit Zod schemas used in Cerebras-routed `useCase` profiles and drop `.max(N)` from string fields. **Adjacent**: gap #515 already flags silent gateway substitution for latency-pinned `match`; #525 already shrank free-tier per-attempt timeouts. **Unblocks**: the entire AI surface (resume scoring, match, Career 360, course generation, article moderation, chat agent) reliably completing under live Cerebras schema-validation regressions without taking down the rest of the dispatch chain. Primary fix is upstream in builderforce.ai; mitigation work tracked here. |
| 1832 | T3 | ⚠️ Partial | Now | P1 | `bug` | **Broken images sitewide: relative `/api/og/…` image srcs don't resolve because the SPA host doesn't proxy `/api`** (opened+mostly-fixed 2026-05-31). The frontend is Cloudflare Pages ([frontend/wrangler.toml](hired.video/frontend/wrangler.toml) `pages_build_output_dir`, no `_redirects`/`/api` proxy) and the vite dev server (`:4003`) has no `/api` proxy either, so any `<img src>` pointing at a relative `/api/og/…` URL resolves against the SPA origin (`hired.video` / `localhost:4003`) instead of the API worker (`api.hired.video` / `:8787`) → 404 broken image. Affected: article covers (`articleCoverImageUrl()` → `/api/og/articles`), course covers + in-lesson diagrams (migration 0190 stores `cover_image_url=/api/og/courses?…` and embeds `![](/api/og/lesson-diagram?d=…)` in lesson `body_md`), company OG cards. FIXED by routing every cover/OG consumer through the existing [`buildImageUrl()`](hired.video/frontend/lib/utils.ts#L46) seam (env-aware: prepends `VITE_API_URL` = `localhost:8787` dev / `api.hired.video` prod; absolute upload URLs pass through): `seo-ugc.ts` (`articleCoverImageUrl` + course/company `ogImage`/`image`), ArticleCard, CourseMarketplaceCard, CoursePublicDetail, ProfileArticlesPanel, ArticleInlineBody; and by adding an `img` resolver to the shared [Markdown.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/Markdown.tsx) component (now gains an optional `className`) which CourseLearner lesson bodies + ArticleView article bodies now route through (dropped their duplicate inline `ReactMarkdown`). REMAINING: other direct-`ReactMarkdown` renderers still bypass the resolver — BlogPost body, ArticleEditor preview, MarkdownPreview, ResumeTailor/MatchResults/ValueProposition tool outputs, JobCard, DeclarativeJobRenderer, DetailsPreview, CompanyCareersControl, CreatorEnrollmentWizard, AIChatPanel. They render content that today rarely embeds API-relative images, but each should route through `<Markdown>` (or share `MARKDOWN_COMPONENTS`) so any future `/api/…` image resolves. A cleaner mechanism alternative: add a Cloudflare Pages Function `functions/api/[[path]].js` proxying `/api/*` → `api.hired.video`, making relative `/api` work site-wide (also helps non-image relative `/api` usage). Unblocks: all generated covers/diagrams render in dev + prod. |
| 2043 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `feature` | **Social Media Publishing & Distribution — Studio → TikTok/YouTube/IG/X/FB (two-lane: free via hired.video vs Pro to your own account)** (opened 2026-06-13; PRD authored same day) | Umbrella for the owner's ask: publish rendered Studio content to social platforms with **two lanes** — Lane A = post *through hired.video's own managed brand accounts* (free for everyone, drives owned reach; moderation-gated) and Lane B = post to the *user's own connected account* (Pro-gated). Lane B gate sequence (server-enforced): `canActFor()` → Pro entitlement (else 402 `PRO_REQUIRED`) → OAuth connection check (else 409 `ACCOUNT_NOT_CONNECTED`) → publish. Today only **YouTube** actually publishes ([publishVideoUseCase.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/youtube/publishVideoUseCase.ts), `requirePro`-gated); LinkedIn is scaffolded; TikTok/Shorts/Reels/X/FB + the entire managed-account free lane + scheduling + per-platform variants + external-analytics ingestion **do not exist**. The `PUBLISH_DESTINATIONS` registry ([shared/media-kinds.ts](hired.video/shared/media-kinds.ts)) + `studio_project_publications` ([0196](hired.video/api/drizzle/0196_studio_project_publications.sql)) are the seams to extend. Full design: [PRD — Social Media Publishing & Distribution](hired.video/docs/prd/social-media-publishing-and-distribution.md). Phases #2044–#2048. |
