| 507 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `feature` | **builderforce-sdk contract gap: gateway must NOT make model-selection decisions on our behalf — vendor / model / fallback choice is OUR business logic and stays on our side** (2026-05-09) | First framing of this gap had it backwards (asking the gateway to mirror our `USE_CASE_PROFILES` table). Correct framing: the gateway is a transport, not a policy layer. We keep `USE_CASE_PROFILES` + the fallback chain + the cross-vendor routing decisions on our side ([providers.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/providers.ts) survives the port; only `openai-compat.ts` + `tryProviderChain` go away). For that to work the SDK must accept and pass through verbatim: (a) explicit `model` per call (no "best available" substitution), (b) `temperature` / `max_tokens` / `top_p` (no clamping), (c) `response_format` typed (#500), (d) `tools` / `tool_choice` typed (#499), (e) any vendor-prefixed model id (`openrouter/...`, `cerebras/...`, `ollama/...`) routed to the correct upstream — we drive routing via the model string, not via gateway intelligence, (f) `useCase` accepted as opaque tenant slug for telemetry only (#501), (g) per-call `metadata` (#504) + `idempotencyKey` (#505) round-tripped on the response. Gateway responsibilities: HTTP transport, vendor authentication, per-tenant rate-limit, server-side observability (`_builderforce.resolvedModel` echo confirming our model string was honored without remapping). Unblocks: clean port that preserves our calibrated model choices + cost/latency/quality tradeoffs; gateway gets to focus on transport reliability rather than maintaining a 32-row product-decision table per tenant. |
| 1994 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `feature` | **Voice-clone server synthesis adapter + `POST /voice-clones/:id/synthesize`** (opened 2026-06-13 with the [voice-cloning PRD](hired.video/docs/prd/voice-cloning-and-llm-narration.md) §3.1, #1991) | A clone-capable TTS provider behind a new `services/adapters/tts-provider.ts` (returns audio bytes — kept OUT of the string-only `llm-client.ts`), exposed as owner/licensee-gated `POST /api/studio/voice-clones/:id/synthesize` → `{audioUrl, durationMs, wordTimestamps}` persisted to `studio_voiceovers`. Token-ledger metered (`voice_clone_synthesis`); read-through cached on `sha256(cloneId+text+speed+lang)`. Makes cloning audible on every device regardless of WebGPU. Unblocks #1991, #1995. |
| 2156 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `feature` | **Voice cloning (VibeVoice) is advertised + wired end-to-end except a working clone synthesizer** (found 2026-06-13, marketing-claim audit; PRD authored same day) | The voice-marketplace + Synthesia/HeyGen comparison name VibeVoice as a live cloning engine, and the upload→publish→license→`library` backend is complete, but [tts-engines.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/tts-engines.ts) has `VIBEVOICE_AVAILABLE = false` + empty `VIBEVOICE_CDN` (no published web bundle), and Kokoro/Piper can't clone — so no one can hear a cloned voice. Full plan in [PRD — Voice Cloning + LLM Narration](hired.video/docs/prd/voice-cloning-and-llm-narration.md): converge on a provider-agnostic `clone` engine seam; ship server synthesis first (#1994) for device-independent coverage, add client WebGPU later (#1998). **Until a real synth path ships, scope the VibeVoice marketing copy so it doesn't claim "live."** Unblocks: an audible, honest cloning feature. Phases #1994–#2000 below. |
