| 496 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **OpenRouter model catalog in [providers.ts:101-119](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/providers.ts#L101-L119) hasn't been audited since the 2026-04-20 user-validation note — some entries (e.g. `google/gemma-4-31b-it:free`, `tencent/hy3-preview:free`) may not be live on OpenRouter today, which is the underlying reason `tryProviderChain` was timing out on early-list entries** (2026-05-09) | #495 made the dispatch fail-fast around the catalog, but didn't actually verify that each `models[*]` entry is currently served. If a model 404s or is silently rate-limited, every call burns one timeout-or-error attempt before moving on. Fix: SuperAdmin tool (or scheduled job) that pings every model in the catalog with a 1-token prompt and flags ones returning non-200. Cache health for ~1h so the runtime fallback skips known-down models. Out of scope for the latency fix because the model order also depends on quality, not just availability. Unblocks: confidence that the published catalog matches what's actually serving traffic, and a place for SA to remove rotted models without redeploying. |
| 889 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Paid Cerebras call (`cerebras/llama3.1-8b`) returned 429 in 615ms via the Builderforce gateway — root cause unknown** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced building #888) | The 503 in `correlationId=llm-4c95a353` shows attempt 5 (`cerebras/llama3.1-8b`, `vendor: "cerebras"`) failing with `kind: "rate_limit", status: 429` after 615ms. That's much faster than a real Cerebras-side rate-limit response would surface (TTFT alone is usually ~200ms, plus queueing), suggesting the rejection happened gateway-local — either Builderforce's own per-tenant TPM/RPM cap on Cerebras is set lower than our usage requires, or the gateway's Cerebras account/billing tier is provisioned for a smaller burst than the chain assumes. Either is a config issue, not a code one, but it has to be diagnosed before the new paid-pool terminal in #888 can be relied on as a true safety net. Fix path: (a) reproduce by hitting `/api/admin/impersonate/ai/use-cases` + dispatch a Cerebras-only test from SA tooling, capture the full Builderforce response headers (rate-limit + retry-after), (b) if it's a Builderforce tenant cap, file the SDK gap and upgrade the plan or request a TPM bump; if it's a Cerebras billing tier under Builderforce, escalate to vendor onboarding. Cross-references #515 (Cerebras-only latency contract for `match`) — same vendor surface area. Unblocks: Cerebras stops being a flaky paid fallback; #888's pool can drop to Cerebras-only once headroom is confirmed. |
| 1261 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Existing REST chat surfaces (`AIChatPanel`, `ChatPanel`, Comm Hub) not yet migrated to the new WebSocket transport** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the [ChatRoom Durable Object](hired.video/api/src/durable/ChatRoom.ts) + [`useChatRoom` hook](hired.video/frontend/hooks/use-chat-room.ts) closing the underlying #1230 transport gap). The DO ships message / typing / presence broadcasts at `/api/chat/socket/:conversationId` and the React hook owns reconnect-with-backoff, but the existing chat UIs still poll the REST `messageRoutes` endpoints from messages.ts. Migration is a swap of the polling effect for `useChatRoom(conversationId)` per panel + a server-side persistence echo so DO frames also land in `aiChatMessages` for history. Unblocks: presence indicators in every chat surface; sub-second message delivery; closing the LinkedIn-InMail parity story end-to-end. |
