| 1392 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Outreach sequence drip worker — advance + send enrollments on their due dates** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1357 ship). [recruiterOutreachEnrollments](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/recruiter.ts) rows are inserted with `status='active'`, `currentStep=0`, and `nextSendAt = now + step0.delayDays` from the extension's enroll flow, but no worker advances them — step 0 never actually sends and steps 1..N are never scheduled. To close: add a Cloudflare Cron-triggered job (`workers/recruiter-outreach-tick.ts` matching the existing `recruiter-agent-followup` pattern in [scheduled.ts](hired.video/api/src/scheduled.ts)) that (a) selects `WHERE status='active' AND nextSendAt <= now()` (the partial index from migration 0131 makes this O(due-set)), (b) dispatches the step's channel-specific send (email via SES/Resend, in-app message via existing messages endpoint, SMS via SignalWire), (c) advances `currentStep` and recomputes `nextSendAt` from the next step's `delayDays`, (d) flips `status='completed'` when `currentStep` exceeds `steps.length`, (e) appends a `candidateInteractions` row per send so the activity timeline reflects every drip touch. Unblocks the full Loxo / Salesloft sequence motion. |
