| 381 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Resume card score chips deep-link only to `ai-resume-scorer` history; ATS score is also writable by `resume-optimizer` so optimizer-only runs are invisible from the chip click** (2026-05-05) | `frontend/components/tools/ResumeScoreBadges.tsx` maps every sub-score (ATS / KW / Fmt / Cnt / Imp / Overall) to `ai-resume-scorer` and the heart chip to `sentiment-analysis`. That's right for users who run the full Scorer, but the Optimizer (`/Tools/ResumeOptimizer`) also writes `scores.ats` via `persistResumeScoresIfReferenced`. A user who only ran the Optimizer will see an ATS chip on the card, click it, and land on an empty Scorer accordion (their Optimizer runs sit in a different group below). Fix options: (a) per-score map → tool id list with the panel pre-expanding all matching groups, or (b) collapse Scorer + Optimizer history under a single "resume-analysis" view (related to #376). Unblocks: chip click reliably lands on the run history that produced the score. Identified 2026-05-05 while wiring score chips on the Resumes page. |
| 424 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Drizzle insert-type inference collapses `user_profiles` to `{ userId }` — workaround duplicated in `Career360Service.persistDoc` and `usersRepository.upsertProfile`** (2026-05-06) | `typeof userProfiles.$inferInsert` resolves down to `{ userId: string }` despite the table having ~30 columns. Best guess is drizzle hits a TS expansion-depth ceiling for wide tables. Two call sites already work around it: `repositories/usersRepository.ts::upsertProfile` casts through `as any`, and `services/career360/Career360Service.ts::asInsertPatch` funnels the patch through `Record<string, unknown>`. Fix path: (a) upgrade drizzle-orm to a version that fixed the inference; (b) split `userProfiles` into a 1:1 join to shrink the parent table; (c) define an explicit `UserProfilePatch` type in `db/schema/users.ts` and use that everywhere. Unblocks: dropping the inline casts in `Career360Service` and `usersRepository`. Identified 2026-05-06 while persisting the Career 360 doc. |
| 430 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **`meteredCall` accepts `userId: string \| undefined` and silently skips the charge when undefined — an unauthenticated route that should be Pro-gated would not get caught at the metering layer** (2026-05-07) | The contract is "anonymous routes pass undefined and skip billing" (see app.ts:492 visitor chat — intentional). But the `string \| undefined` shape means a route that forgets `requireAuth` or fails to extract `c.var.user.sub` would burn LLM tokens for free without any test/runtime signal. Defense in depth: split the API into `meteredCall(...)` (REQUIRES `userId: string`) and `meteredCallAnonymous(...)` (explicit zero-charge variant). Forces every caller to pick a side at the type level. Unblocks: catches "forgot auth gate, also forgot to bill" classes of bug at compile time. Identified 2026-05-07 while shipping #428. |
| 516 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Cross-vendor fallback chain in `USE_CASE_PROFILES.fallbacks` may now be redundant — gateway has its own internal failover (surfaced via `_builderforce.retries`)** (2026-05-09) | We kept our `fallbacks` array on `studio_script`, `match`, and `career_360` because gap #511 (gateway-internal-retry billing semantics) is unresolved — we don't know whether the gateway already burns tokens on failed-but-retried attempts that our user-ledger doesn't see. Once #511 clarifies, evaluate dropping our client-side chain entirely: gateway exhausts → returns 503 → we fail closed. Net: simpler dispatch (single SDK call, no chain walk), but loses our control over WHICH model is the fallback (gateway picks). Decision belongs in a follow-up after observing gateway behavior in production for 2 weeks. | Mid-consolidation when the vendor signalled SDK 0.3.0+ inbound. Per the "no legacy" directive (collapse to one client backed by the SDK, file SDK gaps explicitly rather than carry parallel infra), pausing is the right call: a half-migrated tree carries both the legacy `tryProviderChain` path AND the gateway adapter, which is exactly the parallel-infra pattern we agreed to avoid. Current pause state: SDK installed (`@seanhogg/builderforce-sdk@^0.2.0` in [api/package.json](hired.video/api/package.json)); env types include `BUILDERFORCE_API_KEY` + `BUILDERFORCE_GATEWAY_URL` ([api/src/types/index.ts:12-22](hired.video/api/src/types/index.ts)); legacy dispatch in [providers.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/providers.ts) + [ai.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/ai.ts) + [openai-compat.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/openai-compat.ts) + [llm-client.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/llm-client.ts) UNCHANGED — production traffic still routes through `tryProviderChain` and the three vendor keys. Earlier-this-pass hybrid wrapper (builderforce-client.ts + dispatch-shared.ts) deleted as dead code; the two helpers `buildProfileChain`, `chargeLedger`, `parseAndValidateJson`, `stripJsonFences` will need re-extracting when work resumes. Resume checklist when SDK 0.3.0 lands: (1) verify which of #499/500/501 closed (tool calling / typed JSON / missing useCases); (2) re-audit #509/510 (vendor-prefixed routing convention, response_format pass-through) against the new gateway version's docs; (3) execute the consolidation per the agreed shape — one `LLMClient` in `llm-client.ts`, no separate `builderforce-client.ts`, no `LLM_DISPATCH_MODE` flag, no `tryProviderChain`, no per-vendor env keys; (4) for any of #499–#501 still open, the corresponding feature (e.g. chat agent's tool calling) goes through `callMessages` which throws — chat-route's existing try/catch falls through to its mock response path. Unblocks: completing the port without dragging the legacy code along OR leaving the tree in a half-migrated state. |
| 548 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Tool-page tests (`AIResumeScorer`, `JobResumeMatch`, `ResumeTailor`) all fail with `usePersonaPreview must be used within PersonaPreviewProvider`** (2026-05-12, surfaced during the `ToolRunContext` refactor) | [\_\_tests\_\_/pages/AIResumeScorer.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/pages/AIResumeScorer.test.tsx), [JobResumeMatch.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/pages/JobResumeMatch.test.tsx), [ResumeTailor.test.tsx](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/pages/ResumeTailor.test.tsx) all render their respective page directly without wrapping in `PersonaPreviewProvider`. Every page mounts [`ToolPageHeader`](hired.video/frontend/components/tools/ToolPageHeader.tsx), which calls [`useEffectiveRole`](hired.video/frontend/hooks/use-effective-role.ts) → `usePersonaPreview()`, which throws when no provider is in the tree. 24/25 tests in the three files fail before any assertion runs — the test bodies (service-call wiring, validation, auth gate, error paths) are uncovered. Fix: a shared `renderToolPage(ui)` helper that wraps the render in `<PersonaPreviewProvider>` (plus whatever other providers `ToolPageHeader` quietly depends on); applies to all tool-page tests. Unblocks: real regression coverage for the three flagship tool pages, including the resume-scoring path the AI ChRO bug surfaced. |
| 1305 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **#508 — gateway exposes per-call usage records for reconciliation** (opened alongside #1300). `GET /llm/v1/usage/records?since=...&cursor=...` returning per-call rows with `requestId`, `useCase`, `model`, `tokens`, `metadata`. Until landed, SA reconciles aggregated totals against `ai_usage_records` manually. The new catalog-audit endpoint (#1300) covers model availability; row-level reconciliation is the next surface. |
| 1322 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Career360 swaps in a separate `<Career360Marketing>` component for anon users instead of letting them see + interact with the same surface and gating only at the AI Coach hand-off** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1320). [Career360.tsx:491-492](hired.video/frontend/pages/tools/Career360.tsx) branches: when `!isAuthenticated`, render a different marketing component (`<Career360Marketing>`); when authenticated, render the actual gap dashboard. This violates the principle established in #1320 (the user sees the same UI shape regardless of auth state; the gate fires on the action button). The `openCoach` helper at [Career360.tsx:435-438](hired.video/frontend/pages/tools/Career360.tsx) already does `navigate("/login")` on unauth — but that's a hard redirect with no overlay, no `?redirect=` query, and no snapshot. To close: delete `<Career360Marketing>` (or fold its copy into the empty-state of the real dashboard), let anon users see the catalog of gap categories + an empty "Run analysis" CTA, snapshot the user's selected gap/category on Coach-handoff, and route through `<AuthOverlay>` instead of `navigate("/login")` so the user returns to the same scroll position with the same gap focused. |
| 1810 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Gateway `traceId` is surfaced on the success path but NOT on the failure path — `LLMDispatchError` still reports a locally-minted `correlationId` (`llm-${crypto.randomUUID()}`) instead of the gateway's authoritative trace** (opened 2026-05-30 while wiring `_builderforce.traceId` from Builderforce SDK 0.8.2 into API responses). On success, [llm-client.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/llm-client.ts) now threads `_builderforce.traceId` through `LLMUsage.traceId` → `toClientUsage` → the chat + course-generate responses. On failure, `dispatch()` throws `LLMDispatchError` carrying a *client-generated* `correlationId` that was sent **to** the gateway as request metadata — which is NOT the same id the gateway records as its trace. Per the SDK docs the gateway's trace on the error path is `BuilderforceApiError.details.correlationId`; we never read it. Result: a user hitting a 503/502 cannot quote an id that Builderforce support can resolve server-side (the success path can). Fix: in `classifyAttemptError`, capture `(err.details as {correlationId?: string})?.correlationId` onto `LLMDispatchAttempt`, and prefer the gateway trace over the local id when building `LLMDispatchError` (keep the local id only as a fallback for pre-dispatch/non-Builderforce throws). Unblocks: support can trace failed AI calls, not just successful ones. |
| 1835 | T3 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **Legacy `/api/reports` (`contentReportsV2`) route removed — it shadowed the canonical `content_reports` flow** (surfaced+fixed 2026-05-31). Deleted the duplicate `app.route("/api/reports", contentReportsRoutes)` mount, the `routes/content-reports.ts` file, and the now-dead `contentReportsV2` Drizzle schema + types (`gapPass4.ts`) + its unused `users` import. The canonical `reportRoutes` (`content_reports` + ModerationService email/inbox fan-out) now solely owns `/api/reports`. RESIDUAL: the **physical** `content_reports_v2` table is left orphaned (no Drizzle schema, no routes) — it may hold rows that landed there while it shadowed the canonical route, so it needs a data-archive/migrate-into-`content_reports` pass before a `DROP TABLE` (vocab differs: status `actioned/triaged`→`resolved_action_taken/reviewing`, reason `illegal`→`other`, entity kinds `company/comment/video` have no canonical equivalent). Unblocks: physical table cleanup. |
| 1896 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Generation safety guard (#1895) hardening — image-source moderation, evasion robustness, i18n, client UX** (opened 2026-06-04) | The shipped deterministic guard screens the TEXT prompt only and is conservative-English. Open follow-ups: (a) **img2img/inpaint/outpaint accept a `sourceImageUrl`/`sourceImageDataUrl`** — a user could smuggle violent/explicit imagery via the SOURCE image with a benign prompt; needs a vision/image-moderation pass (blocked on the same multimodal-LLM infra as #1864, or a Cloudflare image-classification primitive). (b) **Non-English + obfuscation** (leetspeak beyond the seeded slur variants, unicode homoglyphs, spaced-out tokens) can slip the regex floor; consider an optional LLM safety-classifier second stage (the `reviews`/`content_safety_scan` use case already exists) gated behind the cheap deterministic floor. (c) **No client-side pre-warning** — the block is server-side 422 only; surfacing a friendly inline toast in the studio generate dialogs (MediaPicker / GenerationProgressDialog) before the request would improve UX. (d) **Audit/telemetry** — blocked attempts only `console.warn`; persisting them (reuse `moderation_report` or a new `generation_blocks` log) would let SA spot abuse patterns + repeat offenders. Unblocks: defense-in-depth on the generation surface beyond the text-prompt floor. |
| 2053 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `bug` | **Pre-existing typecheck errors in [Career360.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/tools/Career360.tsx) — two `setState` updaters omit the required `outcomes` field** (found 2026-06-14 during the social-publishing typecheck pass; UNRELATED to that work) | `pages/tools/Career360.tsx:409` (`persistSelected`) and `:420` (`handleSuggest`) call `setState((prev) => ({ doc, history }))`, but the state type is `{ history, outcomes, doc? }` — `outcomes` was added to the shape without updating these two updaters, so `tsc --noEmit` fails with TS2345 (`Property 'outcomes' is missing`). Both should spread `outcomes: prev?.outcomes ?? []` (mirroring how they already carry `history: prev?.history ?? []`). Pre-existing (the social-publishing change touches none of this file or its imports — grep-confirmed); logged so the frontend typecheck is green again. |
| 2129 | T3 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Career 360 inner-ring outcome refinements (follow-on to #421)** (opened 2026-06-14) | **Done 2026-06-16 (TK5):** (a) `computeFunnelCounts` now folds `job_applications` into the applied denominator **deduped by jobId** against the `saved_jobs` pipeline so a job in both surfaces isn't double-counted; (c) `interviewConversionSignal` falls back to `interview_sessions` completed-practice `overallScore` readiness when the real funnel is below the 2-interview floor (reports `rate:null` — a proxy, not a measured rate). 3 new tests; api tsc green. **Residual — (b) cross-track cache invalidation:** `saved_jobs` status mutations live in the jobs domain (TK3: `JobService` saved-job status update, auto-apply) and should call `invalidateCachedKey('c360:funnel:'+userId)` (already exported from `utils/edge-cache.ts`) so the inner ring refreshes immediately instead of waiting out the 120s TTL. Left to TK3 (jobs-domain files). |
