| 1564 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **Marketing-copy alignment audit shipped during the vs-competitors refresh, but FAQ overpromises on 20+ language dubbing scope** (opened 2026-05-26 during #1558 marketing). The dubbing FAQ on [Competitors.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Competitors.tsx) and the `Multi-language video dubbing` row on [CompetitorComparison.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/CompetitorComparison.tsx) say "20+ target languages." `SUPPORTED_DUBBING_LANGUAGES` in [api/src/routes/studio-dubbing.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/studio-dubbing.ts) ships 22 — accurate today. The risk is that the LLM's translation quality drops sharply outside the top ~10 languages, and the WebGPU TTS engines (Kokoro / Piper / VibeVoice) ship voices for fewer languages still. Fix: smoke-test each language end-to-end (translate → synthesize → listen) and either narrow the supported list to the languages with a confirmed voice + acceptable LLM quality, OR keep all 22 but caveat the lower-quality ones in the picker. Unblocks: marketing copy that matches what users will actually experience. |
