| 456 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P1 | `feature` | **Career 360 → Tasks completion is manual — no automatic check that the resume actually contains the credential the task asked for** (2026-05-10) | `CareerItemActions.deriveValidationHint()` already stamps `metadata.validation = { type: "cert", patterns: [...] }` on tasks generated from cert-style gaps/steps (PSPO, PMP, AWS SA, AWS ML Specialty, CFA, CISSP, GCP Architect, Azure Architect — pattern matched off the title + context). Remaining: a `/tasks` UI hook that, for each task with `metadata.validation.type === "cert"`, scans the user's master-resume `content.certificates[].name` for any of the patterns and offers a one-click "Mark complete — verified against resume" button. Backend helper to perform the check + auto-update the task status would round it out. Unblocks: closed-loop Career 360 (gap → task → cert added to resume → task auto-closes → gap re-evaluates to "closed"). Identified 2026-05-10 wiring the Add-to-Tasks flow. |
