GoalSchema` are un-exported route-local consts, so the tests mirror their shape verbatim (documented in each test header); exporting them from the route would remove the drift risk. |
| 1898 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Wave-1 page localization (catalog progress log, 2026-06-04) surfaced child components that still render hardcoded English — a localized page is not truly 100% until these stop leaking** | The 17 wave-1 pages now call `t()` for their own copy, but each renders shared child components that carry their own English literals. Highest-impact, grouped by owner: **shared chrome** — [MarketingFAQ.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/MarketingFAQ.tsx) default `heading="Frequently Asked Questions"` + `"Listen to FAQs"` eyebrow (leaks on every marketing page), [CompetitorComparison.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/CompetitorComparison.tsx) full vendor/feature table, [BillingAddressForm.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/billing/BillingAddressForm.tsx) field labels/placeholders, [PageHeader.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/PageHeader.tsx)/[HeaderSearch.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/HeaderSearch.tsx); **cards/menus** — `JobCard`/`JobActionsMenu`/`JobAnalyticsDialog`, `ResumeCard`/`ResumeActionsMenu`, `CompanyCard`, `PeopleCard`/`DiscoverPeopleGrid`, `AddToListMenu`/`ListsButton`/`ViewModeToggle`/`Pagination`; **dialogs/sheets** — `QRCodeDialog`, `ShareModal`, `EmbedSheet`, `MetadataModal`, `RenameResumeDialog`, `CreateVariationDialog`, `MergeResumeDialog`, `EntityVersionHistoryDialog`, `ToolHistorySheet`, `ContactPanel`; **panels** — `ReviewsSection`, `TeamLeaderboardPanel`, `BadgesGallery`, `ClassroomsPanel`/`LearningPanel`/`MyLearningPanel`, `ReferralLinkBox`, `CreatorEnrollmentWizard`, `ContentCreatorSection`, `ServicesNav`; **enum label maps** — `JOB_APPLICATION_STATUS_COLORS`/`JOB_ALERT_FREQUENCY_LABELS` ([lib/constants/enums](hired.video/frontend/lib/constants/enums.ts)) feed badge text in English. These are tracked as part of the to-100% sweep (each is pulled in alongside the next page that renders it) and are counted in the components surface (~5,600 strings) in the [Localization (i18n) Coverage Catalog](#localization-i18n-coverage-catalog). `ToolCard`/`tools-catalog` is #1897. Unblocks: genuine 100% locale parity on the wave-1 pages, not just their top-level JSX. |
| 2031 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `bug` | **ForRecruiters marketing page asserts a live SOC 2 trust badge + invented stats + fabricated testimonials — contradicts the documented "SOC 2 is roadmap, not delivered" posture** (found 2026-06-13, marketing-page validation) | [ForRecruiters.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/ForRecruiters.tsx) renders a `trust.soc2` badge in its trust bar (~:307) presenting SOC 2 as achieved, while this README (Launch Readiness §, ~line 2459) and [Security.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Security.tsx) (correctly) treat SOC 2/ISO 27001 as `roadmap`. It also ships hardcoded marketing numbers (`STATS` ~:40 — "3× faster", "85% of recruiters rate", "16+ boards", "60s") and three fabricated `TESTIMONIALS` (~:117/:274) with invented names + 5-star ratings. Legal/credibility risk: the SOC 2 claim is a false compliance assertion; the stats/testimonials are unbacked. Fix: drop the SOC 2 badge (or gate it on real attestation), and remove/soft-source the stats + testimonials until they reflect real data/customers. Reference page AffiliateProgram.tsx avoids both patterns. |
| 1387 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Predictive-validity dashboard — which scorecard attributes actually predict hire success** (opened 2026-05-25 during Greenhouse-parity audit). Greenhouse's `Predicts` product (enterprise-only, $10K+/mo) correlates scorecard attribute scores against post-hire outcomes (90-day review, 1-year retention, promotion velocity). We already have the upstream data: `scorecard_submissions` + `scorecard_submission_ratings` + the existing performance-review surface ([services/company/HiringPipeline](hired.video/api/src/services/company/) — has interviews/offers/onboarding/performance) + gamification points/badges. The product would (a) join scorecard attribute averages against 90-day & 12-month outcome flags for every hire of the past 24 months, (b) compute per-attribute Pearson correlation + p-value, (c) surface "Attributes that predict success here" / "Attributes that don't predict anything" panels per role family. To close: schema additions on `users` (hireStartDate, hireOutcome90d, hireOutcome1y, terminationDate, promotionDates[]), a scheduled `workers/predictive-validity-recompute.ts`, and a `PredictiveValidityDashboard.tsx` page gated to employer/HM users. Critical anti-bias layer: surface attributes with low predictive validity so customers stop measuring noise. Pairs with #1382 competency framework. |
