| 2068 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **EnergizeLMS feature-parity gaps — learner-facing AI + engagement completion** (opened 2026-06-14) | Gap analysis of the `energizelms/` prototype (an AI-powered, gamified LMS) against hired.video's shipped LMS found hired.video **meets or exceeds** ~21/30 capabilities (courses/modules/lessons, learning paths/DAG, SCORM 1.2/2004 + xAPI LRS, cohorts/assignments, signed certificates, gamification engine, billing/cart/wishlist, marketplace/payouts, creator/manager/admin tooling, LLM gateway). Full PRD: [energize-lms-feature-parity-and-gaps.md](hired.video/docs/prd/energize-lms-feature-parity-and-gaps.md). Net-new/completion gaps (children): **GAP-1** structured course `learningOutcomes`/`requirements` fields (today only free-text `description`; add to [courses.ts](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/courses.ts) + [CoursePublicDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/marketplace/CoursePublicDetail.tsx)); **GAP-2** context-aware **AI Learning Coach** drawer scoped to current course/lesson/path (reuse LLM gateway + `career-coach.ts` pattern + chat DO + `AIContextType`/[HelpDrawer.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/help/HelpDrawer.tsx) — net-new = learning context payload + one shared drawer, NOT new chat infra); **GAP-3** (highest leverage) **goal → LLM-generated learning plan/path** materializing a draft `learning_path` from a captured `learning_goals` row (reuse learning_paths + gateway, JSON-schema-conformed, cached per goal version); **GAP-4** learner/**XP leaderboard** (global + cohort) over `points_ledger`/`user_points_balance`, version-token-cached, excludes fraud-suspended users (ranking-panel pattern already exists for creator discovery + recruiter pipeline activity — reuse it; only the learner/points board is missing); **GAP-5** learner **learning dashboard / progress analytics** screen consolidating enrollment + gamification + certificate read models (data exists, no consolidated UI); **GAP-6** educator cohort **gradebook** roll-up grid (members × assignments) over `learning_assignments` + `course_enrollments`; **GAP-7** standalone **quiz/question-bank authoring** (validate author demand first — knowledge checks via `studio_video_forms` already cover the common case); **GAP-8** wire learning/gamification engine events → typed notifications (badge/streak-at-risk/recommendation/assignment-due/cert-issued) via the existing notifications aggregate (pairs with #1949). GAP-9 (LLM-ranked recs) already tracked separately; fold into GAP-3's gateway-profile family. Explicitly NOT gaps / do-not-port: EnergizeLMS's $29/$99 pricing tiers (hired uses $9.95 + token packs) and its localStorage/simulated-AI architecture. Unblocks: the learner-facing AI + engagement experience that hired.video's strong backend isn't yet matched by. |
| 1645 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P2 | `feature` | **UGC relocation guide flow with gamification hooks — "City Guide" badge + 500 points + verified-author check + moderation queue** (opened 2026-05-26 from #1628 pass-3 closure). **Pass-4 disposition (2026-05-28): deliberately NOT closed — this is net-new product scope beyond the Resource-Maps feature, not an engineering gap in it.** Note the AUTHORING path already works today: a creator can write a relocation guide as an article + tag it with a location (locationsService) AND an audience (contentAudiencesService, #1644) — it surfaces on the matching /in + /for pages immediately. What #1645 adds is the INCENTIVE + TRUST layer (City Guide badge, 500-point award, residency-tenure verification, dedup detection, dedicated moderation routing) — each touches the gamification + moderation domains and needs its own design/scoping, so it's left as a tracked roadmap item rather than fake-closed. Geographic landing pages render today via [LocationLandingPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/landing/LocationLandingPage.tsx) but rely on existing articles for relocation content. To scale relocation coverage beyond top-10 in-house editorial, build the community submission flow: (a) article-publish UI gets a "Relocation guide" article-type opt-in that requires picking a location (cityId / stateId / countryId); (b) submission goes to a moderation queue ([api/src/routes/admin-articles.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/admin-articles.ts) already has approval scaffolding from the editorial review flow); (c) author residency tenure check — surfaced from `user_profiles.home_city_id` + how long the user has held that home location; (d) gamification: award "City Guide" badge ([project_gamification](memory/project_gamification.md)) + 500 points on approval + bonus pool when guide gets top-rated reviews; (e) moderation reviewer toolset — surface duplicate-city detection ("3 other guides for Austin already published"). **Unblocks**: scales relocation content from 10 hand-written to 1000+ community-written guides without editorial bottleneck. |
| 1649 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P2 | `perf` | **Time-series partitioning for audit-required append-only tables** (opened 2026-05-26 from pass-9 scale audit). `points_ledger`, `point_redemptions`, `usage_ledger`, `xapi_statements`, `admin_audit_log` are append-only with no retention path (financial / compliance audit). At 1M users they'll cross 100M rows within 18 months. Conversion plan per table: (1) CREATE TABLE foo_new (...) PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at); (2) CREATE TABLE foo_yYYYY_mMM PARTITION OF foo_new FOR VALUES FROM ... TO ...; (3) INSERT INTO foo_new SELECT * FROM foo; (4) RENAME; (5) recreate FKs from dependent tables. Risky multi-step migration that requires a maintenance window — deferred until table row counts cross 10M (currently well below). **Unblocks**: parallel scans, efficient retention archive (drop old partition vs. millions of DELETEs), faster query plans at high cardinality. |
| 2148 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P2 | `quality` | **3D world multiplayer — DO ↔ Worker service binding so `claim_challenge` writes the ledger inside the DO** (opened 2026-05-26, follow-on to #1636). Today `useGameRoom.claimChallenge` issues the `/api/games/:projectId/challenge-complete` POST from the browser AND broadcasts to the room. The DO's `handleClaim` notes "fetch becomes a no-op without a service binding." Currently low-impact (fetch is the SSoT — points still land). **Fix path**: wire a Worker service binding so the DO can call the award path from its own runtime; move the ledger write fully inside the DO with the client only sending the broadcast. **Unblocks**: client-side claim can't be tampered with. |
| 823 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Frontend V1 `decideStudioQuota` caller bypasses ServiceProcessor** (opened 2026-05-18 — surfaced migrating server-side studio video quota to SP) | [StudioLayout.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioLayout.tsx) (V1 editor) still imports `decideStudioQuota` from `@shared/studio-quota` for the client-side pre-flight before hitting `/api/studio/upload`. Server side now routes through `servicesProcessor.enforce(c, "video_publish")` which uses the same lifetime semantic, so the two stay aligned — but the V1 caller will be deleted under #639 (V1 deprecation), at which point [shared/studio-quota.ts](hired.video/shared/studio-quota.ts) + its test + the `FREE_VIDEO_QUOTA` constant all become dead code. Either (a) wait for #639 cull (preferred — single coordinated deletion), or (b) replace the V1 client-side check with a `servicesProcessor.gate()`-equivalent SDK call from the frontend (lower leverage, more code now). Unblocks: zero parallel-source-of-truth at the client/server boundary; closes once #639 lands. |
| 1001 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Gamification — task-close detection only triggers via the legacy `metadata.legacyStatus` field; the new Drizzle `status` column on `tasks` is ignored** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #992 — surfaced wiring task completion to points) | [task.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/task.ts) uses `metadata.legacyStatus` (numeric ProductivityItemStatus) for the completion check because the legacy frontend payload writes it there. The Drizzle [productivity.ts](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/productivity.ts) `tasks.status` column (string default "todo") is the new home; nothing writes to it today (the existing route stores everything in jsonb metadata). To close: as part of the next task-API modernisation pass, dual-write status to both the column and metadata.legacyStatus, then move the points trigger to inspect the column. Holds until the legacy field is fully retired so we don't double-fire awards. |
| 1117 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Gamification fraud — device-fingerprint aggregation not sourced; the `device_cluster` heuristic no-ops because no telemetry table aggregates "active accounts on fingerprint X"** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #995) | [fraud-engine.ts](hired.video/api/src/domains/gamification/fraud-engine.ts) accepts `accountsOnDeviceFingerprint` as input and fires a medium-severity `device_cluster` flag when ≥3 — but [fraud-sweep.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/gamification/fraud-sweep.ts) leaves the value `undefined` because no upstream collector exists. Extension telemetry rows (`extension_telemetry`) have a per-event device id but it isn't denormalised into a queryable "accounts per device" view. To close: (a) add a `user_device_fingerprints` aggregate table (`user_id`, `fingerprint`, `last_seen_at`) populated by extension + PWA on boot; (b) extend the sweep with `count(distinct user_id) WHERE fingerprint = $current_user_fingerprint`; (c) write a backfill from existing telemetry. Pairs with #995. |
| 1120 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Gamification `markW9Collected` — collects only last-4 of tax id; the W-9 PDF + full identifier should live in encrypted KYC vendor storage, not nowhere** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #994 — surfaced building cashout) | [points-service](hired.video/api/src/domains/gamification/index.ts) `markW9Collected` records `tax_id_last4` + `legal_name` + `tax_classification` to `user_tax_status`, but the actual W-9 form (with full SSN/EIN, signature, mailing address) is not stored anywhere. IRS requires keeping the form for 4 years. To close: integrate a KYC vendor that handles W-9 collection + encrypted storage (Persona, Stripe Identity, or Veriff). Replace the current SA-types-it-in endpoint with a "send W-9 collection link" flow. The link captures the form, the vendor stores it, our row only holds the pointer + last-4. Unblocks: real 1099 reporting at year-end + audit-defensible W-9 trail. |
| 1146 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **`/rewards` not linked from public marketing nav — discovery for unauthenticated visitors is only via direct URL or a deep link from /points (which requires sign-in to be useful)** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1144) | The whole point of the page is incentive — visitors who see what they could earn before they sign up. Today they only find it if they navigate manually to `/rewards`. To close: add a "Rewards" entry to the public homepage nav (header link near /pricing), add an OG card meta in [useSEO](hired.video/frontend/lib/seo.ts), include /rewards in the sitemap.xml, and consider a small "earn $5+ in rewards" badge on /pricing pointing to /rewards. Pairs with #1144 + #1125 (UGC SEO audit). |
| 1632 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`fetchTemplates` already filtered by query but `fetchArticles` / `fetchGuides` / `fetchTools` / `fetchFaqs` didn't — fixed 2026-05-26, but the dispersed-search pattern remains a smell** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside the static-fetcher push-down fix). [card-feed.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/card-feed.ts) now has 5 static fetchers (`fetchTemplates`, `fetchArticles`, `fetchGuides`, `fetchTools`, `fetchFaqs`) each independently filtering its in-memory catalogue via a shared `matchesNeedle` helper. The fix is DRY at the *helper* level but the *call sites* still repeat the same pattern: `array.filter(item => matchesNeedle(search, item.title, item.summary, ...))`. Three follow-ups should land together: (a) factor each static catalogue into a `StaticContentSource<T>` interface — `{ all(): T[]; project(item: T): RawApiItem; matchFields(item: T): string[] }` — and have one shared `fetchStatic(source, limit, page, search)` driver; (b) make sure every static content type that ships in the future (events feed, learning paths feed, etc.) goes through `fetchStatic` instead of forking a new fetcher; (c) consider a generated search index (mini-Lunr or precomputed inverted index emitted at build time from BLOG_POSTS + HELP_GUIDES + TOOLS_CATALOG + HELP_FAQS) so the runtime cost stays sub-millisecond even as catalogues grow past ~1000 entries each. **Unblocks**: removes the "next person adding a static content kind forgets to wire search and the new entries are invisible until typed exactly" failure mode. |
| 1803 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **PLATFORM_PRESETS Pro-only gating is advertised but not enforced — `youtube-4k60` / `vimeo-prores-master` / `broadcast-1080i` reach the render facade without an entitlement check** (opened 2026-05-30 during #342 closure). [export-profiles.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/timeline/export-profiles.ts) ships `proOnly: true` on three presets. `ExportProfilePicker` paints a lock badge + disables the click handler when `proLocked` is true. But the render facade itself doesn't enforce entitlement — a caller that wires the picker without setting `proLocked` (or that constructs a `PlatformExportProfile` programmatically) can ship a 4K export on a free account. Fix: extend `renderTimeline` to check `opts.platformProfile.proOnly && !opts.isPro` and throw a `PRO_REQUIRED` error, mirroring the existing `requirePro("4K export")` middleware pattern on the server. Pairs with the #283 ProRes/DNxHR export work. |
