| 2009 | T2 | ⚠️ Partial | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Homepage positioning is individual-only — omits the platform's full breadth (B2B/ATS/recruiter, creator, learning, gamification)** (opened 2026-06-13) | The live hero WAS job-seeker-only and never surfaced the employer/recruiter side (ATS, recruiter marketplace, screening, People Ops), the creator economy, learning pathways/cohorts, or gamification. **Hero broadened 2026-06-13** (per user "broaden the hero") across en/es/fr-CA: `marketing.home.brandTagline` → "The All-in-One Talent Platform", `heroTitle` → "One AI Platform to Get Hired, Hire, and Grow", `heroSubtitle` + `faq.home.whatA` rewritten to span job seekers, recruiters, employers, and creators ([en.json](hired.video/frontend/public/locales/en.json#L867)). HR back-office deliberately EXCLUDED from live copy (it arrives via the embedded BurnRateOS suite #2008 — not yet shipped, would be overclaiming). **Residual (still job-seeker-narrow):** (1) the `/` SEO `title`/`description`/keywords in [seo.ts:95](hired.video/frontend/lib/seo.ts#L95) (deliberate "AI video resume" keyword-ranking artifact — broaden carefully without losing the SEO target); (2) the `HOME_FEATURES` + `HOME_HOW_IT_WORKS` + testimonials + stats blocks in [Home.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Home.tsx) still tell a single job-seeker story below the fold. Unblocks: full-page positioning that matches shipped breadth (not just the hero). |
| 2070 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Dashboard speedometer: add a real role-cohort average needle (today the benchmark is an honest fixed target)** (opened 2026-06-14 with the role-aware gauge) | The dials ([SpeedometerGauge](hired.video/frontend/components/dashboard/gauge/SpeedometerGauge.tsx) + builders in [lib/dashboard/gauge.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/dashboard/gauge.ts)) render a `benchmark` needle labelled honestly as a TARGET ("Job-ready / Established / Healthy / Cash out") — it is NOT presented as a fake "org average", so nothing is misleading. Adding a true peer-average like the reference screenshot is a deliberate follow-up, not a quick win: the composite score includes `onboardingCompletionPercentage`, which is computed per-user (not a column), so averaging the real score across a role cohort means either (a) an O(N-users) live recompute of onboarding per request — the exact recompute-slow-data / fan-out perf anti-pattern our conventions forbid — or (b) materializing a per-user score column + a recompute job. **Plan**: extract the score formula into `shared/`, add a nightly/materialized per-user score, then a cached (`getOrSetCached`, role-keyed) `/api/dashboard/benchmarks` endpoint averaging it; feed into `GaugeModel.benchmark`. **Unblocks**: the "you vs. your peers" needle. |
| 2121 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **/search list-view (non-grid) titles aren't hyperlinks for marketplace result types** (opened 2026-06-07 alongside the "make every result-card title a hyperlink" pass) | The grid view now links every card title to its detail page, and the list view's `entityHref()` ([UnifiedSearch.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/UnifiedSearch.tsx)) maps resume/job/company/people/video/`href` → a `<Link>` title. But `course` / `service` / `voice` / `template` results (folded into `combinedItems`) have no entry in `entityHref()`, so in **list view only** their titles fall back to a no-op `<button>` (`handleView` also no-ops for them) — they're neither clickable nor right-clickable. Grid view is unaffected (each renders its dedicated card with a linked title). Fix: extend `entityHref()` with the marketplace routes (`/courses/:authorSlug/:slug`, `/people/:providerSlug?tab=services`, `/marketplace/voices/:voiceCloneId`, `/marketplace/templates/:slug`) — ideally promoting it to a shared result→URL helper. Unblocks: consistent deep-linking + right-click-open across both view modes. (Note: the parallel `DiscoverPreview` discover rail that previously duplicated this mapping was deleted 2026-06-14 — the dashboard now reuses `UnifiedSearch`.) |
