| 1119 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **Gamification — dedicated saved-search runner that fires `saved_search.run` when the search delivers ≥1 new match (not just on create)** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #999) | The Phase-5 wiring fires `onSavedSearchRun` on POST /api/search/saved (create), which is the strongest signal we have today. The original product intent ("Saved-search delivered new jobs") needs a periodic worker that re-runs each `saved_searches` row, diffs against the user's prior matches, and fires the award once per day a new job lands. To close: register a worker in [workers/registry.ts](hired.video/api/src/workers/registry.ts) following the existing pattern (`job-scraper` is the closest analogue); per-user cadence; on each tick run the saved-search query, hash the result set, compare to the stored hash, fire `onSavedSearchRun` if delta > 0. Unblocks: streak counter advances purely from passive saved-search delivery, not just active creation. Pairs with #999. |
| 1135 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **Gamification — server-push badge unlocks instead of 60s client poll** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1134) | [BadgeUnlockToaster.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/badges/BadgeUnlockToaster.tsx) polls `GET /api/points/me` every 60s + on window focus and diffs the badges list against a localStorage snapshot. Good enough for v1; the unlock toast can lag the earning action by up to 60 seconds (or until the next focus). To close: either (a) integrate SignalR / WebSocket push for `badge.unlocked` events (the SignalR client already lives at [signalr-service.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/signalr-service.ts) — the GamificationService's `onBadgeUnlock` would emit), or (b) have award-firing routes (POST /task/save, POST /feed/posts, etc.) return a `badgesUnlocked: PointsBadge[]` field in their response so the calling component invalidates `["points", "me"]` immediately. Option (b) is cheaper but only catches client-initiated unlocks; option (a) also catches server-side unlocks (e.g. nightly fraud sweep reversals). |
