| 2052 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Per-platform social OAuth endpoint/scope strings need verification against live developer apps; X PKCE + TikTok `client_key` + Meta IG-Business flow unverified** (opened 2026-06-14 during #2051 implementation) | The config-driven OAuth runner ([platform-config.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/social/platform-config.ts) + [social-oauth.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/social/social-oauth.ts)) is provider-agnostic and follows each platform's published OAuth docs, but the exact authorize/token URLs, scope strings, and token-response parsing per platform have NOT been exercised against real credentials (none provisioned yet). Known things to confirm on first live connect: TikTok uses `client_key` (not `client_id`) + the `open.tiktokapis.com` token host (distinct from the ads `business-api` app); X requires OAuth2 PKCE + a paid tier; Instagram publishing needs a Business/Creator acct linked to an FB Page (personal → manual-upload fallback). A wrong scope/endpoint is a one-line fix in the config table — but it can't be validated until the developer apps + Secrets exist. Pairs with the per-platform app-review prerequisite (#2045). |
