| 2113 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Creator templates absent from organic SEO — the discovery engine doesn't index `studio_templates` and there's no AI-generated landing page for template categories ("Best onboarding templates", "Best CTA templates")** (2026-05-14 — publish-templates gap analysis) | [discovery.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/discovery.ts) covers talent feed, job board, salary insights, resume guides but has no studio-template handler. The voice clone marketplace, jobs, and resume guides all have AI-generated SEO landing pages (e.g. `GET /api/discovery/seo/resume-guide/:jobSlug`); studio templates have none. Also no confirmation that `/marketplace/templates/:slug` is in the XML sitemap or that robots.txt permits indexing. Fix: (a) add `GET /api/discovery/seo/template-guide/:categorySlug` returning an AI-generated guide ("Best testimonial video templates") with 24h CDN cache; (b) include marketplace template URLs in the sitemap generator; (c) verify robots.txt. Unblocks: organic discovery — creators see traffic that doesn't depend on logged-in marketplace browsing. |
| 892 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`/services/creator` header is conditionally hidden, but `/services/inquiries` + the dashboard still render "Services / Dashboard, offerings, and incoming leads" — the header is inconsistent across the four sub-tabs** (opened 2026-05-20 — surfaced fixing #890's header request) | Per user feedback the `<h1>Services</h1>` + subheading on [ServicesManagement.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/ServicesManagement.tsx) is redundant on `/services/creator` because Content Creator already renders its own heading inside [ContentCreatorSection](hired.video/frontend/components/creator/ContentCreatorSection.tsx). The fix this pass gates the header with `activeTab !== "creator"`, but dashboard + inquiries still carry it. Either the header should drop everywhere (the `ServicesNav` tab strip already labels which surface you're on) OR every sub-tab should host its own H1 the way Content Creator does. Pick one — the half-and-half state is the worst-of-both. Unblocks: consistent page header shape across `/services`, `/services/creator`, `/services/inquiries`, `/services/offerings`. |
| 923 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Voice templates (Phase 4) ship with audio-only WAV export but the voice-specific intake + voice-marketplace publish handler + profile audio embed are still stubs** (opened 2026-05-21 — Phase 4 of [docs/prd/studio-media-kinds.md](hired.video/docs/prd/studio-media-kinds.md); landed alongside the catalog entries) | The Phase 4 catalog entries (`voice_audition_reel / voice_ivr_prompt / voice_audiobook_chapter`) reuse the generic `BasicIntake` (prose prompt) instead of a kind-shaped form, and `publishDestinationsFor("voice")` returns rows whose handlers are still undefined — the menu disables them with the existing "soon" hint. To close: (a) `VoiceIntake.tsx` with a script textarea (incl. character count + WPM-at-150wpm estimate), voice-clone picker reading `studio_voice_clones` from the existing marketplace ([project_voice_marketplace](hired.video/.claude/projects/c--code-hired/memory/project_voice_marketplace.md)), and a language / gender / accent chip row that writes to the future `voice_listings` metadata; swap each voice template's `IntakeForm` from `BasicIntake → VoiceIntake`. (b) `publishHandlers["voice-marketplace"]` callback in `StudioEditorV2` that mints a `studio_voice_clones` row from the rendered WAV + the source project metadata, marks it `visibility = 'unlisted'`, and routes the creator to `/marketplace/voices/:slug` for final pricing. (c) `publishHandlers["profile-audio-embed"]` callback that uploads the WAV to R2 + writes a `creator_audio_embeds` row pointing the user's profile page at it. (d) Per-kind metadata in `ProjectDetailsSheet` for voice — script word count, language, voice-clone-id, target platform — symmetric with the podcast metadata follow-on tracked in #907. Pairs with #907 (per-kind metadata + ID3 transcode share infrastructure). Unblocks: voice projects authored on hired.video can ship as marketplace listings or profile audio embeds, instead of dead-ending at "download WAV". |
| 1631 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **UnifiedSearch query is exact-substring only — no typo tolerance / stemming / synonyms** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside the static-fetcher push-down fix that made `/?q=research` return the Employer Research tool + the "How to Use the Employer Research Tool" blog post). After this pass, each per-type static fetcher in [card-feed.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/card-feed.ts) filters its in-memory catalogue with a lowercased substring match BEFORE pagination — without this, the recency sort buried relevant articles off page 1 (first 2 articles fetched were always the newest by `publishedAt`, even when none matched the query). `matchesNeedle` is intentionally simple — it doesn't tolerate typos (`reserach` → `research`), doesn't stem (`researching` → `research`), and has no synonym table (`employer` ↔ `company`, `salary` ↔ `compensation` ↔ `pay`, `research` ↔ `audit` ↔ `review`). All three are real user expectations on a search box that says "Search" not "Exact substring search". **Fix path**: (a) cheap win — handcrafted synonym map in `card-feed.ts` for the top ~30 employment-domain pairs, applied on both sides of the match; (b) fuzzy match — wire Fuse.js or a manual Levenshtein-distance-2 check against title/name so single-character typos still hit; (c) stemming — Porter stemmer is ~3kB and tolerates `-ing` / `-ed` / `-s`. None of these are in place today; the current pass deliberately scoped to "fix the literal-match case for the article the user named" and left these as the obvious follow-ups. **Adjacent**: the same fetchers ignore Unicode normalisation, so an accented input or a smart quote doesn't normalise to its ASCII equivalent — surfaces when international content lands on the platform (#1148). |
| 1904 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **UnifiedSearch facet "Available for sessions"** (opened 2026-06-04 from #1648 close). The bookings program is wired through `creator_profiles.bookings_active` but UnifiedSearch ([UnifiedSearch.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/UnifiedSearch.tsx)) doesn't yet surface a "Available for sessions" filter that pivots off it. Fix: (a) backend — add an `audience: bookings` row to [content_audiences](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/contentAudiences.ts) on every host with at least one active `booking_offerings` row (write-side hook on offering create/deactivate); (b) frontend — add a "Available for sessions" toggle in the People facet panel that adds `?audience=bookings` to the search query; (c) discovery boost — sort hosts with upcoming availability above hosts whose grid is fully booked for the next 7 days. Aligns with the existing audience taxonomy infrastructure from #1629. Unblocks: visitors can find coaches by "I want to book a session" intent instead of having to know the coach's name in advance. |
| 1962 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Dashboard feed — organic auto-aggregation of recent public content** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1961) | #1961 ships ONLY the SuperAdmin-curated layer. The original ask also wanted "if other users create public content it shows in the feed." Add an organic tier below the curated cards: pull recent PUBLIC articles/videos/public resumes (gated by the existing creator-visibility + privacy rules) via the `fetchCardFeed` pipeline (or a backend aggregator), de-duped against curated picks and the viewer's own content, cached with a version-token key. Unblocks: the dashboard staying fresh without per-role manual curation. |
