| 756 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **Orphaned i18n keys after HeroVideoSpotlight cleanup** (2026-05-17 — surfaced while removing the click-through overlay and "Browse Number Video Resumes" button) | These [en.json](hired.video/frontend/public/locales/en.json) entries no longer have a consumer: `labels.openVideoResumeAria`, `labels.nowPlaying`, `labels.featured`, `actions.watch`, `actions.createYours`, `actions.browseNumberVideoResumes`, `actions.browseVideoResumes`, `labels.byCreator`. Fix: grep all locale files, drop the orphan keys, audit with a CI lint that fails the build when an i18n key has zero `t("…")` references. Unblocks: smaller translation bundle, no dead copy in fr/es/de mirrors. |
| 868 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **Per-program tab strip can carry 7+ tabs (Profile + Company + 5 programs) and overflows narrow viewports** (opened 2026-05-19 — same per-program tab refactor) | [`PageHeader`](hired.video/frontend/components/PageHeader.tsx) renders tabs in a horizontal underlined row. A creator enrolled in all 5 programs on an employer profile gets Profile + Company + Video Promo + Voice Clone + Services + Articles + Courses = 7 tabs, exceeding the visible row on phones and short laptop widths. The existing PageHeader has no overflow handling — tabs wrap onto a second line. Fix: either (a) make PageHeader's tab row horizontally scrollable on overflow (matches /jobs and /search behaviour with the chip strip), or (b) collapse low-priority tabs into a "More ▾" menu past N visible. Same pattern would apply to any other surface that ever grows past 5 tabs. Unblocks: clean tab strip for creators enrolled in many programs and for the future-state when sub-programs (#867 counts gate, sub-tabs per program) land. |
| 954 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **/studio marketing landing Testimonials section deleted — real customer quotes needed before re-adding** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced closing #953; partial closure 2026-05-22 — Stats grid replaced with architecture-driven facts + Testimonials section removed because the existing 3 quotes were placeholder names with fabricated copy; remains open until we have actual creator quotes to ship) | **Status: Stats half closed; Testimonials half intentionally deferred.** Stats grid (was "60s / 3× / 85% / 500K+ Video resumes created") replaced with architecturally-true facts derived from the kind registry: ``${listShippableKindPitches().length}+ Creator formats in one studio`` (computed — ticks up as new kinds ship), `60s AI scaffolds your first scene`, `100% In-browser render — no install`, `Free First project on every account`. Testimonials section (was "Sarah Chen / Michael Rodriguez / Emma Johnson" with fabricated interview-win quotes) **deleted entirely** per the user directive "don't use fake creator quotes." Hero's `HeroVideoSpotlight` still surfaces SA-curated real public projects, so anonymous visitors see actual creator output without us fabricating. To re-open the social-proof slot: gather 1-2 testimonials per shipping format from beta users / friendly creators with permission to attribute. Until then the gap is a positioning weakness, not a UX bug — every other surface (What you can make, Features, FAQ) carries the multi-kind story. |
| 2069 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Synth patch persistence + preset library + marketplace (file-only presets aren't a first-class asset)** (opened 2026-06-14) | The APEX synth port (#457 ✅) saves/loads patches only as downloaded JSON files ([synth-preset.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/audio/synth-preset.ts)) — there is no persistent library, no browse/search, and no way to share or sell a patch, even though the standalone APEX app *mocked* a `/presets` browser. Meanwhile voice clones ([studio_voice_clones], `project_voice_marketplace`) and templates ([studio_templates] + `template_licenses`, `project_template_marketplace`) already have the full publish→price→license→buy machinery. A `SynthPatch` is a *smaller* asset (pure JSONB, no R2 media, no consent surface). Fix: new `studio_synth_patches` table mirroring `studioVoiceClones`'s columns (visibility/priceCents/platformFeeBps/view+purchase counts), reuse the polymorphic `template_licenses` ledger (add `templateKind:'synth_patch'`) rather than a bespoke license table, route family mirroring `/api/studio/voice-clones/*` (`library`/`marketplace`/`POST`/`PATCH`/`claim`/cart-checkout) with read-through cache + write-invalidation + version-token marketplace key, and a "My patches / Browse patches" surface reusing the existing marketplace card + cart. Keep file export as the portable escape hatch. Full spec: [synthesizer-apex-music-studio.md §6 Phase 2](hired.video/docs/prd/synthesizer-apex-music-studio.md). Unblocks: synth patches as a shareable/monetizable creator asset + the real version of APEX's mock preset browser. |
