| 910 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **`promoteWithoutAuth` tabs only show creator programs an owner has formally enrolled in — a creator who has services / articles / courses but skipped `/api/creators/opt-in` still presents no creator tabs to unauthenticated visitors** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced while fixing the owner-view "no tabs" bug) | The PeopleDetail tab strip is now `isOwner ? all : enrolledOnly` so the owner case is handled, but visitors (including the unauthenticated `promoteWithoutAuth` traffic) still see only programs where `creator_profiles.*_active = true`. A creator who has 3 service offerings + 2 published articles but never POSTed to `/api/creators/opt-in` shows zero creator tabs to a promotion-traffic visitor — the entire reason they enabled `promoteWithoutAuth` is wasted. Fix: derive the visitor tab list from "owner has content OR is enrolled" instead of enrollment alone — query existing content counts per program when building the public DTO (`services.count > 0` for services tab, `articles.count > 0` for articles, etc.) and union with the `*_active` flags. Avoids forcing every casual content publisher through a formal enrollment wizard before their work surfaces on their own profile. Pairs with #887 (unauth gate propagation to detail pages — same DRY hook target). Unblocks: a creator opt-ing into `promoteWithoutAuth` immediately gets a useful promotional landing page even before completing the creator-program opt-in flow. |
| 950 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **MediaPicker Library tab lists only the 100 most recent uploads with no pagination + no per-asset metadata (dimensions, project-of-origin, creation date as a sortable column)** (opened 2026-05-22 — surfaced wiring #933 Phase 1; the LibraryTab is a single-page grid for now) | The new "Library" tab in `MediaPicker.tsx` calls `listMyImages()` which calls `GET /api/upload/images` with `limit: 100`. For prolific creators that fills up quickly. Fix: (a) server-side cursor pagination on `bucket.list({ cursor })`; (b) client-side infinite scroll via IntersectionObserver; (c) per-asset metadata sidebar (the `creator_assets` table from #940 / #933 Phase 2 would carry these fields — uploadedAt is already returned but dimensions / originProject would come from that table). Pairs with #940 Phase 2 + #933 Phase 2 — the metadata table closes both gaps in one pass. |
