| 1152 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Future | P3 | `feature` | **Europe expansion — data-residency schema (`country_code` / `data_region` / `jurisdiction` on users) + dual-region routing layer (US + EU Neon/R2/Worker), fr-FR + de-DE locales, GDPR rights section, DPA + Article 30 records + DPO, EU AI Act compliance audit for resume scoring / matching / voice cloning, VAT MOSS via Stripe Tax, optional UK GDPR variant** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1148) | Full design in PRD §3 (data-residency architecture) + §8 Phase 3. Depends on #1148/#1149/#1150/#1151/#1153 + a sustained business case for EU expansion. The data-residency work is the engineering bulk: (a) add `country_code` (user-declared, not geo-IP), `data_region` ('us'\|'eu', frozen at signup), `jurisdiction` (derived label) columns on `users`; (b) JWT carries `region` claim; (c) CF Worker reads region claim + cookie and proxies to US or EU origin; (d) spin up EU Neon `eu-west-1` + EU R2 bucket; (e) catalogues (template marketplace, voice clone marketplace, public jobs, public articles) stay US-only — only user-owned PII region-pinned; (f) federated cross-region read for US-recruiter-EU-applicant flow via Postgres logical replication of `application_inbox` materialized view (open question — see PRD §9). Plus the compliance + i18n work for the EU market. Doing this BEFORE EU revenue is premature; the schema can land before the infra (no-op while `data_region='us'` is the only value) to avoid a hard cutover. |
