| 2163 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `quality` | **`BlogIndex` fetches up to 120 articles client-side with no pagination + no caching** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1315; intentionally deferred 2026-05-25). [BlogIndex.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/blog/BlogIndex.tsx) calls `articleService.listPublished({ limit: 120 })` on mount and merges client-side with the 9 static `BLOG_POSTS`. Today the total is ~23 items — well under the 120 ceiling — and the page renders in one fetch. Deferred to P4 because shipping cursor pagination now is premature optimisation: at current volume the in-memory chip-filter UX (instant filtering, no fetch on chip click) is materially better than paginated chunks. Re-open when `articles` row count crosses ~500 (creator authoring + AI-assisted drafts scale faster than editorial). To close at that point: (a) add `cursor` query param to `/api/articles/public` keyed on `published_at`, (b) frontend `useInfinitePosts(query, category)` hook with `IntersectionObserver` on the last grid row, (c) restore a chip-count source that doesn't require the full set in memory (server returns category facet counts alongside the page). |

