| 2044 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Now | P1 | `feature` | **Phase 1 — `SocialPublisher` seam + YouTube refactor + generalized Lane-B gate + `social_connections`** (opened 2026-06-13, [PRD](hired.video/docs/prd/social-media-publishing-and-distribution.md) §5.1/§5.2/§8, #2043) | One `SocialAdapter` interface + `buildSocialPublisher(env)` factory (the `match-handlers.ts`/`LLMClient` DI pattern); refactor the working YouTube publish behind it with **zero behavior change** and drop the bespoke route code (dead-code rule). Generalize `requirePro("YouTube Publishing")` → a reusable `runSelfPublishGate` (entitlement→connection→token-refresh→publish) returning typed envelopes so the client renders the right inline prompt. New `social_connections` table (generalizes `youtube_accounts`; encrypted tokens per the [oauth.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/oauth.ts) precedent, never shipped to browser) + `/settings/connections` for YouTube. Migration `0217_social_connections.sql` (idempotent per #1625). **NB: the connection-layer half (`social_connections` + OAuth connect/disconnect + `/settings/connections` + the cached Lane-B availability gate) SHIPPED under #2051 (2026-06-14).** Remaining for this phase: the `SocialAdapter` publish/upload seam + refactoring the existing YouTube *upload* behind it + `runSelfPublishGate` wrapping the actual publish call. |
