| 1688 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `quality` | **#1627/#1673-#1679 exec-suite — deploy-ordering, route-test coverage, and scale watch-items (self-assessment 2026-05-28)** surfaced reviewing the senior-exec batch; logged, not yet addressed. **(a) Deploy ordering [P1-flavored]**: migrations 0166/0169/0174 add columns that EXISTING read paths now hard-depend on — 0169 `confidential_mode` is referenced by the public people search ([search.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/search.ts) people clause + [/api/users/public](hired.video/api/src/routes/users.ts)) and 0174 `confidential_blocklist` by recruiter search; 0166 `content_audiences`/`cities.slug`/`population` by the audience filter + sitemap + LocationService. If code deploys BEFORE these migrations run, those endpoints 500 (not just the new feature — the whole people/recruiter search). The `_sql_migrations` runner applies migrations on deploy, so the deploy step MUST run migrations before serving new code; verify the deploy sequence. None of these have been run against the DB yet — 0166/0167/0168/0169/0173/0174/0175/0176 are all PENDING. **(b) Route-handler test coverage gap**: pure logic is unit-tested (employment-types 5/5, comp-analyzer 6/6, pipeline-masking 5/5 = 16) but the DB-touching handlers are NOT — references ACL/NDA flow, network warm-intro graph walk, retained-search filters, recruiter-search blocklist gating, and the pipeline-masking integration have no integration tests and weren't run against a DB. Add handler tests (node:test + a fake/seeded db) before relying on these in prod. **(c) Scale watch-items**: network warm-intros ([network.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/network.ts)) loads the caller's connections + all THEIR connections in-memory — fine for typical users, but a super-connector (10k+ edges) makes the `edges` query large; cap or paginate. Recruiter-search blocklist is a per-candidate-row correlated `NOT EXISTS` subquery (cheap PK lookup + tiny jsonb unnest) — fine for normal result sets, watch at very large N. **Unblocks**: hardening the exec suite for production — none of these block functional correctness, but (a) is a real deploy hazard and (b) is the verification debt from building 8 features without a live DB/browser. |
| 758 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **PWA Service Worker `periodicSync` not wired — client sync only fires when a tab is open + the user clicks Sync** (2026-05-17 — surfaced while closing #755) | [`EmailSyncButton`](hired.video/frontend/components/communication/EmailSyncButton.tsx) fires `runClientSync` on user click; no background-sync registration exists. Chromium browsers support `navigator.serviceWorker.ready` → `registration.periodicSync.register("email-sync", { minInterval: 15min })` with the `periodic-background-sync` permission — Service Worker can call the ingest endpoint while the app is closed. Firefox/Safari don't support periodicSync; for those, tab-focus polling (already attached to `useGatedResource`) is the best we can do. Fix: (a) extend [`vite.config.ts`](hired.video/frontend/vite.config.ts) VitePWA registration to include a Service Worker that handles the `periodicsync` event by POSTing to `/api/inbox/external-emails/ingest` directly. (b) Register the periodic sync on first successful manual sync. (c) Show a "Background sync: on/off" toggle in InboxSettingsSheet. Unblocks: inbox stays fresh even when the user hasn't opened the tab in days, without the original Cloudflare Workers subrequest budget being touched. |
| 977 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Bing Ads adapter — geo / demographic / device criteria not wired** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #975) | [adapters/bing/index.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/paid-media/adapters/bing/index.ts) `createAdSet()` creates the AdGroup but skips `/campaignCriterions` + `/adGroupCriterions` calls. Same shape as #976 but against the Microsoft REST surface. Without it, Bing ad groups run untargeted. To close: add a follow-up mutate batch after `createAdSet()` that iterates `TargetingSpec`, mapping geo → `LocationCriterion`, age → `AgeCriterion`, gender → `GenderCriterion`, device → `DeviceCriterion`. Mirror the pattern from the upcoming #976 fix so Google + Bing share a `applyTargetingCriteria(ctx, adGroupId, spec)` helper hoisted into [services/paid-media/targeting.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/paid-media/targeting.ts). |
| 1822 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **CHRO roster: invite-on-add + accept-time identity relink** (opened 2026-05-31, from the reuse review). Today "Add employee" with an email that matches an active company member auto-links the `user_id`; a non-member email becomes a placeholder. The full foundation reuse is: a non-member add should call the existing `inviteAccountUser()` (services/user/account.ts → `account_invitations`, role=employee) and set `people_employees.invitation_id`; then on invite **accept** (acceptInvitation) a hook should relink that roster row's `invitation_id → user_id` so the placeholder/invited row becomes a native member without a duplicate. Unblocks: the roster drives the invite funnel end-to-end (employer adds → invite sent → accept → billable seat), instead of placeholders that never convert. |
| 1841 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Scheduled check-in dispatch cron runner** (opened 2026-05-31). `people_scheduled_check_ins` carries frequency/day/time/timezone + `next_scheduled_at`, but no runner sends them yet. Wire a job in scheduled.ts that, per Segment timezone, finds due check-ins, dispatches (notification/email), stamps `last_sent_at` + recomputes `next_scheduled_at` (idempotent, no double-send in a window). Closes the PO-6 "schema but no runner" build requirement. |
| 1905 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `bug` | **Magic-link email delivery for new reservations** (opened 2026-06-04 from #1648 close). [BookingsService.createReservation](hired.video/api/src/services/bookings/BookingsService.ts) returns the `magicLinkToken` in the immediate POST response, and the frontend [BookPage](hired.video/frontend/pages/bookings/BookPage.tsx) redirects the booker to `/book/:handle/r/:token` on the same session — so the booker has the link **for this browser session only**. If they close the tab or use a different device, the token is lost (the magic link was never emailed). Fix: on `createReservation`, enqueue an email send to `bookerEmail` with the magic-link URL and reservation summary, via the existing [scheduled.ts](hired.video/api/src/scheduled.ts) email dispatcher path (the `send_email` queue type wires through SendGrid). Second pass: send a reminder email 24h + 1h before the reservation. Unblocks: bookers retain access to their reservation across devices; reduces no-shows via reminders. |
| 2032 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `bug` | **About + Careers marketing pages ship fabricated, mutually-inconsistent vanity stats; About's "team" is one hardcoded person** (found 2026-06-13, marketing-page validation) | [About.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/About.tsx) (~:103) hardcodes "50K+ active users / 1M+ videos created / 500+ companies / 95% satisfaction"; [Careers.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Careers.tsx) (~:142) hardcodes "50+ team members / 100K+ users helped / 15+ countries / 95% satisfaction" — the user count (50K vs 100K) directly contradicts About. None are data-sourced. Separately, About's "Our Team" grid (`lg:grid-cols-4`, ~:248) fetches the single profile `userService.getUserBySlug("seanhogg")` and renders it under a team heading, implying a team that isn't shown. Careers also hardcodes its hiring-process/FAQ/CTA copy in English (~:351-458), bypassing the `t()` i18n used elsewhere on the page (breaks es/fr-CA). Fix: source stats from real metrics or remove; reconcile the two pages; reframe the team section as "Founder" or populate a real roster; move Careers static copy into the translation catalog. |
