| 2008 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Embeddable HR suite — BurnRateOS-built, hired.video-embedded (makes "all-in-one HR platform" true by embedding)** (opened 2026-06-13) | hired.video's People Ops stops at roster + org-chart + 1:1s + action items (`native-only for now`, [project_chro_people_ops]); there is no personnel file, PTO/leave, performance cycle, comp/benefits, or signed-document trail, so the employer-side "HR platform" claim is aspirational. Per the deliberate moat split ([integrations-and-sourcing.md §0](hired.video/docs/prd/integrations-and-sourcing.md)), the HR back-office is a B2B-ops product **BurnRateOS builds + owns**; hired.video embeds it via a billed `/v1/hr/*` external API + an HR `<script>` widget, surfaced inside the existing People Ops chrome. Full spec: [embeddable-hr-suite.md](hired.video/docs/prd/embeddable-hr-suite.md) (5 phases: Personnel+identity-bridge → Time/Leave → Performance → Comp/Benefits/Docs → Analytics). hired.video build is thin: `burnrateos_employee_id` foreign ref on `user_company_role_associations`, embedded read-through-cached panels, a shared `useHrEntitlement()` gate, `canActFor()` + tenant-isolation on both sides, HR as a paid add-on SKU (not a per-seat bump). PII/PHI + DSR + residency concentrate in BurnRateOS per [international-expansion-and-data-residency.md](hired.video/docs/prd/international-expansion-and-data-residency.md). Unblocks: the legitimate "all-in-one HR platform" positioning. |
