| 370 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **6 profile edit dialogs duplicate the same `updateProfile → refreshUser → onSaved → onOpenChange` save flow** | `frontend/components/profile/dialogs/{EditHeader,EditAbout,EditContact,EditSocialProfiles,EditSkills,EditCustomUrl}Dialog.tsx` each open-code an identical `useState(saving) + try/await updateProfile + refreshUser + onSaved?.() + onOpenChange(false) + catch console.error + finally setSaving(false)` block. Per the DRY rule. Fix: extract `useProfileSectionSaver({ onClose, onSaved, errorMessage })` returning `{ saving, save(updates) }` so each dialog drops the boilerplate to one hook + one form-payload `save()` call. Identified 2026-05-05 while wiring `onSaved` into all six dialogs to fix the post-edit refresh bug on `/people/:uuid`. |
| 440 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`PeopleCard.test.tsx` requires AuthProvider but the test setup doesn't supply one — 8 tests fail with "useAuth must be used within an AuthProvider" because `EntityVideos` mounted by `PeopleCard` calls `useApiReady`** (2026-05-07) | Pre-existing failure surfaced when verifying ownership-bug fix. Either wrap the test render in a stub AuthProvider or mock `useApiReady` in the test setup. Unblocks: `PeopleCard` regressions can be caught by CI. Identified 2026-05-07 fixing /jobs Delete-on-non-owned bug. |
| 803 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`addTrackedPerson` / `removeTrackedPerson` in People.tsx are console.log stubs — Follow / Unfollow on /people is a no-op** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced refactoring connection-status fetch out of People.tsx) | [People.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/People.tsx) lines 414-435 contain two async helpers whose entire body is `console.log("Track person X for user Y")` plus a commented-out `userService.followUser(personId)` call. They're wired to `handleTrackPerson` / `handleUntrackPerson` → `PeopleCard`'s Follow chip. Clicking Follow on a person on /people does nothing visible (no optimistic state, no network call) and the underlying [userService.followUser / unfollowUser](hired.video/frontend/lib/services/user-service.ts) endpoints already exist. Spec: replace the console.log with the real service call, mirror the optimistic pattern used by `JobCard` (#676) so the chip flips immediately on click, refetch on settle. Pairs with #802 — once a real tracked list flows in, the toggle has somewhere to land. Unblocks: working Follow / Unfollow on the People surface. |
| 880 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`check429`'s USAGE_LIMIT upgrade pill still posts into the global `#quickStatus` banner — same root cause as #879 for the row-action 429 case** (opened 2026-05-20 — surfaced building #879) | [check429](hiredvideo-chrome-extension/shared/utils.js) renders a full upgrade-CTA card (progress bar + "Upgrade" button + usage X/Y) into the element id passed as `targetId` — every caller passes `'quickStatus'`, which is the shared page-banner element. When a row-action (`rowTailorJob`, `rowScoreJob`, etc.) hits the per-user token budget, the upgrade pill lands in the top page banner instead of the row that triggered the 429 — same visual disconnect #879 just fixed for plain errors. Fix: thread a `target` (element-or-id) through every row-action call, point it at a new `.tracked-job-row-rate-limit` slot in the row template (mirrors `.tracked-job-row-error` from #879), and DRY the upgrade-pill HTML out into a helper that both the global banner and the row slot reuse. Unblocks: full per-row error/limit/upgrade UX consistency; no "why is my Tailor failure showing up in a banner about a totally different job" reports. |
| 1324 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Discover map sub-view ignores the q/category/format filters that narrow the grid sub-view** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1323). [EventDiscoveryPanel.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/events/EventDiscoveryPanel.tsx) renders one filter row (search box + category select + format select) that drives the grid via `eventsService.search()`. The map sub-view uses [/api/map](hired.video/api/src/routes/map.ts) which only accepts a bounding box (`minLat/maxLat/minLng/maxLng`) — flipping to the map view drops the filter narrowing the user is looking at. To close: extend `/api/map` to accept `q`, `category`, `format`, and `scope` query params; mirror the where-clause used by `EventService.search()`; thread the same `q/category/format` state from `EventDiscoveryPanel` into the map fetch URL so toggling Grid ↔ Map preserves the filter narrowing. Map endpoint should also collapse very dense bbox responses with marker clustering (#1259) so filter+zoom UX is consistent. |
| 2103 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **`/for/[audience]` landing pages + shared audience registry body copy still English** (opened 2026-06-07 with the W-language chrome sweep) | The footer resource-maps ([AudienceLinks.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/landing/AudienceLinks.tsx)) now resolve the short audience LABEL through i18n (`audiences.<key>.label`, registry-label fallback) for all 14 life-stage audiences. But the rest of the shared registry ([shared/audiences-registry.ts](hired.video/shared/audiences-registry.ts)) — each audience's `thesis`, the `FEATURES.*` `label`+`blurb` catalog, and `ctaPrimary`/`ctaSecondary` labels — is still raw English, consumed by the `/for/[audience]` hero + `<ToolShowcase>` tabs. Extend the same `audiences.<key>.*` / `audienceFeatures.<key>.*` key convention with a shared resolver so the landing pages localize too. Unblocks: fully localized audience landing pages. |
