| 867 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Visitors see per-program tabs even when the creator has zero published items in that program — tab strip carries "empty" tabs as noise** (opened 2026-05-19 — same per-program tab refactor) | [`PeopleDetail.tsx`](hired.video/frontend/pages/PeopleDetail.tsx) derives the tab list from `profile.creatorPrograms` (enrollment), not from "has at least one public item". An enrolled-but-empty program shows a visitor tab that opens to a tiny "Nothing published yet" card. For owners that's correct (they see the publish CTA), but for visitors it's clutter. Fix: extend `toUserProfileDto` ([users.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/users.ts)) to return per-program **counts** (cheap COUNT(*) on each table where `userId = ? AND status = 'published'`), and filter the visitor tab strip on `count > 0`. Owners still see all enrolled tabs. Pairs with the existing `creatorPrograms` flag shape so the wire stays one object. Unblocks: clean tab strip for visitors viewing creators with selective publishing. |
| 1844 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **People-Ops UI is partly generic — bespoke pages for the richest surfaces** (opened 2026-05-31). All 13 People-Ops surfaces are functional via `/api/people/*` + rendered through the generic descriptor-driven `ResourceManager` at `/people/s/*` (list + create + delete). The flagship surfaces deserve bespoke UIs beyond generic CRUD: objectives with nested outcomes/milestones + rollup, scorecards with the metric-snapshot grid, weekly-syncs agenda/metrics editor, meeting-intelligence summarize button + extracted-action-item view, workflow action-builder + run/execution history, headcount plan builder with the `/:id/summary`. Unblocks: first-class UX for the high-interaction surfaces (the generic manager covers CRUD but not the nested/compute affordances the APIs already expose). |
| 1968 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Feed link-preview endpoint is still a stub** (opened 2026-06-07, pre-existing) | `POST /api/feed/link-preview` ([feed.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/feed.ts)) echoes the URL back with empty title/description/image — the composer's link card shows the bare URL only. Wire real OpenGraph scraping (reuse the OG fetch path the page-embed/marketing surfaces use) so pasted links render a proper preview card. Also: the standalone `Feed.tsx` default page export is dead (only its named `FeedFilterTabs`/`FeedRightPanel` exports are reused by Home; `/feed`→`/dashboard`) — fold the live feed into Home or delete the dead default export. |
| 887 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **`promoteWithoutAuth` only suppresses the AuthOverlay on `/people/:slug` — `/resumes/:slug`, `/v/:videoId`, course / article / service detail pages still log-wall anonymous visitors regardless of the creator's promote flag** (opened 2026-05-20 — surfaced while wiring the new promote toggle in migration 0097) | [PeopleDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/PeopleDetail.tsx) now reads `profile.promoteWithoutAuth` and skips `<AuthOverlay contentType="person">` when set, but the other creator-output surfaces — [ResumeDetail.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/ResumeDetail.tsx), [PublicVideoResume.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/PublicVideoResume.tsx) (already public), course / article / service detail — each carry their own AuthOverlay branch that still blocks anonymous viewers. A creator promoting via a profile link works, but the moment that visitor clicks through to one of the creator's listed services or resumes, the login wall reappears. Fix: propagate the owner's `promoteWithoutAuth` setting into the public detail responses for each surface (resume, service, course, article) the way `GET /api/users/:id` now exposes it, and gate each surface's AuthOverlay the same way. Probably worth extracting a `useUnauthGate(owner)` hook so the rule lives in one place (DRY — see hooks reminder) rather than three. Unblocks: a coherent creator-promotion experience where a single opt-in opens the entire portfolio to anonymous traffic, not just the profile card. |
| 1140 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **`buildArtifactMetrics` reads `cta_click` events but not `impression` events** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1137) | [`artifactAnalytics.ts`](hired.video/api/src/services/analytics/artifactAnalytics.ts) `buildArtifactMetrics` queries `videoAnalytics` for `event = "cta_click"` rows to populate `ctaClicks` + `ctaClickThroughRate`, but doesn't query for `event = "impression"` rows. Once #1139 lands the ingestion path, this builder needs a parallel `impressionCount` rollup + an "Impressions" StatCard on `MetricsPanel`. Also add an `impressionCtr = ctaClicks / impressions` distinct from the existing `viewCtr = ctaClicks / totalViews` (the IAB-standard CTR is impression-based, not view-based). Pairs with #1137 / #1139. |
| 1157 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **Geo — drop legacy free-text `location` varchars on `job_items / user_profiles / job_alerts / job_preferences / talent_pool_candidates` once UI migration is complete** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1154) | Migration 0109 dual-wrote: structured rows in `content_locations` + the free-text column kept in place for one bake window. Search routes already prefer structured allowlists when set and fall back to ilike only when none is. Once #1155 closes (every form uses the picker), open a migration to drop the five free-text columns and remove the ilike fallback in [JobService.getPublicJobs](hired.video/api/src/services/job/JobService.ts) + [routes/search.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/search.ts) `/recruiter`. Until then DO NOT delete — old saved searches + email-alert links rely on the legacy params. |
