| 795 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P1 | `feature` | **`author_type` enum column on every content-listing table + publisher-role-driven persistence** (opened 2026-04-20 — half (d) of #789) | Single migration adding `author_type author_type_enum NOT NULL DEFAULT 'community'` to `articles`, `courses`, `studio_templates`, `resume_templates`, `studio_voice_clones`, `service_offerings` (and any other creator-listing table). New enum `CREATE TYPE author_type_enum AS ENUM ('platform','community')`. Each table's create/publish route reads the publishing user's superadmin role + sets `author_type = 'platform'` when `isSuperAdmin || isAdmin` else `'community'`; admin-only override endpoint for migration / seed scripts that aren't authored by a real user. Then update each public-list endpoint to project `author_type` into the response so [card-feed.ts:272](hired.video/frontend/lib/card-feed.ts#L272) can pull from the persistent column instead of the per-source hardcode. Unblocks: marketplace filter toggle (#796), ranking boost (#797), and consistency between the editorial blog (currently hardcoded `isOfficial: true`) and platform-authored articles once user articles are seeded. |
