| 438 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `arch` | **Backend `requireJobOwner` / `requireCompanyOwner` still bypass for SuperAdmin — UI override removed but API can still be called directly** (2026-05-07) | `hired.video/api/src/services/jobs/jobOwnership.ts:62` and `companyOwnership.ts` short-circuit `isSuperAdmin || ownerId === userId` → success. Frontend SA admin-override was removed from `useEntityOwnership` so SA no longer sees Edit/Delete/Create Video on entities they don't own; impersonation is the new path. The backend still allows SA to invoke `DELETE /api/jobs/:id/...` and pipeline mutations directly via curl/admin tooling against any job. Decide: (a) keep server-side bypass for `/admin/*` tooling; (b) remove and require impersonation for ALL writes too. Unblocks: tightens the UI/API privilege model symmetry. Identified 2026-05-07 fixing /jobs Delete-on-non-owned bug. |
| 2036 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Now | P2 | `feature` | **SuperAdmin Role Feature & Navigation Access Manager (per-role RBAC manifest — the "app feels too complex" lever)** (opened 2026-06-13; PRD authored same day) | Umbrella for the owner's ask: one SuperAdmin surface to assign features to roles + enable/disable menus and features per role (job_seeker/recruiter/employer/employee/affiliate/creator), so each persona sees only what's relevant — editable without a deploy. Role→surface visibility is today hardcoded across **6 disconnected SSoTs** ([Sidebar.tsx `hideForRoles`](hired.video/frontend/components/Sidebar.tsx#L70), [MobileBottomNav switch](hired.video/frontend/components/MobileBottomNav.tsx#L30), [tools-catalog `audienceRoles`](hired.video/frontend/data/tools-catalog.ts#L115), [screening `audienceRoles`](hired.video/shared/screening.ts#L120), [admin-permissions `ADMIN_CRUD`](hired.video/frontend/lib/admin-permissions.ts#L37), and the **global-only** [modules](hired.video/api/src/db/schema/admin.ts#L67)+[moduleGate](hired.video/api/src/middleware/moduleGate.ts)). Solution = a code-declared Feature Registry (SSoT catalog + defaults) + a `role_feature_access` deltas table + one shared `resolveRoleAccess`/`useRoleAccess()` resolver every gate self-consumes (DRY), read-through cached + invalidated, defaulting to today's behavior (zero regression). Supersedes the menu-only scope of #1995. **Fully shipped 2026-06-13** — #2037 (registry+resolver+table+admin+Sidebar), #2038 (mobile+tools convergence), #2039 (per-role module enforcement), #2040 (nav reorder + admin-tab gating), #2041 (tests), #2042 (per-user tier + capability seam), plus cleanups #2061 (screening dead field) / #2062 (mobile CTA) and the usage/engagement extension #2063–#2066 (PRD §10; one residual #2067 = DSR-on-account-deletion). 30 unit tests green; api+frontend tsc clean. NOT yet run against a live DB (migrations 0214/0215 unapplied). Full design: [PRD — Role Feature & Navigation Access Manager](hired.video/docs/prd/role-feature-access-manager.md). |
