anagement.tsx) 46 (recruiter), [ResumeViewer.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/ResumeViewer.tsx) 24 (high-traffic), [SearchBar.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/SearchBar.tsx) 100+ (audit caught 26 but Select options balloon it — used on every search page so leverage is high), [StudioSidebar.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioSidebar.tsx) 33, [InterviewPractice.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/InterviewPractice.tsx) 18. **Defer (lawyer-grade copy):** [TermsOfService.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/TermsOfService.tsx) 106, [PrivacyPolicy.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/PrivacyPolicy.tsx) 87, [CookiePolicy.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/CookiePolicy.tsx) 34 — need professional translation, tackle via content track. **Defer (staff-only):** `pages/admin/*` and `pages/superadmin/*`. Categories: (a) inline JSX, (b) attrs, (c) toasts (mostly DONE for Jobs+People), (d) legal bodies. Unblocks: real Spanish locale parity + readiness for new locales. |
| 782 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Non-admin team members can't see invitations they sent** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced during the Team Members DTO drift fix) | [listAccountUsers](hired.video/api/src/services/user/account.ts) only returns the viewer's own row unless the JWT role is `admin`. An employer who calls `POST /api/account/invite` to bring in recruiters never sees those invitations in Team Members — only the SuperAdmin / legacy `admin` role does. Spec: when the viewer's role is in `canManageUsers` (employer or admin), surface (a) the viewer's own user row, (b) every still-open invitation row whose `invitedBy = viewer.id`, and (c) every user row the viewer invited (resolvable via `invitedBy` once we record it on the accepted user). Requires either an `invited_by` column on `users` populated by `acceptInvitation`, or a join through `account_invitations` history. Today the multi-tenant model is single-account so admin-only is "fine"; once company-scoped membership lands this gap blocks the Team Members surface for employer accounts. Unblocks: real team management without forcing every action through a SuperAdmin. |
| 1869 | T1 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **`require-page-chrome` migration: 335 findings across 145 page files, hidden until #1868 un-broke ESLint** (opened 2026-05-31) | With the lint config fixed (#1868), the `require-page-chrome` rule (severity `error`, [eslint.config.js:181](hired.video/frontend/eslint.config.js#L181)) runs for the first time and flags **335 issues in 145 of ~200 `frontend/pages/**/*.tsx` files**: **141 missing `useBreadcrumbs`, 114 missing `useSEO`, 79 missing `<AppShell>`, 1 missing default export**. Most pages predate the [feedback_new_page_checklist] convention (reference: AffiliateProgram.tsx). This is a genuine content-bearing migration (correct per-page SEO + breadcrumb trails), NOT a mechanical sweep — placeholder chrome would be worse than none, so it was deliberately NOT auto-applied in the #1860 fix pass. NB the rule is also too naive about layout composition: ~23 `pages/admin/*` files get real chrome from `<AdminLayout>` (which renders `<AppShell>`) yet are flagged — those are false positives. `npm run lint`/`check`/`lint:ci` were already red (the config crashed before #1868), so this is no new CI regression, but it IS now the blocker. **Plan:** (a) teach the rule to treat a layout-wrapper page (admin) as chromed, or opt those out; (b) add `// eslint-page-chrome: skip — <reason>` to legitimately-chromeless surfaces (studio editors, `/embed`/iframe pages, auth/OAuth callbacks, full-screen tools); (c) add real `<AppShell>`+`useSEO`+`useBreadcrumbs` to the genuine marketing/app pages; (d) optionally downgrade the rule to `warn` as an interim so `lint` is usable mid-migration. [StudioEditorV2.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/v2/StudioEditorV2.tsx) was opted out this pass (the file #1860 touched). Unblocks: a green, enforced page-chrome guardrail. **Update 2026-05-31 (KEPT the clean wins, REVERTED the bulk silencing):** kept (1) the composition-aware rule — recognises chrome-provider wrappers (`ToolShell`, `ResumeAnalysisToolPage`, `MarketplaceItemShell`, any `*Layout`) + exempts the admin route-wrapper tree (clears ~46 false positives correctly); (2) the shared `usePageChrome()` + `useDefaultBreadcrumbs()` hooks ([lib/seo.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/seo.ts)) applied to ~20 genuine public pages (real SEO+breadcrumbs). **Reverted** the ~76 bulk `eslint-page-chrome: skip` opt-outs — that was metric-gaming (and the scripted edits broke 4 files' imports, caught by CI). **Set the rule to `warn`** ([eslint.config.js](hired.video/frontend/eslint.config.js)) as the honest interim: the remaining ~99 pages surface as warnings (visible, not blocking) pending a DELIBERATE migration. Recommended end-state: split the rule into "layout chrome everywhere (via composition)" + "SEO/breadcrumbs on public pages only", so authed-app pages need neither an opt-out nor pointless SEO. Remaining work: that split + adding real chrome to the genuine public pages still warning. |
| 1970 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Migrate user-facing Outreach CampaignsTab onto the new campaign engine** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1969) | `frontend/pages/Outreach.tsx` + [CampaignsTab.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/outreach/tabs/CampaignsTab.tsx) still consume the legacy numeric-enum `EmailCampaignDTO` from `/api/communication/email-campaigns` (raw DB rows, no `stats`/`audience`), so the new reusable `<CampaignList>`/`<CampaignComposerDialog>` are only wired into the SuperAdmin surface, not Outreach. The legacy status comparison `campaign.status === EmailCampaignStatus.Sent` is also string-vs-number and always false (pre-existing drift the string-status SSoT now exposes). Fix: add a user-scoped `CampaignService.list`/endpoint returning `CampaignDTO[]` filtered to `createdByUserId`, point Outreach at `campaignService`, and swap CampaignsTab's bespoke email cards for `<CampaignList>`. Unblocks one engine across both surfaces. |
| 250 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P2 | `feature` | **Custom Roles (per-tenant RBAC beyond superadmin/owner)** | Extends `users.role` (system-wide) with `workspaceRoles` + `workspaceRolePermissions` matrix. Admin UI to define a role + flip per-feature toggles. Read by `requireWorkspacePermission()` middleware. |
| 497 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **No dispatch telemetry — when a call falls back across providers, we don't record which profile actually answered or how many attempts it took** (2026-05-09) | The `console.warn` lines in `tryProviderChain` and the dispatch loop in `llm-client.ts` are the only visibility into fallback events. There's no per-call record of "primary failed → fallback X succeeded → 28s wall-clock" surfaced to SuperAdmin or token-ledger. Without this, we can't tell from production data which use cases are actually leaning on their cross-provider fallback (i.e. their primary model is unreliable in practice) — we just see a slow request. Fix: extend `tokenLedger.charge` with `{ profileChain: string[]; attemptCount: number; totalLatencyMs: number }` so SA can rank "use cases where the primary failed > 10% of the time this week". Out of scope for #495's latency fix; tracked separately because the schema delta touches `ai_usage_records`. Unblocks: data-driven decisions on which use case primaries to swap out. NOTE: largely obsoleted by the planned port to `@seanhogg/builderforce-sdk` (#498) — gateway already returns `_builderforce.{resolvedModel, retries, pool}` per response. |
| 1303 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **#412 — team-picker UI for users with `accountTeamRoleAssignments.length > 1`** (opened alongside #1300). Existing AccountSwitcher covers account-level switching only. Decision: extend AccountSwitcher with nested team list OR build a separate `<TeamSwitcher />` next to it. API already returns `accountTeamRoleAssignments` on `/auth/profile`. |
| 2158 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `arch` | **`(schema as any).table` casts across route/service files defeat compile-time column-drift detection** (found 2026-06-13 while fixing the `/api/audit/me` 500) | The `/api/audit/me` 500 (`Cannot convert undefined or null to object`) was schema drift: [userAuditLog.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/audit/userAuditLog.ts) selected `impersonationSessions.actorId` (real column `superAdminId`) and `emailChangeRequests.completedAt` (real column `consumedAt`) via `(schema as any).table` + `rows as any[]`. An undefined column reference makes drizzle's `orderSelectedFields` recurse into `Object.entries(undefined)` during the **synchronous** `_prepare()`, which throws *before* the `.catch(() => [])` is attached → uncaught 500. Fixed that file by importing the tables typed (drift now a compile error) + mapping to the real columns (also un-breaks the never-emitted "Email changed" event). **Remaining gap:** ~14 other sites still use `(schema as any).tableName` (e.g. [discovery.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/discovery.ts), [featured-creators.ts](hired.video/frontend/../api/src/routes/featured-creators.ts), [job-analytics.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/job-analytics.ts), [targeting-evaluator.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/advertising/targeting-evaluator.ts)) — each is a latent same-class 500 if a referenced column/table is renamed. Sweep them to typed imports (or a typed `requireTable` helper) so column drift fails `tsc`, not prod. |
| 1183 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **Manual DPO tooling for verified data-subject erasure requests — replaces the auto-purge worker user declined in #1149** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1149 — renumbered from #1168 — explicit user decision: "I don't think we should hard delete any user… delete shouldn't delete but rather anonymize the existing content and make private") | `deleteAccount()` in [account.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/user/account.ts) is now anonymize-on-delete: PII is scrubbed, videos go private, the row stays so historical activity (applications, transactions, audit trails) keeps a stable user_id. For verifiable GDPR Art. 17 / CCPA "Right to Delete" requests where the data subject specifically asks for ROW erasure (not just anonymization), we need a SuperAdmin-only tool that: (1) authenticates the request (subject identity verified — sign-in + email confirm, or DPO-attested manual review for unauthenticated requests routed via privacy@hired.video), (2) shows a preview of what would be hard-deleted vs cascade-nulled (jobs they posted, messages they sent, ledger entries, etc.), (3) executes the DELETE inside an explicit admin action with audit logging (admin_id + reason + before/after row counts). NOT a scheduled sweep — every hard-delete is a single human-attended operation. Until built, the DPO handles these requests manually via direct DB access + an audit-log entry. |
| 1263 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `data` | **Assessment norms worker cadence (24h) means new assessment kinds publish percentiles a day late** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the [assessmentNormsWorker](hired.video/api/src/workers/assessment-norms-recompute.ts) shipping). First-time recompute for a brand-new kind takes one cron tick (24h) before `assessment_dimension_norms` returns a row; until then the /complete endpoint returns raw scores with no `percentiles` block. To close: (a) expose `POST /api/admin/workers/assessment-norms-recompute/run` for SuperAdmin manual triggers, (b) emit a domain event from `/complete` that opportunistically calls `computePercentileCurve` for the just-updated dimension when the sample exceeds 100 since last recompute. Unblocks: same-day percentile bands for any newly-launched assessment kind. |
| 1654 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **`admin_audit_log` cold-storage archive path (S3 export + delete-after-confirmed)** (opened 2026-05-26 alongside #1613 closure). The 365d retention from #1613 keeps the hot DB bounded but loses the 7y-class compliance trail. The archive shape: nightly export of rows-about-to-be-deleted to S3 (parquet, partition by month), confirm checksum, then delete locally. Requires: a `services/maintenance/admin-audit-archive.ts` module, S3 bucket + lifecycle policy, a way to surface the archive in admin tooling. Not load-bearing until SOC 2 audit asks for 7y of admin actions. |
| 2132 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `feature` | **#1201 — per-kind Theme/Style wizard step for non-video kinds — left as a follow-on after #1230** (2026-05-25). The asymmetry is documented inline in [StudioWizard.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/studio/StudioWizard.tsx) `kindNeedsThemeStep` JSDoc. Comic mostly addressed by per-template genre encoding at step 0; remaining work is a real chooser for voice (default voice id), image / animation (base style + size), game (sprite pack), cad (drawing template). Each kind needs its own UX design pass — not a small drop-in. To close: design + ship a `kindExtrasStep` framework with one component per kind, gated by feature flag until the chooser sets exist for every kind that needs one. |
| 263 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P4 | `feature` | **Default currency / country / timezone (workspace-level)** | `accountPreferences` extension. Threads into formatting helpers (Intl.NumberFormat / DateTimeFormat) across the app. |
| 2124 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P4 | `feature` | **Synth/music studio discoverability + role-feature-access registration** (opened 2026-06-14) | The full APEX synth instrument is only reachable three levels deep (Studio → Actions → Original Music → "Synth" tab in [MusicComposer.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/studio/music/MusicComposer.tsx)); in standalone APEX it was a top-level `/synth` route. It is not registered as a named tool in the role-feature access manifest (`project_role_feature_access_manager`, #2036–#2042), so SuperAdmin can't show/hide it per role and there's no discoverable entry point. Fix: register the music/synth studio in the static registry so `resolveRoleAccess` gates it, and surface a discoverable launcher. Unblocks: per-role enablement + actual reachability of a shipped-but-buried feature. |

### TK10 — integrations-comms — Integrations, Email & Notifications — 67 active

**Owned paths:** `api/src/services/{email*,messaging,notifications,enrichment}/**`, `api/src/routes/push*`, `api/src/services/workforce/connectors/**`

| # | Rev | Status | Phase | Priority | Type | Gap | Notes |
