| 1758 | T1 | ⚠️ Partial | Mid | P1 | `billing` | **Real contact-enrichment vendor — Hunter.io adapter wired** (provider shipped 2026-06-16, TK10) | **Shipped:** the first real `EnrichmentProvider` — [services/enrichment/hunter.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/enrichment/hunter.ts) (`HunterEnrichmentProvider`) mapping Hunter's Email Finder onto `EnrichmentInput`/`EnrichmentResult`; selected via `ENRICHMENT_PROVIDER=hunter` in `getActiveEnrichmentProvider()`. Defensive parsing (any unexpected shape → `enriched:false`, never throws the credit path), honest config-missing handling (no `HUNTER_API_KEY` → non-enriched + CONFIG excerpt), full request/response/error mapping. 10 unit tests against a mocked `fetch`. `enrichment_provider_calls` now carries real `http_status` + `response_excerpt` when active. **Residual:** live validation against a real Hunter account pending an API key (ops); a final vendor choice (PeopleDataLabs/Apollo/ZoomInfo) remains a product decision — each is now a one-file add behind the same seam. |
| 146 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Email integration for auto-status updates (Gmail / Outlook)** | Connect Gmail or Outlook via OAuth and run a background parser that scans incoming emails for job application responses (interview invites, rejections, offers). Auto-updates `savedJobs.status` from "applied" → "interviewing" / "rejected" / "offered" based on email content analysis via LLM. OAuth consent screens, token refresh, email polling via Cloudflare Cron, and privacy controls (user selects which labels/folders to scan, data never stored beyond status classification). Replaces manual status updates in the Chrome extension's job pipeline tracker. Prerequisite: `savedJobs.status` column (implemented in extension analytics PR). |
| 536 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Email sync per-message LLM cost is unbounded — full-mailbox first sync on a heavy mailbox can fire hundreds of `email_classify` + `email_summary` calls in one cron tick** (2026-05-10) | [sync.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/email-integration/sync.ts) classifies every new message that wasn't caught by Stage-1 rules, then summarises every job-related message above 0.6. Heavy users (200+ unread inbox) on first connect could fire 100+ LLM calls in a single sync run — no per-user budget gate, no back-pressure, no batch dispatch. Today this is shielded by Stage-1 rules catching the obvious ATS senders, but if the user has lots of recruiter outreach below the rules' precision floor it can spike fast. Fix: (a) pass the user's `JwtPayload` into `runEmailSyncSweep` so per-user token-budget 429s land cleanly, (b) batch the summary stage (one LLM call summarising ≤10 messages at once via `callMessages`), (c) hard-cap per-sync-run classify count and roll the overflow into the next tick. Unblocks: predictable cost on full-mailbox-sync MVP. |
| 549 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **Frontend ships with no `VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` — backend's `TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY` is set, so every login was being hard-rejected with `400 TURNSTILE_FAIL`** (2026-05-12, reported via `/login?source=extension` flow from the Chrome extension) | The site key is referenced by [TurnstileWidget.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/TurnstileWidget.tsx) and [use-turnstile.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/hooks/use-turnstile.ts) but does NOT appear in any `.env*` or `wrangler.toml` — Vite's build inlines it as `undefined`, the widget short-circuits via `if (!siteKey) return null`, and the form posts with no `cfTurnstileToken`. Backend was returning `TURNSTILE_FAIL` and locking everyone out (extension's "Continue in browser" tab + the in-popup email/password form both hit the same wall). **Mitigation in place (this commit):** [AuthService.handleLogin](hired.video/api/src/services/auth/AuthService.ts) now treats a captcha miss as a soft signal — records the bot_block_event and forces the email-OTP step-up after password verification (`captchaFailed → requiresMfa`). Real account holders prove humanness via inbox; bots without mailbox access stall at the second factor. Extension popup ([shared/login.js](hiredvideo-chrome-extension/shared/login.js) + [shared/login.html](hiredvideo-chrome-extension/shared/login.html)) hosts the OTP entry inline so users don't have to start over in a new tab. **Real fix still owed:** add `VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` to the production frontend build (Cloudflare Pages env vars or `frontend/.env.production`) paired to the backend secret, so the silent challenge runs and only users who fail it get the OTP fallback. **Adjacent gap:** signup is still hard-blocked because [signupGuard.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/auth/signupGuard.ts) hasn't been given the same step-up rail (and adding email-OTP step-up to a NEW user creation flow is a bigger UX call). Unblocks: production sign-in for everyone, and re-enables silent bot defense once the site key ships. |
| 976 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Google Ads adapter — geo / demographic / device targeting criteria not wired** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #975 — paid-media foundation ships without per-criterion mutates) | [adapters/google/index.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/paid-media/adapters/google/index.ts) `createAdSet()` creates the AdGroup but does NOT translate `TargetingSpec` → `campaignCriterion` + `adGroupCriterion` mutates (Google Ads keeps targeting on separate resource families). Without these, every ad group runs untargeted by geo / age / device / language. To close: add a follow-up mutate batch in `createAdSet()` + `updateAdSet()` that for each `TargetingSpec` field calls `customers/{id}/campaignCriteria:mutate` (geo, language) or `customers/{id}/adGroupCriteria:mutate` (age range, device, interest, custom audience). Maintain idempotency by reading existing criteria first via GAQL and only applying the delta. Pairs with #975 (foundation), #980 (insights backfill — needs targeting to be meaningful). |
| 978 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **TikTok video upload pipeline — adapter requires pre-uploaded `tiktok_video_id` but no upload route exists** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #975) | [adapters/tiktok/index.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/paid-media/adapters/tiktok/index.ts) `createAd()` throws if `metadata.tiktokVideoId` and `metadata.tiktokIdentityId` are missing — the assumption is the service layer uploaded the video to TikTok's `/file/video/ad/upload/` endpoint first. That upload route is NOT yet implemented. To close: add `services/paid-media/adapters/tiktok/uploadVideo.ts` that streams the creative's `assetUrl` from R2 to TikTok's `multipart/form-data` upload endpoint, returns the `video_id`. Wire it into `services/paid-media/sync.ts:syncCreativeToAccount()` so creating a TikTok creative auto-uploads. Until then, customers must manually upload to TikTok Ads Manager and paste the video_id into the creative metadata. |
| 979 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `arch` | **Cloudflare Queue-based async sync for large multi-platform pushes** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #975) | Today [services/paid-media/sync.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/paid-media/sync.ts) is fully synchronous: one HTTP request per platform per resource, all inside a single Cloudflare Worker invocation (~30s CPU budget). For a "create 1 campaign + 3 ad sets + 12 ads + sync to 5 platforms" flow that's 80 calls — risks the CPU limit. To close: introduce a `paid-media-sync` Cloudflare Queue + a consumer worker that drains the queue, calls the adapter, writes `paid_media_sync_runs`. API routes enqueue + return 202 with a tracking job id; the SPA polls a `GET /api/paid-media/jobs/:id` route for status. Mirror the pattern from `email-integration` background sync. Pairs with #975 (foundation), #980 (insights backfill is the heaviest consumer of the queue). |
| 985 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Pixel verification flow — send a "test event" to each configured pixel/CAPI on save and surface "verified ✓" in the Pixels tab** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #975) | `paid_media_pixels.verified` JSONB column exists in the schema but the verification call is not implemented. To close: on `PUT /api/paid-media/pixels`, fire a synthetic conversion event (`event_name: "TestEvent"`) through `services/paid-media/conversions/capi.ts` to each platform whose pixel id + access token are both set; record the result into `paid_media_pixels.verified.{platform}` (true on success, error string on failure). Frontend ([PaidMediaPage.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/paid-media/PaidMediaPage.tsx) PixelsTab) renders a green check / red X next to each input. Re-verification button per platform. Unblocks: customers can self-diagnose pixel misconfiguration without leaving the app. |
| 1181 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **`users.do_not_share` flag is set by /privacy/opt-out but no server-side enforcement on CAPI fan-out or audience-export jobs reads it** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1149 — renumbered from #1166) | Schema column added in [0111_user_deleted_at_do_not_share.sql](hired.video/api/drizzle/0111_user_deleted_at_do_not_share.sql) and the page + endpoint flip it correctly, but the seam consumers haven't been wired yet. To close: (1) `paid-media-service.recordConversion()` (Meta CAPI / Google Ads server-side / LinkedIn CAPI / TikTok Events API) reads `users.do_not_share` for the converting user and suppresses email/phone/IP/ad-id fields in the outbound payload (event still fires; identifiers stripped — matches CCPA "service provider" model). (2) Any nightly audience-export job that pushes user lists to ad platforms `WHERE NOT do_not_share`. (3) Update [Settings → Privacy](hired.video/frontend/pages/Settings.tsx) panel to mirror the toggle so users land there too. Cookie-level gating already in place from #1149; this gap is the row-level belt + suspenders the CAPI path needs. |
| 1230 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Real-time chat is REST-polled — no WebSocket transport, no presence, no typing indicators** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside the Competitors.tsx parity-row update). [api/src/routes/messages.ts](hired.video/api/src/routes/messages.ts) ships `aiChatSessions` + `aiChatMessages` reads/writes over plain HTTP. LinkedIn InMail and modern ATSes (Greenhouse, Bullhorn, Front) all ship a WebSocket-backed message transport with online presence, typing indicators, and sub-second delivery — the gap is highlighted as the "Real-time chat" row on `/vs-competitors`. To close: stand up a Cloudflare Durable Object per conversation (or a single chat-room DO keyed by `conversationId`), add a `WebSocketPair` upgrade handler at `/api/chat/socket/:id`, broadcast `message`, `typing`, `presence` events, and migrate the frontend `chat` panel from polling to a `useChannel(conversationId)` hook. Durable Objects are the right fit because they already underpin the worker runtime and have built-in WebSocket hibernation — no Redis required for a v1. Unblocks: parity claim on the competitors page, lower latency on AI chat panel, presence indicators on Comm Hub. |
| 1901 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Google + Outlook two-way calendar OAuth sync for bookings hosts** (opened 2026-06-04 from #1648 close). The `booking_external_calendar_links` table is in the PRD but was not added in the 0195 migration — v1 hosts manage their availability entirely inside hired.video, which means a personal commitment in Google Calendar that ISN'T in the bookings system can be double-booked. Build: (a) `booking_external_calendar_links` table (provider + OAuth tokens encrypted at rest + sync cursor); (b) Google OAuth + Microsoft Graph OAuth flows wired into `/bookings` settings; (c) **read** path — every confirmed external event blocks the corresponding window in `resolveAvailableSlots` (treated as a busy-window entry alongside reservations); (d) **write** path — every confirmed reservation mirrored as a calendar event with attendee = booker email + link to magic-link reservation page; (e) reconciliation queue for events the host manually deletes from the external calendar. Per PRD [§8](hired.video/docs/prd/bookings-and-reservations.md). Unblocks: hosts can mix BurnRateOS/hired.video bookings with their existing calendar without manually duplicating windows. |
| 1903 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Signup picker — surface "Creator / Coach / Entrepreneur" as a top-level choice** (opened 2026-06-04 from #1648 close). Today [Signup.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Signup.tsx) offers the three USER_ROLES (job_seeker / recruiter / employer). The user explicitly raised the "coach / entrepreneur" gap during the #1648 design conversation: a gymnastics coach isn't a job_seeker semantically, but adding a 4th role contradicts [project_creator_persona_model.md](memory/project_creator_persona_model.md) ("Creator = profileMode on existing job_seeker role, NOT a 4th role") and [feedback_role_means_user_role.md](memory/feedback_role_means_user_role.md) ("Role in hired.video = USER_ROLES enum"). Resolution: add a 4th picker tile **"I'm a creator / coach / consultant / entrepreneur"** that under the hood routes to `role=job_seeker` + sets `profileMode=channel` + calls `/api/creators/opt-in` with `programs: ['bookings']` so the new user lands on `/bookings` ready to configure offerings. The internal role name never appears in the UI. Unblocks: the gymnastics-coach signup flow (and every other "I monetize my expertise, I'm not looking for a job" persona) without a USER_ROLES expansion or a permissions-system rewrite. |
| 1966 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `quality` | **Feed routes have no DB-backed integration tests** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1965) | The feed's reshare visibility gate (can't reshare a post you can't see), the view-recording owner-skip, the analytics owner-or-super-admin 403, and the DTO reshare-count batching live in route handlers that need a real DB and aren't unit-testable — #1965 only unit-covers the shared/service layers (`FeedFeatureService`, `artifact-views` contract, `FeedPostCard` wiring). Stand up a DB-backed integration harness (or a repo-mock seam for the feed route, mirroring the `*-handlers.ts` DI split #1327) and cover those four behaviors. Unblocks: confidence that visibility/ownership gates can't regress silently. |
| 1974 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Region-aware double-opt-in (GDPR/CASL) + GPC honoring** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1973) | Consent model shipped as US opt-out (CAN-SPAM). For EEA + Quebec, marketing requires affirmative confirmed consent (double-opt-in) before the first send, and GPC/DNT signals should be honored. Hook the existing [shared/jurisdictions.ts](hired.video/shared/jurisdictions.ts) (`EEA_COUNTRIES`, `matchesJurisdiction`) + the planned `users.country_code`/`jurisdiction` columns (gap #1152): gate `MarketingConsentService.filterMailable` to require an explicit opt-in row for EEA/Quebec recipients, and render per-jurisdiction footer/unsubscribe copy. Unblocks compliant EU/Canada marketing. |
| 1975 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `bug` | **Bounce/complaint → hard suppression not wired** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1973) | `email_suppressions` (the hard, non-user-reversible list) is read by `MarketingConsentService.filterMailable` but nothing writes it — there's no SendPulse bounce/complaint webhook. Add a webhook route that classifies bounces/spam-complaints and calls a `recordHardSuppression(email, reason)` path so repeatedly-bouncing/complaining addresses drop out of every send (sender-reputation + CAN-SPAM complaint handling). |
