| 788 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Multi-job auto-create off — digest alerts don't seed N tracked jobs** (opened 2026-05-18 alongside #786) | [`autoCreateJobFromEmail`](hired.video/api/src/services/email-integration/dedup.ts) creates at most one row per email — by design today, since a single LinkedIn alert containing 5 unfamiliar roles auto-spawning 5 tracked jobs would dump unwanted noise into the user's board. Need an explicit opt-in (per-account or per-rule "Auto-track jobs from this sender" toggle) plus per-anchor title/company parsing so the auto-created row has a meaningful title — currently we'd inherit the digest subject ("Your job alert for vice president of technology") on every spawned job. Unblocks: closing the loop from "see 5 roles in an alert" → "5 tracked jobs to compare" without leaving the inbox. |
| 873 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `quality` | **Server-side `extractJobLinks` still includes alert-management anchors in the stored `apply_urls` payload — every read pays the filter cost** (opened 2026-05-20 — surfaced building #872) | The new admin-link filter in [groupJobLinks](hired.video/frontend/lib/email-rendering/group-job-links.ts) runs at render time so the stored row keeps the raw "Manage alerts" / "Edit alert" / "Your job alert for X" anchors. Pushing the same filter down into [`extractJobLinks`](hired.video/api/src/services/email-integration/dedup.ts) at ingest time would (a) shrink the persisted jsonb payload, (b) let server-side multi-job auto-create (#788) iterate over only real roles, and (c) make the helper reusable from a future `shared/` location instead of frontend-only. Fix: promote the `ADMIN_LABEL_RE` + `ADMIN_PATH_RE` regex pair into `shared/email-extraction/admin-anchor-filter.ts`, call it inside `extractJobLinks` before the seen-map insert, and drop the frontend's defensive filter when every ingest path has been re-run. Unblocks: server-side multi-job grouping; smaller row payloads; one canonical filter not two. |
| 981 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Custom audience sync — push internal segments (e.g. "viewed 3+ video resumes but didn't sign up") as platform custom audiences** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside #975) | `paid_media_audiences` table + service shell exist in #975 but the push pipeline does not. To close: implement `services/paid-media/audiences/sync.ts` that resolves a `sourceSpec.query` against `paid_media_conversions` + `paid_media_insights` + `user_events`, hashes resulting email/external_id with SHA-256, and POSTs to each platform's custom-audience endpoint (Meta `/customaudiences`, Google `/userLists`, LinkedIn `/dmpSegments`, TikTok `/dmp/custom_audience/file/upload/`, Bing `/customerLists`). Lookalike push (`sourceKind: "lookalike"`) wraps the platform's lookalike-from-seed call. Each push records into `paid_media_sync_runs` + creates a `paid_media_platform_refs` row with `resourceKind: "audience"` so the audience can be referenced in `TargetingSpec.customAudienceIds`. |
| 1525 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Contact.tsx still embeds the BurnRateOS form (`data-bro-form`) — second contact mechanism running alongside the new shared ContactPanel** (opened 2026-05-26 during the ContactPanel consolidation pass; renumbered from #1517 to avoid collision). [Contact.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Contact.tsx) embeds `BURNRATE_EMBED_SRC` + a `data-bro-form="908f62d0-…"` block that posts to BurnRateOS, while every in-app CTA (Pricing's 3 cards, About hero, Help's Email Support) now opens [ContactPanel.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/ContactPanel.tsx) — which POSTs to `/api/marketing/contact`, lands in `marketing_leads`, AND notifies every super_admin via the `notifications` table (which feeds the existing `/outreach` Inbox tab + bell dropdown). Two pipelines collect contact inquiries in two places. Footer's "Contact Us" still routes here for SEO permalink purposes. Fix: swap the BurnRateOS embed in Contact.tsx for the in-page ContactPanel form (or a permanent inline variant of it), so /contact and every in-app CTA collect through one source. Unblocks: one inbox to triage, no missed inquiries from people who land on /contact via a footer link or search engine. |
