| 2136 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P3 | `feature` | **Multi-job dedup is single-link only** (opened 2026-05-18 alongside #786) | When a digest email matches multiple jobs the candidate already tracks (e.g. 3 of 5 roles in a LinkedIn alert), [`dedupAgainst`](hired.video/api/src/services/email-integration/dedup.ts) still returns ONE `linkedJobId` (highest-confidence apply-URL hit), losing the other links. Fix: replace the `linkedJobId: uuid` column with a join table `external_email_message_job_links (messageId, jobId, applyUrl, dedupScore, dedupMethod, position)` (one row per match), update `dedupAgainst` to return `DedupResult[]`, surface the matched-job badges per Apply button in [JobMailCTAs](hired.video/frontend/components/communication/JobMailCTAs.tsx). Unblocks: full multi-job inbox parity — every role in a digest can show "Linked to job X" / "Tailor resume for Y". |
