| 393 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **No proactive monitoring for OAuth client-secret expiry** (2026-05-05) | Microsoft secrets expire (24-month max since the 2021 Azure default change), GitHub PATs/secrets can be rotated, LinkedIn/Google secrets don't expire by default but can be revoked. Today there's nothing watching `oauthAccounts.tokenExpiresAt` or the *provider-side* secret expiry — the first signal is users hitting AADSTS7000215 / `invalid_client` and bouncing through `/login?error=auth_failed`. Fix: nightly cron that exchanges a known-bad code per provider and pages on any `invalid_client` response, OR (cheaper) a calendar reminder seeded from each secret's known expiry. Unblocks: catching expired secrets before users do. Identified 2026-05-05 from the AADSTS7000215 incident. |
| 537 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **Gmail sync fetches messages serially — bursts >50 messages will time out on a Cloudflare Workers sub-request budget** (2026-05-10) | [providers/gmail.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/email-integration/providers/gmail.ts) walks `users.messages.list` ids and calls `users.messages.get` one-at-a-time. ~300ms per call × 50 = 15s, ~200 messages = a minute, hits the 50-subrequest soft limit and the 30s CPU budget on Workers free tier. Outlook delta endpoint returns full message bodies in pages so it's fine. Fix: parallelise Gmail's `fetchMessage` loop with a small concurrency window (e.g. `Promise.allSettled` × 5), AND use `users.messages.batchGet` (not yet on the public REST API — would need the batch HTTP endpoint with a multipart body) when the count exceeds a threshold. Unblocks: reliable first-sync on heavy mailboxes. |
| 538 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `arch` | **No 429 / Retry-After handling on Gmail or Graph calls — provider rate-limit fails the whole sync run instead of backing off** (2026-05-10) | Both [providers/gmail.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/email-integration/providers/gmail.ts) and [providers/outlook.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/email-integration/providers/outlook.ts) throw on any non-2xx, which marks the `email_sync_runs` row `error` and the account `status=error`. Gmail returns 429 with `Retry-After` + per-user quota guidance; Graph returns 429 with `Retry-After` + per-app throttling. Fix: shared `providerFetch` wrapper that honours `Retry-After` (single retry, capped delay so a worker invocation doesn't exceed the 30s CPU budget) and downgrades 429 to a `partial` sync rather than an `error`. Unblocks: graceful degradation on transient throttling. |
| 539 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **Inbox row exposes `linkedJobId` but never renders the linked job's title/company — user can't see WHICH job an email is bound to** (2026-05-10) | [InboxPanel.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/communication/InboxPanel.tsx) switches the icon to a briefcase when `item.linkedJobId` is set (since #530 P0), but the row body still only shows the email subject + sender. Auto-created and dedup-linked emails should ideally show `"→ Senior Engineer at Acme"` so the candidate sees the connection without clicking through. Fix: extend `InboxExternalEmailDto` with `linkedJobTitle` + `linkedJobCompany` (joined in `inboxService` via `repos.jobs.findJobsByIds`), thread through `HubItem`, render below the preview line. Carry over to the row click handler so clicking opens the job page when a link exists. Unblocks: the candidate-side "see what email is about which job" close-the-loop UX that motivated this whole feature. |
| 817 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **`useEmailAccounts()` is per-component state — disconnect optimism from one panel doesn't propagate to another mounted side-by-side** (opened 2026-05-17 — surfaced wiring the shared hook into ConnectMailboxButtons + EmailInboxesPanel) | The shared [useEmailAccounts](hired.video/frontend/hooks/use-email-accounts.ts) hook is built on `useGatedResource`, which is component-local state — every component that calls `useEmailAccounts()` gets its own fetch + cache. When EmailInboxesPanel disconnects a mailbox, the at-cap state inside `<ConnectMailboxButtons />` (sitting on the same page) doesn't flip until that component re-mounts or its own poll fires. The current panel happens to refresh its hook on mount, which masks the issue, but a shared context / SWR-style cache would let optimistic updates fan out. Pairs with the `useSubscription` pattern (also per-component today; same drift risk). Spec: introduce a tiny `EmailAccountsProvider` context that wraps the Settings + Communication Hub surfaces, or migrate the project to a shared cache (TanStack Query is already in the dependency graph for some surfaces). Unblocks: instant UI consistency across panels on every mailbox mutation. |
| 917 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **No proactive token-health check — `invalid_grant` is only discovered when the user (or sync button) triggers an `/access-token` call** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced fixing the `invalid_grant` 502 toast) | The PWA-side sync at [sync-client.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/email-integration/sync-client.ts) only calls `/api/integrations/email/accounts/:id/access-token` when the user is on the Inbox tab and clicks Sync. A mailbox whose refresh token Google revoked overnight stays silently broken for days — the `status: "error"` flip in the route only fires on the next user-initiated sync. Worse, message backfill stalls without notification: users assume the lull is real-world inbox quiet, not a token-rotation failure. Fix: (a) a daily Worker cron `email-token-health` that calls `refreshAccessToken()` for every `status: "active"` row, marks the row `status: "error"` + `lastError` on `invalid_grant`, and skips the access-token result (we only need the refresh side-effect), (b) on first transition into `status: "error"`, enqueue a notification row ("Gmail (sean@…) needs reconnecting") so the user sees it in the same Inbox they're trying to use, (c) optionally email a transactional reminder if `error` persists > 72h. Unblocks: a user opens Outreach Monday morning to find a Reconnect prompt already waiting, instead of "why am I getting no emails?" Pairs with #915 (popover banner) — same surface lights up the notification. |
| 919 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `bug` | **No detection or migration path for `EXTERNAL_EMAIL_TOKEN_KEY` rotation — every existing refresh token becomes undecryptable garbage, the route then surfaces it as `invalid_grant` and floods every user with bogus Reconnect prompts** (opened 2026-05-21 — surfaced fixing `invalid_grant` toast) | [encryption.ts deriveKey](hired.video/api/src/services/email-integration/encryption.ts) derives an AES-GCM key from `EXTERNAL_EMAIL_TOKEN_KEY` (falls back to `JWT_SECRET` for dev). If that env rotates, `decryptToken()` either throws (caught) or decodes ciphertext to nonsense, the nonsense string gets POSTed as `refresh_token=...`, and Google returns `invalid_grant`. With #918's classifier in place, every mailbox would simultaneously transition to `status: "error"` and prompt users to reconnect — even though the tokens at Google's end are perfectly fine. Fix bundles: (a) version-tag the ciphertext blob (`v1:iv:ct`) so a key-rotation can ship `v1` + `v2` keys in parallel and decrypt either, (b) catch `decryptToken` failure specifically (vs. token-refresh failure) in [email-integration.ts /accounts/:id/access-token](hired.video/api/src/routes/email-integration.ts) and return `MAILBOX_DECRYPT_FAILED` (different code from `MAILBOX_REAUTH_REQUIRED`) so the UI can say "this isn't your fault — operator action needed" instead of asking the user to reconnect for nothing, (c) an admin migration script that decrypts-with-old-key + re-encrypts-with-new-key over the `external_email_accounts` table during rotation. Unblocks: safe key rotation + no user-facing mass-reconnect prompt when ops swaps the seed. |
| 1976 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `quality` | **Retire superseded `account_preferences.marketingEmailsEnabled` coarse toggle** (opened 2026-06-07 with #1973) | The new email-keyed ledger is authoritative and is what the send path honors; the old `account_preferences.marketingEmailsEnabled` column + `settingsService.updateNotificationSettings({marketing})` + the `settings.notifications.marketingLabel/Desc` i18n keys are now superseded (the Settings marketing toggle UI was replaced by `<EmailPreferencesPanel>`). Migrate any existing `marketingEmailsEnabled=false` rows into `email_marketing_preferences.unsubscribed_all=true`, then drop the column + dead service path + i18n keys. |
| 1987 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Onboarding doesn't auto-stamp `active_profile_id` for new recruiters** (opened 2026-06-12 with #1984) | `defaultPresetKeyForRole` ([presets.ts](hired.video/shared/email-classification/presets.ts)) is the SSoT and the InboxSettingsSheet picker defaults to "Job Hunter (default)", but signup / role-switch do not yet write `external_email_accounts.active_profile_id` from that resolver — a new recruiter's first sync runs under Job Hunter until they manually pick a recruiter preset. Stamp the role-appropriate preset id on mailbox connect (or first sync) so the default is correct without a manual step. |
| 1989 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Switching a mailbox's profile doesn't retroactively re-classify already-synced mail** (opened 2026-06-12 with #1979) | `external_email_messages.is_relevant` + `category` + `extracted` are computed at ingest from the then-active profile. Changing `active_profile_id` (or editing a profile's taxonomy visibility / prompt) only affects mail synced AFTER the change; existing rows keep their ingest-time classification until a re-sync re-touches them. The per-account score slider DOES re-filter live (it's applied in the read query), but category visibility does not. Add a "re-classify existing messages" action (bounded background pass) so a profile switch can backfill, or document the re-sync requirement in the editor. |
| 2099 | T4 | ⚠️ Partial | Mid | P3 | `feature` | **Notification matrix: email channel now enforced; SMS + handler-consolidation residual** (opened 2026-06-14 with #254; email half shipped 2026-06-16, TK10) | **Shipped (email channel):** the unified dispatcher now has a real, preference-gated EMAIL channel. `EmitNotificationInput`/`NotifyInput` gained an opt-in `email?: boolean` (default off — most notifications stay bell+push only to avoid inbox spam); when set, [notificationService.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/notifications/notificationService.ts) `fanOutChannels` resolves recipient emails in ONE query (no N+1), gates each on `isChannelAllowed(prefs,'email',type)`, and sends via the new generic [adapters/email.ts](hired.video/api/src/services/adapters/email.ts) `buildNotificationEmail`/`sendNotificationEmail` (escaped title/message + validated CTA href; no-ops when SendPulse creds absent). Push + email now share ONE per-recipient prefs load (gate unified). Added a `__setEmailProvider` test seam; 8 new tests (builder escaping/CTA-safety + opt-in/gated/no-provider fan-out) green. **Residual (still open):** (a) **SMS channel** — `isChannelAllowed(prefs,'sms',type)` exists but no SMS provider is wired, so the sms* toggles persist but gate nothing (blocked on a Twilio-class provider + #255 inbound routing); (b) **settings-handlers consolidation** — `settings-handlers.ts` is a tested-but-unmounted parallel of the live `routes/settings.ts` (pref logic is DRY via shared helpers, but the duplicate handler surface persists behind a `settings-handlers ↔ routes/settings` import cycle). Unblocks: SMS preference enforcement + removal of the parallel handler module. |
| 759 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `arch` | **Service Worker JWT plumbing TBD — `localStorage` not readable from a SW context** (2026-05-17 — surfaced while planning #758) | When #758 lands `periodicSync` handlers, the Service Worker fetch context needs the user's auth token to call `/api/inbox/external-emails/ingest`. `localStorage.getItem("auth_token")` (current pattern in [api-client.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/api-client.ts)) is unavailable in a SW. Fix: on every successful auth handshake, also write the token to an IndexedDB store the SW reads on demand. Or use cookies (HttpOnly + SameSite=Strict) for auth, which the SW gets for free. Unblocks: #758 actually working in the background. |
| 760 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **Client-driven sync makes no progress UI distinction between "pulling from Gmail" vs "ingesting"** (2026-05-17 — surfaced while landing #755) | [`runClientSync`](hired.video/frontend/lib/email-integration/sync-client.ts) accepts an `onProgress` callback that distinguishes `phase: "auth" \| "pull" \| "ingest"` and reports `ingested / total`, but the [`EmailSyncButton`](hired.video/frontend/components/communication/EmailSyncButton.tsx) doesn't subscribe — it just shows the final rollup. For a backfill of 50+ messages the user sees a spinner for 10s with no progress signal. Fix: thread the onProgress callback through, render a small progress strip ("Pulling Gmail · 12/30 ingested") below the button while syncing. Unblocks: usable feedback during long backfills. |
