| 2114 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **OAuth signup doesn't forward pre-auth locale** | The new [Signup.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Signup.tsx) → [RegisterSchema](hired.video/api/src/routes/auth.ts) → [account_preferences.language](hired.video/api/src/services/auth/AuthService.ts) handshake only seeds the visitor's locale on the email/password register path. OAuth signups via [/api/oauth/callback](hired.video/api/src/routes/oauth.ts) (Google / LinkedIn) skip the form entirely so the visitor's pre-auth `i18n.language` is lost — `LocaleSync` then overwrites their session with the DB default `"en"` the moment the redirect lands. Fix: forward the active locale through the OAuth start URL as a state-bound param (signed via existing `state` JWT to prevent tampering) and persist it in the same `accountPreferences` seed inside `handleOAuthCallback`. Unblocks: complete pre-auth locale carry-through promised by #1148. |
| 2115 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P2 | `feature` | **Province-level geo for fr-CA suggestion precision** | [GET /api/_meta/geo](hired.video/api/src/routes/meta.ts) returns ISO-3166-1 country only, so [GeoLocaleSuggestionBanner](hired.video/frontend/components/i18n/GeoLocaleSuggestionBanner.tsx) suggests `fr-CA` to every Canadian visitor — including English-Canadian visitors in Toronto / Vancouver who'd see an unwanted French prompt. Cloudflare exposes `cf-iplocation.subdivision` / `request.cf.region` in the worker; surfacing that through the geo endpoint lets the banner gate fr-CA to QC + NB (officially bilingual) and skip the prompt elsewhere. Until then, the dismiss-once-per-browser flag keeps the blast radius small. |
