| 2120 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **Settings language picker uses translated labels instead of native script** | [Settings.tsx:1397-1401](hired.video/frontend/pages/Settings.tsx#L1397-L1401) renders each option via `t("settings.appearance.languageOption.${loc}")`, so the same row reads "Spanish" when UI=en, "Inglés" / "Español" when UI=es, etc. The universal i18n convention (LinkedIn / Stripe / GitHub) is to show every language in its OWN script regardless of the active locale, so the new [LocaleSwitcher](hired.video/frontend/components/i18n/LocaleSwitcher.tsx) consumes the `NATIVE_LABELS` map in [lib/i18n/locale-labels.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/i18n/locale-labels.ts). Settings should swap to the same map for consistency (and the `settings.appearance.languageOption.*` keys can then be deleted everywhere they appear in `en.json` / `es.json` / `fr-CA.json`). Easy DRY win. |
| 2171 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P3 | `quality` | **Marketing hero/section description copy is hand-rolled per page — no shared lede/section-subtitle component, so layout decisions (max-width, alignment) drift across ~15 marketing pages** (opened 2026-05-31 while fixing the centered-text-not-full-width report). Fix pass removed the `max-w-*xl mx-auto` width caps from the centered description `<p>` elements across Tools, Home, About, Careers, ChromeExtension, ForRecruiters, Companies, Competitors, Security, Rewards, Pricing, Resumes, Help, InterviewPractice, Outreach so the lede fills the same width as its full-width sibling heading (the headings were never capped). Each page still inlines the same `text-xl text-muted-foreground mb-8` lede + `text-muted-foreground … mb-* text-center` section-subtitle markup, so the next styling change must be made in ~15 places again. To close: extract `<MarketingLede>` + `<MarketingSectionSubtitle>` presentational components (className passthrough + children) and migrate the marketing pages onto them, alongside the existing `<MarketingFAQ>`/AppShell page-chrome convention. Unblocks: one-line control over marketing body-copy width/typography; prevents this exact drift from recurring. |
| 339 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P4 | `quality` | **Each `/tools/*` page open-codes the AppShell + AuthOverlay + max-w-6xl/7xl wrapper** | All 13 files under `pages/tools/` repeat the same `<AppShell><div className={showAuthOverlay ? "relative" : undefined}>{showAuthOverlay && <AuthOverlay …/>}<div className="max-w-6xl mx-auto p-6">…body…</div></div></AppShell>` scaffolding. The duplicate `pt-16` was stripped 2026-05-04 but the wrapper itself is still copy-pasted. Fix: extract a `<ToolPageShell toolId icon iconBg title description authOverlay={…}>` component that owns the chrome + ToolPageHeader so each tool page becomes `return <ToolPageShell …>{body}</ToolPageShell>`. Unblocks: future global tool-page changes (Crisp targeting, ad slots, layout tweaks) ship in one file instead of 13. Identified 2026-05-04. |
| 1325 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P4 | `bug` | **Tasks.test.tsx — 11 tests fail with `getVerificationStatus is not a function` because the test's `mockUseAuth.mockReturnValue` doesn't stub it** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1323, pre-existing). [`__tests__/pages/Tasks.test.tsx:87-92`](hired.video/frontend/__tests__/pages/Tasks.test.tsx) mocks `useAuth()` returning `{ user, isAuthenticated, isLoading, isEmailVerified }`. AppShell mounts [EmailVerificationBanner](hired.video/frontend/components/auth/EmailVerificationBanner.tsx), which calls `getVerificationStatus()` in a `useEffect`; the mock returns `undefined` for that field, so calling it throws. Not caused by the #1323 surface consolidation — the same failure occurs in any Tasks render path. To close: add `getVerificationStatus: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ emailConfirmed: true })` + `resendEmailVerification: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined)` to the mock, or extract a shared `mockAuth(overrides)` helper that mirrors `AuthContextValue` so the mock can't drift from the real shape (this fix probably belongs at a single test-helper file rather than per-test, to prevent the same drift on Studio / Profile / Settings tests). |
| 1326 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Soon | P4 | `bug` | **`npm run lint:ci` fails to even start — `eslint.config.js` imports `./eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js` but that file has no default export** (opened 2026-05-25 alongside #1323, pre-existing). `frontend/eslint.config.js:9` does `import requirePageChrome from "./eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js";` — the rule module must `export default` an ESLint rule object (or the config must use a named import). Until fixed, every `lint:ci` / `lint:strict` / `lint:fix` invocation throws `SyntaxError: The requested module './eslint-rules/require-page-chrome.js' does not provide an export named 'default'` before a single file is linted, which means the [feedback_new_page_checklist] ESLint backstop is not actually running on CI. To close: either add `export default <ruleObject>` to `require-page-chrome.js`, OR change the import in `eslint.config.js` to the actual exported name. Cross-check `quality-check.mjs` for the same broken-config path. |
| 991 | T3 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **Localise XYZ wand strings — currently English-only labels/toasts/dialog copy** (opened 2026-05-23 alongside the XYZ wand pass) | The first-pass XYZ wand surface ([HighlightsEditor.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/resume-sections/HighlightsEditor.tsx), [XyzTextWand.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/resume-sections/XyzTextWand.tsx), [BulletReviewDialog.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/resume-sections/BulletReviewDialog.tsx)) hardcodes English copy ("Review XYZ-format bullets", "Bullets rewritten in XYZ format", tooltips like "Rewrite this summary with AI"). The rest of the resume editor goes through `t("…")` keys in [en.json](hired.video/frontend/public/locales/en.json) + [es.json](hired.video/frontend/public/locales/es.json). To close: extract the strings, add keys under `aiWand.xyz.*`, wire `useTranslation()`, supply Spanish translations to match the existing locale parity. Low priority — internal-facing first pass — but flagged so the i18n debt doesn't compound. |
| 1147 | T2 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `feature` | **`/rewards` page copy is English-only; the FAQ + section bodies don't go through `useTranslation()` like the rest of the marketing surface** (opened 2026-05-24 alongside #1144) | All section titles, FAQ Q/As, callout text, and CTA copy in [Rewards.tsx](hired.video/frontend/pages/Rewards.tsx) are hard-coded English strings. The platform's marketing pages use `t(...)` keys backed by [en.json + es.json](hired.video/frontend/public/locales/). To close: extract the strings into `rewards.*` keys, add Spanish translations to match the existing locale parity, and wire `useTranslation()` at the page level. Pairs with #991 (XYZ wand i18n) since both are "static page copy not yet localised" gaps with the same fix shape. |
| 2110 | T4 | 🔲 Open | Later | P4 | `quality` | **Imperative dialog titles are literal English, not i18n'd** (opened 2026-05-30 during the `window.alert`/`confirm`/`prompt` → branded-modal sweep). Replaced every browser-native dialog across the frontend with the new `confirmDialog`/`alertDialog`/`promptDialog` API ([lib/dialogs.ts](hired.video/frontend/lib/dialogs.ts) + [components/ui/DialogHost.tsx](hired.video/frontend/components/ui/DialogHost.tsx), mounted once in App.tsx). The migrated call sites correctly preserve existing `t(...)` translations for the message/`description`, but the new short `title` strings (e.g. "Delete service", "Release number", "Error") were added as literal English to avoid touching locale JSON in a wide mechanical sweep. To close: add i18n keys for the ~30 dialog titles (group under a `dialogs.*` namespace) and replace the literals. Low risk, purely additive. Unblocks: full localization parity for confirmation/alert/prompt modals. |

